(16, 'Minicon', 'Norgestrel', 40.04, 1, 'x 28\'s tablet strip', '28\'s in a strip', 'Tablet', '0.075 mg', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications of Minicon</strong></p><p>Minicon tablets are indicated for use by females of reproductive potential to prevent pregnancy. This tablet are not for use as emergency contraception.</p><p><strong>Theropeutic Class</strong></p><p>Emergency Contraceptive Pill, Oral Contraceptive preparations</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Minicon (and more specifically the active stereoisomer levoMinicon ) binds to the progesterone and estrogen receptors within the female reproductive tract, the mammary gland, the hypothalamus, and the pituitary. Once bound to the receptor, progestins like levoMinicon will slow the frequency of release of gonadotropin releasing hormone (GnRH) from the hypothalamus and blunt the pre-ovulatory LH (luteinizing hormone) surge. Loss of the LH surge inhibits ovulation and thereby prevents pregnancy.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration of Minicon</strong></p><p>0.075 mg at same time each day</p><p><strong>Dosage of Minicon</strong></p><p>To achieve maximum contraceptive effectiveness, Minicon Tablets must be taken exactly as directed. The woman should take one tablet every day, at the same time. The administration is continuous, with no interruption between pill packs.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Minicon tablet is contraindicated for use by women who are known to have the following conditions: Known or suspected pregnancy Known or suspected carcinoma of the breast, or other progestin-sensitive cancer, now or in the past Undiagnosed abnormal uterine bleeding Hypersensitivity to any component of this product Benign or malignant liver tumors</p><p><strong>Side Effects of Minicon</strong></p><p>An increased risk of the following adverse reactions has been reported with the use of progestin-only oral contraceptives: Delayed follicular atresia/ovarian cysts, Menstrual irregularity, changes in menstrual flow; breakthrough bleeding/spotting; amenorrhea, prolonged bleeding. The following adverse reactions were reported in ≥5% of subjects in the Minicon&nbsp;Tablet clinical studies: Headache Dizziness Nausea Increased appetite Abdominal pain, cramps and bloating Fatigue Vaginal discharge Dysmenorrhea Nervousness Backache Breast discomfort Acne</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><p>Pregnancy Category: XLactation: unsafe</p><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><p>Migraine/Headache: The onset or exacerbation of migraine, or development of headache with a new pattern that is recurrent, persistent, or severe requires evaluation of the cause because women with migraine may be at increased risk of stroke.Drug Interactions: The effectiveness of progestin-only pills is reduced by hepatic enzyme-inducing drugs such as phenytoin, carbamazepine, barbiturates, rifampin, efavirenz, bosentan and herbal preparations containing St. John’s Wort (hypericum perforatum ). This could result in unintended pregnancy or breakthrough bleeding. During concomitant use of Minicon and substances that may affect its efficacy, it is recommended that a nonhormonal back-up method of contraception (such as condom) be used in addition to the regular intake of Minicon Tablets. Use of a nonhormonal back-up method is recommeded for 28 days after discontinuation of substances that have led to induction of hepatic microsomal enzymes. For women receiving long-term therapy with hepatic enzyme inducers, another method of contraception should be considered. Effectiveness of progestin-containing hormonal contraceptives and emergency contraceptive ulipristal acetate may be decreased if progestin-containing hormonal contraceptives are used within five days after ulipristal acetate dosing. If a woman wishes to use Minicon Tablets after using ulipristal acetate, she should do so no sooner than 5 days after the intake of ulipristal acetate and she should use a reliable barrier method for subsequent acts of intercourse until her next menstrual period. Gastrointestinal: Diarrhea and/or vomiting within 4 hours after taking a pill may reduce hormone absorption. Women should use of a nonhormonal back-up method of birth control (such as a condom or spermicide) during the next 48 hours.Interactions with Laboratory Tests: The following endocrine tests may be affected by Minicon Tablets use: Sex hormone-binding globulin (SHBG) concentrations may be decreased. Total thyroxine concentrations may be decreased, due to a decrease in thyroid binding globulin (TBG). However, free thyroxine level should remain unchanged.</p><p><strong>Overdose Effects of Minicon</strong></p><p>Symptoms of oral contraceptive overdosage may include nausea, vomiting, breast tenderness, dizziness, somnolence ( drowsiness/fatigue), and withdrawal bleeding in females. There is no specific antidote and further treatment of overdose, if necessary, is directed to the symptoms.</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Store at controlled room temperature between 20° to 25°C.</p><p><strong>Drug Classes</strong></p><p>Oral Contraceptive preparations</p><p><strong>Mode Of Action</strong></p><p>Progestin-only oral contraceptives such as Minicon tablets prevent conception by suppres sing ovulation in approximately half of the cycles in users, thickening the cervical mucus to inhibit sperm penetration, lowering the midcycle LH and FSH peaks, slowing the movement of the ovum through the fallopian tubes, and altering the endometrium. Serum progestin levels peak about two hours after oral administration, followed by rapid distribution and elimination. By 24 hours after drug ingestion, serum levels are near baseline, making efficacy dependent upon rigid adherence to the dosing schedule. There are large variations in serum levels among individual users. Progestin-only administration results in lower steady-state progestin levels and a shorter elimination half-life than concomitant administration with estrogens.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy</strong></p><p>Pregnancy: Minicon Tablets are contraindicated for use in pregnant women because there is no need for pregnancy prevention in a woman who is already pregnant. Published studies report no harmful effects on fetal development associated with long-term use of contraceptive doses of oral progestins in pregnant women. Discontinue Minicon Tablets if pregnancy is confirmed.Nursing Mothers: Small amounts of progestin pass into the breast milk, resulting in steroid levels in infant plasma. No adverse effects have been reported on breastfeeding performance or infant health. The developmental and health benefits of breastfeeding should be considered along with the mother’s clinical need for Minicon Tablets and any potential adverse effects on the breastfed infant from Minicon Tablets or from the underlying maternal condition.</p><p><strong>Pediatric Uses</strong></p><p>Pediatric Use: The safety and efficacy of Minicon tablets have been established in women of reproductive age, including adolescents as young as 15 years of age, and almost 30% of subjects in the clinical trials who were under 20 years of age. Use of this product before menarche is not indicated.Geriatric Use: Minicon tablet Tablets have not been studied in postmenopausal women and is not indicated in this population.</p>', 'active', '1174_1733402012.webp', 12, 3, NULL, '2024-12-05 17:33:32', '2024-12-14 21:58:39'),
(17, 'Senora Panty', 'Sanitary Napkin', 130.00, 1, 'Box', '15\'s pads in a box', 'Pad', '15 pads', 'no', 'yes', '<p>Stay confident and worry-free on your heavy flow days with Senora Panty 15 Pads. Its advanced features keep you dry, fresh and comfortable. The pad’s interior instantly absorbs and evenly distributes fluid. Also, it has an extra layer of protection to prevent back leakage.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions Of Senora Panty 15 Pads:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Choose the right size and absorbency for your flow.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Apply the Senora Panty 15 Pads to your underwear, with the adhesive side down.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Secure the Senora Panty 15 Pads in place by folding the wings down.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Change the Senora Panty 15 Pads every 4 to 6 hours, or more often if it becomes wet or soiled.</span></li></ul><p><strong>Storage Guidelines Of Senora Panty 15 Pads:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Store Senora Panty 15 Padss in a cool and dry place.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Do not store Senora Panty 15 Padss in a humid environment.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Keep Senora Panty 15 Padss out of reach of children.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Do not store used Senora Panty 15 Padss.</span>&nbsp;</li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Choose the right size and absorbency for your flow.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Secure the Senora Panty 15 Pads in place by folding the wings down.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Change the Senora Panty 15 Pads every 4 to 6 hours, or more often if it becomes wet or soiled.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Dispose of the used Senora Panty 15 Pads in a sealed bag or container.</span></li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '595_1733402741.jpg', 13, 3, NULL, '2024-12-05 17:45:41', '2024-12-05 17:45:41'),
(18, 'Senora Belt', 'Sanitary Napkin', 130.00, 1, 'Box', '15 pads in a box', 'Pad', '15 pads', 'no', 'yes', '<p>Stay confident and worry-free on your heavy flow days with Senora Belt 15 Pads. Its advanced features keep you dry, fresh and comfortable. The pad’s interior instantly absorbs and evenly distributes fluid. Also, it has an extra layer of protection to prevent back leakage.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions Of Senora Belt 15 Pads:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Choose the right size and absorbency for your flow.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Apply the Senora Belt 15 Pads to your underwear, with the adhesive side down.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Secure the Senora Belt 15 Pads in place by folding the wings down.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Change the Senora Belt 15 Pads every 4 to 6 hours, or more often if it becomes wet or soiled.</span></li></ul><p><strong>Storage Guidelines Of Senora Belt 15 Pads:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Store Senora Belt 15 Padss in a cool and dry place.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Do not store Senora Belt 15 Padss in a humid environment.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Keep Senora Belt 15 Padss out of reach of children.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Do not store used Senora Belt 15 Padss.</span></li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Choose the right size and absorbency for your flow.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Secure the Senora Belt 15 Pads in place by folding the wings down.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Change the Senora Belt 15 Pads every 4 to 6 hours, or more often if it becomes wet or soiled.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Dispose of the used Senora Belt 15 Pads in a sealed bag or container.</span></li></ul>', 'active', '1495_1733410826.webp', 13, 3, NULL, '2024-12-05 17:59:05', '2024-12-05 20:00:26'),
(19, 'Get Sure HCG Urine Pregnancy Test Cassette', 'Pregnancy Test Strip', 80.00, 1, 'Cassette', '1\'s in box', 'Cassette', '1 pc', 'no', 'yes', '<ul><li><strong>Early detection of pregnancy.</strong></li><li><strong>Can be used any time of the day.</strong></li><li><strong>Fast and easy to use.</strong></li><li><strong>Accurate results in 3 to 5 minutes.</strong></li><li><strong>Suitable for self-testing and professional use.</strong></li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Get Sure HCG Urine Pregnancy Test Cassette is a pregnancy detection kit for early pregnancy detection at home. It is an instant detector that is easy to use</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">How to use</strong></p><ol><li>Collect urine specimen (morning\'s first sample is preferable) using a urine cup.</li><li>Remove the test cassette from its foil pouch.</li><li>Use the dropper to draw a urine sample and dispense 2 drops into the sample well on the cassette. Avoid overfilling.</li><li>Read results within 5 minutes, but not more than 10 minutes.</li><li>Dispose of the test device after a single use in the dustbin.</li></ol><p><strong>Result</strong>:</p><ul><li>Negative: One pink line appears in the control area, indicating not pregnant.</li><li>Positive: Two pink lines appear in both the control area and test area, indicating pregnancy. The lines may vary in intensity.</li><li>Inconclusive: No distinct pink-purple-colored band is visible in both areas or only in the test area. Repeat the test in this case.</li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information</strong></p><ul><li>Do not be exposed to sunlight or extreme temperatures.&nbsp;Keep out of reach of children.</li><li>Discard after the use</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p>', 'active', '1355_1733412678.png', 15, 3, NULL, '2024-12-05 20:31:18', '2024-12-05 20:43:28'),
(20, 'WHISPER MAXI NIGHTS', 'Sanitary Napkin', 430.00, 1, 'Box', '15 pads in a box', 'Pad', '15 pads', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Stay Confident on Heavy Flow Days with MAXI NIGHTS Pads</strong></p><p>Feel secure and comfortable during your heavy flow days with MAXI NIGHTS Pads. Designed for overnight protection, these pads feature advanced technology that quickly absorbs and evenly distributes fluid, keeping you dry and fresh. With an additional layer of protection, they help prevent leakage, so you can sleep worry-free.</p><p><strong>Instructions for Use:</strong></p><ol><li>Select the appropriate size and absorbency based on your flow.</li><li>Attach the pad to your underwear, ensuring the adhesive side is facing down.</li><li>Fold the wings around the sides of your underwear to secure the pad in place.</li><li>Replace the pad every 4 to 6 hours, or sooner if it becomes wet or soiled.</li></ol><p><strong>Storage Guidelines:</strong></p><ol><li>Keep pads in a cool, dry place.</li><li>Avoid storing in humid areas.</li><li>Ensure pads are out of reach of children.</li><li>Do not store used pads.</li></ol><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ol><li>Always select the right absorbency and size for your needs.</li><li>Secure the pad in place by folding the wings around the sides.</li><li>Change the pad regularly, at least every 4 to 6 hours, or more frequently if necessary.</li><li>Dispose of used pads in a sealed container or bag.</li></ol>', 'active', '283_1733547299.jpeg', 16, 3, NULL, '2024-12-07 09:54:59', '2024-12-07 09:57:49'),
(21, 'Joya Sanitary Napkin (Belt)', 'Sanitary Napkin', 60.00, 1, 'Box', '8 pads in a box', 'Pad', '8 pads', 'no', 'no', '<p>Stay confident and worry-free on your heavy flow days with Joya Sanitary Napkin (Belt) 8 Pads. Its advanced features keep you dry, fresh and comfortable. The pad’s interior instantly absorbs and evenly distributes fluid. Also, it has an extra layer of protection to prevent back leakage.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions Of Joya Sanitary Napkin (Belt) 8 Pads:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Choose the right size and absorbency for your flow.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Apply the Joya Sanitary Napkin (Belt) 8 Pads to your underwear, with the adhesive side down.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Secure the Joya Sanitary Napkin (Belt) 8 Pads in place by folding the wings down.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Change the Joya Sanitary Napkin (Belt) 8 Pads every 4 to 6 hours, or more often if it becomes wet or soiled.</span></li></ul><p><strong>Storage Guidelines Of Joya Sanitary Napkin (Belt) 8 Pads:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Store Joya Sanitary Napkin (Belt) 8 Padss in a cool and dry place.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Do not store Joya Sanitary Napkin (Belt) 8 Padss in a humid environment.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Keep Joya Sanitary Napkin (Belt) 8 Padss out of reach of children.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Do not store used Joya Sanitary Napkin (Belt) 8 Padss.</span></li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Choose the right size and absorbency for your flow.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Secure the Joya Sanitary Napkin (Belt) 8 Pads in place by folding the wings down.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Change the Joya Sanitary Napkin (Belt) 8 Pads every 4 to 6 hours, or more often if it becomes wet or soiled.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Dispose of the used Joya Sanitary Napkin (Belt) 8 Pads in a sealed bag or container.</span></li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '717_1733547950.jpg', 12, 3, NULL, '2024-12-07 10:05:50', '2024-12-07 10:05:50'),
(22, 'Freedom Heavy Flow Wings', 'Sanitary Napkin', 110.00, 1, 'Box', '8 pad\'s in a box', 'Pad', '8 pads', 'no', 'no', '<p><strong>Stay Confident and Comfortable with Freedom Heavy Flow Wings Pads</strong></p><p>Experience reliable protection on your heaviest days with Freedom Heavy Flow Wings Pads. Designed to keep you dry, fresh, and comfortable, these pads feature advanced absorbency technology that quickly absorbs and evenly distributes fluid. Plus, an extra layer of protection helps prevent leaks at the back.</p><p><strong>How to Use Freedom Heavy Flow Wings Pads:</strong></p><ol><li>Select the right pad size and absorbency level based on your flow.</li><li>Attach the pad to your underwear with the adhesive side facing down.</li><li>Secure the wings by folding them over the sides of your underwear for added comfort and security.</li><li>Replace the pad every 4 to 6 hours, or sooner if it becomes wet or soiled.</li></ol><p><strong>Storage Instructions:</strong></p><ul><li>Keep pads in a cool, dry place.</li><li>Avoid storing pads in damp or humid areas.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li><li>Do not store used pads.</li></ul><p><strong>Safety Tips:</strong></p><ul><li>Always choose the correct size and absorbency for your needs.</li><li>Be sure to fold the wings securely to keep the pad in place.</li><li>Replace pads every 4 to 6 hours, or more frequently if needed.</li><li>Dispose of used pads in a sealed bag or container to ensure hygiene.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '683_1733548986.webp', 14, 3, NULL, '2024-12-07 10:23:06', '2024-12-07 10:23:06'),
(23, 'Whisper Ultra Comfort XL', 'Sanitary Napkin', 195.00, 1, 'Box', '8 pads in a box', 'Pad', '8 pads', 'no', 'no', '<p><strong>Stay Confident and Comfortable with Ultra Comfort XL Pads</strong></p><p>Feel confident and worry-free during heavy flow days with Ultra Comfort XL Pads. Designed to keep you dry, fresh, and comfortable, these pads feature advanced technology that instantly absorbs and evenly distributes fluid. An additional protective layer helps prevent leaks at the back for extra peace of mind.</p><p><strong>How to Use Ultra Comfort XL Pads:</strong></p><ol><li>Select the right size and absorbency based on your flow.</li><li>Attach the pad to your underwear with the adhesive side facing down.</li><li>Secure the wings by folding them over the sides of your underwear to keep the pad in place.</li><li>Change the pad every 4 to 6 hours, or more often if needed.</li></ol><p><strong>Storage Instructions:</strong></p><ul><li>Store pads in a cool, dry place.</li><li>Keep away from humid environments.</li><li>Store out of reach of children.</li><li>Do not store used pads.</li></ul><p><strong>Safety Tips:</strong></p><ul><li>Always choose the correct size and absorbency for your flow.</li><li>Secure the wings to keep the pad in place.</li><li>Change pads every 4 to 6 hours, or sooner if needed.</li><li>Dispose of used pads in a sealed bag or container.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '237_1733549508.png', 16, 3, NULL, '2024-12-07 10:31:48', '2024-12-07 10:31:48'),
(24, 'I-Pill DS', 'Levonorgestrel', 70.00, 1, 'tablet packet', '1 tablet pack', 'Tablet', '1.5 mg', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications for Emergency Contraception with I-Pill DS 1.5 mg</strong></p><p>I-Pill DS 1.5 mg is used as an emergency contraceptive to prevent pregnancy after unprotected sexual intercourse. This method is most effective when taken as soon as possible, preferably within 12 hours and no later than 72 hours (3 days) after the incident.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Emergency Contraceptive Pill</li><li>Oral Contraceptive Preparations</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><p>I-Pill DS 1.5 mg contains a synthetic form of progesterone, a hormone that plays a key role in the menstrual cycle. Normally, progesterone helps regulate ovulation and prepares the womb lining for pregnancy. This medication works by maintaining high progesterone levels, which prevents ovulation, making it harder for the sperm to fertilize an egg.</p><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><p>Take one tablet (1.5 mg) orally as soon as possible, but within 72 hours of unprotected intercourse. The pill can be taken at any time during the menstrual cycle, assuming there is no existing pregnancy. For best results, take the tablet within 12 hours of the incident. If a regular contraceptive method is being used, it can be continued as usual. If there is another instance of unprotected sex after taking I-Pill DS 1.5 mg, the pill will not prevent pregnancy.</p><p><strong>Administration:</strong></p><ul><li>Take one tablet with water.</li><li>The tablet should not be chewed, but swallowed whole.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><p>Certain medications, including anticonvulsants (such as phenobarbital, phenytoin, primidone, and carbamazepine), and other drugs like rifampicin and griseofulvin, may reduce the effectiveness of I-Pill DS 1.5 mg.</p><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Do not use if allergic to any ingredient in I-Pill DS 1.5 mg.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><p>Common side effects may include:</p><ul><li>Nausea and vomiting</li><li>Dizziness, fatigue, or headache</li><li>Abdominal pain</li><li>Tenderness in the breasts</li><li>Spotting or irregular bleeding</li></ul><p>If any unusual or severe side effects occur, consult a healthcare provider.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Not recommended during an existing pregnancy.</li><li>While no significant fetal malformations have been observed with progestogen use, it\'s advised to avoid breastfeeding immediately after taking the tablet, as the medication is secreted into breast milk.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>I-Pill DS 1.5 mg is not meant to be used regularly and should only be used as emergency contraception.</li><li>It does not replace regular contraception methods.</li><li>After using the pill, menstrual periods may occur earlier or later than expected. A pregnancy test is recommended if the period is delayed by more than 5 days or if abnormal bleeding occurs.</li><li>The use of I-Pill DS 1.5 mg does not prevent sexually transmitted infections.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose:</strong></p><p>There have been no reports of acute toxicity with multiple doses of the medication. However, if vomiting occurs within two hours of taking the pill, take another tablet immediately.</p><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><p>Store in a cool, dry place away from light. Keep out of reach of children.</p>', 'active', '671_1733550793.png', 17, 3, NULL, '2024-12-07 10:53:13', '2024-12-07 10:54:28'),
(25, 'Norpill', 'Levonorgestrel', 70.00, 1, 'tablet packet', '1 tablet pack', 'Tablet', '1.5 mg', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Emergency Contraception with Norpill 1.5 mg</strong></p><p>Norpill 1.5 mg is an emergency contraceptive designed to prevent pregnancy following unprotected sexual intercourse. It should be used as soon as possible, ideally within 12 hours, but no later than 72 hours (3 days) after the incident.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Emergency Contraceptive Pill</li><li>Oral Contraceptive Preparations</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><p>Norpill 1.5 mg contains a synthetic form of progesterone, a naturally occurring female hormone. In the menstrual cycle, progesterone helps regulate ovulation and prepares the womb for pregnancy. If pregnancy doesn\'t occur, progesterone levels drop, causing menstruation. Norpill 1.5 mg increases progesterone levels, preventing ovulation and stopping further eggs from being released, thus reducing the risk of pregnancy.</p><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><p>Take one tablet (1.5 mg) as soon as possible after unprotected intercourse, within a 72-hour window. For best results, take it within 12 hours. Norpill 1.5 mg can be taken at any point in the menstrual cycle, assuming there is no existing pregnancy. The tablet should be swallowed whole with a glass of water. If another instance of unprotected sex occurs after taking Norpill 1.5 mg, the pill will not work again.</p><p>If you are using a regular method of contraception (such as birth control pills), continue to use it as usual after taking Norpill 1.5 mg. If menstruation doesn\'t occur during the next pill-free period after using Norpill 1.5 mg, perform a pregnancy test to rule out pregnancy.</p><p><strong>Administration:</strong></p><ul><li>Take one tablet orally with water, without chewing.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><p>Certain medications, including anticonvulsants (phenobarbital, phenytoin, primidone, carbamazepine) and other drugs like rifampicin and griseofulvin, may reduce the effectiveness of Norpill 1.5 mg.</p><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Do not use if you are allergic to any ingredient in Norpill 1.5 mg.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><p>Common side effects may include:</p><ul><li>Nausea and vomiting</li><li>Dizziness, headache, or fatigue</li><li>Abdominal pain</li><li>Tenderness in the breasts</li><li>Spotting or irregular bleeding</li></ul><p>Consult a healthcare provider if any severe or unusual side effects occur.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Norpill 1.5 mg is not intended for use during pregnancy and will not interrupt an existing pregnancy.</li><li>Epidemiological studies indicate no major risk of fetal malformation from progestogen use.</li><li>It is safe to breastfeed, but as Norpill 1.5 mg is secreted into breast milk, it is recommended to breastfeed immediately before taking the pill and avoid breastfeeding for a period after taking it.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Emergency contraception should only be used in exceptional circumstances, not as a regular method of birth control.</li><li>It is important to use another contraceptive method (e.g., condoms) until the next menstrual cycle after using Norpill 1.5 mg.</li><li>After taking the pill, periods may occur earlier or later than expected. If your period is delayed by more than 5 days or if there is abnormal bleeding, a pregnancy test should be performed.</li><li>Emergency contraception does not protect against sexually transmitted diseases.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose:</strong></p><p>There are no reported cases of acute toxicity from taking multiple doses of Norpill 1.5 mg. If vomiting occurs within 2 hours after taking the pill, take another tablet immediately.</p><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><p>Store Norpill 1.5 mg in a cool, dry place, away from light. Keep out of reach of children.</p>', 'active', '1837_1733551396.webp', 4, 3, NULL, '2024-12-07 11:03:16', '2024-12-07 11:03:16'),
(26, 'WHISPER MAXI FIT', 'Sanitary Napkin', 430.00, 1, 'Box', '15 pads in a box', 'Pad', '15 pads L wings', 'no', 'yes', '<p>Stay confident and worry-free on your heavy flow days with WHISPER MAXI FIT 15 Pads L Wings. Its advanced features keep you dry, fresh and comfortable. The pad’s interior instantly absorbs and evenly distributes fluid. Also, it has an extra layer of protection to prevent back leakage.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions Of WHISPER MAXI FIT 15 Pads L Wings:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Choose the right size and absorbency for your flow.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Apply the WHISPER MAXI FIT 15 Pads L Wings to your underwear, with the adhesive side down.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Secure the WHISPER MAXI FIT 15 Pads L Wings in place by folding the wings down.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Change the WHISPER MAXI FIT 15 Pads L Wings every 4 to 6 hours, or more often if it becomes wet or soiled.</span></li></ul><p><strong>Storage Guidelines Of WHISPER MAXI FIT 15 Pads L Wings:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Store WHISPER MAXI FIT 15 Pads L Wingss in a cool and dry place.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Do not store WHISPER MAXI FIT 15 Pads L Wingss in a humid environment.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Keep WHISPER MAXI FIT 15 Pads L Wingss out of reach of children.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Do not store used WHISPER MAXI FIT 15 Pads L Wingss.</span></li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Choose the right size and absorbency for your flow.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Secure the WHISPER MAXI FIT 15 Pads L Wings in place by folding the wings down.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Change the WHISPER MAXI FIT 15 Pads L Wings every 4 to 6 hours, or more often if it becomes wet or soiled.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Dispose of the used WHISPER MAXI FIT 15 Pads L Wings in a sealed bag or container.</span></li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '635_1733552348.jpg', 16, 3, NULL, '2024-12-07 11:19:08', '2024-12-07 11:19:08'),
