(29, 'Freedom Belt System', 'Sanitary Napkin', 60.00, 1, 'Box', '8 pad\'s in a box', 'Pad', '8 pad\'s', 'no', 'yes', '<p>Stay confident and worry-free on your heavy flow days with Freedom Belt System 8 Pads. Its advanced features keep you dry, fresh and comfortable. The pad’s interior instantly absorbs and evenly distributes fluid. Also, it has an extra layer of protection to prevent back leakage.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions Of Freedom Belt System 8 Pads:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Choose the right size and absorbency for your flow.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Apply the Freedom Belt System 8 Pads to your underwear, with the adhesive side down.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Secure the Freedom Belt System 8 Pads in place by folding the wings down.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Change the Freedom Belt System 8 Pads every 4 to 6 hours, or more often if it becomes wet or soiled.</span></li></ul><p><strong>Storage Guidelines Of Freedom Belt System 8 Pads:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Store Freedom Belt System 8 Padss in a cool and dry place.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Do not store Freedom Belt System 8 Padss in a humid environment.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Keep Freedom Belt System 8 Padss out of reach of children.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Do not store used Freedom Belt System 8 Padss.</span></li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Choose the right size and absorbency for your flow.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Secure the Freedom Belt System 8 Pads in place by folding the wings down.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Change the Freedom Belt System 8 Pads every 4 to 6 hours, or more often if it becomes wet or soiled.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Dispose of the used Freedom Belt System 8 Pads in a sealed bag or container.</span></li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1516_1733554366.webp', 14, 3, NULL, '2024-12-07 11:52:46', '2024-12-07 11:52:46'),
(30, 'Joya Extra Heavy Flow Wings', 'Sanitary Napkin', 110.00, 1, 'Box', '8 pad\'s in a box', 'Pad', '8 pads', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Stay Confident and Comfortable with Joya Extra Heavy Flow Wings Pads</strong></p><p>Experience worry-free protection on your heavy flow days with Joya Extra Heavy Flow Wings Pads. Designed with advanced features, these pads provide dryness, comfort, and freshness. The interior of the pad quickly absorbs and distributes fluid, while an extra layer of protection prevents back leakage.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions:</strong></p><ol><li>Select the appropriate size and absorbency based on your flow.</li><li>Apply the Joya Extra Heavy Flow Wings Pad to your underwear with the adhesive side facing down.</li><li>Secure the pad in place by folding the wings around the sides of your underwear.</li><li>Change the pad every 4 to 6 hours, or more frequently if it becomes wet or soiled.</li></ol><p><strong>Storage Guidelines:</strong></p><ul><li>Store the pads in a cool, dry place.</li><li>Keep them away from humid environments to maintain their effectiveness.</li><li>Store out of reach of children.</li><li>Do not store used pads.</li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Ensure you choose the right size and absorbency for your flow.</li><li>Always secure the wings properly to prevent shifting.</li><li>Change the pad every 4 to 6 hours or sooner if it becomes saturated.</li><li>Dispose of used pads in a sealed bag or container to maintain hygiene.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '748_1733557916.png', 12, 3, NULL, '2024-12-07 12:51:56', '2024-12-07 12:51:56'),
(31, 'Joya All Night Wings', 'Sanitary Napkin', 120.00, 1, 'Box', '8 pad\'s in a box', 'Pad', '8 pad\'s', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Stay Confident and Comfortable with Joya All Night Wings Pads</strong></p><p>Feel confident and worry-free during your heavy flow nights with Joya All Night Wings Pads. Designed with advanced features to keep you dry, fresh, and comfortable, these pads feature an interior that instantly absorbs and evenly distributes fluid. They also have an extra layer of protection to prevent back leakage.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions:</strong></p><ol><li>Select the right size and absorbency based on your flow.</li><li>Place the Joya All Night Wings Pad onto your underwear, with the adhesive side facing down.</li><li>Fold the wings around the sides of your underwear to secure the pad in place.</li><li>Change the pad every 4 to 6 hours, or more frequently if it becomes wet or soiled.</li></ol><p><strong>Storage Guidelines:</strong></p><ul><li>Store pads in a cool, dry place.</li><li>Avoid storing in a humid environment.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li><li>Do not store used pads.</li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Choose the appropriate size and absorbency for your flow.</li><li>Secure the wings properly to prevent shifting.</li><li>Change the pad every 4 to 6 hours, or sooner if it becomes saturated.</li><li>Dispose of used pads in a sealed bag or container to maintain hygiene.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '656_1733558153.webp', 12, 3, NULL, '2024-12-07 12:55:53', '2024-12-07 12:55:53'),
(32, 'Femipil', 'Ethinyl Estradiol + Levonorgestrel + Ferrous Fumarate', 24.50, 1, 'x 28 tablet\'s strip', '28\'s in a strip', 'Tablet', '0.03 mg+0.15 mg+75 mg', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications of Femipil 0.030+0.15mg</strong></p><p>Femipil is an oral contraceptive pill that works through several mechanisms to prevent pregnancy. It inhibits ovulation, thickens cervical mucus to prevent sperm from entering the uterus, and alters the endometrium to prevent the implantation of a fertilized egg. The pill also reduces sperm motility in the fallopian tubes, making it more difficult for sperm to reach the egg.</p><p><strong>Suitable for:</strong></p><ul><li>Women aged 15-69 years (except smokers and regular tobacco users).</li><li>Women seeking an effective, temporary contraceptive method.</li><li>Women suffering from anemia due to excessive menstrual blood loss.</li><li>Women with irregular menstrual cycles.</li><li>Breastfeeding mothers (if the child is older than 6 months).</li></ul><p><strong>Composition:</strong></p><ul><li>Each white tablet contains Ethinylestradiol USP 0.03 mg &amp; Levonorgestrel USP 0.15 mg.</li><li>Each brown tablet contains Ferrous Fumarate BP 75 mg.</li></ul><h3><strong>Dosage of Femipil 0.030+0.15mg</strong></h3><ul><li>Begin taking the pill from the first day of menstruation, or within the first 5 days of your period.</li><li>Take one white tablet daily for 21 days, preferably after dinner or before sleeping.</li><li>After completing the 21 white tablets, take one brown tablet daily for the next 7 days.</li><li>If your period starts while taking the brown tablets, do not stop the medication.</li><li>If pregnancy is confirmed, start the regimen from any day of menstruation, but use a condom for the next 7 days.</li><li>If you miss a dose, take the missed tablet as soon as you remember, and take the regular dose as scheduled.</li><li>If you miss two consecutive doses, the contraceptive effect may be reduced. To maintain your cycle, take two tablets at once.</li></ul><h3><strong>Drug Interactions:</strong></h3><ul><li>Medications or herbal products that induce certain enzymes (e.g., CYP3A4) may reduce the effectiveness of Femipil or cause breakthrough bleeding.</li><li>Avoid caffeine, dairy, and foods containing phytic acid while using the pill.</li></ul><h3><strong>Contraindications:</strong></h3><ul><li>Femipil should not be used if you are hypersensitive to any of its components.</li></ul><h3><strong>Side Effects:</strong></h3><ul><li><strong>Common</strong>: Headache, nausea, mood changes (including depression), vaginal infections, irregular vaginal bleeding, abdominal discomfort.</li><li><strong>Rare</strong>: Liver tumors, jaundice, high blood pressure, gallbladder problems.</li></ul><h3><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></h3><ul><li><strong>Thrombotic disorder and vascular issues</strong>: Discontinue if thrombotic disorders occur, and stop at least 4 weeks before major surgery.</li><li><strong>Liver disease</strong>: Discontinue if jaundice develops.</li><li><strong>High blood pressure</strong>: Monitor blood pressure in those with well-controlled hypertension.</li><li><strong>Metabolic effects</strong>: Women with prediabetes or uncontrolled lipid disorders should be monitored closely.</li><li><strong>Headache</strong>: Discontinue if significant changes in headache occur.</li><li><strong>Irregular bleeding</strong>: Monitor for any significant changes in bleeding patterns.</li></ul><h3><strong>Overdose Effects:</strong></h3><ul><li>There are no serious reported effects from overdose, though it may cause withdrawal bleeding or nausea.</li></ul><h3><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong></h3><ul><li>Store Femipil below 30°C, away from light and moisture.</li><li>Keep all medicines out of reach of children.</li></ul><h3><strong>Drug Class:</strong></h3><ul><li>Oral Contraceptive Preparations</li></ul><h3><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></h3><p>Femipil contains two active hormones, Levonorgestrel and Ethinylestradiol. This combination works by preventing ovulation, altering cervical mucus to block sperm entry, and modifying the uterine lining to prevent implantation. Each strip contains 28 tablets, with 21 hormone tablets and 7 iron tablets.</p><p><br></p><h3><strong>Pregnancy:</strong></h3><p>Femipil is contraindicated during pregnancy and should be discontinued if pregnancy occurs. Combined hormonal contraceptives (CHCs) and their metabolites are present in human milk, which can reduce milk production in breastfeeding women.</p><p><br></p><h3><strong>Pediatric Use:</strong></h3><p>The safety and efficacy of Femipil have been established for women of reproductive age. It is not intended for use before menarche, and its efficacy is expected to be the same in adolescents under 18 as in women over 18.</p>', 'active', '443_1733559351.webp', 12, 3, NULL, '2024-12-07 13:15:51', '2024-12-14 21:07:40'),
(33, 'Whisper Ultra Clean XL+ Plus', 'Sanitary Napkins', 185.00, 1, 'Box', '7 pads in box', 'Pad', '7 pads', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>How to Use a Sanitary Pad:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Choose the right pad:</strong></li><li>Select a sanitary pad that fits your flow (light, moderate, or heavy) and is the appropriate size for your body and activities. There are various options available, including day pads, overnight pads, and panty liners.</li><li><strong>Prepare the pad:</strong></li><li>Remove the sanitary pad from its packaging. If the pad is individually wrapped, unwrap it carefully.</li><li><strong>Placement:</strong></li><li>Stick the adhesive side of the pad to the inside of your underwear, ensuring it is placed securely in the center. Most pads have wings, which should be folded around the sides of your underwear for extra security.</li><li><strong>Wear the pad:</strong></li><li>Adjust the pad as needed to ensure it feels comfortable and stays in place. Make sure the pad covers the area that is most likely to absorb menstrual flow.</li><li><strong>Change regularly:</strong></li><li>Change your pad every 4-6 hours or more often if it becomes saturated to avoid discomfort or leaks. If you experience heavy flow, you may need to change it more frequently.</li><li><strong>Disposal:</strong></li><li>After use, roll up the pad securely with the adhesive strips and dispose of it in a sealed bag or waste bin. Avoid flushing sanitary pads down the toilet as they may clog plumbing.</li></ol><p><strong>Storage Tips for Sanitary Pads:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Keep them in a cool, dry place:</strong> Store pads in their original packaging or in a clean, dry space to avoid exposure to moisture, which could damage the pad.</li><li><strong>Avoid storing pads in a humid environment:</strong> Humidity can compromise the pad’s effectiveness.</li></ul><p><strong>Additional Tips:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Avoid wearing pads for extended periods:</strong> Try not to wear a pad for more than 8 hours at a time to reduce the risk of irritation and infection.</li><li><strong>Use appropriate pad types for your activity:</strong> If you\'re active, consider using pads designed for sports or those with additional features like extra absorbency and comfort.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '410_1733559897.webp', 16, 3, NULL, '2024-12-07 13:24:57', '2024-12-07 13:24:57');
