(47, 'Coral Mixed Fruit Flavors Condoms', 'Condom', 40.00, 1, 'Box', '3\'s pack in box', 'Condom', '3\'s pack', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Coral Mixed Fruit Flavors Condoms</strong> offer both protection and a fun, pleasurable experience with their fruity flavor. Here\'s a comprehensive guide on how to use, store, and handle them properly:</p><p><strong>Product Features:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Maximum Protection</strong>: Provides reliable protection against unwanted pregnancies and sexually transmitted diseases (STDs).</li><li><strong>Durable Latex</strong>: Made from high-grade, durable latex for strength and reliability.</li><li><strong>Fruity Flavor</strong>: The mixed fruit flavor adds an enjoyable twist, enhancing the experience for both partners.</li><li><strong>Natural Lubrication</strong>: Offers a comfortable, natural-feeling lubrication to ensure maximum comfort and pleasure.</li><li><strong>Safety Standards</strong>: Rigorously tested to meet international safety standards.</li></ul><p><strong>Usage Instructions:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Before Intercourse</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Always check the expiry date to ensure the condom is effective.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Place the condom on the erect genital just before sexual intercourse.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ensure that the roll of the condom is on the outside.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Applying the Condom</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Squeeze the tip of the condom to release any trapped air before putting it on.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">With one hand, hold the tip and place the condom on top of the genital. Use the other hand to roll it down.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>After Ejaculation</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">After ejaculation, while the genital is still erect, hold the base of the condom firmly.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Carefully remove the condom to avoid any spillage.</li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Expiry Date</strong>: Always check the expiry date before use for maximum effectiveness.</li><li><strong>Single Use</strong>: Designed for single use only—never reuse a condom.</li><li><strong>Opening the Packaging</strong>: Avoid using sharp objects to open the packaging to prevent damage to the condom.</li><li><strong>Disposal</strong>: Dispose of the used condom responsibly. Do not flush it down the toilet.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Open the package carefully, ensuring that no sharp objects are used that might damage the condom.</li><li>Always check the expiry date before use. Using expired condoms may reduce their effectiveness.</li><li>If you experience any discomfort, irritation, or allergic reactions, discontinue use and consult a healthcare provider.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong></p><ul><li>Store condoms in a <strong>cool</strong> (below 30°C), <strong>dry</strong> place, away from direct sunlight and heat sources.</li><li>Keep them in a safe place where they will not be exposed to extreme temperatures or humidity, which could compromise the latex.</li></ul><p><strong>Conclusion:</strong></p><p>By following these instructions, <strong>Coral Mixed Fruit Flavors Condoms</strong> will provide a safe, fun, and pleasurable experience. Ensure that you check the expiry date, store them properly, and dispose of used condoms responsibly for the best protection and enjoyment.</p>', 'active', '766_1733586679.webp', 22, 4, NULL, '2024-12-07 20:51:19', '2024-12-07 20:56:22'),
(48, 'Montair', 'Montelukast', 17.50, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Prophylaxis and chronic treatment of asthma</li><li>Prevention of Exercise-Induced Bronchoconstriction (EIB)</li><li>Relief of Seasonal &amp; Perennial Allergic Rhinitis</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p><strong> </strong>Leukotriene receptor antagonists</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li>Adults &amp; adolescents (15+ years): 10 mg once daily</li><li>Children:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">6–14 years: 5 mg once daily</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">2–5 years: 4 mg once daily (tablet or granules)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">6 months–2 years: 4 mg granules once daily</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Not for acute asthma attacks</li><li>Use with caution in aspirin-sensitive asthmatics</li><li>Gradual reduction of inhaled corticosteroids under supervision</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><p>Common: Headache, nausea, diarrhea, fever</p><p>Rare: Angioedema, hallucinations, liver issues</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><p>Category B. Use only if clearly needed; caution in breastfeeding.</p><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><p>Store below 30°C in a dry, cool place, away from light and children.</p><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><p>Selective leukotriene receptor antagonist (CysLT1), reducing airway inflammation and symptoms of asthma and rhinitis.</p>', 'active', '578_1733595162.png', 2, 1, NULL, '2024-12-07 23:12:42', '2024-12-07 23:18:54'),
(49, 'Finix', 'Rabeprazole Sodium', 7.00, 20, 'Tablet', '20 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '20 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Uses:</strong></p><ul><li>Duodenal and gastric ulcers</li><li>GERD (acute and maintenance)</li><li>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome</li><li>H. pylori eradication (with antibiotics)</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li>Ulcers: 20 mg daily for 4-6 weeks</li><li>GERD: 20 mg daily for 4-8 weeks; maintenance: 10-20 mg daily</li><li>H. pylori: 20 mg twice daily with antibiotics for 7 days</li><li>Zollinger-Ellison: Starting at 60 mg daily, adjustable</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><p>Headache, nausea, diarrhea, dizziness; rare: fractures, liver issues</p><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Rule out malignancy before use</li><li>Long-term use may increase fracture risk</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><p>Category C; avoid unless necessary.</p><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><p>Store below 30°C, away from moisture and children.</p>', 'active', '1151_1733595915.webp', 7, 1, NULL, '2024-12-07 23:25:15', '2024-12-07 23:25:15'),
(50, 'Provair', 'Montelukast', 17.50, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Asthma (prophylaxis and chronic treatment)</li><li>Exercise-Induced Bronchoconstriction (EIB) prevention</li><li>Seasonal &amp; perennial allergic rhinitis</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li>Adults (≥15 years): 10 mg once daily</li><li>Children (6-14 years): 5 mg once daily</li><li>Pediatric (6 months–5 years): 4 mg oral granules once daily</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><p>Common: Headache, nausea, fever, diarrhea</p><p>Rare: Liver issues, hallucinations, depression, tremors</p><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Not for acute asthma attacks</li><li>Avoid NSAIDs in aspirin-sensitive patients</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><p>Category B; use only if necessary.</p><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><p>Keep below 30°C, in a dry place, away from light and children.</p>', 'active', '308_1733596467.jpg', 8, 1, NULL, '2024-12-07 23:34:27', '2024-12-07 23:34:27');
