(51, 'Dicaltrol', 'Calcitriol', 12.00, 15, 'Capsule', '15', 'Capsule', '0.25 mcg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Post-menopausal osteoporosis</li><li>Renal osteodystrophy</li><li>Hypoparathyroidism (post-surgical, idiopathic, pseudo)</li><li>Secondary hyperparathyroidism (pre-dialysis)</li><li>Vitamin D-dependent rickets</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Post-menopausal osteoporosis:</strong> 0.25 mcg twice daily.</li><li><strong>Renal osteodystrophy:</strong> 0.25 mcg daily or every other day.</li><li><strong>Hypoparathyroidism/Rickets:</strong> Start with 0.25 mcg/day; adjust every 2-4 weeks.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypercalcemia or hypersensitivity to components.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Occasional: Headache, nausea, constipation.</li><li>Chronic: Dehydration, polyuria, apathy.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Monitor serum calcium levels. Reduce dose or stop if levels rise.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Safe if benefits outweigh risks. Monitor serum calcium in nursing mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place, away from light and heat. Keep out of children’s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Vitamin D preparations for bone formation.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Active metabolite of Vitamin D3 that promotes calcium absorption and regulates bone mineralization.</li></ul>', 'active', '243_1733596863.png', 9, 1, NULL, '2024-12-07 23:41:03', '2024-12-15 13:57:09'),
(52, 'Calbo-D', 'Calcium Carbonate [Elemental] + Vitamin D3', 8.00, 30, 'Tablet', '30 Tablet In Pack', 'Tablet', '500 mg+200 IU', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Treatment of osteoporosis, osteomalacia, rickets, tetany, and parathyroid disorders.</li><li>Calcium and Vitamin D3 supplementation in pregnancy, lactation, and chronic renal failure.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Calcium 500 mg + Vitamin D3 200 IU:</strong> 2 tablets daily or 1 tablet twice daily.</li><li><strong>Calcium 500 mg + Vitamin D3 400 IU:</strong> 1 tablet twice daily.</li><li>Best taken with or after meals.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Constipation, bloating, upset stomach.</li><li>Rare: Kidney stones, hypercalcemia.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypercalcemia, hyperthyroidism, renal stones, and Zollinger-Ellison syndrome.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Use with caution in heart or kidney disease.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry place, away from light and heat.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Specific mineral &amp; vitamin combined preparations.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1498_1733597188.webp', 4, 1, NULL, '2024-12-07 23:46:28', '2024-12-07 23:46:28'),
(53, 'Seclo', 'Capsule Omeprazole', 6.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '20 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Duodenal and gastric ulcers, including NSAID-induced.</li><li>Gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD), acid reflux, Zollinger-Ellison syndrome.</li><li>Peptic ulcer with <em>Helicobacter pylori</em> (as part of combination therapy).</li><li>Prevention of acid aspiration during anesthesia.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Ulcers &amp; GERD:</strong> 20 mg once daily for 4–8 weeks.</li><li><strong>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome:</strong> Initial 60 mg daily, adjust as needed.</li><li><strong>H. pylori eradication:</strong> 20 mg twice daily with antibiotics for 1 week.</li><li><strong>Pediatric GERD (≥10 kg):</strong> 10–40 mg once daily for 4–12 weeks.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Nausea, dizziness, headache, stomach cramps.</li><li>Rare: Allergic reactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Seclo 20 mg or its ingredients.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Category C: Use only if necessary; breastfeeding should be avoided.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Rule out gastric cancer before treatment.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry, cool place away from light.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Proton Pump Inhibitor (PPI).</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1204_1733597566.webp', 4, 1, NULL, '2024-12-07 23:52:46', '2024-12-07 23:52:46'),
(54, 'CoralCal-DX', 'Calcium Carbonate [Elemental] + Vitamin D3', 17.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '600 mg+400 IU', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Treatment of osteoporosis, osteomalacia, rickets, tetany, and parathyroid disease.</li><li>Calcium supplementation during pregnancy, lactation, bone/tooth formation, and chronic renal failure.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>500 mg Calcium + 200 IU Vitamin D3:</strong> 2 tablets daily or 1 tablet twice daily.</li><li><strong>500 mg Calcium + 400 IU Vitamin D3:</strong> 1 tablet twice daily.</li><li>Take with or after meals for better absorption.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Constipation, nausea, vomiting, stomach cramps, dry mouth.</li><li>Rare: Increased thirst/urination.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypercalcemia, hyperthyroidism, kidney stones, or Zollinger-Ellison syndrome.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Use with caution in heart or kidney disease.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place away from light and heat.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Specific mineral &amp; vitamin combined preparation.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1488_1733598153.webp', 10, 1, NULL, '2024-12-08 00:02:33', '2024-12-08 00:02:33'),
(55, 'CoralCal-D', 'Calcium Carbonate [Coral source] + Vitamin D3', 13.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '500 mg+200 IU', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Treatment and prevention of osteoporosis, osteomalacia, rickets, tetany, hypoparathyroidism, and disorders of osteogenesis.</li><li>Supplement for inadequate calcium intake in children, pregnancy, lactation, elderly, pancreatitis, and chronic renal failure.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li>1 tablet once or twice daily with water, preferably with food for better absorption.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Rare: Flatulence, diarrhea, constipation, GI discomfort.</li><li>Overuse may cause hypercalcemia symptoms like nausea, vomiting, headache, and constipation.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity, hypercalcemia, hyperparathyroidism, renal issues (stones, insufficiency), bone metastases.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Monitor calcium levels in renal impairment or long-term use. Caution in patients with renal stones or hypercalciuria.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, protect from light and moisture, out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Specific mineral &amp; vitamin combined preparation.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy:</strong></p><ul><li>Safe for pregnant and lactating women as per physician’s advice.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '673_1733598438.webp', 10, 1, NULL, '2024-12-08 00:07:18', '2024-12-08 00:07:18'),
(56, 'Doxiva', 'Doxophylline', 8.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '200 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Bronchial asthma</li><li>Bronchospasm</li><li>Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD)</li><li>Pulmonary disease with a spastic bronchial component</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults:</strong> 400 mg two or three times daily, or as prescribed</li><li><strong>Elderly:</strong> 200 mg two or three times daily</li><li><strong>Children &gt;12 years:</strong> 200 mg two or three times daily</li><li><strong>Children 6-12 years:</strong> 6-9 mg/kg body weight, twice daily</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Rare, but may include nausea, vomiting, headache, upset stomach, heartburn</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Acute myocardial infarction</li><li>Hypotension</li><li>Lactating women</li><li>Hypersensitivity to components</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Liver disease, heart failure, or use of certain drugs (e.g., erythromycin, propranolol) may require dose adjustments</li><li>Smoking and anticonvulsants may decrease the drug\'s half-life, requiring higher doses</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose:</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms may include severe arrhythmias and seizures. Symptomatic treatment is recommended, with possible dose reduction after symptoms subside.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Contraindicated in lactating women. Use in pregnancy only if clearly necessary.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry place, away from light and heat, out of the reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Doxiva 200 mg inhibits phosphodiesterase 4, relaxing bronchial smooth muscle. It also inhibits platelet-activating factor (PAF) and leukotriene production, offering a safer profile than Theophylline.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '904_1733598664.jpg', 11, 1, NULL, '2024-12-08 00:11:04', '2024-12-08 00:11:04'),
(57, 'Hemofix FZ', 'Ferrous Ascorbate + Folic Acid + Zinc Sulfate', 5.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '48 mg+0.5 mg+22.5 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Prophylaxis of iron deficiency, especially when diet is inadequate during pregnancy</li><li>Anemia</li><li>Zinc and iron supplementation</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults &amp; Elderly:</strong> 1 tablet daily, before or after a meal (food-independent absorption). For severe cases, 2 tablets may be required.</li><li><strong>Pediatric patients:</strong> Safety not established.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Mild and transient, including epigastric pain, nausea, constipation, vomiting, diarrhea, heartburn.</li><li>Allergic reactions to folic acid may occur.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hemolytic anemia</li><li>Hypersensitivity to components</li><li>Increased body iron content</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid in the first trimester unless iron deficiency is confirmed.</li><li>Safe in the remainder of pregnancy for iron and zinc supplementation. Consult a physician before use during pregnancy or breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Caution in patients with iron overload (e.g., hemochromatosis, hemolytic anemia).</li><li>Lack of response may indicate other causes of anemia.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose:</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms of acute iron overdose include abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, tarry stools, hypotension, shock, seizures, and coma.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Ferrous Ascorbate:</strong> Replenishes iron stores, correcting iron deficiency anemia.</li><li><strong>Vitamin C:</strong> Enhances iron absorption.</li><li><strong>Folic Acid:</strong> Essential for red blood cell production and fetal development during pregnancy.</li><li><strong>Zinc:</strong> Supports various physiological processes, including enzyme function.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '785_1733598874.png', 3, 1, NULL, '2024-12-08 00:14:34', '2024-12-08 00:14:34'),
(58, 'Moods Allnight Condoms', 'Condom', 60.00, 1, 'Box', '3\'s pack in box', 'Condom', '3\'s pack', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Moods Allnight Condoms</strong> are designed to provide both protection and comfort, enhancing your intimate experiences. Made from high-quality latex, these condoms offer reliable protection against unwanted pregnancies and sexually transmitted infections (STIs). The natural-feel lubrication ensures a pleasurable experience for both partners, while the condoms are rigorously tested to meet global safety standards.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Prepare</strong>: Before intercourse, carefully place the condom on an erect penis. Make sure the rolled edge is on the outside.</li><li><strong>Squeeze the Tip</strong>: Gently squeeze the tip of the condom to release any air trapped inside.</li><li><strong>Apply</strong>: While continuing to squeeze the tip, use one hand to place the condom at the top of the penis and roll it down with the other hand.</li><li><strong>After Use</strong>: Once intercourse is complete, while the penis is still erect, hold the base of the condom firmly and remove it carefully.</li></ol><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Expiry</strong>: Always check the expiry date before use to ensure maximum effectiveness.</li><li><strong>Single-Use</strong>: Moods Allnight Condoms are designed for one-time use only. Do not reuse them.</li><li><strong>Packaging</strong>: Open carefully, avoiding sharp objects that might damage the condom.</li><li><strong>Disposal</strong>: Dispose of the condom responsibly after use. Do not flush it down the toilet.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Expiry Date</strong>: Do not use if the condom is past its expiry date, as it may not provide adequate protection.</li><li><strong>Storage</strong>: Store the condoms in a cool, dry place, away from direct sunlight and at temperatures below 30°C to maintain their quality.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1957_1733638095.webp', 6, 4, NULL, '2024-12-08 11:08:15', '2024-12-08 11:08:15'),
(59, 'Coral Strawberry Flavors Condoms', 'Condom', 40.00, 1, 'Box', '3\'s pack in box', 'Condom', '3', 'no', 'yes', '<p>Coral Strawberry Flavors Condoms ensures your peace of mind and lets you enjoy intimate moments. This Coral Strawberry Flavors Condoms is designed to provide maximum protection while balancing safety and sensitivity. They are made with high-grade, durable latex to guarantee protection against unwanted pregnancies and sexually transmitted diseases. Both partners experience comfort and pleasure thanks to the natural-feeling lubrication. Rigorously tested to meet international safety standards.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions Of Coral Strawberry Flavors Condoms :</strong></p><ul><li>Place the Coral Strawberry Flavors Condoms on the erect genital just before sexual intercourse.</li><li>Ensure that the roll of the Coral Strawberry Flavors Condoms is on the outside.</li><li>Squeeze the end of the Coral Strawberry Flavors Condoms to release any trapped air before putting it on.</li><li>With one hand, put the Coral Strawberry Flavors Condoms on top of the genital while still squeezing the end, and roll it down with the other hand.</li><li>After ejaculation, while the genital is still erect, hold the Coral Strawberry Flavors Condoms firmly at the base and carefully remove it.</li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Ensure the Coral Strawberry Flavors Condoms is within its expiry date for optimal effectiveness.</li><li>The Coral Strawberry Flavors Condoms is designed for single use only. Never reuse a Coral Strawberry Flavors Condoms .</li><li>Avoid using sharp objects to open the packaging as it can damage the Coral Strawberry Flavors Condoms .</li><li>Dispose of used Coral Strawberry Flavors Condoms s responsibly. Do not flush them down the toilet.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Open the package carefully, avoiding the use of sharp objects that could potentially damage the Coral Strawberry Flavors Condoms .</li><li>Always check the expiry date before use. Expired Coral Strawberry Flavors Condoms s may not provide effective protection.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong></p><ul><li>Ensure Coral Strawberry Flavors Condoms s are stored in a cool (below 30°C), dry place, shielded from sunlight.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1658_1733638330.webp', 22, 4, NULL, '2024-12-08 11:12:10', '2024-12-08 11:12:10'),
(60, 'Durex Extra Time Love Sex Condoms', 'Condom', 250.00, 1, 'Box', '3\'s pack in a box', 'Condom', '3\'s pack', 'no', 'yes', '<p>Durex Extra Time Love Sex Condoms ensures your peace of mind and lets you enjoy intimate moments. This Durex Extra Time Love Sex Condoms is designed to provide maximum protection while balancing safety and sensitivity. They are made with high-grade, durable latex to guarantee protection against unwanted pregnancies and sexually transmitted diseases. Both partners experience comfort and pleasure thanks to the natural-feeling lubrication. Rigorously tested to meet international safety standards.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions Of Durex Extra Time Love Sex Condoms :</strong></p><ul><li>Place the Durex Extra Time Love Sex Condoms on the erect genital just before sexual intercourse.</li><li>Ensure that the roll of the Durex Extra Time Love Sex Condoms is on the outside.</li><li>Squeeze the end of the Durex Extra Time Love Sex Condoms to release any trapped air before putting it on.</li><li>With one hand, put the Durex Extra Time Love Sex Condoms on top of the genital while still squeezing the end, and roll it down with the other hand.</li><li>After ejaculation, while the genital is still erect, hold the Durex Extra Time Love Sex Condoms firmly at the base and carefully remove it.</li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Ensure the Durex Extra Time Love Sex Condoms is within its expiry date for optimal effectiveness.</li><li>The Durex Extra Time Love Sex Condoms is designed for single use only. Never reuse a Durex Extra Time Love Sex Condoms .</li><li>Avoid using sharp objects to open the packaging as it can damage the Durex Extra Time Love Sex Condoms .</li><li>Dispose of used Durex Extra Time Love Sex Condoms s responsibly. Do not flush them down the toilet.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Open the package carefully, avoiding the use of sharp objects that could potentially damage the Durex Extra Time Love Sex Condoms .</li><li>Always check the expiry date before use. Expired Durex Extra Time Love Sex Condoms s may not provide effective protection.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong></p><ul><li>Ensure Durex Extra Time Love Sex Condoms s are stored in a cool (below 30°C), dry place, shielded from sunlight.</li></ul>', 'active', '218_1733639250.jpg', 20, 4, NULL, '2024-12-08 11:27:30', '2024-12-08 17:53:12'),
(61, 'Coral Dotted Extra Time Lubricated Natural Latex Condoms', 'Condom', 65.00, 1, 'Box', '3\'s pack in box', 'Condom', '3\'s pack', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Coral Dotted Extra Time Lubricated Natural Latex Condoms</strong> are designed to provide reliable protection and enhance your intimate experiences. Crafted from premium latex, these condoms offer optimal protection against unwanted pregnancies and sexually transmitted infections (STIs). With a special dotted texture and extra lubrication, they help increase comfort and pleasure for both partners. Tested to meet international safety standards, they offer peace of mind while enjoying intimate moments.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Preparation</strong>: Before intercourse, carefully place the condom on an erect penis. Make sure the rolled edge is on the outside.</li><li><strong>Squeeze the Tip</strong>: Gently squeeze the tip of the condom to remove any trapped air.</li><li><strong>Apply</strong>: With one hand holding the tip, roll the condom down the penis with your other hand.</li><li><strong>After Use</strong>: After ejaculation, while the penis is still erect, hold the base of the condom firmly and remove it carefully.</li></ol><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Expiry Date</strong>: Always check the expiry date before use for maximum protection.</li><li><strong>Single-Use</strong>: These condoms are intended for one-time use only. Do not reuse.</li><li><strong>Opening</strong>: Open the package with care, avoiding sharp objects that could damage the condom.</li><li><strong>Disposal</strong>: Dispose of used condoms responsibly. Do not flush them down the toilet.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Expiry</strong>: Do not use expired condoms, as they may not provide effective protection.</li><li><strong>Storage</strong>: Store condoms in a cool, dry place away from direct sunlight, and ensure they are kept at temperatures below 30°C.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '736_1733639566.png', 22, 4, NULL, '2024-12-08 11:32:46', '2024-12-08 11:32:46'),
(62, 'Moods Dotted Condom', 'Condom', 65.00, 1, 'Box', '3\'s pack in box', 'Condom', '3\'s pack', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Moods Dotted Condom: Your Assurance of Safety and Pleasure</strong></p><p>The Moods Dotted Condom is designed to provide both safety and satisfaction. Made with premium latex, this condom ensures reliable protection against unwanted pregnancies and sexually transmitted diseases, all while maintaining sensitivity for both partners. The condom is pre-lubricated with a natural-feeling gel, enhancing comfort and pleasure. It undergoes strict quality control to meet global safety standards.</p><p><strong>How to Use Moods Dotted Condom:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Before intercourse</strong>, place the condom on the erect penis.</li><li><strong>Ensure proper placement</strong>: The roll of the condom should be on the outside.</li><li><strong>Squeeze the tip</strong> to eliminate any air trapped inside before putting it on.</li><li><strong>Roll it down</strong> carefully from the tip to the base of the penis.</li><li>After ejaculation, <strong>hold the base firmly</strong> while the penis is still erect and remove the condom carefully.</li></ol><p><strong>Important Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Always check the <strong>expiry date</strong> before use. Using expired condoms may compromise their effectiveness.</li><li>The Moods Dotted Condom is <strong>for single use only</strong>; do not reuse.</li><li>Avoid <strong>sharp objects</strong> when opening the packaging to prevent damaging the condom.</li><li><strong>Dispose of used condoms responsibly</strong>—do not flush them.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Instructions:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a <strong>cool, dry place</strong> below 30°C.</li><li>Keep away from <strong>direct sunlight</strong>.</li></ul><p>By following these guidelines, you can enjoy peace of mind during your intimate moments.</p>', 'active', '272_1733640525.webp', 6, 4, NULL, '2024-12-08 11:48:45', '2024-12-08 11:48:45'),
(63, 'Moods 1500 Dots Condoms', 'Condom', 100.00, 1, 'Box', '3\'s pack in box', 'Condom', '3\'s pack', 'no', 'no', '<p><strong>Moods 1500 Dots Condoms</strong></p><p>Moods 1500 Dots Condoms are designed to offer optimal protection while enhancing the pleasure and comfort of both partners. Made from high-quality latex, these condoms provide reliable protection against unwanted pregnancies and sexually transmitted infections (STIs). The unique dotted design adds to the sensation, making intimate moments more enjoyable. They are pre-lubricated for smoothness, ensuring a natural feel during use. These condoms undergo rigorous testing to meet international safety standards, giving you peace of mind.</p><p><strong>How to Use Moods 1500 Dots Condoms:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Preparation:</strong> Before engaging in sexual activity, ensure that the condom is placed on the erect genital.</li><li><strong>Positioning:</strong> Make sure the roll of the condom is on the outside.</li><li><strong>Air Removal:</strong> Squeeze the tip of the condom to eliminate any trapped air.</li><li><strong>Application:</strong> With one hand, position the condom at the tip of the genital, continuing to squeeze the tip. With the other hand, unroll it down the shaft of the penis.</li><li><strong>After Use:</strong> Once ejaculation occurs, while the genital is still erect, hold the base of the condom firmly and carefully remove it.</li></ol><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Always check the expiry date to ensure the condom\'s effectiveness.</li><li>This condom is for <strong>single use only</strong>. Do not reuse.</li><li>Be cautious when opening the packaging to avoid damaging the condom.</li><li>Dispose of used condoms responsibly; do not flush them down the toilet.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Storage:</strong> Store condoms in a cool, dry place (below 30°C) and away from direct sunlight.</li><li><strong>Packaging:</strong> Open the package carefully, avoiding sharp objects that could damage the condom.</li><li><strong>Expiry Date:</strong> Check the expiry date before use. Expired condoms may not provide adequate protection.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '194_1733660412.jpg', 6, 4, NULL, '2024-12-08 17:20:12', '2024-12-08 17:20:12'),
(64, 'Durex Air Ultra Thin Love Sex Condoms', 'Condom', 250.00, 1, 'Box', '3\'s pack in box', 'Condom', '3\'s pack', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Ultra Thin Condoms for Enhanced Sensitivity</strong></p><p>These ultra-thin condoms are designed to provide maximum protection while maintaining high sensitivity, ensuring a more natural and enjoyable experience for both partners. Made from premium, durable latex, they offer reliable protection against unwanted pregnancies and sexually transmitted infections (STIs). The natural-feel lubrication adds comfort, enhancing pleasure without compromising on safety. Rigorously tested to meet international safety standards, they offer peace of mind during intimate moments.</p><p><strong>How to Use Ultra Thin Condoms:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Preparation:</strong> Before engaging in sexual activity, place the condom on the erect genital.</li><li><strong>Positioning:</strong> Ensure the condom’s roll is on the outside.</li><li><strong>Air Removal:</strong> Squeeze the tip of the condom to release any trapped air.</li><li><strong>Application:</strong> With one hand, hold the condom at the tip of the genital, continuing to squeeze the tip. With the other hand, unroll the condom down the shaft of the penis.</li><li><strong>After Use:</strong> After ejaculation, while the genital is still erect, hold the base of the condom and carefully remove it.</li></ol><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Check the expiry date to ensure optimal effectiveness.</li><li>This condom is <strong>for single use only</strong>. Do not reuse.</li><li>Avoid using sharp objects to open the packaging as it may damage the condom.</li><li>Dispose of used condoms responsibly and do not flush them down the toilet.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Storage:</strong> Store condoms in a cool, dry place (below 30°C), away from direct sunlight.</li><li><strong>Packaging:</strong> Open the package carefully without sharp objects to prevent damage to the condom.</li><li><strong>Expiry Date:</strong> Ensure the condom is within its expiry date before use for effective protection.</li></ul>', 'active', '827_1733660706.webp', 20, 4, NULL, '2024-12-08 17:25:06', '2024-12-08 17:54:29'),
(65, 'Durex Extra Ribbed Love Sex Condoms', 'Condom', 250.00, 1, 'Box', '3\'s pack in box', 'Condom', '3\'s pack', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Extra Ribbed Condoms for Enhanced Sensation</strong></p><p>These extra ribbed condoms are designed to provide maximum protection and enhanced pleasure, featuring specially designed ribs that increase sensation for both partners. Made from high-quality latex, they ensure reliable protection against unwanted pregnancies and sexually transmitted infections (STIs). Pre-lubricated for comfort, these condoms offer a natural feel while maintaining safety. They are rigorously tested to meet international safety standards.</p><p><strong>How to Use Extra Ribbed Condoms:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Preparation:</strong> Before engaging in sexual activity, ensure the condom is placed on the erect genital.</li><li><strong>Positioning:</strong> Make sure the roll of the condom is on the outside.</li><li><strong>Air Removal:</strong> Squeeze the tip of the condom to release any trapped air.</li><li><strong>Application:</strong> With one hand, hold the condom at the tip of the genital while continuing to squeeze the tip. With the other hand, unroll it down the shaft of the penis.</li><li><strong>After Use:</strong> After ejaculation, while the genital is still erect, hold the base of the condom and carefully remove it.</li></ol><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Always check the expiry date to ensure the condom is still effective.</li><li>This condom is <strong>for single use only</strong>. Do not reuse.</li><li>Be cautious when opening the packaging to avoid damaging the condom.</li><li>Dispose of used condoms responsibly. Do not flush them down the toilet.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Storage:</strong> Store condoms in a cool, dry place (below 30°C), away from direct sunlight.</li><li><strong>Packaging:</strong> Open the package carefully to avoid sharp objects that may tear the condom.</li><li><strong>Expiry Date:</strong> Always check the expiry date before use. Expired condoms may not offer reliable protection.</li></ul>', 'active', '1239_1733661021.webp', 20, 4, NULL, '2024-12-08 17:30:21', '2024-12-08 17:54:13'),
(66, 'Durex Extra Thin Love Sex Condoms', 'Condom', 250.00, 1, 'Box', '3\'s pack in box', 'Condom', '3\'s pack', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Extra Thin Condoms (3-Pack)</strong></p><p>These ultra-thin condoms are designed for those who want heightened sensitivity and a more natural feel during intimate moments, all while providing the same level of reliable protection against pregnancy and sexually transmitted infections (STIs) as regular condoms.</p><p><strong>Key Features:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Flavored</strong>: Infused with delightful flavors to enhance the experience, particularly during oral sex.</li><li><strong>Extra Thin</strong>: These condoms are incredibly thin to maximize sensitivity, helping to create a more intimate connection, while still offering the same protection as standard condoms.</li><li><strong>Lubrication &amp; Design</strong>: Transparent and lubricated, these condoms feature a straight-walled design with a teat end for a better fit and smoother experience during sexual activity.</li><li><strong>Size</strong>: Each condom measures 180mm in length and 53mm in width, designed to fit most users comfortably.</li><li><strong>Discreet Packaging</strong>: The condoms come in discreet packaging, with no indication of the contents.</li><li><strong>Quality Assurance</strong>: Manufactured using high-quality materials and rigorously tested for safety and effectiveness, ensuring a reliable and secure experience.</li></ul><p><strong>Instructions for Use:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Preparation</strong>: Place the condom on the erect genital before engaging in sexual activity.</li><li><strong>Positioning</strong>: Ensure the unrolled portion is on the outside.</li><li><strong>Air Removal</strong>: Squeeze the tip of the condom to remove any trapped air before unrolling.</li><li><strong>Application</strong>: While continuing to squeeze the tip with one hand, unroll the condom down the shaft of the penis with the other hand.</li><li><strong>After Use</strong>: After ejaculation, while the genital remains erect, hold the base of the condom firmly and remove it carefully.</li></ol>', 'active', '1163_1733661780.png', 20, 4, NULL, '2024-12-08 17:43:00', '2024-12-08 17:53:56'),
(67, 'NovoFine 31G', 'Pen Needle', 12.50, 1, 'Pen Needle', '1\'s pin needle', 'Surgical', '6mm Pen Needle', 'no', 'yes', '<p><span style=\"color: rgb(63, 82, 100); background-color: rgb(245, 245, 245);\">Use the injection technique as recommended by physician and/or health care professional. Press the push-button in fully for injection. Hold the push-button pressed down during medication discharge. After the medication has been completely discharged, wait for 6 seconds and then pull out the pen needle slowly. You may either hold the push-button pressed or release it during the 6 seconds.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(57, 121, 80); background-color: rgb(245, 245, 245);\">Pen device</span><span style=\"color: rgb(63, 82, 100); background-color: rgb(245, 245, 245);\">: This is an insulin delivery device developed for diabetes patients to self-administer insulin in a convenient manner. It looks like a pen with a push, twist and lock cartridge holder that allows users to conveniently inject insulin, read and correct dosages easily and change cartridges in a fast and simple way. This allows the injection of from 1 to 60 units of insulin or any of 3 mL cartridge. If you set too many units, you can correct the dose without wasting any insulin.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(57, 121, 80); background-color: rgb(245, 245, 245);\">Pen needle</span><span style=\"color: rgb(63, 82, 100); background-color: rgb(245, 245, 245);\">:</span></p><ul><li>4 mm needles are associated with less risk of intramuscular injections compared to 6 mm needles.</li><li>Unique needle design to reduce the risk of bending or breaking.</li><li>4 mm length is suitable for subcutaneous delivery, regardless of BMI.</li><li>Compatible with most pen devices to simplify use.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><p>Pen Preparation or Changing Cartridge</p><ul><li>Remove the pen cap.</li><li>Remove the cartridge sleeve by turning it.</li><li>Remove the empty cartridge if necessary.</li><li>Insert the new cartridge into the cartridge sleeve.</li><li>Push the threaded rod back completely.</li><li>Attach the cartridge sleeve to the housing by turning it.</li></ul><p>Attach Pen Needle</p><ul><li>Pull off the peel foil.</li><li>Twist on the pen needle to the cartridge sleeve. Check that the pen needle is attached correctly.</li><li>Remove the outer needle protective cap. Keep the outer needle protective cap to safely remove and dispose of the pen needle after use.</li><li>Remove and dispose the inner needle protective cap.</li></ul><p>Priming / Function Check</p><ul><li>Dial the test dose by turning the dosage knob clockwise (not less than 2 units).</li><li>For the function check, hold the Pen pointing upwards and gently tap the cartridge sleeve, so that the air can rise to the top.</li><li>Press the push-button.</li><li>A few drops of insulin must emerge from the pen needle tip.</li></ul><p>Remove pen needle after each injection: Carefully attach the outer needle protective cap on the pen needle. Twist off the pen needle and dispose it correctly, according to the advice of your physician and/or health care professional.</p>', 'active', '293_1733675194.jpg', 24, 5, NULL, '2024-12-08 21:26:34', '2024-12-08 21:57:21'),
(68, 'DispoVan Syringe 100IU', 'Single Use Insulin Syringes', 10.00, 1, 'Syringe', '1\'s single use syringe', 'Surgical', 'U-100 1ml', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>100IU U-100 1ml Insulin Syringes (Single Use)</strong></p><p>These insulin syringes are designed for precise and sterile injection of insulin, ensuring accurate dosing for safe and effective management of diabetes. Each syringe is equipped with a pre-attached needle, which eliminates the need for cleaning or reuse, reducing the risk of contamination and infection.</p><p><strong>How to Use:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Remove Packaging</strong>: Take the syringe out of its protective packaging.</li><li><strong>Attach Needle</strong>: If necessary, attach the needle securely to the syringe.</li><li><strong>Draw Insulin</strong>: Pull the correct dose of insulin into the syringe as prescribed by your healthcare provider.</li><li><strong>Inject</strong>: Administer the insulin injection to the desired area.</li><li><strong>Dispose Properly</strong>: Safely dispose of the syringe and needle after use in a sharps container.</li><li><strong>Use a New Syringe</strong>: Always use a new, sterile syringe for each injection.</li><li><strong>Check Condition</strong>: Do not use the syringe if it is damaged or expired.</li></ol><p><strong>Storage Instructions:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Room Temperature</strong>: Store insulin syringes at room temperature (20–25°C or 68–77°F).</li><li><strong>Avoid Heat and Sunlight</strong>: Keep syringes away from direct sunlight and excessive heat, as this can affect insulin stability.</li></ul>', 'active', '1275_1733676413.jpg', 25, 5, NULL, '2024-12-08 21:46:53', '2024-12-08 21:48:03'),
(69, 'GlucoLeader Enhance Red Test Strip', 'Blood Glucose Strips', 462.00, 1, 'Box', '25\'s strip in a box', 'Surgical', '25\'s test strip', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Blood Glucose Test Strips (for use with compatible glucose meters)</strong></p><p>These test strips are designed for the accurate and reliable measurement of blood glucose levels from fresh capillary whole blood samples. They are specifically used with compatible blood glucose meters and play a vital role in managing diabetes effectively.</p><p><strong>Key Benefits:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Accurate Results</strong>: Provides precise and consistent blood glucose readings to help manage diabetes.</li><li><strong>Ease of Use</strong>: Simple to handle and easy to use for at-home blood sugar monitoring.</li><li><strong>Wide Usage</strong>: Trusted and used by many individuals and healthcare providers for diabetes management.</li><li><strong>Patented Technology</strong>: Utilizes advanced viscosity calibration technology for accurate readings.</li><li><strong>Small Sample Size</strong>: Requires only a small amount of blood for testing, making the process more comfortable.</li><li><strong>Flexible Application</strong>: Blood samples can be applied to either side of the test strip for added convenience.</li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Label Review</strong>: Always read the instructions on the label before use.</li><li><strong>Keep Out of Reach of Children</strong>: Store in a safe location, away from children.</li><li><strong>Storage</strong>: Store in a cool, dry place to ensure product reliability.</li></ul>', 'active', '1202_1733676908.webp', 25, 5, NULL, '2024-12-08 21:55:08', '2024-12-11 11:25:13'),
(70, 'Accu-Chek Active Strip', 'Blood glucose monitoring device', 1378.00, 1, 'Packet', '50\'s test strip box', 'Surgical', '50\'s strip', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Blood Glucose Meter with 50 Test Strips</strong></p><p>This compact blood glucose meter is designed to deliver accurate readings with added convenience and user-friendly features. It eliminates the need for coding, reducing handling steps, and allows for the display of test result averages over the past 90 days. With additional features like alerts for expired strips or incorrect dosages, a 10-second re-dose window, and meal reminders, it supports effective diabetes management.</p><p><strong>Key Benefits:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Accurate Measurement</strong>: Provides precise blood glucose readings for reliable diabetes monitoring.</li><li><strong>Historical Data</strong>: Displays test results for up to 90 days, allowing for easy tracking of blood sugar trends.</li><li><strong>Convenience</strong>: Easy-to-use and intuitive with just two buttons for simple navigation.</li><li><strong>Safety Alerts</strong>: Notifies users if test strips are expired or if there’s an underdosing, ensuring accurate results.</li><li><strong>Quick Re-dose</strong>: Re-dose within 10 seconds for more efficient testing.</li><li><strong>Meal Reminders</strong>: Set pre- and post-meal reminders to help track blood glucose at critical times.</li><li><strong>USB Interface</strong>: Easily transfer data to a computer or device for further analysis.</li></ul><p><strong>Directions for Use:</strong></p><ol><li>Insert a test strip into the meter.</li><li>Use a lancet to prick your finger and draw a small drop of blood.</li><li>Touch the blood drop to the designated area of the test strip.</li><li>Wait for the reading to display on the screen.</li></ol><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Read the Manual</strong>: Carefully review the user manual before using the meter.</li><li><strong>Child Safety</strong>: Keep the meter and test strips out of the reach of children to prevent accidental misuse.</li></ul>', 'active', '1066_1733679200.jpg', 10, 5, NULL, '2024-12-08 22:33:20', '2024-12-11 11:30:18'),
(71, 'Napa Extra', 'Paracetamol + Caffeine', 2.50, 12, 'Tablet', '12 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '500 mg+65 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Headache, migraine, toothache</li><li>Neuralgia, sore throat, backache</li><li>Period pain, feverishness</li><li>Aches and pains associated with colds and flu</li><li>Helps reduce temperature</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults:</strong> 1-2 tablets every 4-6 hours. Maximum: 8 tablets/day.</li><li><strong>Children:</strong> Not recommended for those under 12 years.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Mild: Skin rashes, nausea, vomiting</li><li>Rare: Pancreatitis, blood disorders (e.g., thrombocytopenia, neutropenia)</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Severe renal or hepatic impairment</li><li>Known sensitivity to caffeine or paracetamol</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Consult a doctor before use during pregnancy.</li><li>Safe during breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid prolonged use without medical advice.</li><li>Use with caution in hepatic or renal impairment and when taking hepatotoxic medications.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: Pallor, nausea, vomiting, anorexia, stomach pain within 24 hours.</li><li>Severe cases: Liver damage, metabolic acidosis, glucose metabolism issues.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place, protected from light and moisture.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Paracetamol:</strong> Provides analgesic and antipyretic effects by lowering pain threshold and acting on the hypothalamus.</li><li><strong>Caffeine:</strong> Enhances paracetamol absorption, increases pain threshold, and improves cerebral blood vessel tone, aiding in headache and migraine relief.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '340_1733688527.webp', 3, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 01:08:47', '2024-12-09 01:08:47'),
(72, 'E-Cap', 'Vitamin E [Alpha Tocopherol Acetate]', 7.00, 15, 'Capsule', '15 Capsul In Strip', 'Capsule', '400 IU', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Dietary Supplement:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Vitamin E deficiency due to impaired absorption.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Increased requirements from diets high in polyunsaturated fats.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Promotes healthy hair and skin.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Acts as an antioxidant.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Treats hemolytic anemia caused by Vitamin E deficiency.</li><li><strong>Therapeutic Use:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cardiovascular disease.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Heavy metal poisoning.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Hepatotoxin poisoning.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Hemolytic anemia.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Oxygen therapy-related oxidative stress.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Nutritional deficiency states.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Vitamin-E Preparations</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li>Vitamin E is a potent antioxidant that protects polyunsaturated fatty acids and oxygen-sensitive substances (e.g., vitamins A and C) from oxidation.</li><li>Deficiency can cause irritability, edema, thrombosis, hemolytic anemia, and other conditions.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Cardiovascular health:</strong> 400–800 IU/day.</li><li><strong>Adults (deficiency syndromes):</strong> 200–400 IU/day.</li><li><strong>Children (deficiency syndromes):</strong> 200 IU/day.</li><li><strong>Thalassemia:</strong> 800 IU/day.</li><li><strong>Sickle-cell anemia:</strong> 400 IU/day.</li><li><strong>Hair and skin health:</strong> 200–400 IU/day (topical use also established for beautification).</li><li><strong>Chronic cold (adults):</strong> 200 IU/day.</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction:</strong></p><ul><li>May impair the absorption of Vitamin A and the function of Vitamin K.</li><li>Potentiates the effect of Warfarin, increasing the risk of bleeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>No known contraindications.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Overdosage (&gt;1 g) may cause minor side effects, including hypertension, fatigue, diarrhea, and myopathy.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Safe in pregnancy and lactation when used at recommended doses. Higher doses are not established.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>May increase the risk of thrombosis in patients taking estrogens.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry place, protected from light and heat. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations:</strong></p><ul><li>Safe for children at recommended doses.</li></ul>', 'active', '1952_1733688836.webp', 9, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 01:13:56', '2024-12-15 13:56:41');
INSERT INTO `products` (`id`, `productName`, `genericName`, `retail_max_price`, `cart_qty_inc`, `cart_text`, `unit_in_pack`, `type`, `quantity`, `prescription`, `feature`, `description`, `status`, `coverImage`, `company_id`, `category_id`, `add_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(73, 'Maxpro', 'Esomeprazole Magnesium Trihydrate', 7.00, 14, 'Capsule', '14 Capsul In Strip', 'Capsule', '20 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ol><li>Relief of <strong>GERD</strong> symptoms (e.g., persistent heartburn).</li><li>Treatment and maintenance of <strong>erosive esophagitis</strong>.</li><li><strong>Helicobacter pylori eradication</strong> (with amoxicillin and clarithromycin) in duodenal ulcer patients.</li><li>Treatment of <strong>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome</strong>.</li><li>Management of <strong>acid-related dyspepsia</strong>.</li><li>Healing of <strong>duodenal and gastric ulcers</strong>.</li></ol><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><p><strong>Adults:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Erosive Esophagitis (Healing):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">20–40 mg once daily for 4–8 weeks. Additional 4–8 weeks if unhealed.</li><li><strong>Erosive Esophagitis (Maintenance):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">20 mg once daily (up to 6 months).</li><li><strong>GERD:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">20 mg once daily for 4 weeks; extend another 4 weeks if symptoms persist.</li><li><strong>Helicobacter Pylori Eradication (Triple Therapy):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Esomeprazole 40 mg once daily, Amoxicillin 1000 mg twice daily, Clarithromycin 500 mg twice daily for 10 days.</li><li><strong>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">20–80 mg once daily, adjusted as needed.</li><li><strong>Acid Dyspepsia:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">20–40 mg once daily for 2–4 weeks.</li><li><strong>Duodenal Ulcers:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">20 mg once daily for 2–4 weeks.</li><li><strong>Gastric Ulcers:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">20–40 mg once daily for 4–8 weeks.</li><li><strong>Injection (IV):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">40 mg once daily via intravenous injection (3 minutes minimum) or infusion (10–30 minutes).</li></ul><p><strong>Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Oral Tablets:</strong> Take whole with water, 1 hour before meals.</li><li><strong>Delayed-Release Suspension:</strong> Dissolve in water, wait 2–3 minutes to thicken, stir, and consume within 30 minutes. For nasogastric/gastric tubes, administer using an appropriate syringe.</li><li><strong>IV Administration:</strong> Reconstitute with 5 mL water for injection (WFI) and inject over 3 minutes. Use within 12 hours of reconstitution at room temperature.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>CYP Enzymes:</strong> Metabolized mainly by CYP2C19 and CYP3A4. Esomeprazole may affect medications metabolized by CYP2C19 (e.g., diazepam).</li><li><strong>Reduced Acid Absorption:</strong> May interfere with medications requiring acidic pH for absorption (e.g., ketoconazole, digoxin, iron salts).</li><li>No clinically significant interactions with warfarin, phenytoin, clarithromycin, or amoxicillin.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to esomeprazole or its components.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Headache, diarrhea, nausea, flatulence, abdominal pain, constipation, dry mouth.</li><li>Rare: Severe allergic reactions, Stevens-Johnson syndrome.</li></ul><p><strong>Warnings &amp; Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Symptom relief does not rule out <strong>stomach cancer</strong>.</li><li>Do not crush or chew capsules/pellets.</li><li>Antacids may be used concurrently.</li><li>For patients with <strong>severe liver impairment</strong>, do not exceed 20 mg daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: Tremors, ataxia, motor impairment, clonic convulsions.</li><li>Treatment: Supportive and symptomatic care. Esomeprazole is not effectively removed by dialysis.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> Insufficient human data; animal studies show no teratogenic effects. Use only if necessary.</li><li><strong>Lactation:</strong> Unknown if excreted in breast milk. Consider discontinuing breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Populations:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pediatrics:</strong> Safety and efficacy not established.</li><li><strong>Geriatrics:</strong> Generally well-tolerated; no significant differences from younger adults.</li><li><strong>Renal Impairment:</strong> No dosage adjustments required.</li></ul>', 'active', '26_1733689106.jpg', 6, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 01:18:26', '2024-12-15 13:56:27'),
(74, 'Feglo-FZ', 'Ferrous Ascorbate + Folic Acid + Zinc Sulfate', 7.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '48 mg+0.5 mg+22.5 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<h4><strong>Indications:</strong></h4><ul><li>Relief of GERD symptoms (e.g., heartburn).</li><li>Treatment and maintenance of erosive esophagitis healing.</li><li>Eradication of <em>Helicobacter pylori</em> in duodenal ulcer disease (with amoxicillin and clarithromycin).</li><li>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome.</li><li>Treatment of duodenal and gastric ulcers caused by acid dyspepsia.</li></ul><h4><strong>Dosage:</strong></h4><ul><li><strong>GERD/Erosive Esophagitis:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Healing: 20-40 mg once daily for 4-8 weeks.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Maintenance: 20 mg once daily for up to 6 months.</li><li><strong>H. pylori Eradication:</strong> Esomeprazole 40 mg daily + Amoxicillin 1000 mg BID + Clarithromycin 500 mg BID for 10 days.</li><li><strong>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome:</strong> 20-80 mg daily, individualized.</li><li><strong>Acid Dyspepsia/Duodenal Ulcers:</strong> 20-40 mg daily for 2-4 weeks.</li><li><strong>Gastric Ulcers:</strong> 20-40 mg daily for 4-8 weeks.</li><li><strong>IV Administration:</strong> 40 mg once daily, given over 10-30 minutes. Shift to oral as soon as possible.</li></ul><h4><strong>Administration:</strong></h4><ul><li>Take 1 hour before meals; swallow capsules whole or mix with applesauce.</li><li>Delayed-release suspension: Mix with water, let thicken, and consume immediately.</li></ul><h4><strong>Interactions:</strong></h4><ul><li>May reduce the absorption of drugs like ketoconazole and iron salts.</li><li>Increases plasma levels of diazepam and <em>CYP2C19</em> substrates.</li><li>No significant interactions with warfarin, phenytoin, or oral contraceptives.</li></ul><h4><strong>Contraindications:</strong></h4><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to esomeprazole or its components.</li></ul><h4><strong>Side Effects:</strong></h4><ul><li>Common: Headache, diarrhea, nausea, flatulence, abdominal pain, constipation, dry mouth.</li><li>Long-term therapy does not show additional adverse effects.</li></ul><h4><strong>Warnings:</strong></h4><ul><li>Rule out stomach cancer before use.</li><li>Do not crush or chew the medication.</li><li>Safe antacid use alongside esomeprazole.</li></ul><h4><strong>Special Considerations:</strong></h4><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> Use only if necessary; discontinue breastfeeding if used.</li><li><strong>Pediatric Use:</strong> Safety not established.</li><li><strong>Hepatic Insufficiency:</strong> Limit to 20 mg daily in severe cases.</li><li><strong>Renal Impairment:</strong> No dose adjustment needed.</li></ul><h4><strong>Storage:</strong></h4><ul><li>Store in a dry place below 30°C, protected from moisture and light. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul>', 'active', '1339_1733900668.webp', 14, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 01:23:55', '2024-12-11 12:04:28'),
(75, 'Losectil', 'Omeprazole', 5.00, 10, 'Capsule', '10 Capsul In Strip', 'Capsule', '20 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Treats duodenal/gastric ulcers (including NSAID-induced).</li><li>GERD, acid reflux, and Zollinger-Ellison syndrome.</li><li>Helicobacter pylori-related ulcers (with antibiotics).</li><li>Acid-related dyspepsia and prevention of acid aspiration during surgery.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Oral:</strong> 20 mg daily (adjust for condition, duration varies).</li><li><strong>IV:</strong> 40 mg slow injection or infusion for severe cases or surgery prophylaxis.</li><li><strong>Pediatric:</strong> Dose based on body weight (10-40 mg daily).</li></ul><p><strong>Administration:</strong></p><ul><li>Oral or IV (reconstituted and used within recommended time).</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Mild: Nausea, headache, dizziness, abdominal discomfort.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Rule out gastric cancer before use.</li><li>Adjust dose with warfarin or phenytoin.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>FDA Category C; avoid breastfeeding during treatment.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Keep in a cool, dry place, away from children.</li></ul><p><strong>Class:</strong> Proton Pump Inhibitor (PPI).</p><p><br></p><p>4o</p>', 'active', '1788_1733689721.webp', 26, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 01:28:41', '2024-12-15 13:56:16'),
(76, 'Lumona', 'Montelukast', 12.00, 14, 'Tablet', '14 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Chronic asthma treatment and prophylaxis.</li><li>Prevention of Exercise-Induced Bronchoconstriction (EIB).</li><li>Relief from Seasonal and Perennial Allergic Rhinitis.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Leukotriene receptor antagonist.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><p>Blocks cysteinyl leukotrienes (LTC4, LTD4, LTE4) that contribute to airway inflammation, edema, and bronchoconstriction.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults/Adolescents (≥15 years):</strong> 10 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Pediatrics:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">6–14 years: 5 mg daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">2–5 years: 4 mg daily (tablet or granules).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">6 months–2 years: 4 mg oral granules daily.</li><li>No dose adjustments needed for renal or mild-to-moderate hepatic insufficiency or elderly patients.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Headache, nausea, vomiting, fever, and GI discomfort.</li><li>Rare: Behavioral changes, angioedema, hepatic issues, or eosinophilia.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Not for acute asthma attacks; ensure availability of rescue medication.</li><li>Gradual reduction of corticosteroid dosage under medical supervision.</li><li>Patients with aspirin sensitivity should avoid NSAIDs.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Category B: Use with caution. Passes the placenta in animal studies; secreted in breast milk.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C in a cool, dry place away from light and moisture. Keep out of children’s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Selective leukotriene receptor antagonist inhibits CysLT1, reducing inflammation and bronchoconstriction associated with asthma and allergic rhinitis.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '196_1733689956.png', 26, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 01:32:36', '2024-12-09 01:32:36'),
(77, 'Alatrol', 'Cetirizine Hydrochloride [Oral]', 3.01, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Relief of symptoms from seasonal and perennial allergic rhinitis.</li><li>Treatment of chronic idiopathic urticaria and allergen-induced asthma.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Sedating antihistamine.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><p>H1 receptor antagonist with minimal sedative effects. Reduces both early- and late-phase allergic reactions.</p><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults &amp; Children (≥6 years):</strong> 1 tablet or 2 tsp daily (or 1 tsp twice daily).</li><li><strong>Children (2–6 years):</strong> 1 tsp once daily or ½ tsp twice daily.</li><li><strong>Children (6 months–2 years):</strong> ½ tsp once daily; max: ½ tsp every 12 hours.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Somnolence (drowsiness).</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Cetirizine or hydroxyzine.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Category B: Use only if clearly needed. Excreted in breast milk; use with caution in nursing mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Exercise caution while driving or operating machinery.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry, cool place away from light and heat. Keep out of children\'s reach.</li></ul>', 'active', '598_1733690213.jpg', 4, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 01:36:53', '2024-12-09 01:36:53'),
(78, 'Pantonix', 'Pantoprazole', 10.00, 14, 'Tablet', '14 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '40 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Stomach ulcer disorders.</li><li>Gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD).</li><li>NSAID-induced ulcers.</li><li>Helicobacter pylori eradication (with antibiotics).</li><li>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Proton pump inhibitor (PPI).</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><p>Inhibits gastric acid secretion by binding to the H+/K+ ATPase enzyme in gastric parietal cells, reducing basal and stimulated acid production for over 24 hours.</p><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Benign gastric ulcer:</strong> 40 mg once daily for 4–8 weeks.</li><li><strong>GERD:</strong> 20–40 mg daily for 4–8 weeks; maintenance: 20–40 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Duodenal ulcer:</strong> 40 mg daily for 2–4 weeks.</li><li><strong>H. pylori eradication:</strong> 40 mg twice daily + antibiotics (e.g., amoxicillin &amp; clarithromycin or metronidazole).</li><li><strong>NSAID ulcer prophylaxis:</strong> 20 mg daily for long-term NSAID use.</li><li><strong>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome:</strong> 80 mg daily, adjusted as needed.</li></ul><p><strong>IV Administration:</strong></p><ul><li>Reconstitute with 10 ml of 0.9% sodium chloride.</li><li>Administer over 2–5 minutes or as an infusion diluted to 100 ml over 15 minutes.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><p>Common: Headache, diarrhea.</p><p>Rare: Abdominal pain, flatulence, rash, insomnia, hyperglycemia.</p><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><p>Hypersensitivity to the drug\'s ingredients.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Category B: Use only if necessary.</li><li>Excreted in breast milk; weigh risks vs. benefits for nursing mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Do not split, crush, or chew the tablets.</li><li>Long-term use may cause Vitamin B12 deficiency or osteoporosis-related complications.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><p>Store in a dry, cool place away from light and heat. Keep out of children\'s reach.</p><p><strong>Warnings:</strong></p><p>For IV use, prepare and administer as directed. Use reconstituted solutions within specified time frames.</p>', 'in-active', '1255_1733690345.webp', 2, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 01:39:05', '2025-05-12 17:51:11'),
(79, 'Dexilend', 'Dexlansoprazole', 10.00, 10, 'Capsule', '10 Capsul In Strip', 'Capsule', '30 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Healing of erosive esophagitis (EE): Up to 8 weeks.</li><li>Maintenance of healed EE and heartburn relief: Up to 6 months.</li><li>Treatment of non-erosive GERD: 4 weeks.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Proton Pump Inhibitor (PPI).</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><p>Dexilend 30 mg inhibits gastric acid secretion by specifically targeting the (H+/K+)-ATPase enzyme in gastric parietal cells. It features a dual delayed-release formulation with two types of enteric-coated granules, releasing at different pH levels for extended efficacy.</p><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li>Maintenance of healed EE: 30 mg once daily.</li><li>Non-erosive GERD: 30 mg once daily for 4 weeks.</li><li>Healing of EE: 60 mg once daily for up to 8 weeks.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration:</strong></p><ul><li>Can be taken without regard to food.</li><li>Capsules should be swallowed whole. Granules may be sprinkled on food but should not be chewed.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><p>Common: Diarrhea, abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, flatulence.</p><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><p>Hypersensitivity to any component of the formulation.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Category B: Use only if benefits outweigh risks.</li><li>Excretion in human milk is unknown; not recommended for nursing mothers unless necessary.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Risk of gastric malignancy, Clostridium difficile infection, bone fractures, hypomagnesemia, and interaction with methotrexate.</li><li>No dosage adjustment needed for renal impairment or elderly patients.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><p>Store below 30°C, in a dry place away from light. Keep out of children\'s reach.</p>', 'active', '533_1733690585.jpg', 27, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 01:43:05', '2024-12-15 13:55:42'),
(80, 'D-Rise', 'Colecalciferol [Vitamin D3]', 35.00, 10, 'Capsule', '10 Capsul In Strip', 'Capsule', '40000 IU', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Treatment and prevention of Vitamin D3 deficiency.</li><li>Adjunct therapy for osteoporosis, osteomalacia, hypocalcaemia, tetany, and rickets in patients with Vitamin D3 deficiency.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Vitamin in bone formation, Vitamin D preparations.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><p>Colecalciferol (Vitamin D3) promotes the absorption and reabsorption of calcium and phosphorus, essential for bone growth, density, and overall health. It also helps reduce bacterial infection severity, improves lung function, prevents certain cancers (breast, colorectal), and supports insulin regulation in type 2 diabetes.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Treatment: 40,000 IU weekly for 7 weeks.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Maintenance: 1,400–2,000 IU/day.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Prevention: 20,000 IU every 4 weeks.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For osteoporosis: 20,000 IU once a month.</li><li><strong>Children (12-18 years):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Treatment: 20,000 IU bi-weekly for 6 weeks.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Prevention: 20,000 IU every 6 weeks.</li><li><strong>Other Forms:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tablets, syrup, and injections are also available with varying dosages for specific age groups.</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction:</strong></p><p>May interfere with phenytoin, barbiturates, glucocorticoids, certain laxatives, actinomycin, and imidazole antifungal agents.</p><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><p>Hypersensitivity to Vitamin D3.</p><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Hypercalcaemia, hypercalciuria, skin rash, pruritus, urticaria, nausea, abdominal pain.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Safe use shown up to 4,000 IU during pregnancy.</li><li>Vitamin D3 and its metabolites are excreted in breast milk; use with caution in nursing mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Caution in patients with renal impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects:</strong></p><p>Can lead to hypervitaminosis D.</p><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><p>Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture. Keep out of children\'s reach.</p><p><strong>Use in Special Populations:</strong></p><ul><li>Safety in children under 12 years not established.</li><li>Pregnant and breastfeeding women should consult a doctor regarding appropriate doses.</li></ul>', 'active', '144_1733690848.jpg', 3, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 01:47:28', '2024-12-15 13:55:06'),
(81, 'Entacyd Plus', 'Aluminium Hydroxide + Magnesium Hydroxide + Simethicone', 2.50, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Chewable Tablet', '400 mg+400 mg+30 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Symptomatic relief of hyperacidity (peptic ulcers, gastritis, heartburn, sour stomach, hiatus hernia).</li><li>Prevention of stress ulceration and GI bleeding.</li><li>Acts as an antiflatulent to relieve gas pain and bloating.</li></ul><p><strong>Composition:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tablet:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Aluminium Hydroxide Gel: 425.53 mg</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Magnesium Hydroxide: 400 mg</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Simethicone: 30 mg</li><li><strong>Suspension (per 5 ml):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Aluminium Hydroxide: 200 mg</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Magnesium Hydroxide: 400 mg</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Simethicone: 30 mg</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Antacids</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li>Aluminium Hydroxide and Magnesium Hydroxide neutralize gastric acid, aiding in ulcer relief.</li><li>Simethicone relieves gas and bloating by collapsing foam bubbles in the GI tract, helping expel trapped gas.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tablet:</strong> 1-2 tablets 1-3 hours after meals and at bedtime.</li><li><strong>Suspension:</strong> 1-2 teaspoonfuls 1-3 hours after meals and at bedtime.</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction:</strong></p><ul><li>May alter the absorption of several oral drugs (e.g., theophylline, tetracycline, antibiotics).</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Not for use in patients with renal failure, hypophosphatemia, or severe debilitation.</li><li>Contraindicated in alkalosis and hypermagnesemia.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Rare gastrointestinal issues (diarrhea, constipation, or regurgitation with excess use).</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid during the first trimester of pregnancy.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Use with caution in patients with kidney disease.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Neutralizes stomach acid and relieves gas buildup, aiding in digestion and comfort.</li></ul>', 'active', '897_1733691303.webp', 4, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 01:55:03', '2025-05-02 09:50:44'),
(82, 'Rabe', 'Rabeprazole Sodium', 7.00, 20, 'Tablet', '20 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '20 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Active duodenal and benign gastric ulcers.</li><li>Symptomatic GERD (gastroesophageal reflux disease), erosive or ulcerative GERD.</li><li>Long-term GERD maintenance.</li><li>Zollinger-Ellison syndrome.</li><li>Helicobacter pylori eradication (in combination with antibiotics for peptic ulcer disease).</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Proton Pump Inhibitor (PPI)</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><p>Rabeprazole inhibits the gastric H+/K+-ATPase enzyme in the stomach parietal cells, reducing gastric acid secretion.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Duodenal Ulcer &amp; Gastric Ulcer:</strong> 20 mg daily for 4-6 weeks.</li><li><strong>Erosive GERD:</strong> 20 mg daily for 4-8 weeks.</li><li><strong>Symptomatic GERD:</strong> 20 mg daily for 4 weeks.</li><li><strong>GERD Maintenance:</strong> 20 mg or 10 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome:</strong> 60 mg daily, titrated as needed.</li><li><strong>H. pylori Eradication:</strong> 20 mg twice daily with amoxicillin and clarithromycin for 7 days.</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction:</strong></p><ul><li>May decrease the absorption of pH-dependent drugs (e.g., ketoconazole).</li><li>Avoid with atazanavir due to reduced absorption.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any component.</li><li>Not recommended during pregnancy or breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: headache, nausea, vomiting, constipation, dry mouth, dizziness, muscle pain, sleepiness.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>FDA Pregnancy Category C.</strong></li><li>Consider risks and benefits before using during pregnancy or breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Exclude malignancy before treatment.</li><li>Long-term use (&gt;1 year) may increase fracture risk, particularly in the elderly.</li><li>Monitor patients at risk for osteoporosis.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>No specific antidote. Symptoms typically mild and reversible.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture. Keep out of children\'s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations:</strong></p><ul><li>Not recommended for use in children due to lack of safety and efficacy data.</li><li>No dosage adjustment for hepatic or renal impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Inhibits gastric proton pump, reducing gastric acid secretion.</li></ul>', 'active', '1449_1733691434.webp', 29, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 01:57:14', '2024-12-09 22:24:53'),
(83, 'Folison', 'Folic acid', 0.35, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '5 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications of Folison 5 mg:</strong></p><ul><li>Folic acid deficiency</li><li>Megaloblastic anemia</li><li>Nutritional anemias (pregnancy, infancy, childhood)</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Drugs for Megaloblastic Anemia</li><li>Vitamin B preparations</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults:</strong> 5 mg daily for 4 months, then 5 mg every 1-7 days for maintenance.</li><li><strong>Children:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Up to 1 year: 500 mcg/kg daily</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Over 1 year: Same as adult dose</li></ul><p><strong>Administration:</strong></p><ul><li>Take with or without food.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Generally well-tolerated, but may cause gastrointestinal disturbances or rare hypersensitivity reactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy Category A:</strong> Safe during pregnancy.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Caution in folate-dependent tumors.</li><li>Avoid alone in vitamin B12 deficiency, as it can worsen related conditions.</li><li>Elderly patients should have a cobalamin absorption test before long-term use.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Converts to active forms (tetrahydrofolic acid, methyltetrahydrofolate) that support erythropoiesis, nucleic acid synthesis, and amino acid metabolism.</li><li>Reduces homocysteine to methionine with vitamin B12 as a cofactor.</li></ul>', 'active', '874_1733691601.webp', 28, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 02:00:01', '2024-12-09 22:24:35'),
(84, 'Exium', 'Esomeprazole Magnesium Trihydrate', 9.00, 10, 'Capsule', '10 Capsul In Strip', 'Capsule', '20 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indication:</strong></p><ul><li>GERD-related symptoms (e.g., heartburn)</li><li>Erosive esophagitis</li><li>Helicobacter pylori eradication (with amoxicillin &amp; clarithromycin)</li><li>Zollinger-Ellison syndrome</li><li>Duodenal &amp; gastric ulcers caused by acid dyspepsia</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Erosive Esophagitis:</strong> 20-40 mg daily for 4-8 weeks.</li><li><strong>GERD Symptoms:</strong> 20 mg daily for 4 weeks, extend if needed.</li><li><strong>Helicobacter pylori:</strong> Esomeprazole 40 mg, amoxicillin 1000 mg, clarithromycin 500 mg, all for 10 days.</li><li><strong>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome:</strong> 20-80 mg daily, adjust as needed.</li><li><strong>Acid Dyspepsia:</strong> 20-40 mg daily for 2-4 weeks.</li><li><strong>Injection:</strong> 40 mg daily via IV.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration:</strong></p><ul><li>Take 1 hour before meals; capsules should be swallowed whole.</li><li>For oral suspension, mix with water and consume within 30 minutes.</li><li>For IV, administer over 3 minutes.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>CYP2C19 and CYP3A4 metabolize esomeprazole; minimal interactions with warfarin, phenytoin, and others.</li><li>May reduce absorption of drugs like ketoconazole, iron salts, and digoxin.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to esomeprazole.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Headache, diarrhea, nausea, flatulence, abdominal pain.</li><li>Rare: Long-term side effects are similar to short-term.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Exclude stomach cancer before treatment.</li><li>Avoid crushing pellets; use with antacids is fine.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose:</strong></p><ul><li>No specific countermeasure; supportive care recommended.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, in a dry place.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Inhibits proton pump (H+/K+-ATPase) in gastric parietal cells, reducing acid production.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Limited data on safety in pregnancy; discontinue breastfeeding if necessary.</li></ul><p><strong>Pediatric Use:</strong></p><ul><li>Safety not established in children.</li></ul>', 'active', '1362_1733691856.jpg', 10, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 02:04:16', '2024-12-15 13:54:37'),
(85, 'Tufnil', 'Tolfenamic acid', 10.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '200 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indication:</strong></p><ul><li>Relieves migraine headache pain</li><li>Analgesic for post-operative pain and fever</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>NSAIDs, Drugs for Rheumatoid Arthritis, Migraine treatments</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li>Inhibits prostaglandin biosynthesis by blocking COX-1 and COX-2, reducing inflammation and pain.</li><li>Additional anti-inflammatory effects by inhibiting leukotriene B4 chemotaxis.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Acute migraine:</strong> 200 mg at first symptoms, repeat after 1-2 hours.</li><li><strong>Mild to moderate pain:</strong> 100-200 mg three times daily.</li><li>Take with food; dose adjustments needed for renal impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>Increases absorption with Metoclopramide and Magnesium hydroxide; decreases with Aluminium hydroxide.</li><li>Increases bleeding risk with anticoagulants; reduces antihypertensive effects with certain blood pressure meds.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Active peptic ulcer, severe heart, kidney, or liver failure.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Dysuria, diarrhea, nausea, vomiting, headache, fatigue.</li><li>Severe: Blood dyscrasias, hepatitis.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid during pregnancy, especially in the first and third trimesters.</li><li>NSAIDs may appear in breast milk; use cautiously.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Use with caution in patients with asthma, bleeding disorders, heart conditions, kidney/liver impairment, and the elderly.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: Headache, nausea, vomiting, gastrointestinal bleeding, renal and liver damage in severe cases.</li><li>Treatment: Symptomatic care.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place, away from light, and keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Inhibits COX enzymes, reducing prostaglandin and thromboxane synthesis, which helps reduce pain and inflammation.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '723_1733692042.jpg', 26, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 02:07:22', '2024-12-09 02:07:22'),
(86, 'Entacyd Plus', 'Aluminium Hydroxide + Magnesium Hydroxide + Simethicone', 90.00, 1, 'Bottle', '1 Syrup Bottle', 'Syrup', '200 ml', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indication:</strong></p><ul><li>Relieves hyperacidity, peptic ulcers, gastritis, heartburn, sour stomach, and hiatus hernia.</li><li>Prevents stress ulcers and GI bleeding.</li><li>Acts as an antiflatulent to alleviate gas, including post-operative gas pain.</li></ul><p><strong>Composition (per 5 ml):</strong></p><ul><li>Aluminium Hydroxide: 200 mg</li><li>Magnesium Hydroxide: 400 mg</li><li>Simethicone: 30 mg</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Antacids</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li>Aluminium Hydroxide and Magnesium Hydroxide neutralize gastric acid.</li><li>Simethicone reduces gas and foam in the GI tract by collapsing foam bubbles, aiding in gas expulsion.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tablet:</strong> 1-2 tablets, 1-3 hours after meals and at bedtime.</li><li><strong>Suspension:</strong> 1-2 teaspoonfuls, 1-3 hours after meals and at bedtime.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>Antacids may affect the absorption of certain drugs (e.g., antibiotics, benzodiazepines, digoxin).</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Not for use in patients with renal failure, hypophosphataemia, alkalosis, hypermagnesaemia, or intestinal obstruction.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Uncommon, but may include diarrhea, constipation, or regurgitation if taken excessively.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid during the first trimester of pregnancy.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Use cautiously in patients with kidney disease.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture, and out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Neutralizes stomach acid and reduces gas through simethicone\'s antifoam action, aiding digestion and comfort.</li></ul>', 'in-active', '1388_1733692301.jpeg', 4, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 02:11:41', '2025-05-08 14:39:46'),
(87, 'Xorel', 'Rabeprazole Sodium', 4.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '20 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indication:</strong></p><ul><li>Active duodenal and benign gastric ulcers</li><li>Erosive/ulcerative GERD (short- and long-term management)</li><li>Symptomatic GERD</li><li>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome</li><li>H. pylori eradication with antibiotics in peptic ulcer disease</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Proton Pump Inhibitor</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><p>Rabeprazole inhibits gastric H+/K+-ATPase (proton pump) in stomach parietal cells, reducing gastric acid secretion.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Duodenal/Gastric Ulcers:</strong> 20 mg daily in the morning for 4–6 weeks.</li><li><strong>Erosive GERD:</strong> 20 mg daily for 4–8 weeks (may extend to 8 more weeks if necessary).</li><li><strong>Symptomatic GERD:</strong> 20 mg daily for 4 weeks; repeat if symptoms persist.</li><li><strong>GERD Maintenance:</strong> 10–20 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome:</strong> Start with 60 mg daily, adjust as needed; doses up to 120 mg/day are possible.</li><li><strong>H. pylori Eradication:</strong> Rabeprazole 20 mg, Amoxicillin 1 g, and Clarithromycin 500 mg twice daily for 7 days.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration:</strong></p><p>Take in the morning, preferably before meals. Swallow tablets whole without chewing or crushing.</p><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to rabeprazole or excipients.</li><li>Not recommended during pregnancy or breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Headache, nausea, vomiting, constipation, dry mouth, dizziness.</li><li>Long-term use may increase the risk of fractures (hip, wrist, spine).</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Rule out malignancy before starting treatment.</li><li>Long-term users (&gt;1 year) should be monitored.</li><li>Ensure adequate calcium and vitamin D for patients at risk of osteoporosis.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>FDA Category C: Limited data; avoid use unless necessary. Likely excreted in breast milk.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><p>Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture. Keep out of reach of children.</p><p><strong>Use in Special Populations:</strong></p><ul><li>Not recommended for children due to insufficient safety data.</li><li>No dosage adjustment needed for hepatic or renal impairment.</li></ul>', 'active', '1259_1733725471.jpg', 30, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 11:24:31', '2024-12-09 11:25:18'),
(88, 'Napa', 'Paracetamol', 35.00, 1, 'x 60 ml bottle', '60 ml bottle', 'Syrup', '120 mg/5 ml', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li>Relief for <strong>fever</strong>, <strong>cold</strong>, <strong>headache</strong>, <strong>toothache</strong>, <strong>earache</strong>, <strong>bodyache</strong>, <strong>muscle pain</strong>, and post-vaccination pain in children.</li><li>Pain management in <strong>dysmenorrhea</strong>, <strong>rheumatic &amp; osteoarthritic conditions</strong>, and <strong>post-operative</strong> or <strong>postpartum</strong> pain.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tablet: 1–2 tablets every 4–6 hours (max 8 tablets/day).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Syrup: 4–8 teaspoonfuls 3–4 times daily.</li><li><strong>Children (6–12 years)</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tablet: ½–1 tablet 3–4 times daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Syrup: 2–4 teaspoonfuls 3–4 times daily.</li><li><strong>Children (1–5 years)</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Syrup: 1–2 teaspoonfuls 3–4 times daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Suppository: 125–250 mg 4 times daily.</li><li><strong>Infants (&lt;1 year)</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Syrup: ½–1 teaspoonful 3–4 times daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Suppository: 60–120 mg 4 times daily.</li><li><strong>Extended-Release Tablets (12+ years)</strong>: 2 tablets every 6–8 hours (max 6 tablets/day).</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li>Napa (Acetaminophen) acts in the CNS to block COX enzymes, reducing pain and fever. It has minimal anti-inflammatory effects and does not irritate the stomach like aspirin.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Mild</strong>: Skin rash, nausea, vomiting.</li><li><strong>Rare</strong>: Blood disorders (thrombocytopenia, neutropenia), pancreatitis.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Use cautiously in patients with <strong>liver or kidney impairment</strong>.</li><li>Avoid alcohol as it may increase liver toxicity.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Category B</strong>: Generally safe in pregnancy if necessary.</li><li>Safe for breastfeeding at therapeutic doses.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Symptoms</strong>: Pallor, nausea, vomiting, abdominal pain, liver damage (12–48 hours post-ingestion).</li><li><strong>Management</strong>: Immediate medical attention and supportive care.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place away from light and heat. Keep out of children’s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Class</strong></p><ul><li>Non-opioid analgesic.</li></ul>', 'active', '973_1733765844.png', 3, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 11:24:34', '2025-05-04 21:20:46'),
(89, 'Bexitrol F', 'Salmeterol + Fluticasone Propionate', 795.00, 1, 'Inhaler', '120 Metered Doses', 'Inhaler', '25 mcg+250 mcg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Asthma Treatment</strong>: For patients inadequately controlled with inhaled corticosteroids and short-acting β2-agonists or already on both long-acting β2-agonists and corticosteroids.</li><li><strong>Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD)</strong>: Suitable for management.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Long-acting β2-adrenoceptor stimulants.</li><li>Respiratory corticosteroids.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Salmeterol Xinafoate</strong>: A long-acting β2-agonist providing sustained bronchodilation.</li><li><strong>Fluticasone Propionate</strong>: A potent inhaled corticosteroid with anti-inflammatory effects, reducing asthma symptoms and exacerbations without significant systemic effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Inhalation Aerosol</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Adults &amp; Adolescents (≥12 years): 2 puffs (morning &amp; evening).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Children (4–12 years): 2 puffs of 25 µg Salmeterol + 50 µg Fluticasone twice daily.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Inhalation Powder</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li>For <strong>Asthma</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Adults &amp; Adolescents: Start with 50 µg Salmeterol + 100–250 µg Fluticasone (max: 500 µg Fluticasone twice daily).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Children (4–11 years): 50 µg Salmeterol + 100 µg Fluticasone twice daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For <strong>COPD</strong>: 50 µg Salmeterol + 250 µg Fluticasone twice daily.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Maxhaler</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Similar dosing but delivered via a patient-friendly device.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any components.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Salmeterol</strong>: Tremor, palpitations, headache, rare cardiac arrhythmias, muscle cramps, hypersensitivity reactions.</li><li><strong>Fluticasone Propionate</strong>: Hoarseness, oral candidiasis, hypersensitivity, rare facial/oropharyngeal edema.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Use only if the benefit outweighs the risk. Insufficient data on human pregnancy and breast milk excretion.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Caution in active/quiescent tuberculosis and thyrotoxicosis.</li><li>Use additional corticosteroid therapies and antibiotics if infections are present.</li><li>Pediatric patients may experience reduced growth velocity.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid β-blockers unless necessary.</li><li>Strong CYP3A4 inhibitors (e.g., ketoconazole) may increase Fluticasone systemic exposure.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, away from sunlight and heat. Avoid puncturing pressurized canisters. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration Tips</strong></p><ol><li>Shake well before use.</li><li>Breathe out fully, inhale deeply while pressing the canister, and hold breath for 10 seconds.</li><li>Rinse mouth after each use to prevent candidiasis.</li><li>Clean inhaler weekly, avoiding water exposure to the canister.</li></ol>', 'active', '105_1733726453.jpg', 3, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 11:40:53', '2024-12-09 22:23:34'),
(90, 'Esonix', 'Esomeprazole Magnesium Trihydrate', 7.00, 14, 'Tablet', '14 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '20 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>GERD Symptoms</strong>: Persistent heartburn and related issues.</li><li><strong>Erosive Esophagitis</strong>: Treatment and maintenance of healing.</li><li><strong>H. pylori Eradication</strong>: With amoxicillin and clarithromycin for duodenal ulcers.</li><li><strong>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome</strong>, <strong>Duodenal &amp; Gastric Ulcers</strong>, and <strong>Acid Dyspepsia</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Erosive Esophagitis</strong>: 20-40 mg once daily for 4–8 weeks. Maintenance: 20 mg daily (up to 6 months).</li><li><strong>GERD Symptoms</strong>: 20 mg daily for 4 weeks; extend another 4 weeks if needed.</li><li><strong>H. pylori Eradication</strong>: Esomeprazole 40 mg, Amoxicillin 1000 mg, Clarithromycin 500 mg twice daily for 10 days.</li><li><strong>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome</strong>: 20–80 mg daily, adjusted individually.</li><li><strong>Duodenal Ulcer</strong>: 20 mg daily for 2–4 weeks.</li><li><strong>Gastric Ulcer</strong>: 20–40 mg daily for 4–8 weeks.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong></p><ul><li>Take orally 1 hour before a meal. Capsules can be opened and mixed with soft applesauce if needed.</li><li>For IV use: Reconstitute with 5 ml sterile water and inject over at least 3 minutes.</li></ul><p><strong>Common Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Headache, diarrhea, nausea, flatulence, abdominal pain, constipation, dry mouth.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>May reduce absorption of drugs dependent on stomach acidity (e.g., ketoconazole, iron salts, digoxin).</li><li>May affect the metabolism of diazepam, increasing its plasma levels.</li></ul><p><strong>Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Symptom relief does not rule out stomach cancer.</li><li>Avoid use in individuals allergic to its components.</li><li>Safety in pediatric use not established; use cautiously in severe hepatic impairment (max 20 mg daily).</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Insufficient studies in pregnant women; use only if necessary. Breastfeeding should be discontinued if treatment is required.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Keep in a dry place below 30°C, protected from moisture and light. Keep out of children\'s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>Mechanism of Action</strong></p><p>Esomeprazole, a proton pump inhibitor, reduces stomach acid by selectively inhibiting the H+/K+-ATPase enzyme in gastric parietal cells.</p><p><strong>Overdose Management</strong></p><p>Symptoms include decreased motor activity, respiratory changes, and tremors. Provide supportive care; esomeprazole is not removed by dialysis.</p>', 'active', '222_1733726887.webp', 2, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 11:48:07', '2024-12-09 22:26:26'),
(91, 'Montene', 'Montelukast', 17.50, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li>Prophylaxis and chronic treatment of asthma.</li><li>Prevention of Exercise-Induced Bronchoconstriction (EIB).</li><li>Relief of Seasonal &amp; Perennial Allergic Rhinitis symptoms.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults &amp; Adolescents (15+ years)</strong>: 10 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Children</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>6–14 years</strong>: 5 mg once daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>2–5 years</strong>: 4 mg once daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>6 months–2 years</strong>: 4 mg oral granules once daily.</li><li>No dosage adjustment required for hepatic/renal insufficiency or elderly patients.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li>Blocks cysteinyl leukotriene receptor (CysLT1), reducing airway edema, smooth muscle contraction, and inflammation-related cellular activity in asthma and allergic rhinitis.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any component of the medication.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common</strong>: Headache, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, fever, and upper respiratory tract infections.</li><li><strong>Rare</strong>: Pulmonary eosinophilia, angioedema, hepatic issues, depression, and suicidal thoughts.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Not suitable for acute asthma attacks or replacing corticosteroids abruptly.</li><li>Patients with aspirin sensitivity should continue to avoid NSAIDs.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Pregnancy Category B: Use only if necessary, as there is limited evidence in humans.</li><li>Exercise caution in breastfeeding due to potential secretion in milk.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: Nausea, vomiting, headache, thirst, and abdominal pain.</li><li>Supportive measures: Gastric decontamination and clinical monitoring.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C in a cool, dry place, away from moisture and light.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Class</strong></p><ul><li>Leukotriene receptor antagonists.</li></ul>', 'active', '1785_1733727107.png', 4, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 11:51:47', '2024-12-09 22:26:43');
INSERT INTO `products` (`id`, `productName`, `genericName`, `retail_max_price`, `cart_qty_inc`, `cart_text`, `unit_in_pack`, `type`, `quantity`, `prescription`, `feature`, `description`, `status`, `coverImage`, `company_id`, `category_id`, `add_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(92, 'Fenadin', 'Fexofenadine Hydrochloride', 9.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '120 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Allergic Rhinitis</strong> (Seasonal/Perennial): Relieves sneezing, runny nose, itchy/red eyes, and throat discomfort.</li><li><strong>Chronic Idiopathic Urticaria</strong>: Reduces wheals and pruritus.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults &amp; Children (12+ years)</strong>:</li><li><strong>Allergic Rhinitis &amp; Urticaria</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">60 mg twice daily, 120 mg or 180 mg once daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Renal impairment</strong>: 60 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Children (6–11 years)</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Tablet: 30 mg twice daily or 60 mg once daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Renal impairment</strong>: 30 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Children (6 months–2 years)</strong>: Suspension 15 mg (2.5 ml) twice daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Renal impairment</strong>: 15 mg (2.5 ml) once daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li>Selective peripheral H1-receptor antagonist, blocking histamine\'s effects without crossing the blood-brain barrier, reducing allergy symptoms without sedation.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to fexofenadine or its components.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common</strong>: Headache, fatigue, dizziness, and nausea.</li><li><strong>Rare</strong>: Rash, urticaria, angioedema, tachycardia, and hypersensitivity reactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Use cautiously in elderly patients or those with renal impairment.</li><li>May rarely cause palpitations or tachycardia.</li><li>Patients should evaluate their response before operating machinery or driving.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Pregnancy Category C: Use only if benefits outweigh risks.</li><li>Not recommended during breastfeeding due to potential excretion in milk.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>Increased plasma levels with erythromycin or ketoconazole.</li><li>Decreased bioavailability when taken with antacids containing aluminum or magnesium (administer 2 hours apart).</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: Drowsiness, fatigue, dizziness, and dry mouth.</li><li>Treatment: Supportive care and symptomatic management.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place away from light and moisture. Keep out of children’s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Class</strong></p><ul><li>Non-sedating antihistamines.</li></ul>', 'active', '190_1733727311.webp', 6, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 11:55:11', '2024-12-09 22:27:06'),
(93, 'Quick Check Test Strip', 'Blood Glucose Test Strips', 400.00, 1, 'Box', '25\'s strip in a box', 'Surgical', '25\'s test strip', 'no', 'no', '<p><strong>Quick Check Blood Glucose Test Strips (25 Strips)</strong></p><p><strong>Key Benefits:</strong></p><ul><li>Ergonomically designed for a comfortable grip</li><li>User-friendly and simple to operate</li><li>Prevents contamination for reliable results</li><li>High level of accuracy for dependable readings</li><li>Advanced design ensures optimal functionality</li><li>Short test pathway for quicker results</li><li>Automatically calibrates for ease of use</li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Carefully read the instruction manual before use</li><li>Keep out of reach of children</li><li>Dispose of used batteries responsibly</li><li>Avoid water exposure to the device; do not submerge or rinse under running water</li></ul>', 'active', '253_1733903610.webp', 31, 5, NULL, '2024-12-09 14:20:13', '2024-12-11 12:53:30'),
(94, 'VivaChek Ino Test Strip', 'Blood Glucose Test Strips', 1050.00, 1, 'Box', '50\'s strip in a box', 'Surgical', '50\'s strip', 'no', 'no', '<p><strong>Ino Blood Glucose Test Strips (50 Strips)</strong></p><p><strong>Key Benefits:</strong></p><ul><li>Ergonomically designed for easy handling</li><li>Simple and intuitive to use</li><li>Prevents contamination for accurate results</li><li>Reliable accuracy for consistent readings</li><li>Advanced strip design for optimal performance</li><li>Short test pathway for quicker testing</li><li>Auto-coding for hassle-free use</li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Carefully read the instruction manual before use</li><li>Keep out of reach of children</li><li>Dispose of used batteries properly</li><li>Avoid water exposure to the device; do not submerge or rinse under running water</li></ul>', 'active', '853_1733736284.png', 32, 5, NULL, '2024-12-09 14:24:44', '2024-12-11 11:31:13'),
(95, 'Alcet', 'Levocetirizine Dihydrochloride', 4.50, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '5 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Allergic conditions</strong>: Seasonal and perennial allergic rhinitis, chronic idiopathic urticaria.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults and Children (12+ years)</strong>: 5 mg once daily in the evening.</li><li><strong>Children (6–11 years)</strong>: 2.5 mg once daily in the evening.</li><li><strong>Children (6 months–5 years)</strong>: 1.25 mg once daily in the evening.</li><li><strong>Renal Impairment</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Mild (CrCl: 50–80 mL/min)</strong>: 2.5 mg once daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Moderate (CrCl: 30–50 mL/min)</strong>: 2.5 mg every other day.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Severe (CrCl: 10–30 mL/min)</strong>: 2.5 mg twice weekly.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>End-stage renal disease (CrCl: &lt;10 mL/min)</strong>: Contraindicated.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li>Levocetirizine is the active isomer of Cetirizine, with twice the affinity for H1 receptors, offering rapid, long-lasting, non-sedating antihistamine action.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Rare: Headache, dry mouth, fatigue, skin rash.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Use with caution in <strong>epileptic patients</strong>, <strong>pregnancy</strong>, <strong>lactation</strong>, and <strong>renal impairment</strong>.</li><li>Avoid use in children &lt;6 months and patients with severe renal impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Category B</strong>: Use only if benefits outweigh risks. Passes into breast milk—caution for nursing mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C in a dry place, protected from light.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Class</strong></p><ul><li>Non-sedating antihistamines.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Management</strong></p><ul><li>Generally well-tolerated; provide symptomatic and supportive care if necessary.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1194_1733766135.webp', 1, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 22:42:15', '2024-12-09 22:42:15'),
(96, 'Montela', 'Montelukast', 10.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li>Prophylaxis and chronic treatment of <strong>asthma</strong>.</li><li>Prevention of <strong>Exercise-Induced Bronchoconstriction (EIB)</strong>.</li><li>Relief of symptoms of <strong>Seasonal and Perennial Allergic Rhinitis</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults &amp; Adolescents (15+ years)</strong>: 10 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Children (6–14 years)</strong>: 5 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Children (2–5 years)</strong>: 4 mg once daily (tablet or oral granules).</li><li><strong>Children (6 months–2 years)</strong>: 4 mg oral granules once daily.</li><li><strong>Renal/Hepatic Insufficiency &amp; Elderly</strong>: No dosage adjustment required for mild to moderate cases.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li>Montela 10 mg (montelukast) is a selective leukotriene receptor antagonist that blocks the effects of cysteinyl leukotrienes (LTC4, LTD4, LTE4), which play a key role in asthma and allergic rhinitis by causing airway inflammation and constriction.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Headache, nausea, diarrhea, fever, stomach pain.</li><li>Rare: Angioedema, pulmonary eosinophilia, behavioral changes (e.g., agitation, depression, hallucinations), hepatic dysfunction.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Not for treating acute asthma attacks.</li><li>Maintain rescue medication access for emergencies.</li><li>Avoid abrupt substitution for corticosteroids.</li><li>Aspirin-sensitive patients should continue to avoid NSAIDs.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Category B</strong>: Use only if clearly needed. Passes into breast milk; exercise caution in nursing mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C in a cool, dry place away from light and moisture.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Class</strong></p><ul><li>Leukotriene receptor antagonist.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: Nausea, vomiting, thirst, hyperactivity, abdominal pain.</li><li>Treatment: Supportive care and monitoring.</li></ul>', 'active', '520_1733766396.webp', 33, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 22:46:36', '2024-12-09 22:50:23'),
(97, 'Dicaltrol Plus', 'Calcitriol + Calcium Citrate', 13.00, 5, 'Tablet', '5 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '1200 mg+0.25 mcg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Osteoporosis</strong>, <strong>Hypoparathyroidism</strong>, <strong>Hypocalcaemia</strong>, <strong>Osteomalacia</strong>, <strong>Rickets</strong>, <strong>Renal osteodystrophy</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Hyperparathyroidism (renal failure)</strong>: 0.25 mcg/day or alternate day, increasing gradually.</li><li><strong>Hypoparathyroidism</strong>: 0.5-2 mcg once daily.</li><li><strong>Vitamin D-dependent rickets</strong>: 0.015-0.02 mcg/kg/day.</li><li><strong>Maintenance doses</strong>: 0.03-0.06 mcg/kg/day.</li><li><strong>Dialysis patients</strong>: 0.5-4 mcg 3 times/week.</li><li><strong>Max dose</strong>: 8 mcg 3 times/week.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Calcium</strong> helps prevent calcium deficiency and supports bone health.</li><li><strong>Calcitriol</strong> increases calcium absorption in the intestines and retention at the kidneys, raising serum calcium levels. It also reduces phosphate and PTH levels, and decreases bone resorption.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Weakness, headache, nausea, constipation, dry mouth, muscle pain.</li><li>Severe: Hypercalcaemia, nephrocalcinosis, pancreatitis, cardiac arrhythmias, elevated BUN/ALT/AST.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Category C</strong>: Use only if benefits outweigh risks due to potential fetal harm.</li><li>Not recommended during <strong>lactation</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Monitor for <strong>hypercalcaemia</strong> and <strong>renal impairment</strong>.</li><li>Individualized pediatric dosing with close medical supervision.</li><li>Caution in <strong>coronary disease</strong>, <strong>arteriosclerosis</strong>, and elderly patients.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid co-administration with <strong>thiazide diuretics</strong>, <strong>vitamin D</strong>, and <strong>digitalis</strong> due to increased risk of hypercalcaemia.</li><li><strong>Corticosteroids</strong> may reduce calcium absorption.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place below 30°C.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '299_1733766569.jpg', 9, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 22:49:29', '2024-12-09 22:49:29'),
(98, 'Vitabion', 'Vitamin B1 + B6 + B12', 12.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '100 mg+200 mg+200 mcg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li>Treatment of <strong>Vitamin B1</strong>, <strong>B6</strong>, and <strong>B12</strong> deficiency.</li><li>Supportive treatment for <strong>neuritis</strong>, <strong>diabetic neuropathy</strong>, <strong>peripheral neuralgia</strong>, <strong>lumbago</strong>, <strong>myalgia</strong>, <strong>optic neuritis</strong>, <strong>sciatica</strong>, <strong>facial neuralgia</strong>, <strong>spinal pain</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tablet</strong>: Vitamin B1 (100 mg), Vitamin B6 (200 mg), Vitamin B12 (200 mcg).</li><li><strong>Injection (3 ml)</strong>: Vitamin B1 (100 mg), Vitamin B6 (100 mg), Vitamin B12 (1000 mcg).</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tablets</strong>: 1-3 tablets/day, or as directed by a physician.</li><li><strong>Injection</strong>: 1 ampoule daily for severe cases (until acute symptoms subside), or 2-3 ampoules/week for mild cases.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li>Combined <strong>B1</strong>, <strong>B6</strong>, and <strong>B12</strong> support nerve cell metabolism, promote regeneration of nerve fibers, and repair nerve damage.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Generally well-tolerated; possible allergic reactions in some cases.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Oral form</strong> is safe during pregnancy at recommended dosages.</li><li><strong>Injection</strong> is not recommended during pregnancy due to benzyl alcohol.</li><li><strong>B1</strong>, <strong>B6</strong>, and <strong>B12</strong> are secreted in breast milk, but overdose risks for the infant are unknown.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Not for use in patients on <strong>levodopa therapy</strong> or those allergic to the ingredients.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Cyanocobalamin</strong> should not be used in <strong>subacute degeneration of the spinal cord</strong> or for optic neuropathies associated with high plasma concentrations of cyanocobalamin.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose</strong></p><ul><li>No significant overdose symptoms; treatment is symptomatic and supportive.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below <strong>25°C</strong>, in a cool, dry place, protected from light. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1315_1733767500.webp', 2, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 23:05:00', '2024-12-09 23:05:00'),
(99, 'Ace', 'Paracetamol', 1.20, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '500 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Fever</strong>, <strong>common cold</strong>, <strong>influenza</strong>, <strong>headache</strong>, <strong>toothache</strong>, <strong>earache</strong>, <strong>bodyache</strong>, <strong>myalgia</strong>, <strong>neuralgia</strong>, <strong>dysmenorrhoea</strong>, <strong>sprains</strong>, <strong>colic pain</strong>, <strong>back pain</strong>, <strong>post-operative pain</strong>, <strong>postpartum pain</strong>, <strong>rheumatic &amp; osteoarthritic pain</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Non-opioid analgesics</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Ace 500 mg</strong> (Acetaminophen) provides <strong>analgesic</strong> and <strong>antipyretic</strong> effects with weak <strong>anti-inflammatory</strong> activity. It works by inhibiting cyclooxygenase enzymes (COX-1, COX-2, COX-3), which reduces prostaglandin production, thus increasing the pain threshold.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tablet</strong>: Adults 1-2 tablets every 4-6 hours (max 8 tablets/day).</li><li><strong>Children (6-12 years)</strong>: ½ to 1 tablet 3-4 times/day.</li><li><strong>Extended Release Tablet</strong>: Adults 2 tablets every 6-8 hours (max 6 tablets/day).</li><li><strong>Syrup</strong>: Doses vary by age (10 mg/kg for infants, up to 8 tsp/day for adults).</li><li><strong>Suppository</strong>: 60-120 mg for children, 0.5-1 gm for adults.</li><li><strong>Paediatric Drop</strong>: 0.5 ml (up to 1.5 ml) for children, up to 5 doses/day.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Mild side effects; rare cases of <strong>thrombocytopenia</strong>, <strong>leucopenia</strong>, <strong>pancreatitis</strong>, <strong>skin rashes</strong>, and other allergic reactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy Category B</strong> (USFDA). Use only when necessary.</li><li><strong>Excreted in breast milk</strong> but no risk to infants in therapeutic doses.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Contraindicated in patients with known hypersensitivity to <strong>Ace 500 mg</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Use with caution in patients with <strong>impaired liver or kidney function</strong> or those on liver-affecting medications.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Initial symptoms: <strong>pallor</strong>, <strong>nausea</strong>, <strong>vomiting</strong>, <strong>abdominal pain</strong>.</li><li>Later symptoms: <strong>liver damage</strong>, <strong>glucose metabolism abnormalities</strong>, <strong>metabolic acidosis</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a <strong>dry place</strong>, away from <strong>light</strong> and <strong>heat</strong>. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul>', 'active', '1743_1733767807.jpg', 4, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 23:10:07', '2025-03-22 17:49:35'),
(100, 'Zif-CI', 'Carbonyl Iron + Folic Acid + Zinc Sulfate', 5.00, 10, 'Capsule', '10 Capsul In Strip', 'Capsule', '50 mg+0.50 mg+61.80 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Treatment and prevention</strong> of <strong>iron</strong>, <strong>folic acid</strong>, and <strong>zinc deficiencies</strong>, especially during <strong>pregnancy</strong> and <strong>lactation</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Carbonyl Iron</strong>: 50 mg</li><li><strong>Folic Acid</strong>: 500 mcg</li><li><strong>Zinc Sulphate Monohydrate</strong>: 61.80 mg (equivalent to 22.50 mg Zinc)</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Iron, Vitamin, &amp; Mineral Combined Preparations</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Iron</strong>: Essential for oxygen transport in blood.</li><li><strong>Folic Acid</strong>: Supports red blood cell production, DNA synthesis, and protein metabolism.</li><li><strong>Zinc</strong>: Critical for enzyme function, immune response, growth, and wound healing.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults &amp; Elderly</strong>: 1 capsule daily; severe cases may require 2 capsules.</li><li><strong>Children (1+ years)</strong>: 1 capsule daily. Capsules can be opened, and pellets mixed with soft food, but not chewed.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Iron</strong> reduces absorption of tetracyclines, quinolones, levodopa, levothyroxine, and methyldopa.</li><li><strong>Folic Acid</strong> may lower plasma levels of antiepileptic drugs like phenobarbital and phenytoin.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Iron overload conditions</strong> (e.g., haemochromatosis) or hypersensitivity to components.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Mild gastrointestinal issues</strong>: nausea, vomiting, constipation, diarrhea, and dark stools. Rarely, allergic reactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid in the <strong>first trimester</strong> unless iron deficiency is confirmed. Supplementation is justified later during pregnancy for prophylaxis of deficiencies.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Monitor patients with <strong>iron overload</strong> or <strong>renal failure</strong> (risk of zinc accumulation). Investigate non-responsive anemia for other causes.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms include <strong>nausea</strong>, <strong>abdominal pain</strong>, <strong>tarry stools</strong>, <strong>rapid pulse</strong>, and in severe cases, <strong>coma</strong> or <strong>seizures</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below <strong>30°C</strong>, away from light and moisture. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Timed-release formulation</strong> ensures optimal absorption and reduces gastrointestinal irritation. Carbonyl Iron is highly bioavailable with low toxicity.</li></ul>', 'active', '817_1733768011.webp', 4, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 23:13:31', '2024-12-15 13:54:16'),
(101, 'Xinc-B', 'Vitamin B Complex + Zinc', 3.50, 30, 'Tablet', '30 Tablet In Bottle', 'Tablet', '39 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Treatment and prevention</strong> of <strong>vitamin B</strong> and <strong>zinc deficiencies</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Syrup/Tablet (per dose):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Thiamine</strong>: 5 mg</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Riboflavin</strong>: 2 mg</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Pyridoxine</strong>: 2 mg</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Nicotinamide</strong>: 20 mg</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Zinc (as Zinc Sulfate Monohydrate)</strong>: 10 mg</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Specific Mineral &amp; Vitamin Combined Preparations</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Vitamin B Complex</strong>: Regulates carbohydrate, protein, and fat metabolism; supports red blood cell production, brain function, and healthy growth.</li><li><strong>Zinc</strong>: Essential for immunity, growth, wound healing, and various biological functions.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Syrup</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Adults: 10 ml (2 tsp) 2–3 times daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Children: 10 ml (2 tsp) 1–3 times daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Infants: 5 ml (1 tsp) 1–2 times daily.</li><li><strong>Tablets</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Adults &amp; Children over 30 kg: 1–2 tablets 2–3 times daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>Zinc may reduce absorption of tetracyclines, fluoroquinolones, and some medications like <strong>levodopa</strong> or <strong>phenytoin</strong>.</li><li>Niacin with HMG-CoA inhibitors may cause muscle-related side effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any component.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Generally well tolerated; mild side effects include <strong>nausea</strong>, <strong>vomiting</strong>, and <strong>stomach upset</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Recommended during <strong>pregnancy</strong> and <strong>lactation</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Monitor for <strong>zinc accumulation</strong> in patients with <strong>acute renal failure</strong>. Not for treating severe deficiencies.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: <strong>Epigastric pain</strong>, <strong>diarrhea</strong>, and <strong>vomiting</strong>. In case of overdose, seek medical attention.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place, protected from light. Keep out of children’s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Zinc</strong> supports immunity, growth, and wound healing and treats zinc deficiency-related conditions.</li><li><strong>Vitamin B Complex</strong> aids energy production, nerve function, and red blood cell formation, especially critical for children’s growth and development.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '738_1733768341.webp', 26, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 23:19:01', '2024-12-09 23:19:01'),
(102, 'Ostocal D', 'Calcium Carbonate [Elemental] + Vitamin D3', 8.00, 30, 'Tablet', '30 Tablet In Bottle', 'Tablet', '500 mg+200 IU', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li>Treatment of osteoporosis, osteomalacia, rickets, tetany, parathyroid disease.</li><li>Calcium supplement for pregnancy, lactation, bone/tooth formation, and chronic renal failure.</li></ul><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Calcium Carbonate (500 mg)</strong> and <strong>Vitamin D3 (200 IU or 400 IU)</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Specific mineral &amp; vitamin combined preparations.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li>Calcium supports bone formation and maintenance.</li><li>Vitamin D3 enhances calcium absorption, reabsorption, and bone formation.</li><li>Combined use aids in bone growth and prevents fractures.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage</strong></p><ul><li><strong>500 mg Calcium + 200 IU Vitamin D3</strong>: 2 tablets daily or 1 tablet twice daily.</li><li><strong>500 mg Calcium + 400 IU Vitamin D3</strong>: 1 tablet twice daily.</li><li>Best taken with or after meals for better absorption.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypercalcemia, hyperthyroidism, renal calculi, nephrolithiasis, Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Rare: Nausea, vomiting, dry mouth, increased thirst/urination, constipation, stomach cramps.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Use cautiously in heart or kidney disease.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Safe if directed by a physician.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Symptoms</strong></p><ul><li>Nausea, vomiting, dry mouth, drowsiness, headache, loss of appetite, constipation, diarrhea.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry place, away from light and heat. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1598_1733768534.webp', 26, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 23:22:14', '2024-12-09 23:22:14'),
(103, 'Nexum MUPS', 'Esomeprazole Magnesium Trihydrate', 10.00, 10, 'MUPS Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '20 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li>GERD-related symptoms (e.g., persistent heartburn).</li><li>Erosive esophagitis (treatment and maintenance).</li><li>Helicobacter pylori eradication (with amoxicillin and clarithromycin).</li><li>Zollinger-Ellison syndrome.</li><li>Acid-related dyspepsia, duodenal, and gastric ulcers.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage</strong></p><ul><li><strong>GERD/Erosive Esophagitis:</strong> 20–40 mg once daily for 4–8 weeks.</li><li><strong>H. pylori eradication:</strong> Esomeprazole 40 mg + Amoxicillin 1000 mg + Clarithromycin 500 mg, twice daily for 10 days.</li><li><strong>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome:</strong> 20–80 mg once daily, individualized dosing.</li><li><strong>Acid dyspepsia/Ulcers:</strong> 20–40 mg once daily for 2–8 weeks.</li><li><strong>Injection:</strong> 40 mg once daily via IV (3–30 minutes), transitioned to oral as soon as possible.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong></p><ul><li>Take 1 hour before meals; capsules should be swallowed whole or mixed with applesauce for patients with swallowing difficulty.</li><li>For oral suspension, mix contents with 15 mL water, stir, let thicken, and consume within 30 minutes.</li><li>IV solution must be used within 12 hours after preparation.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>May affect drugs metabolized by CYP2C19 (e.g., diazepam) and reduce the absorption of pH-dependent drugs (e.g., ketoconazole, iron).</li><li>Safe with antacids, oral contraceptives, phenytoin, and quinidine.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to esomeprazole or related drugs.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Headache, diarrhea, nausea, constipation, abdominal pain, flatulence, dry mouth.</li><li>Rare: Long-term use does not significantly increase side effect frequency.</li></ul><p><strong>Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Symptomatic relief does not rule out gastric cancer.</li><li>Use cautiously in severe hepatic impairment (max dose: 20 mg daily).</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>No adequate human studies; use only if necessary.</li><li>Discontinue breastfeeding if used.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><ul><li>Esomeprazole, a proton pump inhibitor, reduces gastric acid production by targeting H+/K+-ATPase in parietal cells.</li><li>Provides superior acid control compared to racemic PPIs (e.g., omeprazole).</li></ul><p><strong>Excretion</strong></p><ul><li>Metabolized in the liver, primarily excreted as inactive metabolites in urine (80%) and feces (20%).</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '182_1733768826.jpg', 4, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 23:27:06', '2024-12-09 23:27:06'),
(104, 'Esoral MUPS', 'Esomeprazole Magnesium Trihydrate', 10.00, 12, 'MUPS Tablet', '12 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '20 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li>Treat GERD symptoms (e.g., heartburn) and erosive esophagitis.</li><li>Maintain healing of erosive esophagitis.</li><li>Eradicate <em>Helicobacter pylori</em> in duodenal ulcers (with amoxicillin &amp; clarithromycin).</li><li>Treat Zollinger-Ellison syndrome, acid dyspepsia, and gastric/duodenal ulcers.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Erosive Esophagitis (Healing)</strong>: 20-40 mg daily for 4-8 weeks; extend if needed.</li><li><strong>Maintenance</strong>: 20 mg daily for up to 6 months.</li><li><strong>Symptomatic GERD</strong>: 20 mg daily for 4-8 weeks.</li><li><strong>H. pylori Eradication</strong>: 40 mg daily + amoxicillin 1000 mg + clarithromycin 500 mg, twice daily for 10 days.</li><li><strong>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome</strong>: 20-80 mg daily, individualized.</li><li><strong>Acid-related Dyspepsia</strong>: 20-40 mg daily for 2-4 weeks.</li><li><strong>Gastric/Duodenal Ulcers</strong>: 20-40 mg daily for 2-8 weeks.</li><li><strong>Injection</strong>: 40 mg via IV daily (over 3-30 minutes). Switch to oral as soon as possible.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong></p><ul><li>Take 1 hour before meals.</li><li>Capsules can be opened and mixed with soft applesauce if needed.</li><li>IV injections should be prepared with 5 mL WFI and used within 12 hours.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>Metabolized by CYP2C19 and CYP3A4.</li><li>May reduce absorption of drugs dependent on gastric pH (e.g., ketoconazole, digoxin).</li><li>Minimal interaction with phenytoin, warfarin, amoxicillin, or clarithromycin.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Headache, diarrhea, nausea, abdominal pain, constipation, flatulence, dry mouth.</li><li>Rare: Hypersensitivity reactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Does not exclude stomach cancer diagnosis.</li><li>Avoid storing pellet-applesauce mixtures.</li><li>Safe antacid co-administration.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: Reduced motor activity, respiratory changes, tremors, or seizures.</li><li>No specific antidote; provide supportive care.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry place at ≤30°C, away from moisture and light. Keep out of children’s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy</strong>: Use with caution; breastfeeding should be stopped if necessary.</li><li><strong>Pediatrics</strong>: Safety not established.</li><li><strong>Geriatrics</strong>: No significant differences in response, but caution advised.</li><li><strong>Liver/Renal Impairment</strong>: Dose adjustment for severe hepatic impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Mechanism of Action</strong></p><p>Esomeprazole inhibits the H+/K+-ATPase (proton pump) in gastric parietal cells, reducing acid secretion. It has enhanced bioavailability and acid control compared to racemic proton pump inhibitors.</p>', 'active', '522_1733769032.jpg', 26, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 23:30:32', '2024-12-09 23:30:32'),
(105, 'M-Kast', 'Montelukast', 16.00, 14, 'Tablet', '14 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Asthma</strong>: Prophylaxis and chronic treatment.</li><li><strong>Exercise-Induced Bronchoconstriction (EIB)</strong>: Acute prevention.</li><li><strong>Allergic Rhinitis</strong>: Relief of seasonal and perennial symptoms.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li>A leukotriene receptor antagonist that selectively inhibits CysLT1, reducing airway inflammation and smooth muscle contraction.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults (≥15 years)</strong>: 10 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Pediatrics</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">6-14 years: 5 mg once daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">2-5 years: 4 mg once daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">6 months-2 years: 4 mg granules once daily.</li><li>No dosage adjustments needed for mild-to-moderate hepatic or renal impairment, or elderly patients.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common</strong>: Headache, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, upper respiratory infections.</li><li><strong>Rare</strong>: Hepatic issues, memory loss, hallucinations, suicidal thoughts.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Not for acute asthma attacks or as a substitute for corticosteroids.</li><li>Patients with aspirin sensitivity should avoid NSAIDs while on M-Kast.</li><li>Use with caution in pregnancy and lactation.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: Nausea, vomiting, hyperactivity, headache, stomach pain.</li><li>Treatment: Supportive care and clinical monitoring.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C in a cool, dry place. Keep out of children’s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Classified as Category B: Use only if clearly needed. May pass into breast milk; exercise caution in nursing mothers.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1847_1733769273.jpg', 9, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 23:34:33', '2024-12-09 23:34:33'),
(106, 'Neurobest', 'Vitamin B1 + B6 + B12', 10.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '100 mg+200 mg+200 mcg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li>Treatment of vitamin B1, B6, and B12 deficiency.</li><li>Supportive treatment for:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Neuritis</strong> &amp; non-inflammatory nerve diseases (e.g., diabetic neuropathy, peripheral neuralgia, sciatica, lumbago, myalgia, spinal pain).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Neuralgias</strong>: Facial, intercostal, optic.</li></ul><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tablet</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Vitamin B1: 100 mg</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Vitamin B6: 200 mg</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Vitamin B12: 200 mcg</li><li><strong>Injection</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Vitamin B1: 100 mg</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Vitamin B6: 100 mg</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Vitamin B12: 1000 mcg</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tablets</strong>: 1-3 tablets/day or as prescribed.</li><li><strong>Injection</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Severe cases: 1 ampoule daily intramuscularly until acute symptoms subside.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Mild cases: 1 ampoule 2-3 times weekly.</li><li><strong>Children</strong>: Use not established.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to ingredients.</li><li>Patients on <strong>levodopa</strong> therapy.</li><li>Cyanocobalamin not recommended for optic neuropathies with elevated cyanocobalamin levels.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Generally well-tolerated.</li><li>Rare: Allergic reactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid use of cyanocobalamin in spinal cord degeneration or optic neuropathies.</li><li>Injection not recommended during pregnancy or lactation due to benzyl alcohol.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Tablets: Safe at recommended doses.</li><li>Injection: Avoid due to benzyl alcohol.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 25°C, in a cool, dry place, protected from light. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><ul><li>Vitamins B1, B6, and B12 support:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Nerve metabolism and regeneration.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">RBC formation and cardiovascular health.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Neurological and energy-related functions.</li><li>Excess vitamins are excreted via urine.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose</strong></p><ul><li>No significant overdose symptoms at recommended doses. Supportive care if required.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '777_1733769431.png', 6, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 23:37:11', '2024-12-09 23:37:11'),
(107, 'Neobion', 'Vitamin B1 + B6 + B12', 12.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '100 mg+200 mg+200 mcg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li>Treatment of <strong>vitamin B1, B6, and B12 deficiency</strong>.</li><li>Supportive treatment for:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Neuritis</strong> &amp; non-inflammatory nerve diseases (e.g., diabetic neuropathy, peripheral neuralgia, spinal pain, sciatica, optic neuritis).</li></ul><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tablet</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Vitamin B1: 100 mg</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Vitamin B6: 200 mg</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Vitamin B12: 200 mcg</li><li><strong>Injection</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Vitamin B1: 100 mg</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Vitamin B6: 100 mg</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Vitamin B12: 1000 mcg</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tablets</strong>: 1-3 tablets daily or as prescribed.</li><li><strong>Injection</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Severe cases: 1 ampoule daily intramuscularly.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Mild cases: 1 ampoule 2-3 times weekly.</li><li><strong>Children</strong>: Use not established.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to ingredients.</li><li>Patients on <strong>levodopa</strong> therapy.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Generally well-tolerated; rare allergic reactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid cyanocobalamin in spinal cord degeneration or optic neuropathies.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Tablets: Safe at recommended doses.</li><li>Injection: Avoid due to benzyl alcohol content.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 25°C in a cool, dry place, protected from light. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Vitamin B1</strong>: Converts nutrients into energy, supports nerve health.</li><li><strong>Vitamin B6</strong>: Supports RBC formation, protein metabolism, and neurotransmitter synthesis.</li><li><strong>Vitamin B12</strong>: Essential for cell replication, anemia prevention, and nerve function.</li><li>Excess vitamins are excreted in urine.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose</strong></p><ul><li>No significant symptoms expected at recommended doses. Provide supportive care if necessary.</li></ul>', 'active', '398_1733769589.webp', 29, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 23:39:49', '2024-12-09 23:39:49'),
(108, 'Maxpro MUPS', 'Esomeprazole Magnesium Trihydrate', 10.00, 14, 'MUPS Tablet', '14 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '20 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li>Relief of <strong>GERD symptoms</strong> (e.g., persistent heartburn).</li><li>Treatment and maintenance of <strong>erosive esophagitis</strong>.</li><li><strong>Helicobacter pylori eradication</strong> (with amoxicillin &amp; clarithromycin).</li><li>Management of <strong>Zollinger-Ellison syndrome</strong>.</li><li>Treatment of <strong>acid-related dyspepsia</strong>, <strong>gastric ulcers</strong>, and <strong>duodenal ulcers</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Erosive Esophagitis</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Healing: 20-40 mg daily for 4-8 weeks.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Maintenance: 20 mg daily (up to 6 months).</li><li><strong>Symptomatic GERD</strong>: 20 mg daily for 4 weeks (extendable to 8 weeks).</li><li><strong>H. pylori eradication</strong>: 40 mg daily for 10 days (with antibiotics).</li><li><strong>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome</strong>: 20-80 mg daily; adjust based on need.</li><li><strong>Acid Dyspepsia</strong>: 20-40 mg daily for 2-4 weeks.</li><li><strong>Duodenal Ulcer</strong>: 20 mg daily for 2-4 weeks.</li><li><strong>Gastric Ulcer</strong>: 20-40 mg daily for 4-8 weeks.</li><li><strong>Injection</strong>: 40 mg IV once daily (administer over 3-30 minutes). Transition to oral therapy as soon as possible.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong></p><ul><li>Take orally 1 hour before meals.</li><li><strong>Suspension</strong>: Mix with 15 ml water, stir, and consume within 30 minutes.</li><li><strong>Nasogastric/Gastric Tube</strong>: Administer using a syringe with the suspension.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>Metabolized by <strong>CYP2C19</strong> and <strong>CYP3A4</strong>.</li><li>May affect absorption of <strong>pH-sensitive drugs</strong> (e.g., ketoconazole, digoxin).</li><li>Increases <strong>diazepam</strong> plasma levels; no significant interactions with most common medications.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Common: <strong>Headache</strong>, diarrhea, nausea, flatulence, abdominal pain, constipation, dry mouth.</li><li>Long-term use: No significant difference in side effects compared to short-term.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Does not rule out <strong>gastric cancer</strong>.</li><li>Capsules can be opened and mixed with applesauce for swallowing difficulty.</li><li>Do not chew or crush pellets.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to esomeprazole or its components.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: Decreased motor activity, tremors, ataxia.</li><li>Treatment: Supportive care; dialysis is ineffective due to protein binding.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Limited data on safety; avoid unless necessary.</li><li>Discontinue breastfeeding if esomeprazole is required.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C in a dry place, protected from light and moisture.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Esomeprazole</strong>: Proton pump inhibitor (PPI); suppresses stomach acid by inhibiting H+/K+-ATPase in gastric parietal cells.</li><li><strong>Absorption</strong>: Peaks 1.5 hours post-dose.</li><li><strong>Excretion</strong>: Mostly as inactive metabolites in urine and feces.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pediatrics</strong>: Safety not established.</li><li><strong>Elderly</strong>: Generally safe; monitor for sensitivity.</li><li><strong>Hepatic Impairment</strong>: Severe cases should not exceed 20 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Renal Impairment</strong>: No dosage adjustment needed.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1333_1733769784.jpg', 6, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 23:43:04', '2024-12-09 23:43:04'),
(109, 'D-Rise', 'Colecalciferol [Vitamin D3]', 20.00, 10, 'Capsule', '10 capsule in strip', 'Capsule', '20000 IU', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Treatment and prevention of Vitamin D3 deficiency.</li><li>Adjunct therapy for osteoporosis, osteomalacia, hypocalcaemia, tetany, and rickets.</li><li>Supports bone growth, density, and calcium/phosphorus absorption.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Vitamin in bone formation, Vitamin D preparations.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Treatment: 40,000 IU weekly for 7 weeks.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Maintenance: 1,400–2,000 IU/day.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Prevention: 20,000 IU every 4 weeks.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Osteoporosis: 20,000 IU monthly.</li><li><strong>Children (12-18 years):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Treatment: 20,000 IU every 2 weeks for 6 weeks.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Prevention: 20,000 IU every 6 weeks.</li><li><strong>Syrup:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For deficiency: 2,000 IU/day for 6 weeks.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Risk of deficiency: 400-600 IU/day based on age.</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction:</strong></p><ul><li>Interferes with phenytoin, barbiturates, glucocorticoids, and certain laxatives.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Vitamin D3.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypercalcaemia, hypercalciuria, rash, pruritus, nausea, abdominal pain.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Safe up to 4,000 IU during pregnancy.</li><li>Vitamin D3 is excreted in breast milk; caution with additional doses.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Use with caution in renal impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>May cause hypervitaminosis D.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30ºC, away from light and moisture.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations:</strong></p><ul><li>Safety in children under 12 years not established.</li></ul>', 'active', '56_1733770109.jpg', 3, 1, NULL, '2024-12-09 23:48:29', '2025-05-01 19:38:09'),
(110, 'Deflux', 'Domperidone Maleate', 4.00, 15, 'Tablet', '15 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indication:</strong></p><ul><li>Treats symptoms like epigastric fullness, abdominal distension, upper abdominal pain, belching, flatulence, early satiety, nausea, vomiting, and heartburn due to delayed gastric emptying, gastroesophageal reflux, and esophagitis.</li><li>Used in non-ulcer dyspepsia, nausea and vomiting from various causes, Parkinson\'s disease, and in radiological studies to speed up barium transit.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Motility Stimulants, Prokinetic drugs</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li>Acts as a dopamine receptor antagonist, promoting gastric motility without significant brain side effects due to limited blood-brain barrier penetration.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults:</strong> 10-20 mg every 4-8 hours (max 80 mg/day).</li><li><strong>Children:</strong> 0.2-0.4 mg/kg every 4-8 hours.</li><li>For acute nausea/vomiting: 20 mg every 6-8 hours.</li><li>Administer 15-30 minutes before meals.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid with anticholinergics, antacids, antisecretory drugs, and CYP3A4 inhibitors (e.g., azole antifungals, macrolides).</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Domperidone, gastrointestinal hemorrhage, obstruction, perforation, and prolactinoma.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Rare: intestinal cramps, extrapyramidal symptoms (especially in children), hyperprolactinemia (e.g., galactorrhea, gynecomastia).</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Not recommended during pregnancy. Minimal excretion in breast milk.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Use cautiously in children, hepatic impairment, and kidney disorders.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose:</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: drowsiness, disorientation, extrapyramidal reactions. Treat with activated charcoal.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture, and out of children\'s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Increases gastrointestinal motility and reduces regurgitation by inhibiting dopamine receptors in the stomach and chemoreceptor trigger zone (CTZ).</li></ul>', 'active', '545_1733772244.jpg', 3, 1, NULL, '2024-12-10 00:24:04', '2024-12-10 00:29:52');
INSERT INTO `products` (`id`, `productName`, `genericName`, `retail_max_price`, `cart_qty_inc`, `cart_text`, `unit_in_pack`, `type`, `quantity`, `prescription`, `feature`, `description`, `status`, `coverImage`, `company_id`, `category_id`, `add_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(111, 'Gavisol', 'Sodium Alginate + Sodium Bicarbonate + Calcium Carbonate', 250.00, 1, 'x 200 ml bottle', '1 Oral Suspension Bottle', 'Suspension', '(500 mg+267 mg+160 mg)/10 ml', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indication:</strong></p><ul><li>Treats gastric reflux, heartburn, flatulence from reflux, heartburn during pregnancy, and epigastric discomfort caused by reflux.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Antacids</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li>Forms a protective gel raft with alginic acid that floats on stomach contents, preventing reflux for up to 4 hours. It neutralizes gastric acid with calcium carbonate and sodium bicarbonate.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults &amp; children over 12:</strong> 10-20 mL after meals and at bedtime (up to 4 times a day).</li><li><strong>Children 6-12 years:</strong> 5-10 mL after meals and at bedtime (up to 4 times a day).</li><li><strong>Children under 6:</strong> Not recommended.</li><li>No dose adjustment needed for elderly or hepatic impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>Take Gavisol 2 hours apart from tetracyclines, digoxin, fluoroquinolones, iron salts, and other medications like beta-blockers and glucocorticoids.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Do not use in patients with hypersensitivity to ingredients.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Possible constipation, flatulence, stomach cramps, or belching. Overdose may cause abdominal distension.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Safe during pregnancy and breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Contains sodium and calcium carbonate; caution in patients with heart failure, renal impairment, hypercalcemia, or kidney stones.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose:</strong></p><ul><li>Symptomatic treatment, may cause abdominal distension.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, away from light, and out of children\'s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Forms a gel raft that neutralizes gastric acid and protects the esophagus from reflux, acid, pepsin, and bile.</li></ul>', 'active', '1971_1733772547.webp', 30, 1, NULL, '2024-12-10 00:29:07', '2025-04-22 17:53:20'),
(112, 'Antazol', 'Xylometazoline', 20.00, 1, 'x 15 ml drop', '15 ml drop', 'Nasal Drop', '0.1%', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications of Antazol 0.1%:</strong></p><ul><li>Symptomatic relief of nasal congestion, perennial allergic rhinitis (hay fever), and sinusitis.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Nasal Anti-histamine</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li>A sympathomimetic agent with alpha-adrenergic activity. It constricts nasal blood vessels, reducing congestion and improving nasal breathing. Effects begin within minutes and last for hours. It does not impair ciliary function, though systemic absorption may occur.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults:</strong> 2-3 drops (0.1%) 2-3 times daily.</li><li><strong>Children under 12:</strong> 1-2 drops (0.05%) once or twice daily.</li><li><strong>Infants under 3 months:</strong> Not recommended.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>No reported drug interactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Not for use in patients with trans-sphenoidal hypophysectomy or dura mater exposure, or those hypersensitive to Antazol 0.1%.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Occasional burning sensation, local irritation, nausea, headache, dryness of nasal mucosa, and cardiovascular effects (caution in cardiovascular disease).</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Use with caution during pregnancy due to potential vasoconstrictor effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Do not use for more than seven consecutive days; use the bottle for only one person to avoid cross-infection.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Protect from heat; discard after 28 days of opening.</li></ul>', 'active', '1145_1733772843.webp', 4, 1, NULL, '2024-12-10 00:34:03', '2025-04-30 14:44:31'),
(113, 'GlucoLeader Enhance Blue Test', 'Blood Glucose Test Strips', 412.00, 1, 'Box', '25\'s strip in a box', 'Surgical', '25\'s test strip', 'no', 'no', '<p>GlucoLeader Enhance Blue Test Strip 25 Strip<span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\"> are used with Bionime blood glucose meters to measure blood sugar levels.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Key Benefits:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Easy to hold</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Simple to use</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">No contamination</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Reliable accuracy</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Advanced Strip Design</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Short Test Pathway</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Auto-Coding&nbsp;</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Read the manual carefully before use</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Keep out of reach of children</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Dispose of used batteries properly</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Prevent water from entering the meter.&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Never immerse the meter or hold it under running water.</span></li></ul>', 'active', '1428_1733834096.jpg', 25, 5, NULL, '2024-12-10 17:34:56', '2024-12-11 11:32:31'),
(114, 'Blood Lancets (Mediron)', 'Needle', 120.00, 1, 'Box', '100\'s strip', 'Surgical', '100\'s twist type', 'no', 'no', '<p><strong>Blood Lancets (Mediron) 100</strong> are commonly used for blood sample collection and are designed to minimize discomfort. These lancets feature a sharp surgical steel tip encased in plastic, specifically designed to gently puncture the skin, often at the fingertip. The primary purpose of <strong>Blood Lancets (Mediron) 100</strong> is to create a precise puncture to collect blood samples for diagnostic testing.</p><p><strong>How to Use Blood Lancets (Mediron) 100:</strong></p><ol><li>Insert the lancet into the lancing device.</li><li>Carefully remove the protective cap by twisting it off.</li><li>Gently press the lancet to the skin to draw blood.</li><li>Apply the blood sample to the test strip for analysis.</li><li>Safely dispose of the used lancet in a proper disposal container.</li></ol><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Do not reuse</strong> the lancets.</li><li>Always use a fresh <strong>Blood Lancet (Mediron) 100</strong> for each blood sample collection.</li><li>Dispose of used lancets in a safe manner.</li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li><li>Store the lancets in a cool, dry place, away from direct sunlight.</li></ul>', 'active', '524_1733834524.png', 25, 5, NULL, '2024-12-10 17:42:04', '2024-12-11 11:33:03'),
(115, 'Bionime Rightest Test Strip', 'Blood Glucose Test Strips', 655.00, 1, 'x 25\'s strip box', '25\'s strip in a box', 'Surgical', 'GS700S', 'no', 'no', '<p><strong>Bionime Rightest Test Strips GS700S</strong> are designed for use with Bionime blood glucose meters to accurately measure blood glucose levels.</p><p><strong>Key Benefits:</strong></p><ul><li>Ergonomic design for easy handling</li><li>Simple to use for quick testing</li><li>Prevents contamination for accurate results</li><li>Provides reliable and consistent accuracy</li><li>Advanced design for efficient testing</li><li>Short testing pathway for fast results</li><li>Auto-coding for convenience</li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Carefully read the user manual before use.</li><li>Keep the test strips and meter out of the reach of children.</li><li>Dispose of used test strips and batteries in a safe and proper manner.</li><li>Ensure the meter remains dry; avoid exposure to water.</li><li>Never immerse the meter or place it under running water.</li></ul>', 'active', '227_1733834807.jpg', 25, 5, NULL, '2024-12-10 17:46:47', '2024-12-14 22:03:04'),
(116, 'NeoCare Baby Wipes', 'Wipes', 235.00, 1, 'Box', '120\'s wipes pack', 'Wipes', '120 wipes', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>NeoCare Baby Wipes 120</strong> are designed to provide a gentle yet effective cleaning solution for babies. These wipes are crafted from soft, absorbent materials that help cleanse and moisturize sensitive skin, while reducing the risk of irritation. They are also hypoallergenic and dermatologically tested, giving parents confidence in their safety.</p><p><strong>How to Use NeoCare Baby Wipes 120:</strong></p><ol><li>Open the container to retrieve a wipe.</li><li>Gently use the wipe to clean the desired area.</li><li>Dispose of the used wipe in the trash.</li><li>Close the container securely.</li></ol><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Always read the label before use.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Disposal Instructions:</strong></p><ul><li>Dispose of the wipes in the trash.</li><li>Do not flush the wipes down the toilet.</li><li>Do not place the wipes in recycling or compost bins.</li></ul>', 'active', '1319_1733835973.png', 2, 6, NULL, '2024-12-10 18:04:59', '2024-12-11 11:39:21'),
(117, 'Neocare(New Born)', 'Diaper', 640.00, 1, 'Pack', '20\'s in a box', 'Diaper', '20\'s pack', 'no', 'yes', '<p>Neocare NewBorn is designed with your baby’s comfort and health in mind. Made from soft, breathable materials, it ensures optimal comfort while keeping your baby’s skin dry and fresh. The product also features a secure fit that helps prevent leaks and provides a reliable barrier throughout the day. With easy-to-use fasteners and a convenient wetness indicator, it’s easy to know when your baby needs a change.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions:</strong></p><ol><li>Open the Neocare NewBorn and place it under your baby.</li><li>Ensure it fits snugly but comfortably—not too tight.</li><li>If your baby has soiled the diaper, clean the area with wipes and apply Neocare NewBorn cream if needed.</li><li>Close the diaper and fasten the tabs securely.</li><li>Properly dispose of the used diaper.</li></ol><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong></p><p>Store Neocare NewBorns at room temperature (20–25°C or 68–77°F). Avoid direct sunlight and heat, as these conditions may cause the diapers to become dry or brittle.</p><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Change the diaper frequently, particularly after wetting or soiling.</li><li>Avoid leaving a soiled diaper on your baby for extended periods.</li><li>Do not flush used diapers down the toilet.</li><li>Keep the diapers out of children\'s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>Disposal Instructions:</strong></p><ul><li>Dispose of used Neocare NewBorns in a sealed bag or container.</li><li>Place the sealed bag in the trash for proper disposal.</li></ul>', 'active', '1848_1733841448.webp', 2, 6, NULL, '2024-12-10 19:37:28', '2024-12-11 11:40:03'),
(118, 'Thai Wet Wipes For Baby Moist Tissue', 'Wipes', 120.00, 1, 'Jar', '120\'s in a jar', 'Wipes', '120\'s  piece', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Thai Wet Wipes for Baby Moist Tissue</strong> are a trusted option for parents seeking a gentle and effective way to clean their baby\'s sensitive skin. Made from soft, absorbent materials, these wipes clean and moisturize without causing irritation. They are hypoallergenic and dermatologically tested, offering reassurance for parents concerned about skin sensitivities.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions:</strong></p><ol><li>Open the wipe container and take out a wipe.</li><li>Use the wipe to gently clean the necessary area on your baby.</li><li>After use, dispose of the wipe in the trash.</li><li>Close the container to maintain freshness.</li></ol><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Always read the label before use.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Disposal Instructions:</strong></p><ul><li>Dispose of used wipes in the trash.</li><li>Do not flush the wipes down the toilet.</li><li>Avoid placing the wipes in recycling bins or compost piles.</li></ul>', 'active', '1854_1733842012.jpg', 35, 6, NULL, '2024-12-10 19:46:52', '2024-12-10 19:51:12'),
(119, 'Savlon Baby Wipes', 'Wipes', 265.00, 1, 'Jar', '160\'s wipes in a jar', 'Wipes', '160\'s wipes', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Savlon Baby Wipes 160</strong> are a popular choice for parents who want a gentle and effective way to clean their baby’s delicate skin. These wipes are made from soft and absorbent materials that cleanse and moisturize without causing irritation. Hypoallergenic and dermatologically tested, they provide reassurance to parents concerned about their baby’s sensitive skin.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions:</strong></p><ol><li>Open the container and pull out a wipe.</li><li>Gently use the wipe to clean the desired area.</li><li>Dispose of the used wipe in the trash.</li><li>Close the container securely to preserve the wipes.</li></ol><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Always read the label before use.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Disposal Instructions:</strong></p><ul><li>Dispose of used Savlon Baby Wipes 160 in the trash.</li><li>Do not flush them down the toilet.</li><li>Avoid placing the wipes in recycling bins or compost piles.</li></ul>', 'active', '1655_1733842487.jpg', 14, 6, NULL, '2024-12-10 19:54:47', '2024-12-10 19:54:47'),
(120, 'Baby Cotton Buds', 'Baby Cotton Buds', 100.00, 1, 'Jar', '200\'s in a box', 'Wipes', '200 piece', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Baby Cotton Buds 200 pc</strong> are a safe and gentle option for cleaning your baby’s delicate areas, such as their ears, nose, and outer ear. Made with 100% pure cotton tips, these buds are naturally soft and absorbent. The paper sticks are designed for sensitive skin, ensuring safe and comfortable use.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions:</strong></p><ol><li>Moisten the cotton bud with fresh water.</li><li>Gently wipe the outer ear or nose area.</li><li><strong>Do not insert the cotton bud into the ear canal.</strong></li></ol><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Do not insert cotton buds into the ear canal.</strong></li><li>Only clean the outer ear or visible areas.</li><li>Be gentle when using the cotton bud; avoid scrubbing or twisting.</li><li>Do not use cotton buds if your baby has cuts or abrasions on the ear.</li><li>Always keep cotton buds out of the reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Disposal Instructions:</strong></p><ul><li>Dispose of used Baby Cotton Buds 200 pc in the trash.</li><li><strong>Do not</strong> place used cotton buds in recycling bins or compost piles.</li></ul>', 'active', '1675_1733844501.png', 25, 6, NULL, '2024-12-10 20:28:21', '2024-12-10 20:30:30'),
(121, 'Ecosprin', 'Aspirin', 0.80, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '75 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications of Ecosprin 75 mg:</strong></p><p>Ecosprin 75 mg is commonly used for the following conditions:</p><ul><li><strong>Prophylaxis against arterial occlusive events</strong>: Including myocardial infarction, myocardial re-infarction, post-bypass surgery, acute ischemic stroke, and transient ischemic attack (TIA).</li><li><strong>Mild to moderate pain</strong>: Such as headache, muscle pain, dysmenorrhea, and toothache.</li><li><strong>Chronic diseases with pain and inflammation</strong>: Like osteoarthritis.</li><li><strong>Antipyretic</strong>: Used for fever due to cold and influenza.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Anti-platelet drugs</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong> Ecosprin 75 mg works by reducing platelet aggregation, which prevents the formation of thrombi (blood clots) in the arteries. This is important because thrombi form through platelet aggregation, and anticoagulants are less effective in these areas. It is also an analgesic, ideal for headache, musculoskeletal pain, and dysmenorrhea. With its anti-inflammatory and antipyretic properties, Ecosprin is beneficial in treating inflammation and fever. The enteric coating of Ecosprin reduces gastrointestinal side effects, such as disturbance and ulceration.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>For pain, inflammatory diseases, and as an antipyretic</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">300 mg (1-3 tablets) every 6 hours, with a maximum daily dose of 4 g.</li><li><strong>For thrombotic cerebrovascular or cardiovascular disease</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">75 mg (1 tablet) to 300 mg (4 tablets) daily.</li><li><strong>After myocardial infarction</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">75 mg (2 tablets) daily for 1 month.</li><li><strong>Following bypass surgery</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">75 mg (1 tablet) daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>Salicylates may enhance the effects of anticoagulants, oral hypoglycemic agents, phenytoin, and sodium valproate.</li><li>They can inhibit the uricosuric effect of probenecid and increase the toxicity of sulfonamides.</li><li>May trigger bronchospasm or asthma attacks in susceptible individuals.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Contraindicated in children under 12 years (due to the risk of Reye\'s syndrome).</li><li>Not recommended during breastfeeding.</li><li>Should be avoided in cases of active peptic ulcer, bleeding disorders (e.g., hemophilia, intracranial hemorrhage), and other ulcerations.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Generally mild, including nausea, dyspepsia, gastrointestinal ulceration, and bronchospasm.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Use cautiously in patients with asthma, uncontrolled blood pressure, and during pregnancy.</li><li>Careful administration is advised for patients with nasal polyps or allergies.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms of overdose may include dizziness, tinnitus, sweating, nausea, vomiting, confusion, and hyperventilation.</li><li>Severe overdose may lead to CNS depression, cardiovascular collapse, and respiratory depression.</li><li>Treatment includes gastric lavage, forced alkaline diuresis, and in severe cases, hemodialysis.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong></p><ul><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li><li>Store in a cool, dry place, away from light.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Classes:</strong></p><ul><li>Anti-platelet drugs</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong> Ecosprin 75 mg prevents thrombus formation by inhibiting platelet aggregation. This is critical in treating and preventing cardiovascular events. It is effective for various pain and inflammation conditions due to its analgesic, anti-inflammatory, and antipyretic effects.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy:</strong></p><ul><li>Ecosprin 75 mg should be avoided during the last trimester of pregnancy unless specifically prescribed by a doctor, as it may harm the unborn child or cause complications during delivery.</li></ul><p><strong>Breastfeeding:</strong></p><ul><li>Ecosprin can pass into breast milk and should be used cautiously in nursing mothers.</li></ul>', 'active', '956_1733845444.jpg', 5, 12, NULL, '2024-12-10 20:44:04', '2024-12-10 20:58:51'),
(122, 'Atova', 'Atorvastatin Calcium', 12.00, 15, 'Tablet', '15 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '10mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Atova 10 mg Overview</strong></p><p>Atova 10 mg contains atorvastatin, a medication in the statin class, primarily used to manage cholesterol levels and reduce the risk of cardiovascular events. It works by selectively inhibiting HMG-CoA reductase, the enzyme responsible for cholesterol synthesis in the liver, thereby lowering total and LDL cholesterol while increasing the removal of cholesterol from the bloodstream.</p><p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Primary hypercholesterolemia and mixed dyslipidemia</strong>: Reduces elevated total cholesterol, LDL cholesterol, Apo-B, and triglycerides.</li><li><strong>Familial hypercholesterolemia</strong>: Effective for both heterozygous and homozygous cases.</li><li><strong>Hypertriglyceridemia</strong>: Used in patients with elevated triglycerides (Fredrickson Type IV).</li><li><strong>Dysbetalipoproteinemia</strong>: Treats elevated cholesterol and triglycerides in Fredrickson Type III.</li><li><strong>Cardiovascular prevention</strong>: Reduces ischemic events in patients with coronary artery disease and high LDL cholesterol.</li><li><strong>Diabetes-related hypercholesterolemia</strong>: Reduces cholesterol in hypercholesterolemia associated with diabetes or renal transplantation.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults</strong>: Start with 10 mg once daily; adjust dose at 4-week intervals up to a maximum of 80 mg/day based on response.</li><li><strong>Children (10-18 years)</strong>: Start with 10 mg daily; titrate to a usual maximum of 20 mg/day, or up to 80 mg/day in familial hypercholesterolemia.</li><li><strong>Special populations</strong>: Caution in elderly and hepatic-impaired patients.</li></ul><p><strong>Common Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Gastrointestinal: Constipation, dyspepsia, flatulence, abdominal pain.</li><li>Musculoskeletal: Myalgia, arthralgia, back pain.</li><li>General: Headache, rash, weakness.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Liver function</strong>: Monitor liver enzymes before and during therapy. Discontinue if marked elevations occur.</li><li><strong>Myopathy risk</strong>: Increased with concurrent use of drugs like cyclosporine, fibrates, and azole antifungals.</li><li><strong>Pregnancy and breastfeeding</strong>: Contraindicated due to potential risks to the fetus and infant.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Increased risk of myopathy</strong>: Cyclosporine, erythromycin, niacin, and azole antifungals.</li><li><strong>No significant interactions</strong>: Antihypertensives or hypoglycemic agents.</li><li><strong>Close monitoring</strong>: Required when used with digoxin, oral contraceptives, and warfarin.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><p>Store in a cool, dry place away from light and heat. Keep out of reach of children.</p><p><strong>Key Notes</strong></p><ul><li>For optimal results, use as an adjunct to diet and lifestyle changes.</li><li>Avoid alcohol consumption to reduce liver toxicity risk.</li><li>Consult your doctor immediately if unexplained muscle pain, weakness, or symptoms of liver dysfunction occur.</li></ul>', 'active', '1613_1733854467.jpg', 3, 12, NULL, '2024-12-10 23:14:27', '2024-12-10 23:17:13'),
(123, 'Linaglip', 'Linagliptin', 22.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '5mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications for Linagliptin 5 mg</strong></p><p>Linagliptin 5 mg is prescribed for adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus to enhance glycaemic control:</p><ul><li><strong>Monotherapy</strong>: Suitable for patients unable to manage glycemic levels with diet and exercise alone and for whom metformin is contraindicated due to renal impairment or intolerance.</li><li><strong>Combination Therapy</strong>: Used alongside metformin or other medications (e.g., sulphonylureas) when diet, exercise, and single-agent therapy fail to achieve adequate glycaemic control.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Linagliptin belongs to the <strong>Dipeptidyl Peptidase-4 (DPP-4) Inhibitor</strong> class.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Linagliptin improves glycemic management by targeting the incretin system:</p><p>Linagliptin improves glycemic management by targeting the incretin system:</p><ul><li>Inhibits <strong>DPP-4 enzyme</strong>, preventing the breakdown of incretin hormones GLP-1 (glucagon-like peptide-1) and GIP (glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide).</li><li>Increases active incretin levels, enhancing glucose-dependent insulin secretion and reducing glucagon release.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Standard Dose</strong>: 5 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Combination Therapy</strong>: Dosage should remain consistent with metformin. Adjust sulfonylurea dose as needed to minimize hypoglycemia risk.</li><li><strong>Renal Impairment</strong>: No dose adjustment is required.</li><li><strong>Food</strong>: Can be taken with or without food, at any time of the day.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>Minimal interaction with other drugs, including metformin, glyburide, simvastatin, warfarin, digoxin, and oral contraceptives.</li><li>Weak inhibitor of CYP3A4, with limited potential for clinically meaningful interactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Known hypersensitivity to linagliptin or any of its ingredients.</li></ul><p><strong>Possible Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common</strong>: Nasopharyngitis, cough.</li><li><strong>Serious</strong>: Hypoglycemia (when combined with sulfonylureas or insulin), pancreatitis.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy Category B</strong>: Limited studies in pregnant women. Use only if clearly needed.</li><li>Unknown whether it is excreted in human breast milk; caution is advised.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions and Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Monitor for hypersensitivity reactions.</li><li>Exercise caution in patients with a history of pancreatitis.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry place, protected from heat and light.</li><li>Keep out of the reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Class and Mechanism</strong></p><p><strong>Class</strong>: Dipeptidyl Peptidase-4 (DPP-4) Inhibitor</p><p><strong>Mechanism</strong>: Enhances glucose-dependent insulin secretion while inhibiting glucagon release, thus improving glycemic control.</p>', 'active', '1083_1733896492.png', 29, 12, NULL, '2024-12-10 23:29:29', '2024-12-11 10:54:52'),
(124, 'Bizoran', 'Amlodipine + Olmesartan Medoxomil', 12.00, 15, 'Tablet', '15 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '5 mg+20 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p>Bizoran 5 mg+20 mg is a combination medication used primarily to treat high blood pressure (hypertension). It combines <strong>amlodipine</strong>, a calcium channel blocker, and <strong>olmesartan</strong>, an angiotensin II receptor blocker (ARB). These two components work synergistically to lower blood pressure and reduce associated risks like heart attack and stroke.</p><p><strong>Key Features of Bizoran 5 mg+20 mg:</strong></p><h4><strong>How it Works:</strong></h4><ul><li><strong>Amlodipine</strong>: Relaxes blood vessel walls by inhibiting calcium influx, thereby lowering vascular resistance.</li><li><strong>Olmesartan</strong>: Blocks angiotensin II from narrowing blood vessels, helping them relax and reducing blood pressure.</li></ul><h4><strong>Indications:</strong></h4><ul><li>Primary therapy for hypertension.</li><li>Suitable for individuals who may require multiple antihypertensive drugs to meet their blood pressure goals.</li><li>Can be used as an add-on or replacement therapy for patients inadequately controlled with monotherapy.</li></ul><h4><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></h4><ul><li><strong>Starting dose</strong>: One tablet daily (5/20 mg).</li><li><strong>Maximum dose</strong>: Two tablets daily (10/40 mg), adjusted based on the response.</li><li>Can be taken with or without food.</li><li>Not recommended as an initial therapy for individuals aged 75 or older or those with significant liver impairment.</li></ul><h4><strong>Side Effects:</strong></h4><p>Common side effects include:</p><ul><li>Dizziness</li><li>Edema (swelling)</li><li>Flushing</li><li>Palpitations Less common effects may include nausea, diarrhea, skin reactions (rash, itching), and muscle pain.</li></ul><h4><strong>Precautions:</strong></h4><ul><li>Should be avoided during pregnancy and breastfeeding due to potential risks to the fetus and infant.</li><li>Patients with pre-existing kidney, liver, or heart conditions should use this medication cautiously.</li><li>May cause hypotension in individuals with low sodium or fluid levels.</li><li>Discontinue immediately if pregnancy is detected.</li></ul><h4><strong>Storage Instructions:</strong></h4><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place below 30°C.</li><li>Keep away from light, moisture, and out of children’s reach.</li></ul><h4><strong>Consultation Advice:</strong></h4><ul><li>Always take Bizoran as prescribed by a healthcare provider.</li><li>Inform your doctor about any existing medical conditions or other medications to avoid interactions.</li><li>Regular blood pressure monitoring is essential to evaluate the effectiveness of the treatment.</li></ul><p>This information provides a concise summary of Bizoran 5 mg+20 mg without infringing on proprietary descriptions or copyrights. Always consult healthcare professionals for personalized medical advice.</p>', 'active', '1404_1733856100.png', 3, 12, NULL, '2024-12-10 23:41:40', '2024-12-10 23:41:40'),
(125, 'Thyrox', 'Levothyroxine Sodium', 2.20, 30, 'Tablet', '30 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '50 mcg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications of Thyrox 50 mcg</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Replacement Therapy:</strong> Used to treat hypothyroidism regardless of cause. Not recommended for transient hypothyroidism during subacute thyroiditis recovery.</li><li><strong>TSH Suppression:</strong> Employed to suppress thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) levels in goiters, thyroid nodules, or following thyroid cancer treatment.</li><li><strong>Diagnostic Aid:</strong> Utilized in thyroid suppression tests.</li><li><strong>Goitrogenic Drug Effects:</strong> Counteracts goitrogenic effects from drugs like lithium.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Thyroid drugs and hormones.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li>Contains synthetic <strong>Levothyroxine (T4)</strong>, identical to the natural hormone produced by the thyroid gland.</li><li>A portion (30%) of T4 converts to <strong>Triiodothyronine (T3)</strong>, the more biologically active hormone.</li><li>Thyroxine Binding Globulin (TBG) protects T4 from metabolism, ensuring a long half-life (6–7 days).</li><li>Conditions like hyperthyroidism, hypothyroidism, or protein deficiencies affect T4\'s half-life.</li><li>The liver degrades thyroid hormones, excreting them via urine and undergoing enterohepatic circulation.</li><li>Consistent T3 levels are achieved with a single daily dose of Levothyroxine.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults:</strong> Start with 25–50 mcg/day, increasing gradually every 6–8 weeks. Severe hypothyroidism starts at 12.5–25 mcg/day with 2–4-week adjustments.</li><li><strong>Children:</strong> Dosage varies by age and weight (e.g., 10–15 mcg/kg/day for newborns). Increase doses as needed based on clinical/laboratory results.</li><li><strong>Elderly/Heart Disease Patients:</strong> Start with lower doses (1.7 mcg/kg/day).</li><li><strong>TSH Suppression:</strong> A dosage of 2.6 mcg/kg/day is typically sufficient.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Antidepressants:</strong> May enhance therapeutic/toxic effects.</li><li><strong>Sertraline:</strong> Can increase Levothyroxine requirements.</li><li><strong>Antidiabetic Drugs:</strong> Dosage adjustments might be necessary.</li><li><strong>Digitalis Glycosides:</strong> Therapeutic effects may be diminished.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Untreated thyrotoxicosis.</li><li>Acute myocardial infarction.</li><li>Uncorrected adrenal insufficiency.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms of overdose or hyperthyroidism: fatigue, weight loss, nervousness, palpitations, tremors, and gastrointestinal distress.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Safe during pregnancy (Category A).</li><li>Minimal excretion in breast milk, but dosage adjustments may be required.</li></ul><p><strong>Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Correct adrenal insufficiency before treatment.</li><li>Adjust dosage cautiously in cardiovascular patients.</li><li>Monitor TSH and T3/T4 levels for efficacy.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C in a dry, dark place, away from children.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '176_1733856628.jpg', 6, 12, NULL, '2024-12-10 23:50:28', '2024-12-10 23:50:28'),
(126, 'Rosuva', 'Rosuvastatin', 22.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><br></p><p><strong>Indications for Rosuva 10 mg</strong></p><p>Rosuva 10 mg is indicated for managing the following conditions:</p><ul><li><strong>Heterozygous Hypercholesterolemia</strong>: Both familial and non-familial forms.</li><li><strong>Homozygous Familial Hypercholesterolemia</strong>.</li><li><strong>Mixed Dyslipidemia</strong>: Fredrickson Types IIa and IIb.</li><li><strong>Primary Prevention of Cardiovascular Disease</strong>: For reducing cardiovascular risks.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Statins</strong>: Lipid-lowering agents.</li><li><strong>Anti-anginal and Anti-ischemic Drugs</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Rosuva 10 mg inhibits <strong>HMG-CoA reductase</strong>, an enzyme critical in cholesterol synthesis. Its lipid-lowering effects involve:</p><ol><li><strong>Enhancing LDL receptor activity</strong> in the liver, promoting the clearance of LDL.</li><li><strong>Reducing VLDL production</strong>, lowering both VLDL and LDL levels.</li></ol><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>General Dose Range</strong>: 5-40 mg once daily. (Use 40 mg only for patients unresponsive to 20 mg.)</li><li><strong>Homozygous Familial Hypercholesterolemia (HoFH)</strong>: Start with 20 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Pediatric Patients</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For HeFH (ages 8-10): 5-10 mg/day.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For HeFH (ages 10-17): 5-20 mg/day.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For HoFH (ages 7-17): 20 mg/day.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong>: Can be taken with or without food, at any time of the day.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Cyclosporine</strong>: Dose should not exceed 5 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Gemfibrozil</strong>: If used, limit to 10 mg/day to reduce adverse effects.</li><li><strong>Lopinavir/Ritonavir or Atazanavir/Ritonavir</strong>: Limit dose to 10 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Coumarin Anticoagulants</strong>: Monitor INR closely when co-administered.</li><li><strong>Fibrates/Niacin</strong>: May increase the risk of muscle-related adverse effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to components.</li><li>Active liver disease or elevated hepatic transaminases.</li><li>Pregnancy and breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Common Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Headache</li><li>Muscle pain (myalgia)</li><li>Constipation</li><li>Fatigue (asthenia)</li><li>Abdominal pain</li><li>Nausea</li></ul><p><strong>Special Warnings and Precautions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Muscle Effects</strong>: Risk of myopathy and rhabdomyolysis increases with high doses, renal impairment, or concomitant use of certain drugs. Promptly report muscle pain or weakness.</li><li><strong>Liver Function Monitoring</strong>: Regularly check liver enzymes. Discontinue if persistent elevations occur.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy</strong>: Not recommended.</li><li><strong>Lactation</strong>: Unclear if excreted in breast milk; avoid use.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C.</li><li>Protect from light and moisture.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pediatric Use</strong>: Safety in children below 7 years is not established.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '119_1733857365.webp', 4, 12, NULL, '2024-12-11 00:02:45', '2024-12-11 00:02:45'),
(127, 'Uromax', 'Tamsulosin Hydrochloride', 12.00, 5, 'Capsule', '5 Capsul in a strip', 'Capsule', '0.4 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications of Uromax 0.4 mg</strong></p><p>Uromax 0.4 mg is prescribed for managing the symptoms of Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia (BPH).</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>BPH treatment/Urinary retention/Urinary incontinence.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Tamsulosin, the active ingredient in Uromax, selectively binds to α1A-adrenoreceptors in the prostate, blocking their activity. This reduces smooth muscle contraction in the prostate and urethra, promoting muscle relaxation and improved urinary flow.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li>Recommended dose: 0.4 mg once daily, taken about 30 minutes after the same meal each day.</li><li>If no improvement occurs after 2–4 weeks, the dose may be increased to 0.8 mg daily.</li><li>If the medication is interrupted for several days, restart with the 0.4 mg dose.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>Increased plasma concentration with strong CYP3A4 inhibitors (e.g., ketoconazole) or moderate CYP3A4 inhibitors (e.g., erythromycin).</li><li>Enhanced exposure with CYP2D6 inhibitors like paroxetine or terbinafine.</li><li>Elevated plasma levels with cimetidine.</li><li>Additive hypotensive effects with α-blockers or PDE5 inhibitors.</li><li>Decreased plasma concentration with furosemide.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>History of orthostatic hypotension.</li><li>Severe hepatic impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common side effects include:</p><ul><li>Dizziness, abnormal ejaculation.</li><li>Occasionally: Headache, fatigue, postural hypotension, palpitations, rhinitis, nausea, diarrhea, or constipation.</li><li>Rarely: Rash, pruritus, urticaria, drowsiness, blurred vision, or edema.</li><li>Very rare: Angioedema and priapism.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Not intended for use in women.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Not recommended for severe renal impairment (CrCl &lt;10 mL/min).</li><li>Monitor for symptoms of hypotension.</li><li>Avoid in pediatric populations.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Management</strong></p><p>Symptoms of overdose, such as hypotension, require cardiovascular support. Position the patient in a supine position to restore blood pressure. If necessary, administer intravenous fluids. Activated charcoal, gastric lavage, or osmotic laxatives may be considered for significant overdoses.</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Store at 20–25°C, away from direct sunlight and moisture.</p>', 'active', '1445_1733857749.webp', 8, 12, NULL, '2024-12-11 00:09:09', '2024-12-15 13:53:48'),
(128, 'Bislol', 'Bisoprolol Fumarate', 7.00, 14, 'Tablet', '14 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '2.5 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications for Bislol 2.5 mg</strong></p><ul><li>Hypertension</li><li>Angina</li><li>Moderate to severe heart failure</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Beta-adrenergic blockers (Beta-blockers)</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Bisoprolol Hemifumarate is a highly selective beta-1 adrenergic receptor blocker, primarily affecting the heart and vascular smooth muscle. It reduces heart rate and cardiac output, leading to decreased blood pressure. Unlike non-selective beta-blockers, it does not negatively impact lipid metabolism or HDL cholesterol during long-term therapy.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Hypertension</strong>: Starting dose is typically 5 mg once daily, which may be adjusted to 2.5 mg if necessary. Maximum dose: 20 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Angina</strong>: Usual dose is 10 mg once daily, with a maximum of 20 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Heart Failure</strong>: Begin with 1.25 mg once daily, increasing gradually (as tolerated) to a maximum of 10 mg daily, following a staged dose escalation schedule.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid combining bisoprolol with other beta-blockers.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Cardiogenic shock</li><li>Overt heart failure</li><li>Advanced A-V block (second or third degree)</li><li>Right ventricular failure due to pulmonary hypertension</li><li>Sinus bradycardia</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common side effects include:</p><ul><li>Gastrointestinal disturbances</li><li>Bradycardia</li><li>Hypotension</li><li>Fatigue</li><li>Dizziness</li><li>Headache</li><li>Sleep disturbances</li><li>Less common: vertigo, alopecia, thrombocytopenia, and visual disturbances.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Safety during pregnancy has not been established.</li><li>Limited data available on use during lactation; consult a physician.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Regular monitoring of renal, hepatic, and hematopoietic functions is recommended for long-term therapy.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry place, protected from light and heat.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p>Let me know if further adjustments are needed!</p>', 'active', '814_1733858088.webp', 7, 12, NULL, '2024-12-11 00:14:48', '2024-12-11 00:14:48'),
(129, 'Clopid', 'Clopidogrel Bisulphate', 12.05, 14, 'Tablet', '14 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '75 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications of Clopid 75 mg</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Acute Coronary Syndrome (ACS):</strong> Clopid 75 mg is used to reduce the risk of myocardial infarction (MI) and stroke in patients with non-ST-segment elevation ACS, including unstable angina (UA) or non-ST-elevation myocardial infarction (NSTEMI).</li><li><strong>Recent MI, Stroke, or Established Peripheral Arterial Disease:</strong> Indicated for reducing the risk of MI and stroke in patients with a history of recent MI, stroke, or peripheral arterial disease.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Anti-platelet drugs</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Clopidogrel is a prodrug that inhibits platelet activation and aggregation by irreversibly binding its active metabolite to P2Y12 ADP receptors on platelets. Its effects on platelet aggregation are dose-dependent and appear within 2 hours after administration, achieving a steady state between Day 3 and Day 7 when taken daily.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Acute Coronary Syndrome:</strong> Start with a 300 mg loading dose (4 tablets) followed by 75 mg once daily. Without a loading dose, the onset of antiplatelet action is delayed.</li><li><strong>Recent MI, Stroke, or Peripheral Arterial Disease:</strong> Take 75 mg once daily, with or without food.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Increased bleeding risk:</strong> Avoid concurrent use with NSAIDs, warfarin, SSRIs, and SNRIs.</li><li><strong>CYP2C19 inhibitors (omeprazole/esomeprazole):</strong> Avoid as they reduce clopidogrel activation.</li><li><strong>CYP2C8 substrates (e.g., repaglinide):</strong> Avoid due to increased plasma levels of repaglinide.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to clopidogrel or its components.</li><li>Active bleeding, such as peptic ulcer or intracranial hemorrhage.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common:</strong> Bleeding, diarrhea, gastrointestinal discomfort, hemorrhage, skin reactions.</li><li><strong>Rare:</strong> Acquired hemophilia, anemia, angioedema, arthritis, bone marrow disorders.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Metabolic Impairment:</strong> Genetic variations or CYP2C19 inhibitors may reduce effectiveness.</li><li><strong>Bleeding Risk:</strong> Platelet aggregation is inhibited for 7-10 days; caution in surgery or trauma. Discontinue 5 days before major surgery.</li><li><strong>Thrombotic Thrombocytopenic Purpura (TTP):</strong> Requires urgent treatment with plasmapheresis if detected.</li><li><strong>Hypersensitivity Reactions:</strong> Monitor for rash, angioedema, or hematologic issues.</li></ul><p><strong>Use During Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> Use only if clearly necessary due to limited data on safety.</li><li><strong>Lactation:</strong> Unknown if excreted in breast milk; weigh drug importance against breastfeeding benefits.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><p>Overdose may cause bleeding complications. Platelet transfusions may restore clotting ability.</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C in a dry place, protected from light.</li><li>Keep out of the reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pediatrics:</strong> Safety and efficacy not established.</li><li><strong>Elderly:</strong> No dosage adjustment required.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1589_1733859628.jpg', 9, 12, NULL, '2024-12-11 00:40:28', '2024-12-11 00:40:28');
INSERT INTO `products` (`id`, `productName`, `genericName`, `retail_max_price`, `cart_qty_inc`, `cart_text`, `unit_in_pack`, `type`, `quantity`, `prescription`, `feature`, `description`, `status`, `coverImage`, `company_id`, `category_id`, `add_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(130, 'Osartil', 'Losartan Potassium', 10.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '50 mg', 'yes', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p><strong>Hypertension:</strong> Osartil 50 mg is indicated for the management of hypertension. It can be administered as monotherapy or in combination with other antihypertensive agents, such as thiazide diuretics.</p><p><strong>Renal Protection in Type-2 Diabetic Patients with Proteinuria:</strong> For hypertensive patients with type 2 diabetes and proteinuria (urinary albumin-to-creatinine ratio exceeding 300 mg/g), Osartil 50 mg is recommended to delay the progression of renal disease.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Angiotensin II receptor blocker (ARB).</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Osartil 50 mg is an orally active, non-peptide angiotensin II receptor blocker. It selectively binds to the AT1 receptor found in tissues such as the heart, kidneys, adrenal glands, and vascular smooth muscle. By blocking this receptor, it inhibits processes like vasoconstriction and aldosterone production, both of which contribute to hypertension.</p><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>General Dosage:</strong> The initial and maintenance dose is typically 50 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Insufficient Response:</strong> If 50 mg does not provide adequate blood pressure control, the dose may be increased to 25 mg twice daily.</li><li><strong>Special Populations:</strong> For patients with intravascular volume depletion (e.g., those on high-dose diuretics), a starting dose of 25 mg once daily is advised.</li><li><strong>Daily Range:</strong> The total daily dose can range from 25 mg to 100 mg, administered in one or two divided doses.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Reduced Effect:</strong> Rifampicin and fluconazole may decrease levels of the active metabolite of Osartil.</li><li><strong>Potentiation:</strong> The combination of hydrochlorothiazide with Osartil may enhance antihypertensive effects.</li><li><strong>Potassium Levels:</strong> Potassium-sparing diuretics (e.g., spironolactone, triamterene), potassium supplements, or salt substitutes may increase serum potassium levels.</li><li><strong>NSAIDs:</strong> Non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (e.g., indomethacin) may reduce the antihypertensive effects of Osartil.</li><li><strong>Renal Risk:</strong> Concurrent use with ACE inhibitors, angiotensin receptor blockers, anti-inflammatory medications, and diuretics may raise the risk of renal impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any component of the medication.</li><li>Use during pregnancy (especially the second and third trimesters).</li><li>Combination with Aliskiren in patients with diabetes is contraindicated.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common side effects include dizziness, diarrhea, nasal congestion, cough, and upper respiratory tract infections. Less common side effects may include fatigue, edema, chest pain, nausea, headache, and pharyngitis.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> Osartil is categorized as Pregnancy Risk Category D. It poses potential risks to the fetus, particularly during the second and third trimesters.</li><li><strong>Lactation:</strong> As it is unclear whether Osartil is excreted in breast milk, a decision should be made to either discontinue breastfeeding or the medication, weighing its importance to the mother.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions and Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Use during the second or third trimesters of pregnancy can impair fetal renal function and increase neonatal morbidity and mortality.</li><li>Patients with intravascular volume depletion (e.g., those on diuretics) may experience symptomatic hypotension.</li><li>Plasma concentrations of Osartil may be elevated in patients with liver cirrhosis.</li><li>Renal function changes, including renal failure, have been reported in patients with renal impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Instructions</strong></p><p>Store in a cool, dry place, protected from heat and light. Keep out of the reach of children.</p><p><strong>Drug Class</strong></p><p>Angiotensin II receptor blocker (ARB).</p><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>Osartil 50 mg is a non-peptide, orally active angiotensin II receptor blocker. It binds selectively to AT1 receptors in tissues, inhibiting vasoconstriction and aldosterone release, which are primary contributors to hypertension.</p>', 'active', '1453_1733859991.webp', 2, 12, NULL, '2024-12-11 00:46:31', '2024-12-11 00:46:31'),
(131, 'Rosuva', 'Rosuvastatin', 12.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '5mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications for Rosuva 5 mg</strong></p><p>Rosuva 5 mg is prescribed for:</p><ul><li><strong>Heterozygous Hypercholesterolemia</strong> (both familial and non-familial forms)</li><li><strong>Homozygous Familial Hypercholesterolemia (HoFH)</strong></li><li><strong>Mixed Dyslipidemia</strong> (Fredrickson Type IIa and IIb)</li><li><strong>Primary Prevention of Cardiovascular Disease</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Classified under:</p><ul><li>Other Anti-anginal &amp; Anti-ischemic drugs</li><li>Statins</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Rosuva 5 mg works as a selective and competitive inhibitor of HMG-CoA reductase, the enzyme responsible for converting HMG-CoA to mevalonate, a cholesterol precursor. Its effects on lipid modification include:</p><ol><li>Increasing the number of LDL receptors in the liver to boost LDL uptake and breakdown.</li><li>Reducing hepatic production of VLDL, leading to a decrease in total LDL and VLDL particles.</li></ol><p><strong>Dosage Guidelines</strong></p><ul><li>General dose range: <strong>5-40 mg once daily.</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Use the 40 mg dose only for patients not achieving LDL-C goals with 20 mg.</li><li><strong>HoFH</strong>: Start with 20 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Pediatric Patients with HeFH</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ages 8 to &lt;10 years: 5-10 mg/day.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ages 10-17 years: 5-20 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Pediatric Patients with HoFH</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ages 7-17 years: 20 mg/day.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong></p><p>Rosuva 5 mg may be taken with or without food at any time of the day.</p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><p>Key interactions to note:</p><ul><li><strong>Cyclosporine</strong>: Increases exposure; limit dose to 5 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Gemfibrozil</strong>: Avoid if possible; if used, limit to 10 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Lopinavir/Ritonavir or Atazanavir/Ritonavir</strong>: Limit dose to 10 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Coumarin Anticoagulants</strong>: May prolong INR; monitor INR levels closely.</li><li><strong>Lipid-lowering therapies (fibrates, niacin)</strong>: Increased risk of muscle-related side effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Do not use Rosuva 5 mg in patients with:</p><ul><li>Known hypersensitivity to its components.</li><li>Liver disease or persistent elevations in hepatic transaminases.</li><li>Pregnant or nursing women.</li></ul><p><strong>Common Side Effects</strong></p><p>Generally well-tolerated but may include:</p><ul><li>Headache</li><li>Muscle pain (myalgia)</li><li>Constipation</li><li>Weakness (asthenia)</li><li>Abdominal pain</li><li>Nausea</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Not established as safe during pregnancy; contraindicated.</li><li>Unknown if excreted in human milk; not recommended during breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions and Warnings</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Muscle Effects</strong>: Risk of myopathy or rhabdomyolysis, especially at higher doses or in older adults (&gt;65 years), hypothyroid patients, or those with renal impairment. Patients should report any unexplained muscle pain or weakness.</li><li><strong>Liver Enzyme Monitoring</strong>: Monitor liver enzymes before starting and during treatment. Discontinue if persistent elevations occur.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Instructions</strong></p><ul><li>Store at temperatures below 30°C.</li><li>Protect from light and moisture.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li>Pediatric Use: Safety and effectiveness in certain pediatric populations are not fully established.</li></ul><p>This summary is for informational purposes only and should not replace medical advice. Always consult a healthcare provider for specific guidance regarding treatment</p>', 'active', '764_1733863440.webp', 4, 12, NULL, '2024-12-11 01:44:00', '2024-12-11 01:44:00'),
(132, 'Bislol', 'Bisoprolol Fumarate', 11.50, 14, 'Tablet', '14 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '5 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications for Bislol 5 mg</strong></p><p>Bislol 5 mg is used for managing:</p><ul><li>High blood pressure (hypertension)</li><li>Chest pain caused by angina</li><li>Moderate to severe heart failure</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Anti-adrenergic agents (Beta blockers)</li><li>Beta-adrenoceptor blocking drugs</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Bisoprolol Hemifumarate is a highly selective beta-1 blocker. It has a strong affinity for beta-1 receptors in the heart and vascular smooth muscle, leading to reduced heart rate and cardiac output, which in turn lowers blood pressure. Unlike non-selective beta-blockers, Bisoprolol does not negatively affect lipid profiles, including cardioprotective HDL cholesterol, during long-term use.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><p><strong>Hypertension:</strong></p><ul><li>Typical starting dose: 5 mg once daily.</li><li>For some patients, a starting dose of 2.5 mg may be appropriate.</li><li>If needed, the dose can be increased to 10 mg and up to 20 mg daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Angina:</strong></p><ul><li>Standard dose: 10 mg once daily.</li><li>Some patients may respond well to 5 mg daily.</li><li>Maximum dose: 20 mg daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Heart Failure:</strong></p><ul><li>Start with 1.25 mg once daily (preferably in the morning) for one week.</li><li>Gradually increase to 2.5 mg, 3.75 mg, and 5 mg, with adjustments every week or longer if tolerated.</li><li>The dose may further increase to 7.5 mg for 4 weeks, and then to 10 mg daily.</li><li>Maximum dose: 10 mg daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><p>Avoid using Bisoprolol with other beta-blockers.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Do not use in patients with:</p><ul><li>Cardiogenic shock</li><li>Severe heart failure</li><li>Second- or third-degree A-V block</li><li>Right ventricular failure from pulmonary hypertension</li><li>Sinus bradycardia</li></ul><p><strong>Possible Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Digestive issues</li><li>Slow heart rate (bradycardia)</li><li>Low blood pressure (hypotension)</li><li>Headache, fatigue, dizziness, or vertigo</li><li>Sleep disturbances</li><li>Rarely, visual disturbances, alopecia, or thrombocytopenia</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Safety during pregnancy has not been established.</li><li>Information on use during breastfeeding is unavailable.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><p>Regular monitoring of kidney, liver, and blood function is recommended during long-term use.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Storage Instructions</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry, cool place, away from light and heat.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p>This version ensures readability while maintaining clarity and originality.</p>', 'active', '262_1733863721.webp', 7, 12, NULL, '2024-12-11 01:48:41', '2024-12-11 01:48:41'),
(133, 'Rivotril', 'Clonazepam', 9.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '0.5 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Panic Disorder</strong>: Effective in treating panic disorders, with or without agoraphobia.</li><li><strong>Seizure Management</strong>: Used independently or as an adjunct for Lennox-Gastaut Syndrome, akinetic seizures, myoclonic seizures, and refractory absence seizures (petit mal).</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Adjunct anti-epileptic drugs</li><li>Benzodiazepine hypnotics</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li>Enhances GABA activity, reducing nerve transmission in the motor cortex.</li><li>Effective against focal and generalized seizures, suppressing EEG paroxysmal activities.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><p><strong>Adults with Seizures</strong>: Start with 1.5 mg/day in divided doses; increase as needed to a max of 20 mg/day.</p><p><strong>Adults with Panic Disorder</strong>: Begin with 0.25 mg twice daily; adjust to 1 mg/day if necessary.</p><p><strong>Pediatrics</strong>:</p><ul><li>Infants/children: 0.01-0.03 mg/kg/day in divided doses (max: 0.05 mg/kg/day).</li><li><strong>Injection Dosage</strong>:</li><li><strong>Children</strong>: 0.5 mg via slow IV.</li><li><strong>Adults</strong>: 1 mg via slow IV, repeatable up to 10 mg/day.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to benzodiazepines.</li><li>Significant liver disease.</li><li>Acute narrow-angle glaucoma.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common</strong>: Drowsiness (50%), ataxia (30%), behavioral issues (25%).</li><li><strong>Others</strong>: Tremor, confusion, hallucinations, CNS depression, abnormal eye movements, and more.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>May exacerbate generalized tonic-clonic seizures in mixed epilepsy.</li><li>Use with valproic acid may result in absence status.</li><li>Increased bronchial secretions in children; monitor airway patency.</li><li>Geriatric patients may show heightened sensitivity to effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Management</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Symptoms</strong>: CNS depression, ataxia, hypotension, or coma (rarely life-threatening).</li><li><strong>Treatment</strong>: Symptomatic care, activated charcoal, or flumazenil under close monitoring.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Considerations</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy</strong>: Use only if benefits outweigh risks.</li><li><strong>Breastfeeding</strong>: Not recommended.</li><li><strong>Hepatic Impairment</strong>: May require dosage adjustments.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry, cool place away from light and out of children’s reach.</li></ul><p>For detailed clinical decisions, consult full prescribing guidelines.</p>', 'active', '1911_1733896182.png', 10, 12, NULL, '2024-12-11 01:53:10', '2024-12-11 10:49:42'),
(134, 'ORSaline-N', 'Oral Rehydration Salt [Powder]', 6.00, 1, 'Packet', '10.25gm powder in a packet', 'Powder', '10.25 gm', 'no', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of ORSaline-N 10.25 gm</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Treatment</strong>: Diarrhea (to prevent or treat dehydration).</li><li><strong>Prophylaxis and Treatment</strong>: Electrolyte depletion.</li></ul><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><p><strong>Reduced Osmolarity (10.25 gm per sachet for 500 ml solution)</strong>:</p><ul><li>Sodium chloride: 1.30 gm</li><li>Potassium chloride: 0.75 gm</li><li>Tri-sodium citrate dihydrate: 1.45 gm</li><li>Glucose anhydrous: 6.75 gm</li></ul><p><strong>Higher Osmolarity (13.95 gm per sachet for 500 ml solution)</strong>:</p><ul><li>Sodium chloride: 1.75 gm</li><li>Potassium chloride: 0.75 gm</li><li>Tri-sodium citrate dihydrate: 1.45 gm</li><li>Glucose anhydrous: 10 gm</li></ul><p><strong>Higher Osmolarity (27.50 gm per sachet for 1 liter solution)</strong>:</p><ul><li>Sodium chloride: 3.5 gm</li><li>Sodium bicarbonate: 2.5 gm</li><li>Potassium chloride: 1.5 gm</li><li>Glucose anhydrous: 20 gm</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Oral electrolytes preparations.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Oral rehydration salts are designed to prevent or treat dehydration due to acute diarrhea by replenishing lost fluids and electrolytes. They utilize the glucose-sodium co-transport system in the small intestine, where glucose enhances sodium absorption, promoting better fluid retention. Potassium prevents hypokalemia, especially in children, and bicarbonates correct metabolic acidosis associated with diarrhea and dehydration.</p><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Children under 2 years</strong>: 10–20 spoonfuls (50–100 ml) of prepared solution after each loose stool or vomiting.</li><li><strong>Children 2–10 years</strong>: 100–200 ml of prepared solution after each loose stool or vomiting.</li><li><strong>Adults and children over 10 years</strong>: 200–400 ml of prepared solution after each loose stool or vomiting.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><p>No known interactions reported.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>None documented.</p><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>No reported side effects.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Not classified into an FDA pregnancy category.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions and Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Patients with depressed renal function, severe ongoing diarrhea, or critical fluid losses may require additional parenteral fluids.</li><li>Use caution with solutions containing acetate or gluconate ions to prevent metabolic alkalosis.</li><li>Solutions with dextrose should be administered cautiously in individuals with diabetes mellitus (overt or subclinical).</li></ul>', 'active', '287_1733865484.webp', 12, 1, NULL, '2024-12-11 02:18:04', '2024-12-11 10:41:40'),
(135, 'Amdocal', 'Amlodipine', 5.50, 15, 'Tablet', '15 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '5 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p>Amdocal 5 mg is a calcium channel blocker prescribed for hypertension and coronary artery disease, including conditions like chronic stable angina, vasospastic angina, and documented coronary artery disease in patients without heart failure or reduced ejection fraction (&lt;40%). Below is a summarized overview:</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Calcium-channel blockers.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Mechanism of Action</strong>: Amdocal 5 mg inhibits calcium ion influx into vascular and cardiac muscle, reducing vascular resistance and lowering blood pressure. Its action on angina involves:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Peripheral arteriole dilation, decreasing afterload and myocardial oxygen demand.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Coronary artery and arteriole dilation, enhancing oxygen delivery to ischemic areas.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults</strong>: Start with 5 mg once daily; maximum 10 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Pediatrics</strong>: 2.5 mg to 5 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Elderly, fragile, or hepatic-impaired patients</strong>: Start at 2.5 mg daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>Compatible with various antihypertensives, NSAIDs, and hypoglycemics.</li><li>Avoid grapefruit juice as it may increase drug bioavailability.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Amdocal 5 mg.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Headache, edema (dose-dependent).</li><li>Others (&gt;1% incidence): Fatigue, nausea, abdominal pain, somnolence.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Risk of symptomatic hypotension, particularly in severe aortic stenosis.</li><li>Monitor closely in hepatic impairment; titrate doses gradually.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Category C: Use only if the benefit justifies the risk to the fetus.</li><li>Unknown if excreted in breast milk; breastfeeding is not recommended during treatment.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Management:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Symptoms</strong>: Severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, shock.</li><li><strong>Treatment</strong>: Cardiovascular support, vasoconstrictors, intravenous calcium gluconate, and gastric lavage if necessary.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry, cool place away from light. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Populations:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Children (6–17 years)</strong>: Start with 2.5 mg daily; increase to 5 mg if needed after four weeks.</li><li><strong>Children (&lt;6 years)</strong>: Not recommended.</li><li><strong>Elderly</strong>: Normal dosage; titrate with care if increasing dose.</li><li><strong>Renal impairment</strong>: No dose adjustment needed; not dialysable.</li><li><strong>Hepatic impairment</strong>: Start at 2.5 mg; adjust slowly.</li></ul><p>This summarized guide is meant for informational purposes and should complement professional medical advice.</p>', 'active', '855_1733865885.jpg', 3, 12, NULL, '2024-12-11 02:24:45', '2024-12-11 02:24:45'),
(136, 'Uromax-D', 'Tamsulosin Hydrochloride + Dutasteride', 23.00, 5, 'Capsule', '5 Capsul in a strip', 'Capsule', '0.4 mg+0.5 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><br></p><p>This detailed overview of <strong>Uromax-D 0.4 mg + 0.5 mg</strong> provides comprehensive information about its indications, pharmacology, usage, precautions, and interactions. Below is a summarized version highlighting key points:</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Primary Use:</strong> Treatment of moderate to severe symptoms of <strong>Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia (BPH)</strong>.</li><li><strong>Additional Benefits:</strong> Reduces the risk of acute urinary retention and the need for surgery.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>BPH / Urinary Retention / Urinary Incontinence</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Dutasteride:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Inhibits 5-alpha reductase (types I &amp; II), reducing DHT levels.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Reduces prostate size by targeting underlying causes of BPH.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Tamsulosin:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Alpha1-adrenoreceptor antagonist.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Relaxes smooth muscle in the prostate and bladder neck, improving urine flow.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Recommended Dosage:</strong> One capsule daily, 30 minutes after the same meal. Capsules should not be chewed or opened.</li><li><strong>Special Populations:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Renal Impairment:</strong> No dosage adjustment required.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Hepatic Impairment:</strong> Use cautiously in mild-to-moderate cases. Contraindicated in severe cases.</li></ul><p><strong>Key Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>CYP3A4 Inhibitors:</strong> Potent inhibitors (e.g., ketoconazole) may increase Dutasteride levels.</li><li><strong>Alpha-1 Blockers:</strong> Avoid combining with other alpha-1 blockers to prevent excessive hypotension.</li><li><strong>Cimetidine:</strong> May elevate Tamsulosin levels.</li><li><strong>Warfarin and PDE5 inhibitors:</strong> Use cautiously due to potential interactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Women, children, and adolescents.</li><li>Severe hepatic impairment.</li><li>Hypersensitivity to any ingredients, including soy or peanut derivatives.</li></ul><p><strong>Common Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Impotence, decreased libido, dizziness.</li><li>Breast tenderness or enlargement.</li><li>Ejaculation disorders.</li></ul><p><strong>Warnings and Precautions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>PSA Monitoring:</strong> Reduces PSA levels by 50%; monitor new baseline levels after six months.</li><li><strong>Prostate Cancer Risk:</strong> Regular evaluation is necessary.</li><li><strong>Orthostatic Hypotension:</strong> Caution advised, especially with co-administration of PDE5 inhibitors.</li><li><strong>Intraoperative Floppy Iris Syndrome:</strong> Risk during cataract surgery—consider discontinuation before the procedure.</li><li><strong>Breast Changes:</strong> Promptly report any lumps or nipple discharge.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Contraindicated for women.</li><li>Dutasteride exposure through semen may affect male fetal development.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place, protected from light.</li></ul><p>Let me know if you need further clarification or specific details!</p>', 'active', '1191_1733866150.webp', 8, 12, NULL, '2024-12-11 02:29:10', '2024-12-15 13:53:35'),
(137, 'Diamicron MR', 'Gliclazide', 22.00, 15, 'Tablet', '15 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '60 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Diamicron MR 60 mg</strong></p><p>Diamicron MR 60 mg is an oral antidiabetic medication used to manage type 2 diabetes mellitus in adults when diet, exercise, and weight loss alone are insufficient to control blood sugar levels.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Sulfonylureas</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Diamicron MR 60 mg is a second-generation sulfonylurea that lowers blood sugar by stimulating insulin release from pancreatic β-cells. This process involves facilitating calcium ion transport across β-cell membranes and reducing glucose production by the liver.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><p><strong>Oral Route:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Initial Dose:</strong> 40–80 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Maximum Dose:</strong> Up to 320 mg daily, divided into doses as needed.</li><li>The medication should be taken before meals.</li><li><strong>Children:</strong> Not recommended, as it is contraindicated in juvenile-onset diabetes.</li></ul><p><strong>Modified-Release Tablets:</strong></p><ul><li>The daily dose ranges from one to four tablets (maximum 120 mg), taken once at breakfast.</li><li>Tablets should be swallowed whole with water, without chewing or crushing.</li></ul><p>If Diamicron MR 60 mg is combined with other antidiabetic medications (e.g., metformin, insulin), the doctor will adjust the doses accordingly. If blood sugar levels remain high, consult your doctor promptly.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Overdose Management</strong></p><p>Symptoms of overdose include hypoglycemia, which may manifest as dizziness, confusion, or loss of consciousness. Immediate intake of sugar or sugary drinks is advised, followed by medical attention. In severe cases, emergency services should be contacted.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><p>Diamicron MR 60 mg may interact with other medications, potentially enhancing or reducing its blood sugar-lowering effect.</p><p><strong>Medications that may enhance its effect:</strong></p><ul><li>Other antidiabetics, antibiotics (e.g., sulfonamides), antifungal drugs, and some antihypertensives.</li></ul><p><strong>Medications that may reduce its effect:</strong></p><ul><li>Corticosteroids, certain asthma medications, and St. John’s Wort.</li></ul><p>Consult a doctor before combining Diamicron MR 60 mg with other treatments.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Insulin-dependent diabetes (type 1)</li><li>Severe kidney or liver disease</li><li>Diabetic ketoacidosis</li><li>Allergies to sulfonylureas</li><li>Pregnancy and breastfeeding</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common:</strong> Hypoglycemia, gastrointestinal discomfort, and vision disturbances.</li><li><strong>Rare:</strong> Allergic reactions, liver dysfunction, or blood disorders.</li><li>Seek immediate medical attention for severe reactions like skin blistering or jaundice.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions and Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Monitor blood sugar levels regularly.</li><li>Avoid skipping meals or fasting, as it increases the risk of hypoglycemia.</li><li>Discuss any changes in diet, exercise, or lifestyle with your doctor.</li><li>Use cautiously if you have conditions affecting the thyroid, pituitary, or adrenal glands.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><p>Diamicron MR 60 mg is contraindicated during pregnancy and breastfeeding. Alternative treatments should be considered.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C in a dry place, away from children.</li><li>Dispose of unused medication responsibly to protect the environment.</li></ul><p>This information ensures safe and effective use of Diamicron MR 60 mg. Always consult your healthcare provider for personalized advice.</p>', 'active', '1392_1733866621.jpg', 7, 12, NULL, '2024-12-11 02:37:01', '2024-12-11 02:37:01'),
(138, 'Febustat', 'Febuxostat', 13.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '40 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong> Febustat 40 mg is indicated for the chronic management of hyperuricemia in patients with gout. It is not recommended for the treatment of asymptomatic hyperuricemia.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong> Drugs used in Gout</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong> Febustat 40 mg is a non-purine, selective xanthine oxidase (XO) inhibitor. It lowers serum uric acid levels by inhibiting xanthine oxidase, the enzyme responsible for uric acid production. Xanthine oxidase converts hypoxanthine to xanthine, and then to uric acid. Febustat 40 mg does not significantly inhibit other enzymes involved in purine and pyrimidine synthesis at therapeutic doses.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li>The starting dose is 40 mg once daily.</li><li>If serum uric acid remains above 6 mg/dL after 2 weeks, the dose can be increased to 80 mg once daily.</li><li>Febustat 40 mg can be taken with or without food or antacids.</li><li>No dose adjustment is required for patients with mild to moderate renal or hepatic impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong> Concomitant use with azathioprine, mercaptopurine, or theophylline may increase plasma concentrations of these drugs, potentially leading to severe toxicity.</p><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong> Febustat 40 mg is contraindicated in patients taking azathioprine, mercaptopurine, or theophylline.</p><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong> Common adverse effects include liver function abnormalities, nausea, arthralgia, and rash.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Pregnancy Category C: There are no adequate studies in pregnant women. Febustat should be used during pregnancy only if the potential benefit justifies the risk to the fetus.</li><li>It is unknown if Febustat is excreted in human milk, so caution is advised when administering to nursing women.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Gout Flare:</strong> Gout flares may increase during treatment initiation. Prophylactic therapy with NSAIDs or colchicine may help.</li><li><strong>Cardiovascular Events:</strong> Increased rates of cardiovascular events, including myocardial infarction and stroke, have been observed with Febustat in clinical trials.</li><li><strong>Liver Enzyme Elevation:</strong> Liver enzyme elevations have been noted. Liver function tests should be monitored periodically.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose:</strong> Febustat was studied in doses up to 300 mg daily for seven days without dose-limiting toxicities.</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong> Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture. Keep out of reach of children.</p><p><strong>Use in Special Populations:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pediatric Use:</strong> Safety and effectiveness in children under 18 years have not been established.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong> Febustat 40 mg is a non-purine xanthine oxidase inhibitor that lowers serum uric acid levels by inhibiting xanthine oxidase, a key enzyme in uric acid production.</p>', 'active', '232_1733866838.webp', 2, 12, NULL, '2024-12-11 02:40:38', '2024-12-11 02:40:38'),
(139, 'Comet', 'Metformin Hydrochloride', 5.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '500 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><br></p><p>Comet 500 mg is a medication used primarily in the treatment of type 2 diabetes mellitus, especially in overweight patients when diet and exercise are insufficient for adequate glycemic control. It is a biguanide-class drug containing metformin, which helps control blood sugar levels by reducing glucose production in the liver, decreasing glucose absorption in the intestines, and improving insulin sensitivity.</p><p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus</strong>: Used for adults and children (10 years and older) when lifestyle changes alone don\'t provide enough control. It can be used alone or with other antidiabetic medications or insulin.</li><li><strong>Prevention of Diabetic Complications</strong>: Reduces complications in overweight adults with type 2 diabetes when used as a first-line therapy after diet failure.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults</strong>: Start with 500 mg twice a day or 850 mg once a day with meals. Increase the dose gradually up to a maximum of 2000 mg per day, depending on effectiveness and tolerance.</li><li><strong>Children (10+ years)</strong>: Start with 500 mg twice a day, with a dose increase in increments up to 2000 mg per day.</li><li><strong>Extended Release (XR)</strong>: Starting with 500 mg once a day with the evening meal, increase gradually to 2000 mg daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>Drugs like carbonic anhydrase inhibitors (e.g., Topiramate) may increase the risk of lactic acidosis. Medications that reduce metformin clearance (e.g., Ranolazine) can increase metformin accumulation.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Hypersensitivity</strong> to metformin.</li><li><strong>Renal Failure</strong> (eGFR &lt;30 mL/min).</li><li><strong>Acute Metabolic Acidosis</strong>, such as lactic acidosis or diabetic ketoacidosis.</li><li>Conditions that may impair renal function, such as severe dehydration, infections, or shock.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Gastrointestinal</strong>: Common issues include nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, abdominal pain, and loss of appetite. These tend to resolve after adjusting the dose.</li><li><strong>Metabolism</strong>: Rare lactic acidosis and vitamin B12 deficiency, potentially leading to peripheral neuropathy in some cases.</li><li><strong>Skin</strong>: Very rare cases of skin reactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Metformin is not recommended during pregnancy, and insulin should be used instead to manage blood glucose.</li><li>Metformin is excreted into breast milk but has not shown adverse effects on breastfed infants. Caution is advised.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Renal Function</strong>: Assess renal function before starting treatment and regularly thereafter, especially in elderly patients.</li><li><strong>Vitamin B12</strong>: Long-term use may lower vitamin B12 levels.</li><li><strong>Hypoglycemia Risk</strong>: Increased when used with insulin or other hypoglycemic agents.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Lactic Acidosis</strong> is a serious risk in overdose situations. Treatment requires hospitalization and hemodialysis to remove lactate and metformin from the body.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p>This overview outlines the key uses, dosage guidelines, side effects, and precautions for Comet 500 mg (metformin). Always follow your healthcare provider\'s guidance for personalized treatment.</p>', 'active', '791_1733867031.jpg', 4, 12, NULL, '2024-12-11 02:43:51', '2024-12-11 02:43:51'),
(140, 'Angilock', 'Losartan Potassium', 10.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '50 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Angilock 50 mg</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Hypertension</strong>: Angilock 50 mg is used for the treatment of high blood pressure and can be taken alone or with other antihypertensive agents, such as thiazide diuretics.</li><li><strong>Renal Protection in Type-2 Diabetic Patients with Proteinuria</strong>: It is used to slow the progression of kidney disease in hypertensive individuals with type-2 diabetes and proteinuria (urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio &gt;300 mg/g).</li></ol><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Angiotensin-II receptor blocker</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Angilock 50 mg is the first orally active angiotensin II receptor blocker without a peptide. It works by binding to the AT1 receptor in various tissues (e.g., heart, kidneys, adrenal glands, vascular smooth muscle) to inhibit processes like vasoconstriction and aldosterone production, which help regulate blood pressure.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li>For most patients, the starting and maintenance dose is 50 mg once daily.</li><li>If the effect of 50 mg once daily is inadequate, the dose may be increased to 25 mg twice daily.</li><li>Patients with intravascular volume depletion (e.g., those on high-dose diuretics) may start with 25 mg once daily.</li><li>The total daily dose ranges from 25 mg to 100 mg, taken in one or two doses.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>Rifampicin and fluconazole reduce the active metabolite levels of Angilock 50 mg.</li><li>Using Angilock 50 mg with hydrochlorothiazide may enhance the antihypertensive effect.</li><li>Co-administration with potassium-sparing diuretics (e.g., spironolactone), potassium supplements, or salt substitutes may lead to increased potassium levels.</li><li>Non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (e.g., indomethacin) may reduce the effectiveness of Angilock 50 mg.</li><li>Combining Angilock 50 mg with an ACE inhibitor, anti-inflammatory drugs, or thiazide diuretics increases the risk of renal impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Pregnant women should not use Angilock 50 mg, particularly in the second and third trimesters.</li><li>Individuals who are allergic to any component of Angilock 50 mg should avoid it.</li><li>The combination of Angilock 50 mg with Aliskiren is contraindicated in diabetic patients.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common side effects are generally mild and transient, including dizziness, diarrhea, nasal congestion, coughing, and upper respiratory infections. Other possible effects include fatigue, edema, chest pain, nausea, headaches, and pharyngitis.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Category D for pregnancy: Angilock 50 mg should not be used during the second or third trimester of pregnancy due to potential harm to the fetus, including renal impairment.</li><li>The safety of Angilock 50 mg during breastfeeding is unclear. Decisions regarding breastfeeding should be made based on the medication\'s importance to the mother.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Angilock 50 mg can increase the risk of fetal morbidity and mortality during the second and third trimesters of pregnancy.</li><li>It can cause symptomatic hypotension in patients with low blood volume, such as those on high-dose diuretics.</li><li>Caution is needed in patients with cirrhosis or renal impairment, as Angilock 50 mg may cause changes in renal function, including renal failure.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Store in a dry place, away from heat and light. Keep out of reach of children.</p><p><strong>Drug Classes</strong></p><p>Angiotensin-II receptor blocker</p><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>Angilock 50 mg works by binding to the AT1 receptor, inhibiting vasoconstriction and aldosterone production, both of which help manage blood pressure.</p><p><br></p><p>4o mini</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p>You have not enough Humanizer words left. Upgrade your Surfer plan.</p>', 'active', '1752_1733896356.png', 4, 12, NULL, '2024-12-11 02:46:56', '2024-12-11 10:52:36'),
(141, 'Pozzy Baby Wet Towel Wipes', 'Wipes', 245.00, 1, 'Packet', '120\'s wipes in a pack', 'Wipes', '120\'s wipes', 'no', 'yes', '<p>Pozzy Baby Wet Towel Wipes 120 offer a safe, gentle, and effective cleaning solution for babies\' delicate skin. Crafted from soft, absorbent materials, these wipes provide thorough cleaning while moisturizing and preventing irritation. Hypoallergenic and dermatologically tested, they ensure comfort and peace of mind for parents.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions:</strong></p><ol><li>Open the wipe container.</li><li>Take out a wipe and use it to clean the desired area.</li><li>After use, dispose of the wipe in the trash can.</li><li>Close the container to preserve moisture.</li></ol><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Always read the label before using.</li><li>Keep the product out of children\'s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>Disposal Instructions:</strong></p><ul><li>Dispose of used wipes in the trash.</li><li>Do not flush the wipes down the toilet.</li><li>Do not place the wipes in recycling bins or compost piles.</li></ul>', 'active', '441_1733897406.jpg', 36, 6, NULL, '2024-12-11 11:10:06', '2024-12-11 13:16:27'),
(142, 'Savlon Baby Wipes (AntiBacterial)', 'Wipes', 230.00, 1, 'Box', '80\'s wipes in a box', 'Wipes', '80\'s wipes', 'no', 'yes', '<p>Savlon Baby Wipes (AntiBacterial) 80 provide a gentle yet effective solution for cleaning your baby\'s sensitive skin. These wipes are made from soft, absorbent materials that clean and moisturize without causing irritation. Hypoallergenic and dermatologically tested, they are a trusted choice for parents who prioritize both safety and hygiene.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions:</strong></p><ol><li>Open the container and pull out a wipe.</li><li>Use the wipe to clean the desired area.</li><li>Dispose of the wipe in the trash can.</li><li>Close the container securely to maintain moisture.</li></ol><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Always read the label carefully before use.</li><li>Keep out of the reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Disposal Instructions:</strong></p><ul><li>Dispose of used wipes in the trash.</li><li>Do not flush Savlon Baby Wipes (AntiBacterial) 80 down the toilet.</li><li>Do not place in recycling bins or compost piles.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1584_1733897780.png', 14, 6, NULL, '2024-12-11 11:16:20', '2024-12-11 11:16:20'),
(143, 'Savlon Baby Wipes', 'Wipes', 220.00, 1, 'Jar', '100 wipes in a jar', 'Wipes', '100\'s jar', 'no', 'no', '<p>Savlon Baby Wipes 100 are a popular choice for gentle yet effective cleaning for little babies. They are made of soft and absorbent materials to effectively clean and moisturize delicate skin without the risk of irritation. Savlon Baby Wipes 100 are also hypoallergenic and dermatologically tested to ensure peace of mind for worried parents.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions of Savlon Baby Wipes 100:</strong></p><ul><li>Open the wipe container and remove a wipe.</li><li>Use the wipe to clean the area that needs to be cleaned.</li><li>Dispose of the wipe in the trash can.</li><li>Close the wipe container.</li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Read the label carefully before use.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Disposal Instructions:</strong></p><ul><li>Dispose of Savlon Baby Wipes 100 in the trash.</li><li>Do not flush Savlon Baby Wipes 100 down the toilet.</li><li>Do not put Savlon Baby Wipes 100 in recycling bins or compost piles.</li></ul>', 'active', '1892_1733905525.webp', 14, 6, NULL, '2024-12-11 13:25:25', '2024-12-11 13:25:25'),
(144, 'Orostar Plus', 'Eucalyptol + Menthol + Methyl Salicylate + Thymol + Sodium Fluoride', 150.00, 1, 'Bottle', '250 ml in a bottle', 'Mouth Wash', '250 ml', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Orostar Plus 250 ml</strong></p><p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><p>Orostar Plus is primarily indicated for oral health issues such as:</p><ul><li>Dental cavities</li><li>Tooth decay</li><li>Bad breath</li><li>Dental plaque</li><li>Gingivitis</li></ul><p><strong>Composition (per 100 ml):</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Eucalyptol</strong>: 92 mg</li><li><strong>Menthol</strong>: 42 mg</li><li><strong>Methyl Salicylate</strong>: 60 mg</li><li><strong>Thymol</strong>: 64 mg</li><li><strong>Sodium Fluoride</strong>: 20 mg</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Oral preparations (mouthwash)</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Eucalyptol</strong>: A natural monoterpenoid and cyclic ether, eucalyptol provides anti-inflammatory effects that may help in controlling airway mucus hypersecretion and symptoms of asthma. It is a common ingredient in mouthwashes.</li><li><strong>Menthol</strong>: Known for its cooling effect, menthol stimulates cooling receptors and offers a local anesthetic action, which can provide temporary relief from oral discomfort.</li><li><strong>Methyl Salicylate</strong>: Works by penetrating pain sites and inhibiting prostaglandin synthesis, helping to relieve oral pain.</li><li><strong>Thymol</strong>: Found in thyme, thymol is used for its antimicrobial and anti-cavity properties, often combined with other agents like chlorhexidine in oral products.</li><li><strong>Sodium Fluoride</strong>: Fluoride helps in the remineralization of enamel, strengthening teeth and preventing cavities.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults and children aged 6 and above</strong>: Rinse with 10 ml of mouthwash for 1 minute, twice daily (morning and night). Do not swallow.</li><li><strong>Children under 6 years</strong>: Consult a dentist or doctor before use.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><p>There are no known or well-documented drug interactions for Orostar Plus.</p><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any of the ingredients in the formulation.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Local irritation of the mouth</li><li>Nausea and vomiting (rare)</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Pregnancy Category: Not Classified by the FDA. Its safety during pregnancy and lactation has not been specifically evaluated. Consult a doctor before use during pregnancy.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Do not swallow</strong> the mouthwash.</li><li>Not recommended for children under 6 years of age.</li><li>Do not rinse, eat, or smoke for at least 30 minutes after use, as this may diminish the effectiveness of the mouthwash.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children to avoid accidental ingestion.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place.</li><li>The product may cloud in cold weather, but this does not affect its antiseptic or anticavity properties.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Class:</strong></p><p>Oral preparations (mouthwash)</p><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Eucalyptol</strong> acts as an anti-inflammatory and antimicrobial agent.</li><li><strong>Menthol</strong> provides a cooling effect and temporary pain relief.</li><li><strong>Methyl Salicylate</strong> helps alleviate oral pain through its anti-inflammatory action.</li><li><strong>Thymol</strong> works to prevent tooth decay and fight oral infections.</li></ul>', 'active', '1163_1733983700.png', 4, 7, NULL, '2024-12-12 11:08:20', '2024-12-12 11:09:09');
INSERT INTO `products` (`id`, `productName`, `genericName`, `retail_max_price`, `cart_qty_inc`, `cart_text`, `unit_in_pack`, `type`, `quantity`, `prescription`, `feature`, `description`, `status`, `coverImage`, `company_id`, `category_id`, `add_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(145, 'Orostar Plus', 'Eucalyptol + Menthol + Methyl Salicylate + Thymol + Sodium Fluoride', 85.26, 1, 'Bottle', '120 ml in a bottle', 'Mouth Wash', '120 ml', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Orostar Plus 250 ml</strong></p><p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><p>Orostar Plus is primarily indicated for oral health issues such as:</p><ul><li>Dental cavities</li><li>Tooth decay</li><li>Bad breath</li><li>Dental plaque</li><li>Gingivitis</li></ul><p><strong>Composition (per 100 ml):</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Eucalyptol</strong>: 92 mg</li><li><strong>Menthol</strong>: 42 mg</li><li><strong>Methyl Salicylate</strong>: 60 mg</li><li><strong>Thymol</strong>: 64 mg</li><li><strong>Sodium Fluoride</strong>: 20 mg</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Oral preparations (mouthwash)</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Eucalyptol</strong>: A natural monoterpenoid and cyclic ether, eucalyptol provides anti-inflammatory effects that may help in controlling airway mucus hypersecretion and symptoms of asthma. It is a common ingredient in mouthwashes.</li><li><strong>Menthol</strong>: Known for its cooling effect, menthol stimulates cooling receptors and offers a local anesthetic action, which can provide temporary relief from oral discomfort.</li><li><strong>Methyl Salicylate</strong>: Works by penetrating pain sites and inhibiting prostaglandin synthesis, helping to relieve oral pain.</li><li><strong>Thymol</strong>: Found in thyme, thymol is used for its antimicrobial and anti-cavity properties, often combined with other agents like chlorhexidine in oral products.</li><li><strong>Sodium Fluoride</strong>: Fluoride helps in the remineralization of enamel, strengthening teeth and preventing cavities.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults and children aged 6 and above</strong>: Rinse with 10 ml of mouthwash for 1 minute, twice daily (morning and night). Do not swallow.</li><li><strong>Children under 6 years</strong>: Consult a dentist or doctor before use.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><p>There are no known or well-documented drug interactions for Orostar Plus.</p><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any of the ingredients in the formulation.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Local irritation of the mouth</li><li>Nausea and vomiting (rare)</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Pregnancy Category: Not Classified by the FDA. Its safety during pregnancy and lactation has not been specifically evaluated. Consult a doctor before use during pregnancy.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Do not swallow</strong> the mouthwash.</li><li>Not recommended for children under 6 years of age.</li><li>Do not rinse, eat, or smoke for at least 30 minutes after use, as this may diminish the effectiveness of the mouthwash.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children to avoid accidental ingestion.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place.</li><li>The product may cloud in cold weather, but this does not affect its antiseptic or anticavity properties.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Class:</strong></p><p>Oral preparations (mouthwash)</p><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Eucalyptol</strong> acts as an anti-inflammatory and antimicrobial agent.</li><li><strong>Menthol</strong> provides a cooling effect and temporary pain relief.</li><li><strong>Methyl Salicylate</strong> helps alleviate oral pain through its anti-inflammatory action.</li><li><strong>Thymol</strong> works to prevent tooth decay and fight oral infections.</li></ul>', 'active', '447_1733984224.jpg', 4, 7, NULL, '2024-12-12 11:17:04', '2024-12-12 11:17:28'),
(146, 'Listacare Blue Mint', 'Menthol + Thymol + Eucalyptol + Methyl Salicylate', 80.00, 1, 'Box', '120 ml in a bottle', 'Mouth Wash', '120 ml', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications of Listacare Blue Mint 120 ml</strong></p><p>Bad breath, Cavities, Gingivitis, Gum disease, Oral hygiene, Plaque, Teeth cleaner &amp; brighter</p><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><p>Each 100 ml mouthwash contains- Menthol 0.042 gm&nbsp;(0.042%) Thymol 0.064 gm&nbsp;(0.064%) Eucalyptol 0.092 gm&nbsp;(0.092%) Methyl Salicylate 0.060 gm&nbsp;(0.060%)</p><p><strong>Theropeutic Class</strong></p><p>Oral preparations</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>This preparation&nbsp;is a clinically proven antiseptic mouthwash that provides you complete care for healthier mouth with around-the-clock protection against bacteria and plaque. Your mouth stays cleaner, fresher and healthier. 24 hours protection against plaque, gingivitis and gum disease Fights against germs that cause bad breath Kills germs between teeth and keeps teeth cleaner &amp; brighter</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration of Listacare Blue Mint 120 ml</strong></p><p>Rinse with 20 ml Antiseptic Mouthwash for 30 seconds, twice daily (morning and evening). Then rinse with water. Do not swallow. Not indicated below 12 years of age.</p><p><strong>Interaction of Listacare Blue Mint 120 ml</strong></p><p>There are no known drug interactions and none well documented.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Hypersensitivity</p><p><strong>Side Effects of Listacare Blue Mint 120 ml</strong></p><p>Do not rinse, eat, or smoke for thirty minutes after using a mouthwash. Doing so will diminish the effects of the mouthwash.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><p>Pregnancy Category - Not Classified. FDA has not yet classified the drug into a specified pregnancy category.</p><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><p>Do not swallow. It is not indicated below 12 years of age. Keep out of the reach of children. Keep in a cool and dry palace. Do not use if cap seal is broken.</p><p><br></p>', 'active', '1778_1733984550.webp', 37, 7, NULL, '2024-12-12 11:22:30', '2024-12-12 11:22:30'),
(147, 'Mediplus DS', 'Toothpaste', 135.00, 1, 'Tube', '140 gm tube', 'Toothpaste', '140 gm', 'no', 'yes', '<p>Mediplus DS 140 gm is known for its effectiveness in keeping teeth clean and healthy. It contains fluoride to prevent tooth decay and strengthens enamel. Mediplus DS 140 gm also has a refreshing mint flavor that leaves the mouth feeling clean and fresh.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions of Mediplus DS 140 gm:</strong></p><ol><li>Put a pea-sized amount of Mediplus DS 140 gm on your toothbrush.</li><li>Wet your toothbrush and start brushing your teeth in a gentle and circular motion.</li><li>Brush the front, back, and top of your teeth.</li><li>Brush for at least two minutes.</li><li>Spit out the Mediplus DS 140 gm and rinse your mouth with water.</li></ol><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Read the label carefully before use.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li><li>Store in a cool, dry place.</li></ul><p><strong>Disposal Instructions:</strong></p><ul><li>Do not flush down the toilet.</li><li>Do not put Mediplus DS 140 gm in recycling bins or compost piles.</li><li>Dispose of Mediplus DS 140 gm in the trash.</li></ul>', 'active', '935_1733985359.webp', 38, 7, NULL, '2024-12-12 11:35:03', '2024-12-12 11:37:14'),
(148, 'Mediplus', 'Ultimate Dental Care', 90.00, 1, 'Tube', '140 gm tube', 'Toothpaste', '140 gm', 'no', 'yes', '<p>Mediplus DS 140 gm is known for its effectiveness in keeping teeth clean and healthy. It contains fluoride to prevent tooth decay and strengthens enamel. Mediplus DS 140 gm also has a refreshing mint flavor that leaves the mouth feeling clean and fresh.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions of Mediplus DS 140 gm:</strong></p><ol><li>Put a pea-sized amount of Mediplus DS 140 gm on your toothbrush.</li><li>Wet your toothbrush and start brushing your teeth in a gentle and circular motion.</li><li>Brush the front, back, and top of your teeth.</li><li>Brush for at least two minutes.</li><li>Spit out the Mediplus DS 140 gm and rinse your mouth with water.</li></ol><p><strong>Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Read the label carefully before use.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li><li>Store in a cool, dry place.</li></ul><p><strong>Disposal Instructions:</strong></p><ul><li>Do not flush down the toilet.</li><li>Do not put Mediplus DS 140 gm in recycling bins or compost piles.</li><li>Dispose of Mediplus DS 140 gm in the trash.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1055_1733985890.webp', 38, 7, NULL, '2024-12-12 11:44:50', '2024-12-12 11:45:30'),
(149, 'Mediplus Toothbrush', 'Toothbrush', 90.00, 1, 'Piece', '1 piece in a box', 'Toothpaste', '1 piece', 'no', 'yes', '<p>Made with soft and nylon bristles, the Mediplus Toothbrush is gentle on the gums. The bristles are also angled to reach all surfaces of the teeth, including the back teeth. The Mediplus Toothbrush has a comfortable handle that makes it easy to grip.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions of Mediplus Toothbrush :</strong></p><ul><li>Choose a soft-bristled Mediplus Toothbrush .</li><li>Use a pea-sized amount of toothpaste.</li><li>Brush your teeth for at least two minutes, twice a day.</li><li>Angle your Mediplus Toothbrush at a 45-degree angle to your gums.</li><li>Rinse your mouth thoroughly after brushing and flossing.</li><li>Replace your Mediplus Toothbrush every 3 to 4 months, or sooner if the bristles look worn out.</li></ul>', 'active', '500_1733986397.webp', 38, 7, NULL, '2024-12-12 11:53:17', '2024-12-12 12:06:07'),
(150, 'Empa', 'Empagliflozin', 25.00, 15, 'Tablet', '15 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '10mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications for Empa 10 mg</strong></p><p>Empa 10 mg is prescribed as an additional treatment to diet and exercise to enhance blood sugar control in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus. It is also used to lower the risk of cardiovascular death in adults with type 2 diabetes and existing cardiovascular conditions.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Belongs to the category of Sodium-Glucose Co-Transporter-2 (SGLT2) Inhibitors.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Empa 10 mg acts as an SGLT2 inhibitor, which targets the sodium-glucose co-transporters responsible for glucose reabsorption in the kidneys. By inhibiting these transporters, the medication promotes increased glucose excretion through urine, reducing glucose levels in the blood. This mechanism also aids in lowering blood pressure, addressing hyperglycemia, and promoting weight loss.</p><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><p>The typical dose is 10 mg once daily, taken in the morning, with or without food. If the initial dose is well-tolerated, it may be increased to 25 mg daily. Patients with volume depletion should have this issue corrected before beginning the medication.</p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Diuretics</strong>: Concurrent use may increase urine volume.</li><li><strong>Insulin or Insulin Secretagogues</strong>: Increases the risk of hypoglycemia.</li><li><strong>Glycemic Monitoring</strong>: Urine glucose tests are not reliable as the drug increases urinary glucose excretion. Alternative methods should be used.</li><li><strong>1,5-Anhydroglucitol (1,5-AG) Assay</strong>: This assay is not suitable for monitoring glycemic control in patients taking SGLT2 inhibitors.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>History of hypersensitivity to Empa 10 mg or its ingredients.</li><li>Severe renal impairment, end-stage renal disease, or dialysis.</li></ul><p><strong>Potential Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common side effects include:</p><ul><li>Urinary tract infections</li><li>Female genital yeast infections</li><li>Dehydration</li><li>Hypotension</li><li>Dizziness, weakness, and increased thirst</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><p>Empa 10 mg should be used during pregnancy only if the potential benefits outweigh the risks, as there are no adequate studies in pregnant women. Its presence in breast milk is unknown, and use during breastfeeding is not recommended.</p><p><strong>Precautions and Warnings</strong></p><p>Renal function should be assessed before starting and periodically during treatment. Avoid initiating the medication in patients with an estimated glomerular filtration rate (eGFR) below 45 ml/min/1.73 m².</p><p><strong>Overdose Management</strong></p><p>In case of overdose, standard supportive measures should be undertaken, including gastrointestinal decontamination, clinical monitoring, and supportive care. The role of hemodialysis in removing the drug remains unstudied.</p><p><strong>Storage Instructions</strong></p><p>Store at a temperature below 30°C, in a cool, dry place, protected from light and moisture. Keep out of children’s reach.</p><p><strong>Drug Class and Mechanism of Action</strong></p><p>As an SGLT2 inhibitor, Empa 10 mg facilitates the excretion of glucose by inhibiting its renal reabsorption, aiding in hyperglycemia management, weight reduction, and blood pressure control.</p>', 'active', '1715_1734095043.webp', 11, 12, NULL, '2024-12-12 18:00:18', '2024-12-13 18:04:03'),
(151, 'Cildip', 'Cilnidipine', 10.00, 14, 'Tablet', '14 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '10mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p>Cildip 10 mg is primarily prescribed for managing hypertension to prevent end-organ damage. It is especially effective in elderly patients and those with diabetes or albuminuria. Additionally, it is commonly used in patients with chronic kidney disease due to its ability to protect renal function.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Cildip 10 mg belongs to the calcium-channel blockers class.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Cildip 10 mg is a dihydropyridine calcium-channel blocker. It works by binding to L-type voltage-dependent calcium channels in vascular smooth muscle cells, inhibiting calcium influx. This results in muscle relaxation and vasodilation, reducing blood pressure. Additionally, it suppresses norepinephrine release from sympathetic nerve endings by inhibiting N-type calcium channels, which helps prevent reflex tachycardia often associated with blood pressure reduction.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults</strong>: The recommended starting dose is 5–10 mg once daily, taken after breakfast. The maximum dose is 20 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Elderly Patients</strong>: Begin with the lowest effective dose (5 mg) to reduce the risk of hypotension.</li><li><strong>Pediatric Use</strong>: Safety and efficacy have not been established for children.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><p>Cildip 10 mg may interact with:</p><ul><li>Other antihypertensives</li><li>Medications causing hypotension (e.g., antipsychotics)</li><li>Drugs like quinidine, carbamazepine, phenytoin, rifampicin, cimetidine, and erythromycin.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Avoid use in patients with hypersensitivity to the drug or its components. It is contraindicated in conditions such as:</p><ul><li>Cardiogenic shock</li><li>Recent myocardial infarction (MI)</li><li>Acute unstable angina</li><li>Severe aortic stenosis.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common side effects include dizziness, flushing, headache, hypotension, peripheral edema, palpitations, gastrointestinal disturbances, lethargy, increased urination frequency, depression, and eye pain.</p><p><strong>Use During Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><p>Cildip 10 mg should not be used during pregnancy or in women who may become pregnant. For nursing mothers, the drug is not recommended unless absolutely necessary, and breastfeeding should be discontinued if administered.</p><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Use cautiously in patients with severe liver dysfunction or those with a history of adverse reactions to calcium antagonists.</li><li>Gradual dose reduction is advised during discontinuation to avoid adverse effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Store the medication at temperatures below 30°C, protected from light and moisture. Keep out of reach of children.</p><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>Cildip 10 mg reduces blood pressure by relaxing vascular smooth muscles through inhibition of calcium influx via L-type channels. Additionally, it suppresses the release of norepinephrine from sympathetic nerves by blocking N-type calcium channels.</p><p>This version avoids duplication while retaining all the critical information in an original format.</p>', 'active', '1388_1734008980.png', 7, 12, NULL, '2024-12-12 18:09:40', '2024-12-12 18:09:40'),
(152, 'Nidocard Retard', 'Nitroglycerin', 5.00, 14, 'Tablet', '14 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '2.6 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><br></p><p><strong>Indications of Nidocard Retard 2.6 mg</strong></p><p>Nidocard Retard 2.6 mg sublingual tablets are indicated for the acute relief or prophylaxis of angina pectoris caused by coronary artery disease.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Nitrates: Coronary vasodilators</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Nidocard Retard 2.6 mg releases nitric oxide (NO), activating guanylate cyclase and increasing guanosine 3\'5\' monophosphate levels in smooth muscle and other tissues. This cascade dephosphorylates myosin light chains, reducing muscle contraction and leading to vasodilation.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><p>Place one sublingual tablet under the tongue at the onset of an anginal attack. Repeat every five minutes as needed, up to three tablets within 15 minutes. Seek medical attention if pain persists.</p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>Monitor for hypotensive effects when combined with antihypertensives, beta-blockers, or phenothiazines.</li><li>Orthostatic hypotension may occur with concurrent use of calcium channel blockers or alcohol.</li><li>Aspirin may enhance the vasodilatory effects.</li><li>Avoid using with ergotamine or related drugs to prevent symptoms of ergotism.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Do not use in:</p><ul><li>Early myocardial infarction</li><li>Severe anemia</li><li>Increased intracranial pressure</li><li>Hypersensitivity to the drug</li><li>Patients on sildenafil citrate, due to increased risk of severe hypotension.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Headache (can be severe and persistent)</li><li>Vertigo, dizziness, weakness</li><li>Palpitations and postural hypotension</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><p>Use in pregnancy only if necessary. It is unknown if the drug is excreted in breast milk.</p><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Use the smallest effective dose to avoid tolerance development.</li><li>Caution in hypotensive or volume-depleted patients.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Store in a cool, dry place, away from light and heat. Keep out of reach of children.</p><p>Let me know if you\'d like more information!</p>', 'active', '281_1734009336.png', 9, 12, NULL, '2024-12-12 18:15:36', '2024-12-12 18:15:36'),
(153, 'Nitrin SR', 'Nitroglycerin', 5.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '2.6 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p>Nitrin SR 2.6 mg sublingual tablets are used for managing acute angina pectoris attacks or for preventing such episodes in individuals with coronary artery disease. Below is a detailed outline of its indications, usage, and precautions:</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Category:</strong> Nitrates</li><li><strong>Action:</strong> Coronary vasodilators</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li>Nitrin SR 2.6 mg generates nitric oxide (NO), which activates guanylate cyclase.</li><li>This increases guanosine 3\',5\'-cyclic monophosphate levels, leading to smooth muscle relaxation and vasodilation.</li><li>The result is reduced myocardial oxygen demand and relief of angina.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li>Place one sublingual tablet under the tongue at the onset of an anginal attack.</li><li>Repeat every 5 minutes if necessary, up to 3 tablets within 15 minutes.</li><li>Seek immediate medical attention if pain persists after 3 doses.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>Combining with antihypertensive drugs, beta-blockers, or phenothiazines may intensify hypotension.</li><li>Calcium channel blockers or alcohol can enhance hypotensive effects.</li><li>Aspirin may amplify vasodilatory and hemodynamic effects.</li><li>Avoid ergotamine or related drugs unless monitored for ergotism.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Not for use in early myocardial infarction, severe anemia, or elevated intracranial pressure.</li><li>Avoid in patients with known hypersensitivity to nitrates.</li><li>Contraindicated with sildenafil citrate due to potentiation of hypotension.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Severe, persistent headache.</li><li>Occasional: Vertigo, dizziness, weakness, palpitations, or postural hypotension.</li></ul><p><strong>Use During Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Use only if necessary during pregnancy.</li><li>Unknown if excreted in breast milk; caution is advised.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Use the minimum effective dose to prevent tolerance.</li><li>Exercise caution in patients with hypotension or volume depletion.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place, away from light and heat.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p>This summary ensures adherence to guidelines while avoiding verbatim copying. Let me know if you need further adjustments!</p>', 'active', '215_1734011549.png', 1, 12, NULL, '2024-12-12 18:52:29', '2024-12-12 18:52:29'),
(154, 'Galvus Met', 'Vildagliptin + Metformin Hydrochloride', 34.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '50 mg+850 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p>Galvus Met 50 mg + 850 mg is prescribed as a supplementary treatment alongside diet and exercise to enhance glycemic control in individuals with type 2 diabetes mellitus. It is specifically intended for patients whose blood sugar levels are inadequately controlled with either Metformin Hydrochloride or Vildagliptin alone, or for those already using the combination of these two medications as separate tablets.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>This medication belongs to the class of combination oral hypoglycemic agents.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Vildagliptin:</strong> Functions as a DPP-4 (Dipeptidyl peptidase-4) inhibitor, which prevents the degradation of incretin hormones GLP-1 and GIP. This action leads to elevated levels of these hormones, enhancing insulin secretion from beta cells and reducing glucagon release from alpha cells. The resulting increase in the insulin-to-glucagon ratio helps lower hepatic glucose production during hyperglycemia, thereby improving fasting and postprandial blood glucose levels.</li><li><strong>Metformin Hydrochloride:</strong> A biguanide oral antidiabetic, it lowers blood sugar levels by reducing hepatic glucose production, enhancing peripheral glucose uptake, and decreasing glucose absorption in the intestines. Unlike sulfonylureas, Metformin does not cause hypoglycemia under normal conditions.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><p>Adults are generally prescribed one tablet twice daily, in the morning and evening, based on their current Metformin dose. Patients switching from separate Vildagliptin and Metformin tablets may transition to this combination at equivalent doses. The total daily dose of Vildagliptin should not exceed 100 mg. To minimize gastrointestinal side effects, it is recommended to take this medication with or just after meals.</p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><p>No significant pharmacokinetic interactions have been reported between Vildagliptin and Metformin. As Vildagliptin does not involve cytochrome P450 enzymes, its potential for drug interactions is minimal. Co-administration with agents such as furosemide, nifedipine, or glyburide may slightly alter Metformin\'s pharmacokinetics without affecting its renal clearance.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Galvus Met 50 mg + 850 mg should not be used in individuals with:</p><ul><li>Known hypersensitivity to its components.</li><li>Renal disease or significant renal dysfunction.</li><li>Conditions such as acute myocardial infarction or septicemia.</li><li>Acute or chronic metabolic acidosis, including diabetic ketoacidosis.</li></ul><p><strong>Warnings and Precautions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Lactic Acidosis Risk:</strong> Monitor for symptoms of lactic acidosis and discontinue immediately if suspected.</li><li><strong>Renal Function:</strong> Check serum creatinine levels regularly, especially in elderly patients or those on medications affecting renal function.</li><li><strong>Hepatic Function:</strong> Liver function tests should be conducted before initiating treatment and periodically thereafter. Discontinue use if significant liver enzyme elevations or liver dysfunction occur.</li><li>Discontinue the medication 48 hours prior to surgeries requiring general anesthesia and resume only after 48 hours post-surgery.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><p>This combination is not recommended during pregnancy unless potential benefits outweigh risks. Its excretion in human milk is unknown, so use in breastfeeding women is not advised.</p><p><strong>Pediatric and Geriatric Use</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pediatrics:</strong> Not recommended for patients under 18 years due to insufficient data on safety and efficacy.</li><li><strong>Geriatrics:</strong> Regular monitoring of renal function is essential as kidney function tends to decline with age.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common side effects include headache, dizziness, nausea, tremors, and hypoglycemia.</p><p><strong>Storage Instructions</strong></p><p>Store in a cool, dry place away from direct light and heat. Keep out of reach of children.</p><p>This revision simplifies and paraphrases the original text, ensuring clarity and uniqueness while maintaining all essential details. Let me know if further refinements are needed!</p>', 'active', '721_1734011906.png', 40, 12, NULL, '2024-12-12 18:58:26', '2024-12-12 18:58:55'),
(155, 'Vastarel MR', 'Trimetazidine Dihydrochloride', 12.00, 30, 'Tablet', '30 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '35 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications for Vastarel MR 35 mg</strong></p><p>Vastarel MR 35 mg is prescribed as an add-on therapy in adults for the symptomatic management of stable angina pectoris. It is intended for patients who are inadequately controlled by or intolerant to first-line antianginal medications.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>This medication belongs to the class of \"Other Anti-anginal &amp; Anti-ischaemic Drugs.\"</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Vastarel MR 35 mg contains trimetazidine, the first 3-keto acyl CoA thiolase (KAT) inhibitor. It works as a metabolic anti-ischemic agent, offering benefits for coronary patients. By blocking the fatty acid metabolic pathway via KAT inhibition, it redirects oxygen to the glucose pathway. The glucose pathway is more efficient in energy production, ensuring better energy output for the heart. Additionally, glucose oxidation reduces lactic acid production, thereby alleviating angina symptoms.</p><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><p>The recommended dosage is:</p><ul><li><strong>35 mg tablet</strong>: Taken twice daily with meals.</li><li><strong>20 mg tablet</strong>: Taken three times daily with meals.</li></ul><p>Patients should be evaluated after three months of treatment, and therapy should be discontinued if no benefits are observed.</p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><p>No significant interactions with other medications have been reported. This includes beta-blockers, calcium channel blockers, nitrates, heparin, lipid-lowering agents, or digitalis preparations.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Trimetazidine should not be used in individuals with:</p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to the active ingredient or excipients.</li><li>Parkinson’s disease, parkinsonian symptoms, tremors, or restless leg syndrome.</li><li>Severe renal impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Trimetazidine is generally well-tolerated. Common side effects may include:</p><ul><li>Dizziness, headache, abdominal discomfort, diarrhea, dyspepsia, nausea, vomiting.</li><li>Skin reactions such as rash, itching, and hives.</li><li>Fatigue or weakness (asthenia).</li></ul><p><strong>Use During Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy</strong>: Limited data is available on its use during pregnancy. While animal studies have not shown harmful reproductive effects, its use during pregnancy is generally avoided as a precaution.</li><li><strong>Breastfeeding</strong>: The excretion of trimetazidine in breast milk is unknown, and potential risks to infants cannot be excluded. It is not recommended for use during breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions and Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Trimetazidine is not intended to treat acute angina attacks, unstable angina, or myocardial infarction.</li><li>It should be used as part of a comprehensive angina management plan.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Instructions</strong></p><p>Store in a dry place, away from light and heat. Keep out of the reach of children.</p><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>Vastarel MR 35 mg optimizes heart metabolism by shifting oxygen utilization from fatty acid oxidation to glucose oxidation, enhancing energy efficiency and reducing lactic acid production, thereby alleviating angina symptoms.</p><p><br></p><p>This revision ensures originality while maintaining the integrity of the information. Let me know if further changes are needed!</p>', 'active', '60_1734012273.jpg', 41, 12, NULL, '2024-12-12 19:04:33', '2024-12-12 19:04:57'),
(156, 'Olmesan', 'Olmesartan Medoxomil', 10.00, 15, 'Tablet', '15 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '20mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p>Olmesan 20 mg is prescribed to manage hypertension and can be used independently or in combination with other antihypertensive medications.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Angiotensin II receptor blocker (ARB).</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Olmesartan medoxomil selectively inhibits the angiotensin II (AT1) receptor, blocking the vasoconstrictive and aldosterone-secreting effects of angiotensin II. This action increases plasma renin and angiotensin levels while reducing plasma aldosterone. Angiotensin II is central to the pathophysiology of hypertension.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults:</strong> Initial dose is 10 mg once daily. If needed, increase to 20 mg daily. Maximum dose: 40 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Geriatric Use:</strong> No dose adjustment needed, though close monitoring is advised.</li><li><strong>Special Populations:</strong> In hepatic or renal impairment, the maximum dose is 20 mg daily. Initiate with caution in volume-depleted patients.</li><li><strong>Pediatrics:</strong> Not established for use.</li><li>Olmesan can be taken with or without food.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>No significant interactions with other drugs.</li><li>Food does not alter its absorption.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Hypersensitivity to any component of Olmesan.</p><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common:</strong> Back pain, headache, diarrhea, respiratory infections, and hyperglycemia.</li><li><strong>Rare:</strong> Chest pain, edema, and arthritis.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> Contraindicated, especially in the second and third trimesters (Category D).</li><li><strong>Lactation:</strong> Excretion in human milk is unknown; consider discontinuing nursing or the drug.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><p>Monitor renal function, particularly in patients with conditions such as severe heart failure, where the renin-angiotensin-aldosterone system is critical. Overuse may lead to renal dysfunction or failure.</p><p><strong>Overdose Management</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Symptoms:</strong> Hypotension and tachycardia, or bradycardia if vagal stimulation occurs.</li><li><strong>Treatment:</strong> Gastric lavage, emesis, and supportive cardiovascular care.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><p>Keep below 30°C, away from light and moisture. Store out of children\'s reach.</p><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>Olmesartan inhibits angiotensin II activity by blocking the AT1 receptor, reducing vasoconstriction and aldosterone secretion without affecting ACE activity or bradykinin degradation.</p><p>This summary avoids duplicating phrasing while maintaining clarity and completeness. Let me know if you need any further adjustments!</p><p><br></p><p><br></p>', 'active', '1670_1734012765.jpg', 3, 12, NULL, '2024-12-12 19:12:45', '2024-12-12 19:12:45'),
(157, 'Linatab', 'Linagliptin', 20.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '5mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Linatab 5 mg</strong></p><p><strong>Linatab 5 mg</strong> is indicated for the management of type 2 diabetes mellitus in adults to improve glycaemic control:</p><ul><li><strong>As monotherapy:</strong> For patients who cannot achieve adequate glycaemic control through diet and exercise alone and for whom metformin is unsuitable due to renal impairment or intolerance.</li><li><strong>As combination therapy:</strong> When metformin alone, or dual therapy with metformin and other agents, fails to provide sufficient glycaemic control. For example, Linatab can be used alongside a sulfonylurea.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Dipeptidyl Peptidase-4 (DPP-4) inhibitor</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Linatab 5 mg works by inhibiting the enzyme <strong>DPP-4</strong>, which degrades incretin hormones such as <strong>GLP-1 (glucagon-like peptide-1)</strong> and <strong>GIP (glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide)</strong>. This results in increased levels of active incretins, which:</p><ol><li>Stimulate insulin secretion from pancreatic beta cells in a glucose-dependent manner.</li><li>Suppress glucagon secretion from pancreatic alpha cells.</li></ol><p>The net effect is improved glucose regulation.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Recommended Dose:</strong> 5 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>With Metformin:</strong> Maintain a consistent dosing regimen when combined with metformin.</li><li><strong>With Sulfonylurea:</strong> Consider reducing the sulfonylurea dose to lower the risk of hypoglycemia.</li><li><strong>Renal Impairment:</strong> No dose adjustment is required.</li><li><strong>Timing:</strong> Can be taken at any time of day, with or without food.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><p>Linatab 5 mg:</p><ul><li>Does not inhibit significant cytochrome P450 enzymes (CYP isozymes).</li><li>Is a weak inhibitor of CYP3A4 but unlikely to cause significant drug interactions.</li><li>Has no major effect on the pharmacokinetics of drugs like metformin, glyburide, simvastatin, warfarin, digoxin, or oral contraceptives.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any active ingredient or excipient in the formulation.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Potential side effects include:</p><ul><li>Hypoglycemia (especially when used with sulfonylurea or insulin).</li><li>Nasopharyngitis.</li><li>Cough.</li><li>Pancreatitis (rare).</li></ul><p><strong>Use During Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy Category B:</strong> Use during pregnancy only if the potential benefit outweighs the risk, as adequate studies in pregnant women are lacking.</li><li><strong>Lactation:</strong> It is unclear if the drug is excreted in breast milk; caution is advised.</li></ul><h3><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></h3><ul><li>Avoid use in individuals with known hypersensitivity to the drug or its components.</li><li>Regular monitoring is recommended to manage the risk of hypoglycemia, particularly when used in combination therapies.</li></ul><h3><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></h3><p>Store in a dry place, protected from heat and light. Keep out of reach of children.</p><p><br></p><p>This summary provides an informative yet concise overview of Linatab 5 mg without copying the original text. Let me know if you’d like any modifications!</p>', 'active', '1429_1734013347.jpg', 2, 12, NULL, '2024-12-12 19:22:27', '2024-12-12 19:22:27'),
(158, 'Metacard MR', 'Trimetazidine Dihydrochloride', 10.00, 14, 'Tablet', '14 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '35 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Metacard MR 35 mg</strong></p><p>Metacard MR 35 mg is recommended as an additional therapy for adults with stable angina pectoris who do not respond adequately to or cannot tolerate first-line antianginal treatments.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Belongs to the class of \"Other Anti-anginal &amp; Anti-ischaemic drugs.\"</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Metacard MR 35 mg contains trimetazidine, a metabolic anti-ischemic agent classified as a 3-ketoacyl-CoA thiolase (KAT) inhibitor. It shifts the energy production of the heart from fatty acids to glucose oxidation by inhibiting the KAT enzyme. This improves energy efficiency since glucose oxidation produces more energy per unit of oxygen than fatty acid oxidation. Additionally, it reduces lactic acid production, which helps alleviate angina symptoms.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><p>The standard dose is 35 mg twice daily, taken during meals. Alternatively, 20 mg tablets may be taken three times daily. After three months of treatment, the benefits should be evaluated, and discontinuation is advised if no significant improvement is observed.</p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><p>No significant interactions with other drugs, including beta-blockers, calcium channel blockers, nitrates, heparin, lipid-lowering agents, or digitalis preparations, have been reported.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Metacard MR 35 mg should not be used in patients with hypersensitivity to trimetazidine or its components, Parkinson’s disease, parkinsonian symptoms, tremors, restless leg syndrome, or severe renal impairment.</p><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common side effects include dizziness, headache, gastrointestinal disturbances (abdominal pain, diarrhea, nausea, vomiting, dyspepsia), skin reactions (rash, pruritus, urticaria), and fatigue.</p><p><strong>Use During Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><p>There is insufficient data on trimetazidine use during pregnancy. Animal studies have not shown harmful reproductive effects, but caution is advised, and use during pregnancy should be avoided. The excretion of trimetazidine in human milk is unknown, so breastfeeding should be avoided while using this medication.</p><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Metacard MR 35 mg is not intended for the treatment of angina attacks or acute coronary syndromes like myocardial infarction.</li><li>It should not replace initial treatment for unstable angina.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Store in a dry, cool place away from light and heat. Keep out of reach of children.</p><p>Let me know if you\'d like further adjustments!</p>', 'active', '33_1734013644.png', 29, 12, NULL, '2024-12-12 19:27:24', '2024-12-12 19:27:24'),
(159, 'Glipita M', 'Sitagliptin + Metformin Hydrochloride', 16.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '50 mg+500 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p>Glipita M is a combination medication used to manage high blood sugar in individuals with type 2 diabetes mellitus. It helps prevent complications such as kidney damage, blindness, heart attacks, or strokes. This medication works best when combined with a healthy diet and regular exercise. It may be prescribed alone or alongside other diabetes medicines.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Combination Oral Hypoglycemic Preparations</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Sitagliptin</strong>: A DPP-4 inhibitor that enhances incretin hormones (GLP-1 and GIP) to regulate glucose levels by increasing insulin secretion and reducing glucagon release when blood glucose is elevated.</li><li><strong>Metformin</strong>: A biguanide that reduces hepatic glucose production, enhances insulin sensitivity, and improves peripheral glucose uptake without causing hypoglycemia or hyperinsulinemia.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Standard Tablet</strong>: Twice daily with meals to reduce gastrointestinal side effects.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Patients not on metformin: Start with 50 mg Sitagliptin/500 mg Metformin twice daily, with gradual dose escalation.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Patients on metformin: Adjust dosage based on current metformin intake, ensuring a total daily Sitagliptin dose of 100 mg.</li><li><strong>Extended-Release Tablet</strong>: Administer once daily with a meal (preferably in the evening). The dose should not exceed 100 mg Sitagliptin and 2000 mg Metformin daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Cationic Drugs</strong>: Use cautiously, as they are eliminated through renal tubular secretion.</li><li><strong>Phenprocoumon &amp; Levothyroxine</strong>: May interact with metformin; monitor blood glucose or INR levels and adjust dosages as necessary.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Renal dysfunction or creatinine clearance issues.</li><li>Metabolic acidosis or diabetic ketoacidosis.</li><li>Hypersensitivity to Sitagliptin or Metformin.</li><li>Temporary discontinuation is advised before radiological studies involving iodinated contrast agents.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Diarrhea, nausea, vomiting, headache, sore throat, or upset stomach.</li><li>Rare: Hypoglycemia (when combined with sulfonylureas or insulin), nasopharyngitis, or lactic acidosis.</li><li>Severe: Allergic reactions (e.g., Stevens-Johnson syndrome, anaphylaxis).</li></ul><p><strong>Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Elderly</strong>: Use cautiously due to potential renal function decline.</li><li><strong>Pediatrics</strong>: Safety and effectiveness in patients under 18 years of age are not established.</li><li><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong>: Limited data available; use only if clearly needed.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Regular monitoring of renal function, blood glucose, and vitamin B12 levels is essential.</li><li>Avoid excessive alcohol consumption.</li><li>Discontinue during stress or illness requiring significant metabolic adjustments (e.g., surgery, infections).</li><li>Immediate medical attention is needed for symptoms of lactic acidosis or pancreatitis.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><p>Store below 25°C in a dry, dark place. Keep out of reach of children. Do not use past the expiry date.</p><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>This tablet combines Sitagliptin (a DPP-4 inhibitor) and Metformin (a biguanide) to enhance glucose regulation through complementary mechanisms: incretin hormone enhancement, hepatic glucose reduction, and improved peripheral insulin sensitivity.</p><p>Ensure regular consultations with healthcare providers for dosage adjustments and monitoring.</p>', 'active', '674_1734029137.jpg', 3, 12, NULL, '2024-12-12 23:45:37', '2024-12-12 23:45:37'),
(160, 'Mixtard 30 Vial', 'Insulin Human [rDNA] + Isophane Insulin Human', 415.00, 1, 'x 10 ml vial', '10 ml vial', 'Injection', '30%+70% in 100 IU/ml', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Mixtard 30 Vial 100 IU/ml</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Type 1 Diabetes</strong>: Suitable for all patients with type 1 diabetes.</li><li><strong>Type 2 Diabetes</strong>: For patients whose blood sugar levels cannot be adequately controlled by diet or oral hypoglycemic agents.</li><li><strong>Acute Conditions</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Hyperosmolar non-ketotic syndrome.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">During periods of significant stress (e.g., serious illness, surgery).</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Gestational Diabetes</strong>: Safe for controlling blood sugar levels during pregnancy.</li></ol><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Insulin Human (rDNA)</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>30/70 Mixture</strong>: Contains 30% soluble insulin (regular) and 70% isophane insulin.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>50/50 Mixture</strong>: Contains 50% soluble insulin and 50% isophane insulin.</li><li><strong>Concentration</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">40 IU/ml (1.388 mg/ml).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">100 IU/ml (3.47 mg/ml).</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Insulin with medium action.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Mechanism</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Structurally identical to natural insulin, produced using recombinant DNA technology.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Facilitates glucose uptake and utilization in liver, muscle, and fat tissues.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Reduces blood sugar by promoting glycogenesis and inhibiting gluconeogenesis.</li><li><strong>Action Profile</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Onset: Within 30 minutes.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Peak: 2–8 hours post-injection.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Duration: Approximately 24 hours.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Type 1 Diabetes</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Average: 0.5–1.0 IU/kg/day.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Pre-pubertal children: 0.7–1.0 IU/kg/day.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Insulin resistance (e.g., puberty, obesity): Higher doses may be required.</li><li><strong>Type 2 Diabetes</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Initial: 0.3–0.6 IU/kg/day.</li><li><strong>Individual Variability</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Dosage influenced by factors like diet, activity level, and medical conditions. Always follow a physician’s guidance.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Timing</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Administer 30 minutes before meals or snacks containing carbohydrates.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Injection Sites</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Upper arm, thigh, buttock, or abdominal wall (preferred for faster absorption).</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Procedure</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Wash hands.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Gently mix the vial by rotating it.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Clean the vial stopper and injection site with alcohol.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Use a syringe to draw the correct dose.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Inject subcutaneously at a 45° angle and hold for at least 6 seconds.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Rotate injection sites to avoid tissue damage.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Increased Insulin Requirement</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Oral contraceptives, thyroid hormones, corticosteroids.</li><li><strong>Reduced Insulin Requirement</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Hypoglycemic agents like salicylates, sulfonamides, and antidepressants.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypoglycemia.</li><li>Known hypersensitivity to insulin or excipients.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Hypoglycemia (most frequent and can occur rapidly).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Local reactions (redness, itching, swelling at injection site).</li><li><strong>Rare</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Allergic reactions due to disinfectants or improper injection techniques.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Safe during pregnancy as insulin does not cross the placental barrier.</li><li>No adverse effects on breastfeeding infants.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Hyperglycemia</strong>: Can occur from improper dosing or discontinuation.</li><li><strong>Hypoglycemia</strong>: May result from excessive dosing, skipped meals, or unplanned physical activity.</li><li><strong>Overdose Management</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Immediate medical attention for hypoglycemia.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Adjust therapy, diet, or exercise if frequent episodes occur.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Refrigerate at 2–8°C. Do not freeze.</li><li>For in-use insulin, store at room temperature (&lt;25°C) for up to 1 month, away from heat and light.</li></ul>', 'active', '9551_1746722117.webp', 42, 12, NULL, '2024-12-13 00:12:23', '2025-05-08 20:35:17');
INSERT INTO `products` (`id`, `productName`, `genericName`, `retail_max_price`, `cart_qty_inc`, `cart_text`, `unit_in_pack`, `type`, `quantity`, `prescription`, `feature`, `description`, `status`, `coverImage`, `company_id`, `category_id`, `add_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(161, 'Lijenta', 'Linagliptin', 22.00, 15, 'Tablet', '15 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '5 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Lijenta 5 mg</strong></p><p>Lijenta 5 mg is used to manage <strong>type 2 diabetes mellitus</strong> in adults, helping to improve glycemic control.</p><ul><li><strong>As Monotherapy</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For patients unable to manage diabetes through diet and exercise alone.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">When metformin is unsuitable due to renal impairment or intolerance.</li><li><strong>As Combination Therapy</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For patients whose glycemic control remains inadequate despite diet, exercise, and metformin alone.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Can be combined with other antidiabetic drugs like sulfonylureas when dual therapy is insufficient.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p><strong>Dipeptidyl Peptidase-4 (DPP-4) Inhibitor</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Lijenta 5 mg helps regulate blood sugar levels by inhibiting <strong>DPP-4</strong>, an enzyme that breaks down incretin hormones such as GLP-1 (glucagon-like peptide-1) and GIP (glucose-dependent insulinotropic polypeptide).</p><ul><li><strong>Action</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Enhances insulin release from pancreatic beta cells in a glucose-dependent manner.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Suppresses glucagon release from pancreatic alpha cells, reducing blood sugar levels.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Standard Dosage</strong>: Take <strong>5 mg once daily</strong>, with or without food.</li><li><strong>Combination Therapy</strong>: When combined with metformin or sulfonylureas, dosing adjustments for sulfonylurea may help reduce hypoglycemia risk.</li><li><strong>Renal Impairment</strong>: No dose adjustment required.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><p>Lijenta 5 mg has minimal potential for clinically significant drug interactions:</p><ul><li>Does not meaningfully affect the pharmacokinetics of drugs such as metformin, glyburide, simvastatin, warfarin, digoxin, or oral contraceptives.</li><li>Weakly inhibits CYP3A4 but does not impact other CYP enzymes.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to <strong>Lijenta 5 mg</strong> or its components.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Possible risks include:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Hypoglycemia (when used with metformin and sulfonylureas).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Nasopharyngitis.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cough.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Pancreatitis (rare).</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy</strong>: Category B. Insufficient studies on pregnant women; use only if clearly needed.</li><li><strong>Lactation</strong>: Unclear if it passes into breast milk; consult with a healthcare provider before use.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid use in cases of known hypersensitivity to any active or inactive ingredients.</li><li>Monitor for signs of pancreatitis or allergic reactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry place, away from heat and light.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>Lijenta 5 mg works by increasing levels of active incretin hormones, which:</p><ul><li>Stimulate insulin secretion in response to meals.</li><li>Suppress excessive glucagon secretion, helping to lower blood glucose.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '165_1734031478.png', 11, 12, NULL, '2024-12-13 00:24:38', '2024-12-13 00:24:38'),
(162, 'Lijenta-M', 'Linagliptin + Metformin Hydrochloride', 13.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '2.5 mg+500 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p>Lijenta-M is prescribed alongside diet and exercise to enhance glycemic control in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus when treatment with both <strong>Linagliptin</strong> and <strong>Metformin Hydrochloride</strong> is considered appropriate.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Oral hypoglycemic combination drugs.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Linagliptin</strong>: A dipeptidyl peptidase-4 (DPP-4) inhibitor that increases active incretin hormone levels, enhancing insulin secretion in response to glucose and reducing glucagon release from pancreatic α-cells.</li><li><strong>Metformin Hydrochloride</strong>: A biguanide class antihyperglycemic that lowers both fasting and post-meal glucose by inhibiting hepatic glucose production, reducing intestinal glucose absorption, and improving peripheral glucose uptake and utilization.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Immediate-Release Tablets</strong>:</li><li>The dosage is tailored for efficacy and tolerance. Maximum: 2.5 mg Linagliptin and 1000 mg Metformin Hydrochloride twice daily, taken with meals.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Initiation in new patients</strong>: Start with 2.5 mg Linagliptin + 500 mg Metformin twice daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For those on Metformin</strong>: Combine 2.5 mg Linagliptin with the current Metformin dose twice daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Switch from individual components</strong>: Use equivalent doses in combination form.</li><li><strong>Extended-Release Tablets</strong>:</li><li>Not to exceed Linagliptin 5 mg and Metformin Hydrochloride 2000 mg daily. Administer once daily with food.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Starting dose for Metformin-naïve patients</strong>: 5 mg Linagliptin + 1000 mg Metformin extended-release once daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For those on Metformin</strong>: Match the Metformin dose and add 5 mg Linagliptin total daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Switch from immediate-release forms</strong>: Match the total daily doses when transitioning to the extended-release version.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Cationic drugs</strong> (e.g., amiloride, digoxin) may reduce Metformin elimination.</li><li><strong>P-glycoprotein/CYP3A4 inducers</strong> (e.g., rifampin) may reduce Linagliptin efficacy.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Renal impairment or conditions associated with a higher risk of lactic acidosis.</li><li>Known hypersensitivity to Linagliptin or Metformin.</li><li>Acute or chronic metabolic acidosis, including diabetic ketoacidosis.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Nasopharyngitis, diarrhea.</li><li>Risk of hypoglycemia when used with sulfonylureas.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Limited data in pregnant or breastfeeding women. Use only if clearly necessary. Exercise caution in lactating mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Discontinue immediately if lactic acidosis is suspected.</li><li>Cases of acute pancreatitis reported; discontinue if suspected.</li><li>Temporarily stop during procedures requiring iodinated contrast or restricted food intake.</li><li>Monitor for Vitamin B12 deficiency with long-term Metformin use.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose</strong></p><ul><li>Linagliptin overdose: Supportive measures; hemodialysis unlikely to be effective.</li><li>Metformin overdose: Risk of lactic acidosis; hemodialysis may assist in removal.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><p>Store below 30°C in a dry place, away from light and moisture. Keep out of reach of children.</p><p><strong>Drug Class</strong></p><p>Oral hypoglycemic combination preparations.</p><p><br></p><p>This version summarizes the key points in an original format without directly copying.</p>', 'active', '1115_1734033695.png', 11, 12, NULL, '2024-12-13 01:01:35', '2024-12-13 01:01:35'),
(163, 'Galvus Met', 'Vildagliptin + Metformin Hydrochloride', 33.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '50 mg+500 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p>Galvus Met 50 mg+500 mg is prescribed to manage blood sugar levels in individuals with type 2 diabetes mellitus. It is used alongside dietary adjustments and exercise in patients whose diabetes remains uncontrolled with either <strong>Metformin Hydrochloride</strong> or <strong>Vildagliptin</strong> alone, or for those already using these two medications as separate tablets.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>This medication belongs to the class of <strong>combination oral hypoglycemic agents</strong>.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p><strong>Vildagliptin</strong> works by inhibiting the DPP-4 enzyme, which breaks down incretin hormones (GLP-1 and GIP). This inhibition boosts incretin levels, enhancing insulin secretion from beta cells and reducing glucagon release from alpha cells. The resulting effect is a decrease in glucose production by the liver, improving blood sugar control during fasting and post-meal periods.</p><p><strong>Metformin Hydrochloride</strong>, a biguanide, lowers glucose levels by reducing its production in the liver, decreasing its intestinal absorption, and improving peripheral insulin sensitivity.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><p>For adults, the dosage depends on the patient’s current Metformin regimen. Typically, one tablet is taken twice daily—morning and evening. If switching from separate Vildagliptin and Metformin tablets, patients can transition to this fixed-dose combination with equivalent components. Doses above 100 mg of Vildagliptin daily are not recommended. To minimize gastrointestinal discomfort, take the medication with or immediately after food.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><p>No significant pharmacokinetic interactions were observed between Vildagliptin and Metformin. However, other drugs like <strong>furosemide</strong>, <strong>nifedipine</strong>, and <strong>glyburide</strong> may influence Metformin levels. Vildagliptin does not interfere with CYP450 enzymes, reducing the risk of interactions with medications processed by these pathways.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>This medication is contraindicated in patients with:</p><ul><li>Known hypersensitivity to its components.</li><li>Renal disease or dysfunction.</li><li>Congestive heart failure or conditions involving acute or chronic metabolic acidosis, including diabetic ketoacidosis.</li><li>Those undergoing radiological procedures involving iodinated contrast agents.</li></ul><p><strong>Common Side Effects</strong></p><p>Patients may experience headache, dizziness, nausea, tremors, or hypoglycemia.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Special Precautions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Lactic Acidosis Risk</strong>: Metformin accumulation may lead to lactic acidosis. Treatment should be discontinued if suspected.</li><li><strong>Liver Function</strong>: Regular liver function tests are recommended. Discontinue use if abnormalities persist or worsen.</li><li><strong>Renal Function</strong>: Periodic monitoring of kidney function is essential, particularly in elderly patients.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong>: Not recommended unless benefits outweigh risks. It is unclear if the components are excreted in breast milk.</li><li><strong>Pediatric Use</strong>: Safety and efficacy in individuals under 18 years have not been established.</li><li><strong>Elderly Patients</strong>: Regular monitoring of kidney function is advised.</li><li><strong>Hepatic Impairment</strong>: Not recommended for patients with significant liver issues.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><p>Store in a dry, cool place away from direct heat and light. Keep out of reach of children.</p><p><br></p><p>This revised content maintains accuracy while ensuring originality. Let me know if you\'d like further refinements or additional sections!</p>', 'active', '859_1734034114.png', 40, 12, NULL, '2024-12-13 01:08:34', '2024-12-13 01:09:16'),
(164, 'Bizoran', 'Amlodipine + Olmesartan Medoxomil', 20.00, 15, 'Tablet', '15 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '5 mg+40 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications for Bizoran 5 mg + 40 mg</strong></p><ul><li>Treatment of hypertension, either as monotherapy or in combination with other antihypertensive agents.</li><li>Suitable as initial therapy for patients likely to require multiple agents to achieve blood pressure control.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Combined antihypertensive preparations.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Amlodipine:</strong> A dihydropyridine calcium channel blocker that reduces blood pressure by inhibiting calcium ion influx in vascular smooth and cardiac muscle, causing vasodilation and decreased peripheral vascular resistance.</li><li><strong>Olmesartan:</strong> An angiotensin II receptor blocker (AT1 subtype) that lowers blood pressure by dilating blood vessels without altering pulse rate.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Initial Therapy:</strong> Begin with one tablet (5 mg/20 mg) daily. Increase dosage after 1–2 weeks if needed, up to two tablets (10 mg/40 mg) daily. Can be taken with or without food. Avoid initiating in patients aged ≥75 years or with hepatic impairment.</li><li><strong>Replacement Therapy:</strong> May replace separately titrated components. Adjust dosages based on individual needs if blood pressure remains uncontrolled.</li><li><strong>Add-on Therapy:</strong> Used to enhance blood pressure control when Amlodipine or Olmesartan alone is insufficient.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>No significant interactions observed between Amlodipine and Olmesartan or their combination with other drugs.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Amlodipine, Olmesartan, or any excipients.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Edema, dizziness, flushing, palpitations.</li><li>Others: Vomiting, diarrhea, rhabdomyolysis, alopecia, pruritus, urticaria.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> Discontinue immediately upon detection of pregnancy. Second and third-trimester use can harm or cause death to the fetus.</li><li><strong>Lactation:</strong> Decide between discontinuing the drug or nursing based on its importance to the mother.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Fetal/Neonatal Risk:</strong> Discontinue if pregnancy is detected.</li><li><strong>Hypotension Risk:</strong> Monitor in volume- or salt-depleted patients.</li><li><strong>Severe Aortic Stenosis:</strong> Use cautiously due to vasodilation risks.</li><li><strong>Coronary Artery Disease:</strong> May increase angina or myocardial infarction risk during initiation or dose adjustments.</li><li><strong>Heart Failure:</strong> Use calcium channel blockers cautiously in patients with congestive heart failure.</li><li><strong>Renal &amp; Hepatic Impairment:</strong> Exercise caution, particularly in severe cases.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Olmesartan:</strong> Potential hypotension, tachycardia, or bradycardia due to vagal stimulation.</li><li><strong>Amlodipine:</strong> Possible severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, or prolonged systemic hypotension, which could lead to shock.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C in a cool, dry place away from light and moisture. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li>Safety and effectiveness in pediatric patients have not been established.</li></ul><p>Let me know if further refinements are needed!</p>', 'active', '510_1734034466.png', 3, 12, NULL, '2024-12-13 01:14:26', '2024-12-13 01:14:26'),
(165, 'NovoMix 30 Penfill', 'Biphasic Insulin Aspart [rDNA]', 780.00, 1, 'piece', '1 piece in a box', 'Penfill', '100IU per ml', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus</strong>: In adults and children.</li><li><strong>Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus</strong>: In adults.</li></ul><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><p>Each ml contains 100 units (3.5 mg) of Insulin Aspart, comprised of:</p><ul><li>30% soluble Insulin Aspart.</li><li>70% Insulin Aspart Protamine suspension.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Combination Insulin.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Mechanism</strong>: A human insulin analog that lowers blood glucose by stimulating peripheral glucose uptake and inhibiting hepatic glucose production.</li><li><strong>Onset and Duration</strong>: Rapid onset and intermediate duration.</li><li><strong>Production</strong>: Synthesized via recombinant DNA technology in <em>Saccharomyces cerevisiae</em>.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Subcutaneous Injection</strong>: Administer 5-10 minutes before meals.</li><li><strong>Insulin Pumps</strong>: Replace insulin every 6 days and infusion sets every 3 days. Avoid mixing with other insulins.</li><li><strong>Intravenous Use</strong>: Use in concentrations from 0.05 U/mL to 1.0 U/mL with appropriate infusion fluids.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong></p><ul><li>Follow hygiene protocols: Wash hands and inspect the vial.</li><li>Ensure thorough mixing (vial should appear cloudy).</li><li>Inject using a syringe with the correct dose, avoiding air bubbles.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Increase effect</strong>: ACE inhibitors, salicylates, oral antidiabetics.</li><li><strong>Decrease effect</strong>: Corticosteroids, diuretics, estrogen, atypical antipsychotics.</li><li><strong>Variable effects</strong>: Alcohol, beta-blockers, clonidine.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypoglycemia.</li><li>Hypersensitivity to Insulin Aspart or excipients.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Hypoglycemia.</li><li>Lipodystrophy.</li><li>Weight gain.</li><li>Peripheral edema.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy</strong>: Category B. Monitor glucose levels closely.</li><li><strong>Lactation</strong>: Uncertain excretion in breast milk; dose adjustments may be needed.</li><li><strong>Pediatrics</strong>: Not studied in children under 2 years with type 1 diabetes or those with type 2 diabetes.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Adjust dose cautiously in renal or hepatic impairment.</li><li>Monitor blood glucose levels regularly.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Management</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Mild Hypoglycemia</strong>: Treat with oral carbohydrates.</li><li><strong>Severe Hypoglycemia</strong>: Use parenteral glucose or glucagon.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Refrigerate at 2°C to 8°C. Do not freeze.</li><li>Insulin in use can be kept at room temperature for up to one month.</li></ul><p>This summary provides guidance but always consult a healthcare professional for personalized advice.</p>', 'active', '819_1734037126.png', 42, 12, NULL, '2024-12-13 01:58:46', '2024-12-13 19:59:56'),
(166, 'Jardian', 'Empagliflozin', 25.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Jardiance 10 mg</strong></p><p><strong>Jardiance 10 mg</strong> (empagliflozin) is used:</p><ol><li>As an adjunct to diet and exercise to enhance glycemic control in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus.</li><li>To lower the risk of cardiovascular death in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus who have established cardiovascular disease.</li></ol><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Sodium-glucose co-transporter-2 (SGLT2) inhibitors.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Jardiance 10 mg works by inhibiting SGLT2 co-transporters, responsible for glucose reabsorption in the kidneys. This action promotes increased glucose excretion in urine, thereby reducing blood glucose levels. Its effects extend to weight reduction, blood pressure control, and lowering hyperglycemia.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Initial Dose</strong>: 10 mg once daily, taken in the morning with or without food.</li><li><strong>Adjustment</strong>: If well-tolerated, the dose can be increased to 25 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Precaution</strong>: Correct any volume depletion before initiating treatment.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ol><li><strong>With Diuretics</strong>: Increases urine output.</li><li><strong>With Insulin or Insulin Secretagogues</strong>: Heightens the risk of hypoglycemia.</li><li><strong>Urine Glucose Tests</strong>: Not recommended for glycemic control monitoring due to increased glucose excretion.</li><li><strong>1,5-AG Assay</strong>: Avoid as it is unreliable for glycemic assessment in patients on SGLT2 inhibitors.</li></ol><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Jardiance 10 mg is contraindicated in:</p><ul><li>Individuals with hypersensitivity to the drug or its ingredients.</li><li>Severe renal impairment, end-stage renal disease, or those on dialysis.</li></ul><p><strong>Common Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Frequent</strong>: Urinary tract infections, female genital mycotic infections.</li><li><strong>Others</strong>: Dehydration, hypotension, dizziness, weakness, and increased thirst.</li></ul><p><strong>Use During Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy</strong>: Use only if the potential benefit outweighs risks to the fetus, as adequate studies are lacking.</li><li><strong>Lactation</strong>: Not recommended due to unknown excretion in breast milk.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Assess renal function before starting and periodically during treatment.</li><li>Not recommended for patients with an eGFR below 45 ml/min/1.73 m².</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Management</strong></p><p>In case of overdose:</p><ul><li>Remove unabsorbed material from the gastrointestinal tract.</li><li>Conduct clinical monitoring and provide supportive care.</li><li>Hemodialysis for empagliflozin removal has not been studied.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><p>Store below 30°C in a dry, cool place, away from light and moisture. Keep out of children\'s reach.</p><p><br></p><h3>Mode of Action</h3><p>Jardiance 10 mg inhibits SGLT2 co-transporters, reducing glucose reabsorption in the kidneys. This leads to increased glucose excretion and improved blood sugar control while aiding in weight loss and lowering blood pressure.</p>', 'active', '1251_1734038205.png', 3, 12, NULL, '2024-12-13 02:16:45', '2024-12-13 02:16:45'),
(167, 'Comet XR', 'Metformin Hydrochloride', 6.02, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '500 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p>Comet XR 500 mg is prescribed for managing type 2 diabetes mellitus, especially in overweight patients when dietary and exercise measures alone are insufficient for controlling blood glucose levels.</p><ul><li><strong>Adults</strong>: It can be used as a standalone treatment or combined with other oral antidiabetic drugs or insulin.</li><li><strong>Children (10 years and older) and Adolescents</strong>: It may be used alone or alongside insulin therapy.</li><li>Studies have shown that metformin reduces complications associated with diabetes in overweight adults when used as first-line treatment after dietary interventions fail.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Biguanides</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Metformin, the active ingredient, is an oral antidiabetic from the biguanide class. It lowers basal and postprandial glucose levels by:</p><ul><li>Reducing hepatic glucose production.</li><li>Decreasing glucose absorption in the intestines.</li><li>Enhancing insulin sensitivity and promoting peripheral glucose uptake and utilization.</li><li>Unlike sulfonylureas, it does not induce hypoglycemia under usual circumstances.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><p><em>Individualized dosing is essential for achieving efficacy while minimizing side effects.</em></p><ul><li><strong>Immediate Release Tablets</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Adults</strong>: Start with 500 mg twice daily or 850 mg once daily with meals. Increase by 500 mg weekly or 850 mg every two weeks, up to a maximum of 2000 mg daily, in divided doses. For patients requiring additional control, doses up to 2550 mg daily are permissible.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Children</strong>: Begin with 500 mg twice daily with meals. Incrementally increase by 500 mg weekly to a maximum of 2000 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Extended Release Tablets</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Adults</strong>: Start with 500 mg once daily with the evening meal. Weekly increments of 500 mg can be made, up to a maximum of 2000 mg daily. Alternatively, the dose may be split into 1000 mg twice daily with meals.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Children</strong>: Extended-release tablets are not recommended.</li><li><strong>Renal Impairment</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Avoid use if eGFR &lt;30 mL/min/1.73 m². Reassess therapy if eGFR falls below 45 mL/min/1.73 m².</li></ul><p><em>Note</em>: Swallow extended-release tablets whole; do not crush or chew.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>Carbonic anhydrase inhibitors (e.g., topiramate) can heighten the risk of lactic acidosis.</li><li>Drugs reducing metformin clearance (e.g., ranolazine, cimetidine) may increase accumulation.</li><li>Alcohol may amplify lactic acidosis risk.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to metformin or excipients.</li><li>Acute metabolic acidosis (e.g., diabetic ketoacidosis, lactic acidosis).</li><li>Severe renal impairment (eGFR &lt;30 mL/min/1.73 m²).</li><li>Acute or chronic diseases causing tissue hypoxia (e.g., heart failure, shock).</li><li>Severe liver dysfunction or excessive alcohol consumption.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common</strong>: Gastrointestinal disturbances like nausea, diarrhea, and abdominal pain (usually during therapy initiation).</li><li><strong>Rare/Serious</strong>: Lactic acidosis, vitamin B12 deficiency, peripheral neuropathy, and hepatobiliary issues (e.g., hepatitis).</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Metformin use in pregnancy should be replaced with insulin to maintain optimal blood sugar levels and reduce fetal risks.</li><li>While metformin is excreted in breast milk, adverse effects in infants are rare. However, caution is advised, and breastfeeding decisions should weigh the drug\'s benefits against potential risks.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Regular monitoring of renal function is essential, particularly in elderly or at-risk patients.</li><li>Metformin may reduce vitamin B12 levels over prolonged use; monitor for deficiency symptoms.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><p>Store below 30°C, shielded from light and moisture, and keep out of reach of children.</p><p>This version maintains the same factual content but ensures originality by rephrasing and restructuring the information.</p>', 'active', '1698_1734038963.png', 4, 12, NULL, '2024-12-13 02:29:23', '2024-12-13 02:29:23'),
(168, 'Atova', 'Atorvastatin Calcium', 20.00, 15, 'Tablet', '15 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '20mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Atova 20 mg Overview</strong></p><p><strong>Indications</strong>: Atova 20 mg is primarily used to manage lipid disorders, including:</p><ol><li><strong>Primary Hypercholesterolemia</strong>: Reduces total cholesterol, LDL cholesterol, and triglycerides.</li><li><strong>Familial Hypercholesterolemia</strong>: Effective in both heterozygous and homozygous types.</li><li><strong>Mixed Dyslipidemia (Fredrickson Type Ia, Ib)</strong>: Targets elevated cholesterol and triglycerides.</li><li><strong>Hypertriglyceridemia (Fredrickson Type IV)</strong>: Reduces elevated triglyceride levels.</li><li><strong>Dysbetalipoproteinemia (Fredrickson Type III)</strong>.</li><li><strong>Prevention of Cardiovascular Events</strong>: Reduces ischemic events in coronary artery disease patients with high LDL levels.</li><li><strong>Diabetes or Renal Transplantation-Associated Hypercholesterolemia</strong>.</li></ol><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Statins (HMG-CoA reductase inhibitors)</li><li>Anti-anginal &amp; Anti-ischemic agents</li></ul><p><strong>Mechanism of Action</strong></p><p>Atova (Atorvastatin) inhibits HMG-CoA reductase, a key enzyme in cholesterol synthesis. This action reduces cholesterol production in the liver and enhances LDL receptor activity, leading to lowered LDL cholesterol and triglyceride levels.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults</strong>: Starting dose is 10 mg once daily; may increase up to 80 mg/day based on response, with adjustments every 4 weeks.</li><li><strong>Children (10–18 years)</strong>: Starting dose is 10 mg daily, with a maximum of 20 mg/day for most indications. For familial hypercholesterolemia, doses up to 80 mg/day may be used.</li><li>Dose adjustments should be based on therapeutic response and tolerance.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><p>Atova 20 mg may interact with:</p><ul><li><strong>Increased Myopathy Risk</strong>: Cyclosporine, fibrates, erythromycin, azole antifungals, niacin.</li><li><strong>Monitoring Needed</strong>: When co-administered with digoxin, oral contraceptives, antacids, warfarin, or colestipol.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to atorvastatin or any component of the formulation.</li><li>Active liver disease or unexplained elevated liver enzyme levels.</li><li>Pregnancy and lactation.</li></ul><p><strong>Warnings &amp; Precautions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Liver Monitoring</strong>: Liver function tests should be performed before initiation and periodically thereafter.</li><li><strong>Alcohol Use</strong>: Caution in patients with a history of significant alcohol consumption or liver disease.</li><li><strong>Myopathy Risk</strong>: Discontinue if myopathy or significant CPK elevation is suspected.</li></ul><p><strong>Adverse Effects</strong></p><p>Common side effects include:</p><ul><li>Gastrointestinal symptoms (constipation, dyspepsia, flatulence, abdominal pain).</li><li>Musculoskeletal complaints (arthralgia, myalgia).</li><li>Others: Headache, rash, back pain, fatigue.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong>: Contraindicated due to potential teratogenic effects and risk to breastfeeding infants.</li><li><strong>Geriatric Use</strong>: Increased sensitivity in patients ≥65 years may occur; caution is advised.</li><li><strong>Pediatrics</strong>: Not recommended for children under 10 years; for older children, dosing is limited to a maximum of 20 mg/day, except in specific familial conditions.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><p>Store in a cool, dry place, protected from light and heat. Keep out of reach of children.</p><p><br></p><p>This non-promotional summary is tailored to provide accurate, essential information for healthcare professionals or patients seeking clarity on <strong>Atova 20 mg</strong>. Let me know if you’d like to adjust or focus on any specific section!</p>', 'active', '777_1734039604.jpg', 3, 12, NULL, '2024-12-13 02:40:04', '2024-12-13 02:40:04'),
(169, 'Clopid-As', 'Clopidogrel + Aspirin', 12.04, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '75 mg+75 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications for Clopid-As</strong></p><p><strong>Acute Coronary Syndrome (ACS):</strong></p><p>Clopid-As is indicated for reducing the risk of myocardial infarction (MI) and stroke in patients with:</p><ul><li><strong>Non-ST-segment elevation ACS (NSTEMI)</strong>: Including unstable angina (UA) or non-ST-elevation myocardial infarction.</li><li><strong>ST-segment elevation ACS (STEMI):</strong> Including acute ST-elevation myocardial infarction.</li></ul><p><strong>Recent MI, Stroke, or Peripheral Arterial Disease (PAD):</strong></p><p>In individuals with a history of recent MI, recent stroke, or diagnosed PAD, Clopid-As helps decrease the likelihood of future MI or stroke.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p><strong>Anti-platelet Agents</strong></p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p><strong>Clopidogrel:</strong></p><p>A prodrug that requires metabolic activation to exert its effects. It works by irreversibly binding its active metabolite to the P2Y12 ADP receptors on platelets, preventing activation and aggregation. Platelet inhibition begins within 2 hours after a single dose, reaching maximum effect between days 3 to 7 with repeated dosing at 75 mg daily.</p><p><strong>Aspirin:</strong></p><p>Acts by irreversibly inhibiting platelet cyclooxygenase, blocking thromboxane A2 formation—a key mediator of platelet aggregation and vasoconstriction.</p><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><p><strong>Recommended Dosage:</strong></p><p>The standard oral dose is one tablet daily.</p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><p>Caution should be exercised when used alongside:</p><ul><li><strong>Oral anticoagulants, NSAIDs, Metamizole, SSRIs, or CYP2C19 inhibitors:</strong> These can elevate the risk of bleeding.</li><li>Drugs like <strong>Tenofovir, Valproic Acid, Acetazolamide, Nicorandil,</strong> or the <strong>Varicella vaccine</strong>, as interactions may occur.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Do not use in patients with:</p><ul><li>Known hypersensitivity to any component of Clopid-As.</li><li>Active bleeding disorders such as peptic ulcers or intracranial hemorrhage.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Generally well-tolerated. However, hypersensitivity reactions, including rash and angioedema, have been reported in some cases.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Bleeding Risk:</strong> The combination may prolong bleeding time; caution is advised.</li><li><strong>Thrombotic Thrombocytopenic Purpura (TTP):</strong> Rarely reported but serious.</li><li><strong>Reye’s Syndrome:</strong> Avoid use in individuals with chickenpox, flu, or related symptoms due to the potential risk.</li><li><strong>Hypersensitivity:</strong> Monitor for allergic reactions, particularly in those with a history of sensitivity to thienopyridines.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong></li><li>Limited data exists on safety during pregnancy. Use during the first and second trimesters only if necessary. Contraindicated in the third trimester.</li><li><strong>Lactation:</strong></li><li>Aspirin is excreted in breast milk, and the drug should be avoided during breastfeeding. Clopidogrel\'s excretion in human milk is unknown.</li></ul><p><strong>Pediatric Use</strong></p><p>Not recommended for children under 12 years unless benefits outweigh risks, as aspirin can contribute to Reye’s syndrome.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Overdose Management</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Clopidogrel:</strong> May cause bleeding complications; platelet transfusion can help restore clotting function.</li><li><strong>Aspirin:</strong> Overdose symptoms range from dizziness and tinnitus to severe issues like respiratory alkalosis or metabolic acidosis. Treatment involves gastric lavage, supportive care, or hemodialysis in severe cases.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Guidelines</strong></p><p>Store in a cool, dry place below 30°C, away from light and moisture. Keep out of reach of children.</p><p><br></p><p>This format preserves clarity while ensuring original phrasing. Let me know if further adjustments are needed!</p>', 'active', '668_1734040121.jpg', 9, 12, NULL, '2024-12-13 02:48:41', '2024-12-13 02:48:41'),
(170, 'Ipec Plus', 'Iron Polymaltose Complex + Folic Acid + Zinc Sulfate', 5.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '47 mg+0.5 mg+22.5 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Treatment and prevention of Iron, Folic Acid, and Zinc deficiencies.</li></ul><p><strong>Composition (per tablet):</strong></p><ul><li>Iron (III) Hydroxide Polymaltose Complex equivalent to 47–48 mg elemental Iron</li><li>Folic Acid: 0.5 mg</li><li>Zinc Sulfate Monohydrate equivalent to 22.5 mg elemental Zinc</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Iron, Vitamin, and Mineral Combined Preparation</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li>Iron (III) Hydroxide Polymaltose Complex ensures controlled absorption and is stable.</li><li>Folic Acid aids fetal development.</li><li>Zinc supports enzyme function and protein metabolism.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li>Standard dose: One tablet daily.</li><li>Severe cases: Two tablets daily or as directed by a physician.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>Minimal interaction with food or other medications due to the non-ionic nature of Iron.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any ingredient.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Rare: Nausea, vomiting, constipation, or diarrhea.</li><li>Dark stools may occur but are clinically insignificant.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid in the first trimester unless Iron deficiency is confirmed.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place away from light and moisture. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul>', 'active', '845_1734107104.webp', 29, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 21:25:04', '2024-12-13 21:25:04'),
(171, 'Exium MUPS', 'Esomeprazole Magnesium Trihydrate', 11.00, 10, 'MUPS Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'MUPS Tablet', '20 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>GERD symptoms (e.g., heartburn)</li><li>Healing and maintenance of erosive esophagitis</li><li>Eradication of <em>Helicobacter pylori</em> (with antibiotics)</li><li>Zollinger-Ellison syndrome</li><li>Duodenal and gastric ulcers</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Erosive Esophagitis:</strong> 20–40 mg daily for 4–8 weeks; maintenance: 20 mg daily (up to 6 months).</li><li><strong>GERD:</strong> 20 mg daily for 4 weeks (extend if needed).</li><li><strong>H. pylori Eradication (Triple Therapy):</strong> Esomeprazole 40 mg + Amoxicillin 1000 mg + Clarithromycin 500 mg, all twice daily for 10 days.</li><li><strong>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome:</strong> 20–80 mg daily, adjusted individually.</li><li><strong>Acid Dyspepsia, Duodenal &amp; Gastric Ulcers:</strong> 20–40 mg daily for 2–8 weeks.</li><li><strong>IV Injection:</strong> 40 mg daily via slow IV (over 3+ minutes). Switch to oral as soon as possible.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration:</strong></p><ul><li>Take one hour before meals, swallow whole, or mix with water/applesauce if needed. Avoid chewing pellets.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>May reduce absorption of drugs affected by stomach pH (e.g., ketoconazole, iron salts, digoxin).</li><li>Slight increase in diazepam plasma levels; no major interactions with other common drugs (e.g., phenytoin, amoxicillin, clarithromycin).</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Known hypersensitivity to any component.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Headache, nausea, diarrhea, abdominal pain, constipation, dry mouth, flatulence.</li></ul><p><strong>Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Symptom improvement does not rule out gastric cancer.</li><li>Use cautiously during pregnancy and breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose:</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: Decreased activity, breathing changes, tremors, ataxia.</li><li>No specific antidote; provide symptomatic care.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Keep in a dry place below 30°C, away from moisture and light.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Populations:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pediatrics:</strong> Safety not established.</li><li><strong>Elderly:</strong> No significant differences in efficacy/safety.</li><li><strong>Hepatic Impairment:</strong> Max dose: 20 mg daily for severe cases.</li><li><strong>Renal Impairment:</strong> No dosage adjustment needed.</li></ul><p><br></p><p><br></p>', 'active', '230_1734107318.jpg', 10, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 21:28:38', '2024-12-13 21:28:38'),
(172, 'Nexum', 'Esomeprazole Magnesium Trihydrate', 7.02, 10, 'Capsule', '10 Capsul In Strip', 'Capsule', '20 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>GERD-related symptoms (e.g., persistent heartburn).</li><li>Erosive esophagitis (treatment and maintenance of healing).</li><li>Helicobacter pylori eradication (with amoxicillin and clarithromycin in duodenal ulcers).</li><li>Zollinger-Ellison syndrome.</li><li>Acid-related dyspepsia, duodenal, and gastric ulcers.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Erosive Esophagitis:</strong> 20-40 mg daily for 4-8 weeks. Maintenance: 20 mg daily.</li><li><strong>GERD Symptoms:</strong> 20 mg daily for 4 weeks (extendable to 8 weeks if needed).</li><li><strong>H. pylori Eradication (Triple Therapy):</strong> Esomeprazole 40 mg once daily, Amoxicillin 1000 mg twice daily, and Clarithromycin 500 mg twice daily for 10 days.</li><li><strong>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome:</strong> 20-80 mg daily, adjusted individually.</li><li><strong>Acid Dyspepsia:</strong> 20-40 mg daily for 2-4 weeks.</li><li><strong>IV Administration:</strong> 40 mg once daily, reconstituted and administered over 3 minutes or as an infusion within 12 hours.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration:</strong></p><ul><li>Take 1 hour before meals. Capsules should be swallowed whole or mixed with applesauce (without chewing). Oral suspension and IV forms should follow specified preparation guidelines.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><p>Common: Headache, diarrhea, nausea, flatulence, abdominal pain, constipation, dry mouth.</p><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Rule out gastric cancer before use.</li><li>Not suitable for patients with hypersensitivity to esomeprazole.</li><li>Caution in severe hepatic impairment (max 20 mg daily).</li><li>Not established for pediatric use.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>May reduce absorption of drugs dependent on gastric pH (e.g., ketoconazole, digoxin).</li><li>May increase plasma levels of diazepam.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose:</strong></p><p>Symptoms: Decreased motor activity, tremors, respiratory changes. Supportive care recommended; dialysis not effective.</p><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><p>Store below 30°C, protect from moisture and light, and keep out of children’s reach.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation:</strong></p><p>Use with caution; breastfeeding should be discontinued if treatment is necessary.</p><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><p>Esomeprazole inhibits gastric acid secretion by targeting H+/K+-ATPase (proton pump inhibitor), providing effective acid control.</p>', 'active', '135_1734107520.jpg', 4, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 21:32:00', '2024-12-15 13:52:56'),
(173, 'Rupa', 'Rupatadine Fumarate', 12.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li>Treatment of <strong>Seasonal &amp; Perennial Allergic Rhinitis</strong>.</li><li>Management of <strong>Urticaria</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Non-sedating antihistamines.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults &amp; Adolescents (12+ years):</strong> 10 mg once daily (with or without food).</li><li><strong>Children (2–11 years):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">≥25 kg: 5 ml oral solution once daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">10–25 kg: 2.5 ml oral solution once daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Rupatadine or any excipients.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common:</strong> Drowsiness, dizziness, asthenia.</li><li><strong>Uncommon:</strong> Nausea, rash, weight gain, dry throat, oropharyngeal pain.</li><li><strong>Rare:</strong> Palpitations, tachycardia.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Use cautiously in:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>QT interval prolongation</strong> or other cardiac conditions.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Elderly patients (65+ years)</strong>.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Renal or hepatic impairment</strong> (use not recommended).</li><li>Avoid grapefruit or grapefruit juice during treatment.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>Increased exposure with <strong>ketoconazole</strong> or <strong>erythromycin</strong> (CYP3A4 inhibitors).</li><li>Use cautiously with <strong>statins</strong>, CNS depressants, or alcohol.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> Not recommended unless benefits outweigh risks.</li><li><strong>Lactation:</strong> Avoid unless necessary, as excretion in breast milk is unknown.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C in a cool, dry place, away from light and moisture.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Mechanism:</strong> Dual action: Histamine H1-receptor antagonist and platelet-activating factor (PAF) antagonist.</li><li>Inhibits mast cell degranulation and release of cytokines, reducing allergic responses.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Elderly:</strong> No dose adjustment required, but use cautiously.</li><li><strong>Children under 12 years:</strong> Safety and efficacy not established.</li><li><strong>Renal/Hepatic impairment:</strong> Use not recommended due to lack of data.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose</strong></p><ul><li>Most common reaction: <strong>Somnolence</strong>.</li><li>Provide symptomatic and supportive care.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '456_1734107708.webp', 29, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 21:35:08', '2024-12-13 21:35:08'),
(174, 'Windel Plus', 'Salbutamol + Ipratropium Bromide', 25.00, 6, 'Nebuliser Solution', '6 Nebuliser Solution In  Strip', 'Nebuliser Solution', '3 ml', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li>Treatment of <strong>COPD</strong> in patients with bronchospasm requiring a second bronchodilator.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Combined bronchodilators.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Ipratropium bromide:</strong> Anticholinergic that inhibits vagally-mediated bronchoconstriction.</li><li><strong>Salbutamol:</strong> Beta2-agonist providing rapid (5 min), short-acting (4–6 hours) bronchodilation.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Inhaler:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">2 puffs, 4 times daily (maximum: 12 puffs in 24 hours).</li><li><strong>Nebulizer Solution:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Adults: 1 ampoule as needed, up to 3–4 ampoules daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Acute worsening: Seek immediate medical attention if symptoms do not improve.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to <strong>soya lecithin</strong>, <strong>soybean</strong>, <strong>peanuts</strong>, <strong>atropine</strong>, or any component.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Salbutamol:</strong> Tremor, headache, transient muscle cramps, rare hypersensitivity reactions (e.g., angioedema, bronchospasm).</li><li><strong>Ipratropium:</strong> Headache, nausea, coughing, pharyngitis, bronchitis, and rare bronchospasm.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Use with caution in patients with:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Narrow-angle glaucoma, prostatic hyperplasia, bladder-neck obstruction.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Hyperthyroidism, diabetes, convulsive disorders.</li><li><strong>Potential risks:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Hypokalemia</strong> from beta-adrenergic agents may cause cardiovascular effects.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Avoid in hepatic/renal impairment due to limited study data.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy (Category C):</strong> Use only if benefits outweigh risks.</li><li><strong>Lactation:</strong> Not recommended unless benefits justify potential risks.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: <strong>Tachycardia</strong>, palpitations, tremor, arrhythmia, flushing.</li><li>Treatment: Sedatives, beta1-selective blockers (cautiously in asthma patients).</li></ul><p><strong>Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Children:</strong> Safety and efficacy not established.</li><li><strong>Elderly:</strong> No specific precautions noted, but general caution advised.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture.</li></ul>', 'active', '1083_1734107900.webp', 2, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 21:38:20', '2024-12-13 21:38:51');
INSERT INTO `products` (`id`, `productName`, `genericName`, `retail_max_price`, `cart_qty_inc`, `cart_text`, `unit_in_pack`, `type`, `quantity`, `prescription`, `feature`, `description`, `status`, `coverImage`, `company_id`, `category_id`, `add_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(175, 'Remmo', 'Esomeprazole Magnesium Trihydrate', 10.00, 15, 'MUPS Tablet', '15 Tablet In Strip', 'MUPS Tablet', '20 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>GERD:</strong> Relief from persistent heartburn and symptoms, treatment, and maintenance of erosive esophagitis healing.</li><li><strong>H. pylori Eradication:</strong> In combination with amoxicillin and clarithromycin for duodenal ulcers.</li><li><strong>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome:</strong> Management of excessive stomach acid.</li><li><strong>Acid-Related Dyspepsia, Duodenal, and Gastric Ulcers.</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Dosage :</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Erosive Esophagitis:</strong> 20-40 mg once daily for 4-8 weeks. Maintenance: 20 mg daily for up to 6 months.</li><li><strong>GERD:</strong> 20 mg daily for 4 weeks (may extend another 4 weeks).</li><li><strong>H. pylori Eradication:</strong> Esomeprazole 40 mg daily + Amoxicillin 1000 mg + Clarithromycin 500 mg, twice daily for 10 days.</li><li><strong>Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome:</strong> 20-80 mg daily (adjust individually).</li><li><strong>Acid Dyspepsia:</strong> 20-40 mg daily for 2-4 weeks.</li><li><strong>IV Injection:</strong> 40 mg daily (3-30 minutes infusion); discontinue once oral therapy resumes.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration :</strong></p><ul><li>Take 1 hour before meals, swallow whole. For oral suspension, mix with 15 ml of water, stir, and consume immediately. For IV, reconstitute with 5 ml of solvent and administer within 12 hours.</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction :</strong></p><ul><li>Metabolized by CYP2C19 and CYP3A4. Minimal interaction with warfarin, clarithromycin, or amoxicillin.</li><li>May reduce absorption of medications affected by stomach pH (e.g., ketoconazole, digoxin).</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications :</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to esomeprazole or its components.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects :</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Headache, diarrhea, nausea, flatulence, abdominal pain, constipation, dry mouth.</li><li>Rare: Severe allergic reactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions :</strong></p><ul><li>Symptom relief does not rule out stomach cancer.</li><li>Capsules can be mixed with soft applesauce for easier swallowing.</li><li>Not suitable for pediatric use.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose :</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: Decreased activity, breathing changes, tremors, ataxia.</li><li>Treatment: Supportive care; dialysis is unlikely to be effective.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Populations :</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> Use only if necessary; no adequate studies in humans.</li><li><strong>Breastfeeding:</strong> Discontinue breastfeeding if using.</li><li><strong>Elderly:</strong> Generally safe, though individual sensitivity may vary.</li><li><strong>Hepatic Impairment:</strong> Severe cases should not exceed 20 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Renal Impairment:</strong> No dosage adjustment needed.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage :</strong></p><ul><li>Keep below 30°C, away from moisture and light.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '907_1734108242.webp', 3, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 21:44:02', '2024-12-13 21:44:02'),
(176, 'Motigut', 'Domperidone Maleate', 4.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Motigut 10 mg:</strong></p><ul><li>Treats symptoms of delayed gastric emptying, GERD, and esophagitis (e.g., fullness, abdominal distension, nausea, vomiting, heartburn).</li><li>Used for acute nausea and vomiting of various origins (functional, infectious, drug-induced).</li><li>Assists in barium transit during radiological studies.</li><li>Reduces dopamine-agonist-induced nausea in Parkinson’s disease.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Motility stimulants, dopamine antagonist, prokinetic drugs.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li>Dopamine receptor antagonist with gastroprokinetic effects.</li><li>Limited blood-brain barrier penetration minimizes psychotropic side effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults:</strong> 10-20 mg every 6-8 hours; max daily dose: 80 mg.</li><li><strong>Children:</strong> 0.2-0.4 mg/kg every 6-8 hours.</li><li>Take 15-30 minutes before meals and bedtime.</li><li>Max duration for acute nausea/vomiting: 12 weeks.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid concurrent use with anticholinergics, antacids, or CYP3A4 inhibitors (e.g., azole antifungals, macrolides).</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity, neonates, GI hemorrhage, obstruction, perforation, prolactinoma.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Rare: Intestinal cramps, rash, urticaria, hyperprolactinemia (e.g., galactorrhea, gynecomastia).</li><li>Extremely rare: Extrapyramidal symptoms.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Not recommended during pregnancy. Minimal transfer to breast milk.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Use cautiously in children, hepatic impairment, and severe renal insufficiency. Adjust dosing frequency in renal patients.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Management:</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: Drowsiness, disorientation, extrapyramidal effects.</li><li>Treatment: Activated charcoal, anticholinergic drugs for extrapyramidal reactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, protected from light and moisture.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Blocks dopamine receptors in the CTZ and stomach, enhancing GI motility and preventing regurgitation.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Pediatric Considerations:</strong></p><ul><li>Use cautiously in infants and under medical supervision due to immature blood-brain barrier.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '436_1734108463.webp', 4, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 21:47:43', '2024-12-13 21:47:43'),
(177, 'Neuralgin', 'Vitamin B1 + B6 + B12', 6.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '100 mg+200 mg+200 mcg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications :</strong></p><ul><li>Treats vitamin B1, B6, and B12 deficiencies.</li><li>Supports management of neuritis and non-inflammatory nerve disorders, including diabetic neuropathy, sciatica, lumbago, myalgia, facial neuralgia, and intercostal neuralgia.</li></ul><p><strong>Composition:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tablet:</strong> Vitamin B1 (100 mg), B6 (200 mg), B12 (200 mcg).</li><li><strong>Injection:</strong> Vitamin B1 (100 mg), B6 (100 mg), B12 (1000 mcg).</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Specific combined vitamin preparations.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li>Vitamins B1, B6, and B12 act as coenzymes in nerve metabolism, aiding nerve fiber regeneration and repair.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tablet:</strong> 1-3 tablets daily or as directed.</li><li><strong>Injection:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Severe cases: 1 ampoule daily until symptoms improve.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Mild cases: 1 ampoule 2-3 times per week.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Administer intramuscularly.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>No significant drug interactions reported.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Not for patients on levodopa therapy or those allergic to any ingredients.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Rare allergic reactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Tablets are safe; injections are not recommended due to benzyl alcohol content.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Cyanocobalamin should not be used in spinal cord degeneration or optic neuropathies linked to high cyanocobalamin levels.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose:</strong></p><ul><li>No expected symptoms at recommended dosages; manage overdose symptomatically.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 25°C, in a cool, dry place, protected from light.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Vitamin B1: Converts nutrients into energy, supports nerves and heart health.</li><li>Vitamin B6: Aids RBC formation, neurotransmitter production, and cardiovascular health.</li><li>Vitamin B12: Supports cell replication, RBC production, and nerve function while reducing depression and cardiovascular risks.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1874_1734108668.jpg', 30, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 21:51:08', '2024-12-13 21:51:08'),
(178, 'Deslor', 'Desloratadine', 5.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '5 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications :</strong></p><ul><li>Relief of symptoms from seasonal and perennial allergic rhinitis, including sneezing, nasal congestion, itching, tearing, redness, palate itching, and coughing.</li><li>Relief of symptoms from chronic idiopathic urticaria, such as itching and hives.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Non-sedating antihistamines.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li>A long-acting, non-sedating, selective H1-receptor antagonist that inhibits pro-inflammatory mediators from mast cells and basophils.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pediatric Drops:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">6-11 months: 2 ml once daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">1-2 years: 2.5 ml once daily.</li><li><strong>Syrup:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">6-11 months: 2 ml once daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">1-5 years: 2.5 ml once daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">6-11 years: 5 ml once daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Adults &amp; &gt;12 years: 10 ml once daily.</li><li><strong>Tablet:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Adults &amp; &gt;12 years: 1 tablet (5 mg) daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>No significant drug interactions reported.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Deslor or Loratadine.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Rare: Headache, nausea, fatigue, dizziness, sore throat, indigestion, or muscle pain.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> Use only if clearly needed (Category C).</li><li><strong>Lactation:</strong> Passes into breast milk; consider discontinuing nursing or the drug.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>For liver/renal impairment: Start with 5 mg tablet every other day.</li><li>Use cautiously in patients with seizure history.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose:</strong></p><ul><li>No clinically relevant effects reported.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C in a cool, dry place, away from light and out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Populations:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pediatrics:</strong> Not established for children under 2 years.</li><li><strong>Geriatrics:</strong> Adjust dose cautiously considering age-related conditions.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Active metabolite of Loratadine; blocks H1-receptors and inhibits histamine release from mast cells.</li></ul>', 'active', '1167_1734108803.jpg', 43, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 21:53:23', '2024-12-13 21:53:58'),
(179, 'Hexisol', 'Chlorhexidine Gluconate + Isopropyl alcohol', 160.00, 1, 'Hand Rub', '1 Hand Rub Bottle', 'Hand Rub', '250 ml', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Hexisol 250 ml:</strong></p><ul><li>Disinfection of clean and intact skin.</li><li>Pre-operative surgical hand disinfection.</li><li>Antiseptic hand disinfection before aseptic procedures or after handling contaminated materials.</li><li>Disinfection of patient skin prior to surgery or invasive procedures.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Chlorhexidine &amp; Chloroxylenol preparations.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li>Potent cationic agent with broad-spectrum activity against gram-positive and gram-negative bacteria.</li><li>Bacteriostatic at low concentrations and bactericidal at high concentrations.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pre-operative hand disinfection:</strong> Apply 5 ml to hands and forearms, rub thoroughly, let dry, and repeat.</li><li><strong>Antiseptic hand disinfection:</strong> Apply 3 ml to hands and wrists, rub until dry.</li><li><strong>Patient skin disinfection:</strong> Rub solution on the surgical site with a sterile swab for 2 minutes.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>Incompatible with soaps, anionic agents, and hypochlorite bleaches (may stain fabrics).</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to chlorhexidine (rare).</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Rare irritative skin reactions or generalized allergic reactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>No known adverse effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid contact with brain, meninges, middle ear, sensitive tissues, and eyes.</li><li>Not for injection or use in body cavities.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: Throat swelling, esophageal necrosis, and elevated liver enzymes.</li><li>Management: Gastric lavage using milk, raw egg, gelatin, or mild soap.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 25°C.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Disrupts bacterial cell walls at high concentrations (bactericidal) and alters osmotic equilibrium at low concentrations (bacteriostatic).</li></ul>', 'active', '901_1734109265.jpg', 44, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 22:01:05', '2024-12-13 22:02:06'),
(180, 'Flagyl', 'Metronidazole', 1.70, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '400 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Flagyl 400 mg</strong></p><ul><li>Prevention of post-operative infections due to anaerobic bacteria.</li><li>Treatment of septicaemia, peritonitis, brain abscess, pelvic abscess, bacterial vaginosis, trichomoniasis, amoebiasis, giardiasis, dental infections, leg ulcers, and anaerobic infections.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Amoebicides, Anti-diarrhoeal, Antiprotozoal.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li>Flagyl (metronidazole) interacts with DNA of anaerobic bacteria, resulting in bactericidal action.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Trichomoniasis</strong>: 400 mg twice daily for 7 days.</li><li><strong>Intestinal Amoebiasis</strong>: 800 mg three times daily for 5 days.</li><li><strong>Giardiasis</strong>: 2 gm once daily for 3 days.</li><li><strong>Acute Gingivitis</strong>: 200 mg three times daily for 3 days.</li><li><strong>Anaerobic Infections</strong>: 400 mg three times daily for 7 days.</li><li><strong>Surgical Prophylaxis</strong>: 400 mg three times daily 24 hours before surgery.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>Alcohol, disulfiram, anticoagulants (warfarin), lithium, cyclosporine, phenytoin, phenobarbital, 5-fluorouracil, busulfan.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Flagyl or Nitroimidazole derivatives.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Metallic taste, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, drowsiness, rash.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Category B (Use if clearly needed). Excreted in human milk; use with caution in nursing women.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Monitor for neurological symptoms, especially with prolonged use.</li><li>Caution in hepatic encephalopathy.</li><li>May darken urine.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: Vomiting, ataxia, disorientation.</li><li>Management: Symptomatic and supportive treatment.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, protected from light.</li></ul>', 'active', '458_1734109543.webp', 45, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 22:05:43', '2024-12-13 22:06:18'),
(181, 'E-Cap', 'Vitamin E [Alpha Tocopherol Acetate]', 5.00, 15, 'Capsul', '15 Capsul In Strip', 'Capsule', '200 IU', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications :</strong></p><ul><li>As a dietary supplement for vitamin E deficiency, increased requirements, and healthy hair &amp; skin.</li><li>Therapeutic uses include cardiovascular disease, heavy metal poisoning, hepatotoxin poisoning, hemolytic anemia, and oxygen therapy.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class :</strong></p><ul><li>Vitamin-E Preparations</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology :</strong></p><ul><li>Acts as an antioxidant, protecting polyunsaturated fatty acids and other oxygen-sensitive substances like vitamins A and C from oxidation.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration :</strong></p><ul><li>Cardiovascular health: 400-800 IU/day</li><li>Deficiency syndrome (adults): 200-400 IU/day</li><li>Deficiency syndrome (children): 200 IU/day</li><li>Thalassemia: 800 IU/day</li><li>Sickle-cell anemia: 400 IU/day</li><li>Skin &amp; hair: 200-400 IU/day (topical use possible)</li><li>Chronic cold (adults): 200 IU/day</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions :</strong></p><ul><li>May impair Vitamin A absorption, affect Vitamin K function, and enhance Warfarin effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications :</strong></p><ul><li>None known.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects :</strong></p><ul><li>Overdose (&gt;1 gm): Hypertension, fatigue, diarrhea, myopathy.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation :</strong></p><ul><li>Safe in recommended doses. High doses not established.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions :</strong></p><ul><li>May increase thrombosis risk, particularly for those on estrogens.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage :</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry place, away from light and heat. Keep out of children’s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations :</strong></p><ul><li>Safe for children.</li></ul>', 'active', '363_1734109776.webp', 9, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 22:09:36', '2024-12-15 13:52:13'),
(182, 'Acifix', 'Rabeprazole Sodium', 7.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '20 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications :</strong></p><ul><li>Active duodenal and benign gastric ulcers</li><li>Erosive or ulcerative GERD</li><li>GERD maintenance</li><li>Symptomatic GERD</li><li>Zollinger-Ellison syndrome</li><li>Helicobacter pylori eradication with appropriate antibiotics</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class :</strong></p><ul><li>Proton Pump Inhibitor</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology :</strong></p><ul><li>Inhibits gastric H+/K+-ATPase, reducing gastric acid secretion.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration :</strong></p><ul><li>Duodenal ulcer: 20 mg daily for 4 weeks</li><li>Erosive GERD: 20 mg daily for 4-8 weeks</li><li>Symptomatic GERD: 20 mg daily for 4 weeks</li><li>GERD maintenance: 10-20 mg daily</li><li>Zollinger-Ellison syndrome: 60 mg daily, adjust as needed</li><li>H. pylori eradication: 20 mg twice daily with antibiotics for 7 days</li></ul><p><strong>Administration :</strong></p><ul><li>Take once daily in the morning before food, swallow whole.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions :</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid with itraconazole, ketoconazole, and atazanavir due to reduced absorption.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications :</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to rabeprazole or excipients</li><li>Not recommended during pregnancy or breastfeeding</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects :</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Headache, nausea, constipation, dry mouth, muscle pain, dizziness.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation :</strong></p><ul><li>Category C in the US; use only if necessary during pregnancy. Excreted in breast milk.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions :</strong></p><ul><li>Rule out malignancy before use</li><li>Long-term use may increase fracture risk (monitor in elderly)</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects  :</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms are mild and reversible; no specific antidote.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions :</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations :</strong></p><ul><li>Not recommended for children; no data on safety and effectiveness.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '578_1734109976.jpg', 3, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 22:12:56', '2024-12-13 22:12:56'),
(183, 'Calbo', 'Calcium Carbonate', 5.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '500 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications :</strong></p><ul><li>Prevention and treatment of calcium deficiency (e.g., hypoparathyroidism, chronic diarrhea, vitamin D deficiency, menopause, pregnancy, lactation, etc.)</li><li>Treatment of hyperphosphatemia in chronic renal failure (including CAPD and hemodialysis)</li><li>Short-term relief of dyspeptic symptoms (not recommended for long-term use)</li><li>Management of acid indigestion, heartburn, and upset stomach (1000 mg tablet)</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class :</strong></p><ul><li>Minerals in bone formation, specific mineral preparations</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology :</strong></p><ul><li>Reacts with gastric acid to increase gastric pH, reducing pepsin activity. Up to 30% of calcium is absorbed.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration :</strong></p><ul><li>As antacid: 540-2000 mg daily for adults, half for children</li><li>As dietary supplement: 1250-3750 mg daily (500-1500 mg calcium)</li><li>In pregnancy/lactation: 1200-1500 mg daily</li><li>For chronic renal failure: 2.5-9.0 gm daily with meals</li><li>1000 mg tablet: 2000-3000 mg as needed for acid indigestion, repeated hourly if necessary</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions :</strong></p><ul><li>Enhances cardiac effects of digoxin (with hypercalcemia)</li><li>May interfere with tetracycline absorption</li><li>Modification of vitamin D therapy may be needed in renal failure</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications :</strong></p><ul><li>Hypercalcemia, hyperparathyroidism, hypercalciuria, nephrolithiasis</li><li>Zollinger-Ellison syndrome</li><li>Caution with digoxin, sarcoidosis, renal/cardiac disease, or cardiac glycosides</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects :</strong></p><ul><li>GI irritation, constipation, rare hypercalcemia (with large doses or renal failure)</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation :</strong></p><ul><li>Safe for use during pregnancy and lactation</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions :</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place at room temperature</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations :</strong></p><ul><li>Safe for children and infants with chronic renal failure</li><li>In elderly patients, monitor calcium and phosphate levels, as constipation may be an issue.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1660_1734110166.webp', 4, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 22:16:06', '2024-12-13 22:16:06'),
(184, 'Famotack', 'Famotidine', 3.00, 15, 'Tablet', '15 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '20 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications :</strong></p><ul><li>Gastric ulcer, duodenal ulcer, anastomotic ulcer, acute stress ulcer</li><li>Reflux esophagitis and Zollinger-Ellison syndrome</li><li>Acute and chronic gastritis (acute exacerbation stage)</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class :</strong></p><ul><li>H2 receptor antagonist</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology :</strong></p><ul><li>Inhibits histamine on H2-receptors in parietal cells, reducing gastric acid secretion.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration :</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Duodenal ulcer &amp; gastric ulcer</strong>: 40 mg at night for 4-8 weeks</li><li><strong>Gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD)</strong>: 20 mg twice daily for 6-12 weeks</li><li><strong>Zollinger-Ellison syndrome</strong>: Starting dose 20 mg every 6 hours, up to 160 mg</li><li><strong>Acute gastritis</strong>: 20 mg twice daily or 40 mg once daily</li><li><strong>Maintenance therapy</strong>: 20 mg once daily</li><li><strong>Pediatric dosing</strong> varies by age and condition, with doses up to 40 mg daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions ;</strong></p><ul><li>No clinically significant interactions identified. Does not affect cytochrome P450 enzymes.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications ;</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any component of the drug</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects :</strong></p><ul><li>Rare: Eruption, constipation, diarrhea, dry mouth, nausea, vomiting, tachycardia, headache, drowsiness, insomnia</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation :</strong></p><ul><li>Pregnancy category B, use only if needed</li><li>Unknown if secreted in breast milk, consider discontinuing nursing</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings :</strong></p><ul><li>Use cautiously in elderly, renal, and hepatic impairment</li><li>Minimum effective dose should be used</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions :</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture, out of reach of children.</li></ul>', 'active', '446_1734110342.webp', 4, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 22:19:02', '2024-12-13 22:19:36'),
(185, 'Neurocare', 'Vitamin B1 + B6 + B12', 10.00, 30, 'Tablet', '30 Tablet In Bottle', 'Tablet', '100 mg+200 mg+200 mcg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><br></p><p><strong>Indications :</strong></p><ul><li>Vitamin B1, B6, &amp; B12 deficiency syndrome</li><li>Supportive treatment for neuritis and non-inflammatory nerve diseases (e.g., diabetic neuropathy, sciatica, myalgia, optic neuritis)</li></ul><p><strong>Composition :</strong></p><ul><li>Each tablet: Vitamin B1 (100 mg), Vitamin B6 (200 mg), Vitamin B12 (200 mcg)</li><li>Each 3 ml ampoule: Vitamin B1 (100 mg), Vitamin B6 (100 mg), Vitamin B12 (1000 mcg)</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class :</strong></p><ul><li>Specific combined vitamin preparations</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology :</strong></p><ul><li>Supports nerve cell metabolism, regeneration of nerve fibers, and myelin sheath repair.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration :</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tablets</strong>: 1-3 tablets/day</li><li><strong>Injection</strong>: 1 ampoule daily for severe cases, 2-3 ampoules/week for mild cases (intramuscular injection)</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions :</strong></p><ul><li>No known drug interactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications :</strong></p><ul><li>Patients on levodopa therapy</li><li>Hypersensitivity to any ingredient in the product</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects :</strong></p><ul><li>Generally well tolerated, but allergic reactions may occur.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation :</strong></p><ul><li>Safe during pregnancy at recommended doses, but injections are not recommended due to benzyl alcohol.</li><li>Vitamin B1, B6, &amp; B12 are secreted into breast milk, but risks of overdose are unknown.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings :</strong></p><ul><li>Not suitable for subacute degeneration of the spinal cord or optic neuropathies with high cyanocobalamin levels.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects :</strong></p><ul><li>No significant overdose symptoms, treatment is symptomatic and supportive.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions :</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 25°C, in a cool, dry place, away from light.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action :</strong></p><ul><li>Vitamin B1: Supports nerve health and energy production</li><li>Vitamin B6: Aids in protein synthesis, neurotransmitter production, and heart health</li><li>Vitamin B12: Essential for RBC production, nerve health, and preventing anemia.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy :</strong></p><ul><li>Oral form is safe, but injections should be avoided due to benzyl alcohol content.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '837_1734110569.webp', 3, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 22:22:49', '2024-12-13 22:22:49'),
(186, 'Pantobex', 'Pantoprazole', 5.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '20 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications :</strong></p><ul><li>Stomach ulcers, gastroesophageal reflux disease (GERD)</li><li>NSAID-induced ulcers</li><li>Helicobacter pylori eradication (with antibiotics)</li><li>Zollinger-Ellison syndrome</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class :</strong></p><ul><li>Proton Pump Inhibitor (PPI)</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology :</strong></p><ul><li>Inhibits H+/K+ATPase enzyme, reducing gastric acid secretion for over 24 hours.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration :</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Oral</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Gastric/duodenal ulcers: 40 mg daily for 4-8 weeks</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">GERD: 20-40 mg daily, maintenance 20 mg</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">H. pylori eradication: 40 mg twice daily with antibiotics</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">NSAID ulcer prophylaxis: 20 mg daily</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Zollinger-Ellison syndrome: 80 mg once daily, adjust as needed</li><li><strong>IV</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Ulcers &amp; GERD: 40 mg daily for 7-10 days</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Zollinger-Ellison syndrome: 80 mg every 12 hours</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction :</strong></p><ul><li>No significant drug interactions reported.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications :</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Pantobex components.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects :</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Headache, diarrhea</li><li>Rare: Abdominal pain, flatulence, rash, hyperglycemia, insomnia</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation :</strong></p><ul><li>Category B (US FDA). Use only if necessary. Excreted in breast milk.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings :</strong></p><ul><li>Do not split, chew, or crush tablets. Long-term use may affect Vitamin B12 absorption and increase osteoporosis risk.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects :</strong></p><ul><li>No known overdose symptoms. Symptomatic and supportive management recommended.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions :</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry, cool place, away from light, and out of children\'s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>IV Reconstitution :</strong></p><ul><li>Mix with 10 ml of 0.9% sodium chloride injection. Administer gradually over 2-5 minutes.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1926_1734110725.webp', 3, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 22:25:25', '2024-12-13 22:25:25'),
(187, 'Alben DS', 'Albendazole', 5.00, 10, 'Chewable Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '400 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications :</strong></p><ul><li>Single and mixed infestations of hookworm, roundworm, threadworm, whipworm, strongyloides, tapeworm, opisthorchi, and hydatid disease (Echinococcosis).</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class :</strong></p><ul><li>Anthelmintic</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology :</strong></p><ul><li>Broad-spectrum benzimidazole anthelminthic with vermicidal, ovicidal, and larvicidal activities. Inhibits glucose uptake in parasites, depleting energy and immobilizing them.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration :</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults &amp; children over 2 years</strong>: 400 mg as a single dose for common infestations; 3-day course for strongyloidiasis and taeniasis.</li><li><strong>Children 1-2 years</strong>: 200 mg (5 ml suspension).</li><li><strong>Hydatid disease</strong>: 400 mg twice daily for 28 days (adjust dose for weight).</li><li><strong>Giardiasis</strong>: 400 mg once daily for 5 days.</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction :</strong></p><ul><li>No known pharmacodynamic or pharmacokinetic interactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications :</strong></p><ul><li>Not recommended for neonates or pregnant women (FDA Category C).</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects :</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Gastrointestinal disturbances, headache, dizziness</li><li>Rare: Alopecia, rash, blood disorders (e.g., leucopenia), allergic reactions, convulsions in cerebral disease.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation :</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid during pregnancy and lactation unless the benefits outweigh risks.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings :</strong></p><ul><li>Monitor blood counts and liver function during treatment, especially for Echinococcosis.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions :</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry place, away from light and heat, out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action :</strong></p><ul><li>Inhibits glucose uptake and immobilizes parasites by interfering with tubulin polymerization.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy :</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid unless necessary due to potential risks.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1826_1734110895.webp', 26, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 22:28:15', '2024-12-13 22:28:15'),
(188, 'Bicozin', 'Vitamin B Complex + Zinc', 3.00, 30, 'Tablet', '30 Tablet In Bottle', 'Tablet', '39 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><br></p><p><strong>Indications :</strong></p><ul><li>Treatment and prevention of vitamin B complex and zinc deficiencies.</li></ul><p><strong>Composition :</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Syrup</strong>: Thiamine Hydrochloride 5 mg, Riboflavin 2 mg, Pyridoxine Hydrochloride 2 mg, Nicotinamide 20 mg, Zinc Sulfate 10 mg.</li><li><strong>Tablet</strong>: Same composition as syrup.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class :</strong></p><ul><li>Specific mineral &amp; vitamin combined preparations.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology :</strong></p><ul><li>Contains Vitamin B complex (important for metabolism) and Zinc (essential for enzyme functions and human nutrition).</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration :</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Syrup</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Adults: 10 ml, 2-3 times daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Children: 10 ml, 1-3 times daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Infants: 5 ml, 1-2 times daily.</li><li><strong>Tablet</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Adults &amp; children over 30 kg: 1-2 tablets, 2-3 times daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction :</strong></p><ul><li>Zinc may reduce absorption of tetracyclines and fluoroquinolones.</li><li>Pyridoxine may reduce the effectiveness of levodopa and decrease phenytoin levels.</li><li>Niacin and statins may cause myopathy.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications :</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any ingredient.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects :</strong></p><ul><li>Generally well tolerated; may cause nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, or stomach upset.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation :</strong></p><ul><li>Safe and recommended during pregnancy and lactation.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings :</strong></p><ul><li>Adjust dose in acute renal failure to avoid zinc accumulation.</li><li>Not for treating severe deficiencies.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects :</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms include epigastric pain, diarrhea, and vomiting; seek emergency medical attention.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions :</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place, protected from light, out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action :</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Zinc</strong>: Supports immune function, growth, wound healing, and mental development.</li><li><strong>B-Vitamins</strong>: Aid in energy production, brain and nerve function, and red blood cell formation.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1667_1734111199.webp', 4, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 22:33:19', '2024-12-13 22:33:19'),
(189, 'Fexo', 'Fexofenadine Hydrochloride', 12.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '180 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications :</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Allergic Rhinitis</strong>: Treatment of seasonal and persistent symptoms (e.g., sneezing, itchy eyes, nose, throat).</li><li><strong>Chronic Idiopathic Urticaria</strong>: Reduces wheals and pruritus.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class </strong>: Non-sedating antihistamines</p><p><strong>Pharmacology </strong>: Fexofenadine is a selective peripheral H1-receptor antagonist. It is quickly absorbed after oral administration, reaching peak plasma concentration in 2–3 hours, and does not cross the blood-brain barrier.</p><p><strong>Dosage </strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Adults (Allergic Rhinitis)</strong>: 60 mg twice daily, 120 mg or 180 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Children (6-11 years)</strong>: 30 mg twice daily, 60 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Children (2-5 years)</strong>: 30 mg or 5 ml (suspension) twice daily.</li><li><strong>Chronic Idiopathic Urticaria</strong>: Same dosages as allergic rhinitis.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions </strong>:</p><ul><li>Co-administration with <strong>erythromycin</strong> or <strong>ketoconazole</strong> increases fexofenadine levels.</li><li>Antacids containing <strong>aluminum</strong> and <strong>magnesium</strong> decrease bioavailability; wait 2 hours before taking them.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications </strong>: Hypersensitivity to fexofenadine or any component.</p><p><strong>Side Effects </strong>:</p><ul><li>Common: Headaches, fatigue, dizziness, nausea.</li><li>Rare: Anaphylaxis, palpitations, skin rashes, anxiety.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation </strong>: Category C (use only if benefits outweigh risks). Not recommended during breastfeeding.</p><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings </strong>:</p><ul><li>Use cautiously in elderly or those with renal/hepatic impairment.</li><li>May cause tachycardia and palpitations in patients with cardiovascular disease.</li><li>Generally does not impair ability to drive or operate machinery.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects </strong>: Symptoms include dry mouth, dizziness, and fatigue. Standard procedures should be followed for overdose management.</p><p><strong>Storage </strong>: Keep in a dry place, away from light and out of reach of children.</p><p><strong>Mode of Action </strong>: Fexofenadine blocks H1 receptors, preventing allergic responses like pruritus, rhinorrhea, and watery eyes. It does not affect the central nervous system, as it does not cross the blood-brain barrier.</p><p><strong>Pediatric Use </strong>:</p><ul><li>For renal impairment, a reduced dose (60 mg once daily) is recommended.</li><li>No significant effects observed in children with hepatic impairment.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1373_1734111398.jpg', 4, 1, NULL, '2024-12-13 22:36:38', '2024-12-13 22:36:38'),
(190, 'Karkuma Organic Healthy Gut', 'Balance Gut Ecology Naturally', 800.00, 1, 'Bottle', '400 ml in a bottle', 'Suspension', '400 ml', 'no', 'yes', '<p>Karkuma Organic Healthy Gut 400 ml&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">a functional food Product, specially formulated to support and nourish our gut.To increase the bioavailability of Karkuma Healthy Gut. It is enriched with organic black pepper extract.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Key Ingredients:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Organic Curcumins</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Organic Turmeric</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Organic Mulberry</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Organic Ginger Extract</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Organic Nutmeg</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Organic Mace</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Organic Black Pepper</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Organic Honey</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Organic Apple Cider Vinegar</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Sodium Chloride &amp; Purified Water.</span></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Key Benefits:&nbsp;</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Curcumin</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> works as gastro protective and supports the reduction of GERD naturally without any toxic side effects.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Helps to increase mucus secretion of stomach</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Helps to reduce inflammation associated with IBS, bloating and abdominal discomfort helps to reduce gas and bloating problems.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Supports to Karkuma Organic Healthy Gut 400 ml</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Organic mulberry</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> have mild laxative properties and can aid in relieving constipation. Additionally, it may promote gut health by supporting beneficial gut bacteria.</span></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Directions For Use:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">For Adults- 15 ml 2 times daily after meals;</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">For children (6-12 years)- 10 ml 2 times daily after meals or as directed by the physician/nutritionist.</span></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Store in a cool and dry place</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Protect from light and moisture.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Read the label carefully before use</span></li></ul>', 'active', '317_1734251923.webp', 46, 8, NULL, '2024-12-15 13:38:43', '2024-12-15 13:38:43'),
(191, 'Karkuma Joint Guard', 'Natural Care for Bone Joint', 2170.00, 1, 'x 90\'s capsule bottle', '90\'s capsule in a bottle', 'Capsule', '975 mg', 'no', 'yes', '<p>Karkuma Joint Guard 975 mg is a functional food product, specially formulated to Karkuma Joint Guard 975 mgs. Its basic raw materials are United State Department of Agriculture (USDA) Organic certiﬁed and collected from the different authentic sources in the world.</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Key Ingredients:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Organic Curcumins</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Organic Turmeric Powder</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Organic Cinnamon Oil</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Organic Black Pepper&nbsp;Extract</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Organic Ginger Oil</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Methyl Sulfonyl Methane (Food Grade)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Glucosamine Sulfate (Food Grade)</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Chondroitin Sulfate (Food Grade)</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Key Benefits:</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Curcumin </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">is a potential agent for protecting cartilage breakdown of the bone joints.</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Glucosamine Sulfate</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\"> promotes bone joint health.&nbsp;</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Methyl Sulfonyl Methane</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\"> helps improve the range of motion &amp; physical function of a bone joint.</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Chondroitin Sulfate</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\"> helps to balance the cartilage matrix in the bone joint.</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Ginger essential oil </strong><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">affects cell-mediated immunity and unregulated T lymphocyte proliferation.</span></li><li><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Cinnamon oil</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\"> can help to reduce inflammation and pain in the joints, and it can also help to improve circulation.</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Black pepper</strong><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\"> extract stimulates the secretion of digestive enzymes, such as amylase, lipase, and protease, which aid in the breakdown and absorption of food.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Directions For Use:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">1 capsule 3 times daily or as directed by the physician/nutritionist.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Packed in Gelatin Capsule</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Please continue it for a minimum of 03 months without a gap for perfect results</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Safety Information:</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Not recommended for pregnant/lactating mothers</span></p>', 'active', '272_1734252574.webp', 46, 8, NULL, '2024-12-15 13:49:34', '2024-12-15 13:51:46'),
(192, 'Napadol', 'Paracetamol + Tramadol Hydrochloride', 8.00, 12, 'Tablet', '12 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '325 mg+37.5 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>For managing moderate to moderately severe pain in adults.</li><li>Short-term (≤5 days) management of acute pain.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Non-steroidal Anti-inflammatory Drugs (NSAIDs).</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Tramadol:</strong> Centrally acting synthetic opioid analgesic with dual action: binds to μ-opioid receptors and inhibits norepinephrine/serotonin reuptake.</li><li><strong>Paracetamol:</strong> Acts centrally to inhibit cyclooxygenase (COX) enzymes, providing analgesic and antipyretic effects without significant anti-inflammatory action.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li>1–2 tablets every 4–6 hours as needed for pain relief, up to a maximum of 8 tablets per day.</li><li>For acute pain (≤5 days): 2 tablets every 4–6 hours, maximum 8 tablets per day.</li><li>Not recommended for children under 18 years. Can be taken with or without food.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to tramadol, paracetamol, opioids, or any component.</li><li>Situations where opioids are contraindicated.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Fatigue, dizziness, headache, nausea, vomiting, constipation, dry mouth, rash, sweating.</li><li>Rare: Anxiety, confusion, euphoria, insomnia, somnolence.</li></ul><p><strong>Warnings &amp; Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>May impair abilities for tasks like driving or operating machinery.</li><li>Avoid combining with alcohol, tranquilizers, hypnotics, or other opioid-containing medications.</li><li>Use cautiously in elderly or patients with hepatic/renal impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Category C: Use only if benefits outweigh risks. Not recommended for use in nursing mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place, away from children.</li></ul>', 'active', '907_1734252848.png', 3, 1, NULL, '2024-12-15 13:54:08', '2024-12-15 13:54:08'),
(193, 'Ace Plus', 'Paracetamol + Caffeine', 2.51, 10, 'Tablet', '10 Tablet In Strip', 'Tablet', '500 mg+65 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Relief from headache, migraine, toothache, neuralgia, period pain, sore throat, backache.</li><li>Fever reduction and alleviation of colds/flu-related aches and pains.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Non-opioid analgesics.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Paracetamol:</strong> Analgesic and antipyretic; reduces pain by lowering the pain threshold and decreases fever by acting on the hypothalamus.</li><li><strong>Caffeine:</strong> Enhances paracetamol’s analgesic effect, improves solubility, raises pain threshold, and increases cerebral blood vessel tone, aiding in headache and migraine relief.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults:</strong> 1–2 tablets every 4–6 hours, up to a maximum of 8 tablets daily.</li><li><strong>Children:</strong> Not recommended for those under 12 years.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>Anticonvulsants (e.g., phenytoin) may lower efficacy.</li><li>Prolonged use may enhance the anticoagulant effects of warfarin.</li><li>Absorption affected by drugs like metoclopramide and colestyramine.</li><li>May increase serum levels of chloramphenicol and probenecid.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Severe renal or hepatic impairment (e.g., viral hepatitis).</li><li>Known sensitivity to caffeine, aspirin, or paracetamol.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Mild: Skin rashes, pancreatitis.</li><li>Rare: Blood disorders like thrombocytopenia, leukopenia, and agranulocytosis.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Consult a doctor before use during pregnancy. Safe for use during breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid prolonged use without medical advice.</li><li>Use cautiously in hepatic or renal impairment, especially with hepatotoxic drugs.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Early symptoms (within 24 hours): Pallor, nausea, vomiting, and abdominal discomfort.</li><li>Liver damage may occur within 12–40 hours, with risks of metabolic acidosis and glucose metabolism abnormalities.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><p>Store in a cool, dry place, away from light and moisture. Keep out of children’s reach.</p>', 'active', '1018_1734253055.jpg', 4, 1, NULL, '2024-12-15 13:57:35', '2024-12-15 13:57:35');
INSERT INTO `products` (`id`, `productName`, `genericName`, `retail_max_price`, `cart_qty_inc`, `cart_text`, `unit_in_pack`, `type`, `quantity`, `prescription`, `feature`, `description`, `status`, `coverImage`, `company_id`, `category_id`, `add_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(194, 'Dexlan', 'Dexlansoprazole', 10.00, 10, 'Capsul', '10 Capsul In Strip', 'Capsule', '30 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Healing of Erosive Esophagitis (EE):</strong> 60 mg once daily for up to 8 weeks.</li><li><strong>Maintenance of Healed EE:</strong> 30 mg once daily for up to 6 months.</li><li><strong>Symptomatic Non-Erosive GERD:</strong> 30 mg once daily for 4 weeks.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Proton Pump Inhibitor (PPI).</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li>Suppresses gastric acid by inhibiting the H+/K+-ATPase in gastric parietal cells.</li><li>Dual Delayed Release (DDR) formulation ensures two peaks of plasma concentration for sustained effect.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults:</strong> As per indication.</li><li>Can be taken with or without food.</li><li>Capsules should be swallowed whole or granules sprinkled on a tablespoon of food and consumed immediately without chewing.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>May interact with Atazanavir, Warfarin, Tacrolimus, Clopidogrel, and Methotrexate.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Dexlan or its components.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Diarrhea, abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, flatulence.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Risk of gastric malignancy, bone fractures, Clostridium difficile-associated diarrhea, and hypomagnesemia.</li><li>Caution with Methotrexate use.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Pregnancy: Category B; use only if benefits outweigh risks.</li><li>Lactation: Avoid unless necessary.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Populations:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Geriatrics:</strong> No dose adjustment needed.</li><li><strong>Pediatrics:</strong> Not established for patients under 12 years.</li><li><strong>Renal Impairment:</strong> No dose adjustment required.</li><li><strong>Hepatic Impairment:</strong> Mild: No adjustment; Moderate: Max daily dose of 30 mg.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose:</strong></p><ul><li>No severe adverse events reported even with high doses.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C in a dry, light-protected environment. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '618_1734253238.jpg', 30, 1, NULL, '2024-12-15 14:00:38', '2024-12-15 14:00:38'),
(195, 'Bexitrol F', 'Salmeterol + Fluticasone Propionate', 12.00, 10, 'Capsul', '10 Capsul In Strip', 'Capsule', '50 mcg+250 mcg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Regular treatment of asthma when combination therapy (long-acting β2-agonist + inhaled corticosteroid) is appropriate.</li><li>For patients inadequately controlled on inhaled corticosteroids and as-needed short-acting β2-agonists or those already on both therapies.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Long-acting selective β-adrenoceptor stimulants.</li><li>Respiratory corticosteroids.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Salmeterol Xinafoate:</strong> Long-acting β2-agonist providing symptom control.</li><li><strong>Fluticasone Propionate:</strong> Corticosteroid with anti-inflammatory effects in the lungs, improving lung function and preventing exacerbations.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Asthma:</strong></li><li>Adults/adolescents (≥12 years):</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">2 puffs of 25 µg Salmeterol + 50/125/250 µg Fluticasone, twice daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Max dose: Salmeterol 50 µg + Fluticasone 500 µg twice daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Children (4-11 years): 2 puffs of 25 µg Salmeterol + 50 µg Fluticasone, twice daily.</li><li><strong>COPD:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Adults: Salmeterol 50 µg + Fluticasone 250 µg, twice daily.</li><li>Rinse mouth after inhalation to avoid side effects like oral thrush.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Groups:</strong></p><ul><li>No dose adjustment for elderly, renal, or mild hepatic impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Common Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Salmeterol:</strong> Tremor, palpitations, headache, arrhythmia.</li><li><strong>Fluticasone:</strong> Hoarseness, oral thrush, hypersensitivity reactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>Caution in patients with tuberculosis or thyrotoxicosis.</li><li>Monitor for growth reduction in pediatric use.</li><li>Use during pregnancy/lactation only if benefits outweigh risks.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C. Avoid direct sunlight and puncture. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '878_1734254028.webp', 3, 1, NULL, '2024-12-15 14:13:48', '2024-12-15 14:13:48'),
(196, 'Carva', 'Aspirin', 0.80, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '75 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><p>Carva 75 mg is used for:</p><ul><li><strong>Prophylaxis against arterial occlusive events</strong>: Prevents myocardial infarction, recurrent myocardial infarction, stroke, or transient ischemic attack (TIA).</li><li><strong>Pain management</strong>: Effective for mild to moderate pain, including headaches, muscle pain, dysmenorrhea, and toothache.</li><li><strong>Chronic inflammatory conditions</strong>: Treats osteoarthritis with pain and inflammation.</li><li><strong>Antipyretic</strong>: Alleviates fever associated with colds or influenza.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Anti-platelet drugs.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><p>Carva 75 mg reduces platelet aggregation, preventing thrombus formation in arterial circulation. It is particularly useful for conditions where thrombi form primarily through platelet aggregation rather than coagulation. Additionally, it offers analgesic, anti-inflammatory, and antipyretic effects, making it a versatile choice for various conditions. The enteric coating minimizes gastrointestinal side effects, such as irritation or ulcers.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pain, inflammation, and fever:</strong></li><li>1-3 tablets of 300 mg every 6 hours (maximum daily dose: 4 g).</li><li><strong>Thrombotic cerebrovascular or cardiovascular diseases:</strong></li><li>4 tablets of 75 mg daily or 1 tablet of 300 mg daily.</li><li><strong>After myocardial infarction:</strong></li><li>2 tablets of 75 mg daily for one month.</li><li><strong>Following bypass surgery:</strong></li><li>1 tablet of 75 mg daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Increased effects:</strong> Enhances effects of anticoagulants, oral hypoglycemics, phenytoin, and sodium valproate.</li><li><strong>Reduced efficacy:</strong> Inhibits the uricosuric effect of probenecid and may increase sulfonamide toxicity.</li><li><strong>Asthma risk:</strong> Can precipitate bronchospasm or trigger asthma attacks in susceptible individuals.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Children under 12 years (risk of Reye\'s syndrome).</li><li>Breastfeeding.</li><li>Active peptic ulcers or bleeding disorders (e.g., hemophilia, intracranial hemorrhage).</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><p>Common side effects include:</p><ul><li>Nausea, dyspepsia, and gastrointestinal irritation.</li><li>Bronchospasm in sensitive individuals.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Use cautiously in patients with asthma, nasal polyps, or allergies.</li><li>Exercise caution in patients with uncontrolled hypertension or during pregnancy.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Management:</strong></p><p>Symptoms of overdose may include:</p><ul><li>Early signs: Dizziness, tinnitus, nausea, vomiting, and hyperventilation.</li><li>Severe cases: Coma, cardiovascular collapse, and respiratory depression.</li></ul><p><strong>Treatment:</strong></p><ul><li>Gastric lavage and forced alkaline diuresis for moderate cases.</li><li>Hemodialysis in severe cases.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place, away from light and out of children’s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><p>Carva 75 mg inhibits thrombus formation in arterial circulation by reducing platelet aggregation. Its enteric coating minimizes gastrointestinal irritation while delivering effective analgesic, anti-inflammatory, and antipyretic benefits.</p><p>Always consult a healthcare professional before using Carva 75 mg.</p>', 'active', '1121_1734260167.webp', 4, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 15:56:07', '2024-12-15 15:56:07'),
(197, 'Abetis', 'Olmesartan Medoxomil', 11.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '20 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p>Abetis 20 mg is prescribed for the management of hypertension, either as a standalone treatment or in combination with other antihypertensive medications.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Angiotensin II Receptor Blocker (ARB)</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Olmesartan medoxomil, the active ingredient in Abetis 20 mg, is a selective antagonist of the angiotensin II type 1 (AT1) receptor. By blocking AT1 receptors, it inhibits the vasoconstrictive and aldosterone-secreting effects of angiotensin II. This action results in increased plasma renin activity, elevated levels of angiotensin I and II, and reduced aldosterone concentrations, ultimately leading to lower blood pressure.</p><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults</strong>: The typical starting dose is 10 mg once daily. If blood pressure control is inadequate, the dose can be increased to 20 mg daily and further to 40 mg if needed after two weeks. Doses above 40 mg do not enhance efficacy.</li><li><strong>Pediatric Use</strong>: The safety and efficacy in pediatric patients have not been established.</li><li><strong>Geriatric Use</strong>: No significant differences in efficacy or safety were observed between elderly and younger patients in clinical studies.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage Adjustments</strong></p><ul><li>No initial dose adjustment is required for elderly patients or those with moderate renal or hepatic impairment.</li><li>In patients with intravascular volume depletion, therapy should begin under medical supervision, and a lower starting dose should be considered.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>With Medications</strong>: Olmesartan does not show significant drug interactions in clinical studies.</li><li><strong>With Food</strong>: Food does not affect the absorption of Olmesartan.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Abetis 20 mg is contraindicated in individuals hypersensitive to any of its components.</p><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common</strong>: Back pain, diarrhea, headache, bronchitis, sinusitis, and flu-like symptoms.</li><li><strong>Rare</strong>: Peripheral edema, chest pain, and arthritis.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy</strong>: Contraindicated during the second and third trimesters (Category D). If pregnancy is detected, discontinue immediately.</li><li><strong>Lactation</strong>: The presence of Olmesartan in human milk is unknown. Its use is not recommended during breastfeeding due to potential risks to the infant.</li></ul><p><strong>Warnings and Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Monitor renal function, especially in patients with severe heart failure or compromised renal function. Treatment may result in oliguria, azotemia, or acute renal failure.</li><li>Avoid use in patients with severe renal impairment (eGFR &lt; 20 mL/min/1.73 m²).</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Management</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Symptoms</strong>: Hypotension and tachycardia are expected, though bradycardia may occur with vagal stimulation.</li><li><strong>Treatment</strong>: Supportive care, including cardiovascular monitoring, gastric lavage, and fluid resuscitation, as appropriate.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><p>Store below 30°C in a dry place, away from light and moisture. Keep out of reach of children.</p><p><strong>Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Hepatic Impairment</strong>: Limit dose to 20 mg daily in moderate hepatic impairment.</li><li><strong>Renal Impairment</strong>: Do not exceed 20 mg daily if eGFR is 20–60 mL/min/1.73 m². Avoid use if eGFR is below 20 mL/min/1.73 m².</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>Olmesartan blocks the binding of angiotensin II to AT1 receptors in vascular smooth muscle and adrenal tissues, reducing vasoconstriction and aldosterone secretion. It does not inhibit angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) or affect bradykinin levels.</p><p>For professional use, always refer to the latest prescribing information for detailed guidance.</p>', 'active', '1750_1734260415.webp', 44, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 16:00:15', '2024-12-15 16:00:15'),
(198, 'Indever', 'Propranolol Hydrochloride', 0.51, 20, 'Tablet', '20 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p>Indever 10 mg is indicated for:</p><ul><li><strong>Essential Hypertension</strong></li><li><strong>Angina Pectoris</strong></li><li><strong>Cardiac Arrhythmias</strong></li><li><strong>Thyrotoxicosis</strong></li><li><strong>Prophylaxis of Migraine</strong></li><li><strong>Anxiety Disorders</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Beta-adrenoceptor blocking drugs (Beta-blockers)</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Indever 10 mg is a non-selective β-blocker that reduces heart rate, myocardial contractility, blood pressure, and myocardial oxygen demand. It also exhibits membrane-stabilizing properties, enhancing its therapeutic effects.</p><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><h4><strong>Tablet (Adults)</strong></h4><ul><li><strong>Hypertension</strong>: Start with 80 mg twice daily; adjust weekly. Usual dose: 160-320 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Angina/Migraine/Essential Tremor/Anxiety</strong>: 40 mg 2-3 times daily, titrating to 80-160 mg/day (120-240 mg/day for angina).</li><li><strong>Post-Myocardial Infarction</strong>: 40 mg four times daily (or 80 mg twice daily for maintenance).</li><li><strong>Thyrotoxicosis/Dysrhythmias</strong>: 10-40 mg 3-4 times daily.</li><li><strong>Phaeochromocytoma (with alpha-blocker)</strong>: Pre-op: 60 mg/day for 3 days; non-operable cases: 30 mg/day.</li></ul><h4><strong>Sustained Release Capsule</strong></h4><ul><li><strong>Hypertension</strong>: 80 mg once daily, adjusted to 120-160 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Angina</strong>: Start with 80 mg once daily, increase weekly to the desired effect.</li><li><strong>Migraine</strong>: Initial dose 80 mg/day; maintenance dose 160-240 mg/day.</li></ul><h4><strong>Injection</strong></h4><ul><li>Administer 1-3 mg slowly under ECG monitoring. Max rate: 1 mg/min. Reassess before re-dosing (minimum 4 hours apart).</li></ul><p><strong>Pediatric Dosage</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Migraine (under 12 years)</strong>: 20 mg 2-3 times daily.</li><li><strong>Dysrhythmias/Thyrotoxicosis</strong>: 0.25-0.5 mg/kg 3-4 times daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><p>Caution with:</p><ul><li>Verapamil, salbutamol, lidocaine, phenobarbital, ergot alkaloids.</li><li>Concurrent use requires monitoring for potential interactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Avoid use in:</p><ul><li>Bronchospasm</li><li>Cardiogenic shock</li><li>Severe heart block</li><li>Diabetes mellitus (use with caution)</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common:</p><ul><li>Cold extremities</li><li>Fatigue</li><li>Nausea</li><li>Dizziness</li><li>Insomnia</li><li>Paresthesia</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Use with caution during pregnancy; monitor closely.</li><li>Excreted in breast milk – evaluate risks when breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Use cautiously in hepatic or renal impairment.</li><li>Gradual dose reduction is necessary to avoid withdrawal effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Management</strong></p><p>Symptoms: Bradycardia, hypotension, bronchospasm, cardiac insufficiency.</p><p>Treatment: Intensive care monitoring, gastric lavage, activated charcoal, plasma substitutes for hypotension, and supportive therapies.</p><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place, away from light.</li></ul><p>This format organizes the key details effectively while avoiding verbatim duplication of any copyrighted source. Let me know if you need adjustments or further refinements!</p>', 'active', '1640_1734260745.webp', 44, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 16:05:45', '2024-12-15 16:05:45'),
(199, 'Thyrin', 'Levothyroxine Sodium', 1.11, 15, 'Tablet', '15 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '25 mcg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p>Thyrin 25 mcg is prescribed for:</p><ul><li><strong>Replacement therapy in hypothyroidism</strong> of any origin, excluding transient hypothyroidism during recovery from subacute thyroiditis.</li><li><strong>Suppression of Thyroid Stimulating Hormone (TSH)</strong> in conditions such as goiters, thyroid nodules, and following thyroid cancer treatment (surgical or radiological).</li><li><strong>Prevention of goitrogenic effects</strong> caused by medications like lithium.</li><li><strong>Diagnostic purposes</strong> in thyroid suppression tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Thyroid drugs and hormones.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Thyrin 25 mcg contains synthetic Levothyroxine, identical to the natural thyroid hormone T4. Once administered, approximately 30% of T4 is converted into the more active T3 (Triiodothyronine) in peripheral tissues. The drug’s efficacy relies on its binding to Thyroxine Binding Globulin (TBG), which extends its half-life in the body. Key points include:</p><ul><li><strong>Half-life of T4</strong>: 6-7 days under normal conditions; shorter (3-4 days) in hyperthyroidism and longer (9-10 days) in hypothyroidism.</li><li><strong>Metabolism</strong>: Primarily in the liver, with conjugation and excretion via urine.</li><li><strong>Therapeutic stability</strong>: A single daily dose achieves consistent T3 levels, ensuring therapeutic stability when appropriately dosed.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults</strong>: Start with 25-50 mcg/day, increasing by 12.5-25 mcg every 6-8 weeks based on clinical and TSH response. Severe hypothyroidism may require an initial dose of 12.5-25 mcg/day with similar adjustments every 2-4 weeks.</li><li><strong>Elderly or cardiac patients</strong>: Begin with 1.7 mcg/kg/day or lower doses to avoid cardiovascular strain.</li><li><strong>Pediatrics</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Newborns</strong>: 10-15 mcg/kg/day, with careful monitoring in infants at risk for cardiac failure.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Infants and children</strong>: Dosing varies by age, with gradual increments based on response. Growth and puberty considerations influence the regimen.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>With antidepressants</strong>: Increased sensitivity to catecholamines may heighten therapeutic/toxic effects.</li><li><strong>With antidiabetic medications</strong>: Adjustments may be necessary as thyroid therapy can influence glycemic control.</li><li><strong>With digitalis glycosides</strong>: Reduced therapeutic effects when transitioning from hypothyroid to euthyroid states.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Untreated thyrotoxicosis.</li><li>Acute myocardial infarction.</li><li>Uncorrected adrenal insufficiency.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Adverse effects often relate to overdosage and hyperthyroid symptoms, such as:</p><ul><li>General: Fatigue, weight loss, excessive sweating.</li><li>CNS: Irritability, insomnia, tremors.</li><li>Cardiovascular: Tachycardia, arrhythmias.</li><li>Gastrointestinal: Abdominal cramps, diarrhea.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><p>Classified as Pregnancy Category A. Requirements for Levothyroxine may increase during pregnancy. Minimal excretion into breast milk, but dosage adjustments are typically required to maintain normal lactation.</p><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Ensure adrenal insufficiency is corrected before starting therapy.</li><li>Use caution with cardiovascular conditions or long-standing severe hypothyroidism to avoid cardiac complications.</li><li>Dosage adjustments are necessary with significant body weight changes.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Management</strong></p><p>Symptoms include hyperthyroid manifestations like agitation, tachycardia, and fever. Reduce dosage or discontinue temporarily. Treat symptoms as needed.</p><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><p>Store below 30°C in a dry, light-protected environment. Keep out of children’s reach.</p><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>Levothyroxine mimics the natural thyroid hormone T4, supporting metabolism, growth, and energy balance in the body. Regular monitoring ensures effective and safe treatment.</p>', 'active', '1438_1734261054.png', 4, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 16:10:54', '2024-12-15 16:10:54'),
(200, 'Fixocard', 'Amlodipine + Atenolol', 8.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '50 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications for Fixocard 50 mg</strong></p><p>Fixocard 50 mg (Amlodipine and Atenolol) is indicated for the following:</p><ul><li>Hypertension not controlled by monotherapy</li><li>Co-existing angina pectoris and hypertension</li><li>Post-myocardial infarction (MI) patients</li><li>Refractory angina pectoris where nitrate therapy has been ineffective</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Combined antihypertensive preparations</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Amlodipine</strong>: A dihydropyridine calcium channel blocker that inhibits calcium influx into vascular smooth muscle and cardiac muscle. It primarily acts on vascular smooth muscle, resulting in vasodilation, reduced peripheral vascular resistance, and lower blood pressure. It also decreases coronary vasoreactivity, reduces afterload, and lowers cardiac oxygen demand.</li><li><strong>Atenolol</strong>: A cardio-selective beta-blocker that lowers blood pressure by decreasing cardiac output, reducing plasma renin activity, and suppressing sympathetic nervous system activity. Atenolol also reduces myocardial oxygen demand by its negative inotropic and chronotropic effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><ul><li>The usual dosage is one tablet daily of either <strong>Amlodipine 5 mg &amp; Atenolol 50 mg</strong> or <strong>Amlodipine 5 mg &amp; Atenolol 25 mg</strong>.</li><li>Dosage adjustment based on therapeutic response may be necessary.</li><li>For elderly patients, it is recommended to start with ½ tablet (2.5 mg Amlodipine and 25 mg Atenolol).</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Amlodipine</strong>: Safe to use with thiazide diuretics, beta-blockers, alpha-blockers, ACE inhibitors, nitrates, NSAIDs, antibiotics, and oral hypoglycemic agents. It does not affect protein binding of drugs such as digoxin, phenytoin, warfarin, or indomethacin.</li><li><strong>Atenolol</strong>: Can reduce the clearance of disopyramide by 20%, potentially causing additive inotropic effects. High doses of ampicillin (≥1 g) may decrease atenolol levels. Atenolol may affect insulin sensitivity and inhibit insulin secretion, although to a lesser degree than non-selective beta-blockers.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Fixocard is contraindicated in:</p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Amlodipine or Atenolol</li><li>Sinus bradycardia</li><li>Second or higher-degree heart block</li><li>Cardiogenic shock</li><li>Hypotension</li><li>Congestive heart failure or poor left ventricular function</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Generally well-tolerated. Reported side effects include:</p><ul><li>Fatigue</li><li>Headache</li><li>Edema</li><li>Nausea</li><li>Drowsiness</li><li>Anxiety</li><li>Depression</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy</strong>: Contraindicated as atenolol crosses the placenta.</li><li><strong>Lactation</strong>: Avoid use during breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions and Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Atenolol may mask symptoms of hyperthyroidism and hypoglycemia.</li><li>It may enhance the effects of hypoglycemic agents in diabetic patients.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place protected from light.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1087_1734261337.png', 2, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 16:15:37', '2024-12-15 16:15:37'),
(201, 'Cildip', 'Cilnidipine', 8.00, 14, 'Tablet', '14 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '5 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Cildip 5 mg</strong></p><p>Cildip 5 mg is prescribed for managing hypertension, particularly to protect end organs from damage due to high blood pressure. It is effective in elderly patients and individuals with conditions such as diabetes and albuminuria. Additionally, Cildip 5 mg is increasingly used for patients with chronic kidney disease.</p><p>Hypertension refers to elevated blood pressure, which occurs when the force of blood flowing through the blood vessels exceeds normal levels, potentially leading to vascular damage.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Cildip 5 mg belongs to the therapeutic class of <strong>calcium-channel blockers</strong>.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Cildip 5 mg acts as a dihydropyridine calcium-channel blocker. It binds to L-type voltage-dependent calcium channels, reducing calcium ion (Ca²⁺) influx into vascular smooth muscle cells. This leads to muscle relaxation and vasodilation, lowering blood pressure.</p><p>It also inhibits N-type calcium channels in sympathetic nerve cell membranes, reducing norepinephrine release. This dual mechanism helps prevent reflex tachycardia following a drop in blood pressure.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults</strong>: The typical dose is 5-10 mg once daily after breakfast, with a maximum of 20 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Elderly</strong>: Begin with the lowest possible dose (5 mg) due to increased susceptibility to hypotension.</li><li><strong>Pediatric Use</strong>: The safety of Cildip 5 mg in children has not been established.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><p>Cildip 5 mg can interact with:</p><ul><li>Other antihypertensives or antipsychotics that may cause hypotension.</li><li>Drugs such as quinidine, carbamazepine, phenytoin, rifampicin, cimetidine, and erythromycin.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Cildip 5 mg is contraindicated in patients with:</p><ul><li>Known hypersensitivity to the drug or its excipients.</li><li>Conditions such as cardiogenic shock, recent myocardial infarction (MI), unstable angina, or severe aortic stenosis.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common side effects include:</p><ul><li>Dizziness, flushing, headache, hypotension, and peripheral edema.</li><li>Gastrointestinal disturbances, palpitations, lethargy, and increased urination frequency.</li><li>Depression, eye pain, and fatigue.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Cildip 5 mg should not be used during pregnancy or in women who might be pregnant.</li><li>Nursing mothers are advised to avoid this medication or discontinue breastfeeding if use is necessary.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions and Warnings</strong></p><p>Exercise caution in patients with:</p><ul><li>Severe hepatic impairment.</li><li>A history of serious adverse reactions to calcium-channel blockers.</li><li>During discontinuation, reduce the dose gradually under medical supervision.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture. Keep out of reach of children.</p>', 'active', '122_1734261748.webp', 7, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 16:22:28', '2024-12-15 16:22:28'),
(202, 'Pregaba', 'Pregabalin', 15.00, 10, 'Capsul', '10 piece in a strip', 'Capsule', '50 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Pregaba 50 mg</strong></p><p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p>Pregaba 50 mg is indicated for the treatment of:</p><ol><li><strong>Neuropathic pain</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Diabetic peripheral neuropathy (DPN).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Postherpetic neuralgia (PHN).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Neuropathic pain associated with spinal cord injury.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Partial-onset seizures</strong> (as adjunctive therapy for patients over one month of age).</li><li><strong>Fibromyalgia</strong>.</li></ol><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Adjunct anti-epileptic medications.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Pregaba 50 mg is structurally related to gamma-aminobutyric acid (GABA), but it does not bind directly to GABAA, GABAB, or benzodiazepine receptors. Instead, it binds with high affinity to the alpha-2-delta subunit of voltage-gated calcium channels in the central nervous system. This binding may contribute to its anti-nociceptive and anti-seizure effects. It has a bioavailability of approximately 90%, is not significantly metabolized, and is primarily excreted unchanged by the kidneys, with an elimination half-life of about 6.3 hours in individuals with normal renal function.</p><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Neuropathic Pain (DPN)</strong>: Start with 50 mg three times daily (150 mg/day). Increase to 300 mg/day within one week, based on response and tolerability.</li><li><strong>Postherpetic Neuralgia (PHN)</strong>: Start with 75 mg twice daily or 50 mg three times daily (150 mg/day). Titrate to 300 mg/day within one week. For insufficient pain relief, doses up to 600 mg/day may be considered.</li><li><strong>Partial-onset Seizures</strong>: Start with 150 mg/day, divided into two or three doses. Maximum: 600 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Fibromyalgia</strong>: Start with 75 mg twice daily (150 mg/day). Increase to 300 mg/day within one week, with a maximum of 450 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Neuropathic Pain (Spinal Cord Injury)</strong>: Start with 75 mg twice daily (150 mg/day). Titrate to 300 mg/day within one week, with a maximum of 600 mg/day.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration Notes</strong></p><ul><li>Capsules can be taken with or without food.</li><li>For extended-release (CR) tablets, take after dinner; do not crush or chew. If a dose is missed, follow specific timing instructions to avoid overlap or omission.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Pregaba 50 mg or its components.</li></ul><p><strong>Common Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults</strong>: Dizziness, somnolence, dry mouth, edema, blurred vision, weight gain, and concentration difficulties.</li><li><strong>Children</strong>: Increased weight and appetite (when treated for partial-onset seizures).</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions and Warnings</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Angioedema</strong>: Discontinue immediately if symptoms occur.</li><li><strong>Hypersensitivity reactions</strong>: Stop treatment if hives, dyspnea, or wheezing are observed.</li><li><strong>Suicidal thoughts</strong>: Monitor for signs of depression or suicidal ideation.</li><li><strong>Respiratory depression</strong>: Risk increases with concurrent CNS depressants or pre-existing respiratory conditions.</li><li><strong>Impaired abilities</strong>: May cause dizziness or drowsiness, affecting the ability to drive or operate machinery.</li><li><strong>Withdrawal</strong>: Taper off gradually over at least two weeks to prevent rebound symptoms or seizures.</li></ol><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Classified as a <strong>Category C</strong> drug. Use only if the benefits outweigh potential risks to the fetus.</li><li>Trace amounts may be found in breast milk; breastfeeding is not recommended due to potential tumorigenicity risks.</li></ul><p><strong>Pediatric Use</strong></p><ul><li>Safety and efficacy have not been established for most indications in children, except for partial-onset seizures in patients over one month old.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Management</strong></p><p>Symptoms: Depressed consciousness, agitation, confusion, seizures, or cardiac issues.</p><p>Treatment: General supportive care, airway protection, and gastric decontamination if necessary.</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place below 30°C. Keep away from light and moisture, and out of children\'s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>Pregaba 50 mg modulates the activity of voltage-gated calcium channels, which may help reduce neuropathic pain and seizure activity.</p><p>This streamlined structure ensures clarity and easy reference while maintaining all critical information. Let me know if you need further refinements!</p>', 'active', '1023_1734262075.png', 7, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 16:27:55', '2024-12-15 16:27:55'),
(203, 'Betaloc', 'Metoprolol Tartrate', 1.55, 14, 'Tablet', '14 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '25 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Betaloc (Metoprolol 25 mg)</strong></p><p>Betaloc is used in the management of:</p><ol><li><strong>Hypertension</strong> (high blood pressure)</li><li><strong>Angina pectoris</strong> (chest pain due to heart-related issues)</li><li><strong>Cardiac arrhythmias</strong>, especially <strong>supraventricular tachyarrhythmias</strong> (abnormal heart rhythms)</li><li>As an <strong>adjunct to the treatment of hyperthyroidism</strong> (to control symptoms)</li><li><strong>Acute myocardial infarction</strong> (heart attack) to reduce infarct size and the risk of ventricular fibrillation. It also helps reduce mortality in these patients.</li><li>It may reduce the need for opiate analgesics, and has been shown to <strong>decrease the incidence of arrhythmias</strong> during an acute heart attack.</li></ol><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Metoprolol is a <strong>selective beta1-blocker</strong>, which primarily affects the heart. It reduces the heart\'s response to catecholamines (stress hormones), thereby lowering heart rate, blood pressure, and contractility. Unlike non-selective beta-blockers, Metoprolol has less impact on insulin release and carbohydrate metabolism, and it interferes less with the cardiovascular response to hypoglycemia.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Hypertension</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Initial dose: 100 mg per day, increasing by 100 mg weekly, up to 400 mg per day.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Divided doses may be required for better control.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Angina</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">50-100 mg, taken 2-3 times daily.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Cardiac Arrhythmias</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">50 mg twice or three times daily. The dose can be increased up to 300 mg per day.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Hyperthyroidism</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">50 mg, taken 4 times daily.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Acute Myocardial Infarction</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Initial oral dose: 50 mg every 6 hours for 48 hours after the last injection. Maintenance dose: 200 mg per day in divided doses.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common side effects include:</p><ul><li>Tiredness, dizziness, and depression</li><li>Gastrointestinal issues like nausea, diarrhea, and constipation</li><li>Slow heart rate, mental confusion, and headache</li><li>Shortness of breath, muscle pain, and blurred vision</li><li>Sleep disturbances like insomnia or nightmares</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Severe bradycardia, heart block, sick-sinus syndrome, and cardiogenic shock</li><li>Known hypersensitivity to Metoprolol or other beta-blockers</li><li>Severe peripheral arterial disease and uncontrolled heart failure</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Bronchospastic Diseases</strong>: Use cautiously in patients with asthma or bronchospasm.</li><li><strong>Diabetes</strong>: May mask the symptoms of hypoglycemia.</li><li><strong>Major Surgery</strong>: Beta-blockers may impair the heart\'s response during surgery.</li><li><strong>Peripheral Vascular Disease</strong>: Can worsen arterial insufficiency.</li><li><strong>Calcium Channel Blockers</strong>: Caution when used together, as they can have additive effects on heart rate and contractility.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects and Treatment</strong></p><p>Overdose can cause severe hypotension, bradycardia, heart failure, bronchospasm, and more. Treatment includes:</p><ul><li>Symptomatic management (e.g., with atropine for bradycardia)</li><li>Glucagon may reverse the effects of overdose.</li><li>Temporary pacing or inotropic agents like dopamine may be needed for severe cases.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><p>Store in a cool, dry place away from light.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Use in Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Renal Impairment</strong>: No dosage adjustment required.</li><li><strong>Hepatic Impairment</strong>: Dose reduction may be necessary in severe liver dysfunction.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>Metoprolol works by blocking the beta1-receptors in the heart, reducing the effects of catecholamines, which results in a decrease in heart rate, blood pressure, and overall cardiac workload. It is more selective for beta1 receptors than non-selective beta-blockers, providing fewer side effects related to other systems like the lungs and metabolism.<strong>Indications of Betaloc (Metoprolol 25 mg)</strong></p><p>Betaloc is used in the management of:</p><ol><li><strong>Hypertension</strong> (high blood pressure)</li><li><strong>Angina pectoris</strong> (chest pain due to heart-related issues)</li><li><strong>Cardiac arrhythmias</strong>, especially <strong>supraventricular tachyarrhythmias</strong> (abnormal heart rhythms)</li><li>As an <strong>adjunct to the treatment of hyperthyroidism</strong> (to control symptoms)</li><li><strong>Acute myocardial infarction</strong> (heart attack) to reduce infarct size and the risk of ventricular fibrillation. It also helps reduce mortality in these patients.</li><li>It may reduce the need for opiate analgesics, and has been shown to <strong>decrease the incidence of arrhythmias</strong> during an acute heart attack.</li></ol><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Metoprolol is a <strong>selective beta1-blocker</strong>, which primarily affects the heart. It reduces the heart\'s response to catecholamines (stress hormones), thereby lowering heart rate, blood pressure, and contractility. Unlike non-selective beta-blockers, Metoprolol has less impact on insulin release and carbohydrate metabolism, and it interferes less with the cardiovascular response to hypoglycemia.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Hypertension</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Initial dose: 100 mg per day, increasing by 100 mg weekly, up to 400 mg per day.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Divided doses may be required for better control.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Angina</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">50-100 mg, taken 2-3 times daily.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Cardiac Arrhythmias</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">50 mg twice or three times daily. The dose can be increased up to 300 mg per day.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Hyperthyroidism</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">50 mg, taken 4 times daily.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Acute Myocardial Infarction</strong>:</li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Initial oral dose: 50 mg every 6 hours for 48 hours after the last injection. Maintenance dose: 200 mg per day in divided doses.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common side effects include:</p><ul><li>Tiredness, dizziness, and depression</li><li>Gastrointestinal issues like nausea, diarrhea, and constipation</li><li>Slow heart rate, mental confusion, and headache</li><li>Shortness of breath, muscle pain, and blurred vision</li><li>Sleep disturbances like insomnia or nightmares</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Severe bradycardia, heart block, sick-sinus syndrome, and cardiogenic shock</li><li>Known hypersensitivity to Metoprolol or other beta-blockers</li><li>Severe peripheral arterial disease and uncontrolled heart failure</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Bronchospastic Diseases</strong>: Use cautiously in patients with asthma or bronchospasm.</li><li><strong>Diabetes</strong>: May mask the symptoms of hypoglycemia.</li><li><strong>Major Surgery</strong>: Beta-blockers may impair the heart\'s response during surgery.</li><li><strong>Peripheral Vascular Disease</strong>: Can worsen arterial insufficiency.</li><li><strong>Calcium Channel Blockers</strong>: Caution when used together, as they can have additive effects on heart rate and contractility.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects and Treatment</strong></p><p>Overdose can cause severe hypotension, bradycardia, heart failure, bronchospasm, and more. Treatment includes:</p><ul><li>Symptomatic management (e.g., with atropine for bradycardia)</li><li>Glucagon may reverse the effects of overdose.</li><li>Temporary pacing or inotropic agents like dopamine may be needed for severe cases.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><p>Store in a cool, dry place away from light.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Use in Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Renal Impairment</strong>: No dosage adjustment required.</li><li><strong>Hepatic Impairment</strong>: Dose reduction may be necessary in severe liver dysfunction.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>Metoprolol works by blocking the beta1-receptors in the heart, reducing the effects of catecholamines, which results in a decrease in heart rate, blood pressure, and overall cardiac workload. It is more selective for beta1 receptors than non-selective beta-blockers, providing fewer side effects related to other systems like the lungs and metabolism.</p>', 'active', '1586_1734262338.jpg', 9, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 16:32:18', '2024-12-15 16:32:18'),
(204, 'Tiginor', 'Atorvastatin Calcium', 11.50, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li>Adjunct to diet for reducing elevated total cholesterol, LDL cholesterol, apolipoprotein B (Apo-B), and triglycerides when dietary and other non-pharmacological measures are insufficient.</li><li>Reduction of total cholesterol and LDL cholesterol in patients with heterozygous and homozygous familial hypercholesterolemia.</li><li>Treatment of mixed dyslipidemia (Fredrickson Type Ia and Ib).</li><li>Management of hypertriglyceridemia (Fredrickson Type IV).</li><li>Treatment of dysbetalipoproteinemia (Fredrickson Type III).</li><li>Reduction of cardiac ischemic events in patients with asymptomatic or mild to moderate coronary artery disease with elevated LDL-cholesterol levels.</li><li>Lowering of cholesterol in hypercholesterolemia exacerbated by diabetes or renal transplantation.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Other Anti-anginal &amp; Anti-ischaemic drugs, Statins</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><p>Atorvastatin inhibits HMG-CoA reductase, the enzyme responsible for converting HMG-CoA to mevalonate, a precursor of sterols, including cholesterol. This reduces plasma cholesterol and lipoprotein levels by inhibiting cholesterol synthesis in the liver and enhancing the uptake and breakdown of LDL through hepatic LDL receptors.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Primary Hypercholesterolemia and Combined Hyperlipidemia:</strong></li><li>Adults: 10 mg once daily, may increase up to 80 mg daily after 4 weeks.</li><li>Children (10-18 years): 10 mg daily, increase to 20 mg daily if needed.</li><li><strong>Familial Hypercholesterolemia:</strong></li><li>Adults: Start with 10 mg daily, increase to 40 mg after 4 weeks, up to 80 mg if necessary.</li><li>Children (10-18 years): Start with 10 mg daily, may increase to 80 mg.</li><li><strong>Prevention of Cardiovascular Events:</strong></li><li>Adults: Start with 10 mg once daily, adjusted according to response.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>Increased risk of myopathy with cyclosporine, fibric acid derivatives, erythromycin, azole antifungals, and niacin.</li><li>No significant interactions with antihypertensives or hypoglycemic agents.</li><li>Close monitoring needed when combined with digoxin, erythromycin, oral contraceptives, colestipol, antacids, and warfarin.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any component.</li><li>Active liver disease or unexplained persistent elevations in serum transaminases.</li><li>Previous serious adverse reactions to HMG-CoA reductase inhibitors.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Constipation, flatulence, dyspepsia, abdominal pain.</li><li>Others: Infection, headache, back pain, rash, fatigue, joint pain, muscle pain.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Contraindicated during pregnancy and breastfeeding. Use effective contraception during therapy. Discontinue if pregnancy occurs.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Monitor liver function before and during treatment.</li><li>Caution in patients with alcohol use or liver disease.</li><li>Discontinue if significant muscle pain or elevated CPK levels occur.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose:</strong></p><ul><li>No specific treatment available. Symptomatic treatment and supportive care should be provided. Monitor liver function and serum CK levels. Hemodialysis is not effective in enhancing atorvastatin clearance.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry place, away from light and heat. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Geriatric Use:</strong> No significant safety or efficacy differences in older adults, but caution is advised due to increased susceptibility to myopathy.</li><li><strong>Hepatic Impairment:</strong> Contraindicated in active liver disease.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Atorvastatin reduces cholesterol and lipoprotein levels by inhibiting HMG-CoA reductase in the liver, increasing hepatic LDL receptors to enhance LDL catabolism.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '950_1734262563.jpg', 2, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 16:36:03', '2024-12-15 16:36:03');
INSERT INTO `products` (`id`, `productName`, `genericName`, `retail_max_price`, `cart_qty_inc`, `cart_text`, `unit_in_pack`, `type`, `quantity`, `prescription`, `feature`, `description`, `status`, `coverImage`, `company_id`, `category_id`, `add_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(205, 'Viglimet', 'Vildagliptin + Metformin Hydrochloride', 22.00, 6, 'Tablet', '6 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '50 mg+850 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p>Viglimet 50 mg + 850 mg is indicated as an adjunct to diet and exercise for improving glycemic control in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus, particularly for those whose diabetes is inadequately controlled by Metformin Hydrochloride or Vildagliptin alone. It may also be prescribed to patients who are already using Vildagliptin and Metformin Hydrochloride in separate tablets.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Combination Oral Hypoglycemic Preparations</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Vildagliptin inhibits Dipeptidyl Peptidase-4 (DPP-4), an enzyme that degrades incretin hormones like GLP-1 and GIP. This inhibition increases insulin secretion and decreases glucagon secretion, resulting in better glucose control. Metformin Hydrochloride works by decreasing hepatic glucose production, improving insulin sensitivity, and reducing intestinal glucose absorption.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><em>Adults</em>: Initiate with 1 tablet twice daily (morning and evening) based on the current Metformin dose. Patients already on separate Vildagliptin and Metformin tablets can be switched to this combination.</li><li><em>Max Dose</em>: Do not exceed 100 mg of Vildagliptin per day.</li><li><em>Administration</em>: Taking the tablet with or just after food can reduce gastrointestinal side effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><p>Viglimet has a low potential for drug interactions, as Vildagliptin does not affect cytochrome P450 enzymes. Co-administration with other common drugs like glibenclamide, pioglitazone, or simvastatin does not result in significant interactions. However, drugs like furosemide, nifedipine, and glyburide may increase the blood levels of Metformin.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any components</li><li>Renal dysfunction or disease</li><li>Congestive heart failure</li><li>Acute or chronic metabolic acidosis, including diabetic ketoacidosis</li><li>Use in patients undergoing radiologic studies with iodinated contrast materials</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common side effects include headache, tremor, dizziness, nausea, and hypoglycemia.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><em>Pregnancy</em>: Should not be used unless the benefits outweigh risks.</li><li><em>Lactation</em>: It is unknown if the drug is excreted in breast milk; not recommended for breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li><em>Lactic acidosis</em>: Risk due to Metformin accumulation, requiring immediate discontinuation if suspected.</li><li>Regular monitoring of serum creatinine and liver function is advised, especially in elderly and patients with existing renal or liver conditions.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><p>Store in a dry, cool place, away from light and heat. Keep out of the reach of children.</p><p><strong>Use in Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li><em>Pediatric</em>: Not recommended for use in children under 18 years.</li><li><em>Elderly</em>: Should only be used with normal renal function, and renal function should be monitored regularly.</li><li><em>Renal impairment</em>: Contraindicated in patients with severe renal impairment (serum creatinine &gt; 1.5 mg/dl in males and &gt; 1.4 mg/dl in females).</li><li><em>Hepatic impairment</em>: Not recommended for patients with liver dysfunction.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><ul><li><em>Vildagliptin</em>: Inhibits DPP-4 to enhance incretin hormones, improving insulin secretion and lowering blood glucose.</li><li><em>Metformin</em>: Reduces glucose production in the liver, improves insulin sensitivity, and increases glucose utilization.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '247_1734262843.png', 4, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 16:40:43', '2024-12-15 16:40:43'),
(206, 'Dimerol', 'Gliclazide', 8.00, 14, 'Tablet', '14 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '80 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><br></p><p><strong>Indications of Dimerol 80 mg</strong></p><p>Dimerol 80 mg is an oral antidiabetic medication used to reduce blood sugar levels in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus. It is prescribed when diet, exercise, and weight management alone are insufficient to control blood glucose levels.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Sulfonylureas</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li>Dimerol 80 mg is a second-generation sulfonylurea that lowers blood glucose by stimulating insulin release from the pancreatic β-cells, improving calcium transport across cell membranes, and reducing hepatic glucose production.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Initial Dose</strong>: 40 to 80 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Maximum Dose</strong>: Up to 320 mg daily in divided doses.</li><li><strong>Administration</strong>: Take before meals. For modified-release (MR) tablets, the typical dose is 120 mg daily, taken in a single dose at breakfast.</li><li><strong>Children</strong>: Not recommended for use in juvenile-onset diabetes.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose</strong>: Overdose may lead to hypoglycemia (low blood sugar). Immediate treatment with sugar or sugary drinks followed by a snack or meal is necessary. In case of unconsciousness, seek emergency medical help.</p><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Increased effect</strong>: Medicines like other oral antidiabetics, beta-blockers, ACE inhibitors, certain antibiotics, and antifungal treatments can enhance Dimerol\'s hypoglycemic effects.</li><li><strong>Decreased effect</strong>: Drugs such as corticosteroids, certain antidepressants, and medications for asthma or labor can reduce its effectiveness.</li><li><strong>Blood clotting</strong>: Dimerol may increase the effects of blood-thinning medicines like warfarin.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Not suitable for patients with type 1 diabetes, severe liver or kidney disease, or those who are pregnant or breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common</strong>: Hypoglycemia (low blood sugar), nausea, abdominal pain, and dizziness.</li><li><strong>Serious</strong>: Severe skin reactions, liver disorders, blood disorders, and visual disturbances.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Contraindicated</strong>: Not recommended for use during pregnancy or breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><ul><li>Regular blood sugar monitoring is necessary, especially in the first few weeks of treatment.</li><li>Avoid alcohol, which may cause unpredictable blood sugar changes.</li><li>In stress conditions (e.g., surgery or fever), temporary insulin therapy may be required.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, away from children, and do not use past the expiration date.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><ul><li>Dimerol stimulates insulin release and reduces glucose production in the liver by targeting pancreatic β-cells and enhancing calcium transport.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '319_1734263057.jpg', 9, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 16:44:17', '2024-12-15 16:44:17'),
(207, 'Thyrin', 'Levothyroxine Sodium', 2.25, 15, 'Tablet', '15 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '50 mcg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Thyrin 50 mcg (Levothyroxine)</strong></p><ul><li>Replacement therapy for hypothyroidism of any cause.</li><li>Not for transient hypothyroidism during the recovery phase of subacute thyroiditis.</li><li>Suppression of Thyroid Stimulating Hormone (TSH) levels in the presence of goitres, nodules, or post-surgical/radiological thyroid cancer treatment.</li><li>Suppression of goitrogenic effects of drugs like Lithium.</li><li>Diagnostic aid in suppression tests.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Thyroid drugs &amp; hormones.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Thyrin contains synthetic Levothyroxine (T4), identical to natural thyroid hormone. It is converted to the more active Triiodothyronine (T3) in peripheral tissues. The long half-life of T4 ensures steady T3 levels from a single daily dose.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Initial dose: 25-50 mcg/day, gradually increased every 6-8 weeks until TSH normalizes.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Severe hypothyroidism: 12.5-25 mcg/day, increased by 25 mcg every 2-4 weeks.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Secondary/tertiary hypothyroidism: Titrated to normal free T4 levels.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For patients over 50 or with cardiac disease: 1.7 mcg/kg/day.</li><li><strong>Pediatrics</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Newborns: 10-15 mcg/kg/day.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Infants: Increase dose after 4-6 weeks based on clinical response.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Children: Starting dose of 25 mcg/day, gradually increased as needed.</li><li><strong>For Goitres &amp; Cancer</strong>: Target TSH suppression, usually 2.6 mcg/kg/day.</li><li><strong>Diagnostic Use</strong>: Dosage varies based on the investigation.</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction</strong></p><ul><li>Increased effects with tricyclic antidepressants, antidiabetics, or insulin.</li><li>Reduced digitalis glycoside levels in hyperthyroidism or euthyroidism.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Untreated thyrotoxicosis.</li><li>Acute myocardial infarction.</li><li>Uncorrected adrenal failure.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Overdose leads to hyperthyroid symptoms: fatigue, weight loss, tremors, anxiety, palpitations, diarrhea, etc.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Category A, but increased requirements may occur during pregnancy.</li><li>Minimal thyroid hormone excretion in milk; cautious use in lactating women.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Correct any adrenocortical insufficiency before initiating therapy.</li><li>Caution in patients with cardiovascular disease or severe hypothyroidism.</li><li>Adjust dosage for significant body weight changes or varying T3/T4 levels.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: agitation, confusion, arrhythmias, fever, diarrhea, convulsions.</li><li>Treatment: Reduce or stop medication temporarily. Symptomatic care.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, in a dry place, away from light, and out of children\'s reach.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><ul><li>Synthetic Levothyroxine (T4) mimics the natural thyroid hormone, leading to the conversion to T3 in peripheral tissues, resulting in a long-term therapeutic effect.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '413_1734263318.png', 4, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 16:48:38', '2024-12-15 16:48:38'),
(208, 'Osartil Plus', 'Losartan Potassium + Hydrochlorothiazide', 10.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '50 mg+12.5 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Osartil Plus 50 mg + 12.5 mg</strong> is a combined medication indicated primarily for the treatment of hypertension. It is also used to reduce the risk of stroke in patients with hypertension and left ventricular hypertrophy.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Combined antihypertensive preparations.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Losartan:</strong> An angiotensin II receptor antagonist, losartan blocks the effects of angiotensin II by selectively antagonizing its binding to AT1 receptors, preventing vasoconstriction and aldosterone secretion.</li><li><strong>Hydrochlorothiazide:</strong> A thiazide diuretic that works by inhibiting sodium reabsorption in the distal tubules, leading to increased excretion of sodium, water, potassium, and hydrogen ions.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Hypertension:</strong> The usual starting dose is 50/12.5 mg once daily, with a maximum dose of 100/25 mg. The dosage may be adjusted depending on the patient\'s response.</li><li><strong>Hypertensive Patients with Left Ventricular Hypertrophy:</strong> Starting dose is 50/12.5 mg, with titration up to 100/25 mg as needed.</li><li><strong>Severe Hypertension:</strong> The initial dose is 50/12.5 mg once daily, and it can be increased to 100/25 mg after 2-4 weeks if necessary.</li></ul><p><strong>Note:</strong> The dosage for elderly patients or those with volume depletion or hepatic impairment may require careful adjustment.</p><p><strong>Administration:</strong></p><ul><li>Can be taken with or without food.</li><li>May be combined with other antihypertensive agents.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Losartan:</strong> No significant drug-drug pharmacokinetic interactions with Hydrochlorothiazide, Digoxin, Warfarin, or Cimetidine. Avoid concurrent use with potassium-sparing diuretics, potassium supplements, or salt substitutes due to risk of hyperkalemia.</li><li><strong>Hydrochlorothiazide:</strong> Can interact with alcohol, barbiturates, narcotics (causing orthostatic hypotension), antidiabetic drugs (requiring dosage adjustments), and other antihypertensive agents (additive effects).</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any components of the drug.</li><li>Contraindicated in patients with anuria or hypersensitivity to sulfonamide-derived drugs.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Symptomatic hypotension, dizziness, hyperkalemia, angioedema, vertigo, headache, and gastro-intestinal disturbances.</li><li>Rare: Hepatitis, syncope, pancreatitis, anaphylaxis, cough, depression, erectile dysfunction, renal impairment, and rhabdomyolysis.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Discontinue the medication if pregnancy is detected.</li><li>Thiazides are excreted in human milk, and due to potential risks, nursing should be discontinued or the drug should be stopped.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Monitor serum electrolytes periodically to detect electrolyte imbalances.</li><li>Caution in patients with impaired renal function, cirrhosis, or hypotension.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Losartan:</strong> Most likely causes hypotension and tachycardia. Treatment involves supportive care.</li><li><strong>Hydrochlorothiazide:</strong> May cause electrolyte depletion (hypokalemia, dehydration). If digitalis is also administered, hypokalemia can worsen cardiac arrhythmias.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C and keep out of the reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pediatric Use:</strong> Safety and efficacy not established.</li><li><strong>Renal Impairment:</strong> Not recommended for severe renal impairment.</li><li><strong>Hepatic Impairment:</strong> Caution is advised, especially during titration, as the 25 mg starting dose of Losartan cannot be given.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Losartan:</strong> Blocks the effects of angiotensin II, reducing vasoconstriction and aldosterone secretion.</li><li><strong>Hydrochlorothiazide:</strong> Increases sodium and chloride excretion, leading to reduced plasma volume and subsequent lowering of blood pressure.</li></ul><p>This combination therapy is designed to provide effective blood pressure control, particularly in patients with hypertension and left ventricular hypertrophy.</p>', 'active', '573_1734263589.webp', 2, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 16:53:09', '2024-12-15 16:53:09'),
(209, 'Telmidip', 'Amlodipine + Telmisartan', 12.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '5 mg+80 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Telmidip 5 mg + 80 mg</strong></p><p>This combination is used to treat <strong>essential hypertension</strong> in adults. It can be used in the following scenarios:</p><ol><li><strong>Replacement Therapy</strong>: Patients who are already on separate telmisartan and amlodipine tablets can switch to this combination for convenience and better adherence to treatment.</li><li><strong>Add-On Therapy</strong>: For patients whose blood pressure is not adequately controlled by either telmisartan or amlodipine alone, this combination may be added.</li><li><strong>Initial Therapy</strong>: It can be used as initial therapy for patients who are likely to need multiple drugs to reach their blood pressure goals. Careful evaluation of benefits and risks should be done before using it as initial therapy.</li></ol><p>This combination is especially relevant for <strong>patients with moderate to severe hypertension</strong>, who are at high risk for cardiovascular events like stroke, heart attacks, and heart failure.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong>: Combined antihypertensive preparations.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Amlodipine</strong> works by relaxing the peripheral and coronary vascular smooth muscles, leading to vasodilation. It inhibits calcium ions from entering the vascular smooth muscle and myocardium, enhancing myocardial oxygen delivery, especially in conditions like vasospastic angina.</li><li><strong>Telmisartan</strong> is an angiotensin II receptor antagonist. It works by preventing angiotensin II from binding to its receptor, thus reducing its vasoconstrictor and aldosterone-secreting effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration of Telmidip 5 mg + 80 mg</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adult Dosage</strong>: One tablet once daily, with a maximum of two tablets per day.</li><li><strong>Replacement Therapy</strong>: For patients already on telmisartan and amlodipine separately, this combination can be used to simplify treatment.</li><li><strong>Add-On Therapy</strong>: For patients whose blood pressure remains uncontrolled with monotherapy.</li><li><strong>Initial Therapy</strong>: Starting dose is <strong>40/5 mg once daily</strong>, especially for those who require multiple medications for blood pressure control. It is not recommended for patients over 75 years or those with hepatic impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong>: Telmisartan &amp; Amlodipine can be taken with or without food.</p><p><strong>Elderly and Children</strong>: No adjustment for elderly, but use is not recommended in children under 18 due to insufficient safety and efficacy data.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><ul><li>No significant drug interactions have been reported in clinical studies for the combination of telmisartan and amlodipine. However, caution is needed when combining these with other antihypertensive drugs or medications that affect the cardiovascular system.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Hypersensitivity</strong> to telmisartan, amlodipine, or any of the excipients.</li><li><strong>Biliary obstructive disorders</strong>, <strong>severe hepatic impairment</strong>, <strong>hypotension</strong>, <strong>cardiogenic shock</strong>, <strong>left ventricle outflow tract obstruction</strong>, and <strong>haemodynamically unstable heart failure after acute myocardial infarction</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common</strong>: Dizziness, peripheral edema, headache, somnolence, vertigo, bradycardia, palpitations, hypotension, orthostatic hypotension, flushing, cough, abdominal pain, diarrhea, nausea, pruritus, muscle spasms, erectile dysfunction, asthenia, fatigue, chest pain, increased hepatic enzymes.</li></ul><p>Patients are advised to consult a healthcare provider if they experience any severe or persistent side effects.</p>', 'active', '672_1734263810.jpg', 2, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 16:56:50', '2024-12-15 16:56:50'),
(210, 'Comprid', 'Gliclazide', 8.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '80 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Sulfonylureas</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><p>Comprid 80 mg is a second-generation sulfonylurea that lowers blood sugar by stimulating the release of insulin from pancreatic β-cells. It also reduces glucose production in the liver by facilitating calcium transport across the β-cell membranes.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Oral route</strong>: The typical initial dose is 40-80 mg daily, which can be increased to a maximum of 320 mg daily in divided doses if needed.</li><li><strong>Timing</strong>: It should be taken before meals.</li><li><strong>Modified Release Preparation</strong>: For patients using the modified-release (MR) tablet, the dose ranges from 40-80 mg daily, with a maximum of 120 mg in one dose, typically at breakfast.</li><li><strong>Combination therapy</strong>: When combined with other diabetes medications (e.g., metformin, insulin), the doctor will determine the appropriate dose.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose:</strong></p><p>If too many tablets are taken, hypoglycemia (low blood sugar) may occur. Symptoms include shaking, dizziness, and confusion. Immediate consumption of sugar (e.g., glucose tablets, sugary drinks) can help, but severe cases may require medical attention.</p><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Enhanced hypoglycemic effect</strong>: When combined with other antidiabetic drugs, beta-blockers, or certain antibiotics (e.g., sulfonamides, clarithromycin).</li><li><strong>Weakened effect</strong>: Medications like corticosteroids, chlorpromazine, and diuretics can reduce its blood-glucose-lowering effect.</li><li><strong>Warfarin</strong>: It may increase the effect of blood-thinning medications.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Insulin-dependent (type 1) diabetes</li><li>Diabetic ketoacidosis or pre-coma</li><li>Severe kidney or liver disease</li><li>Pregnancy and breastfeeding</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common</strong>: Hypoglycemia (low blood sugar), nausea, vomiting, skin rash, and digestive disturbances.</li><li><strong>Serious</strong>: Severe skin reactions, liver disorders, blood disorders (e.g., anemia), and visual disturbances.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Hypoglycemia risk</strong>: Monitor blood sugar regularly, especially during the first weeks of treatment. Avoid skipping meals or excessive alcohol consumption.</li><li><strong>High blood sugar (hyperglycemia)</strong> can occur if the medication dose is insufficient or the treatment plan is not followed.</li><li><strong>Kidney or liver impairment</strong>: Dosage adjustments may be necessary.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Not recommended during pregnancy or breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, away from children, and discard expired medicine properly to protect the environment.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Stimulates insulin release from the pancreas and reduces hepatic glucose output by facilitating calcium transport across pancreatic β-cells.</li></ul><p>This medication requires careful monitoring of blood sugar levels to prevent both hypo- and hyperglycemia, along with adherence to lifestyle modifications as advised by a healthcare provider.</p>', 'active', '57_1734264113.webp', 4, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 17:01:53', '2024-12-15 17:01:53'),
(211, 'Dialiptin-M', 'Vildagliptin + Metformin Hydrochloride', 19.00, 7, 'Tablet', '7 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '50 mg+850 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Combination Oral Hypoglycemic Preparations</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Vildagliptin</strong>: Inhibits DPP-4 (Dipeptidyl peptidase-4), which is responsible for degrading incretin hormones like GLP-1 and GIP. This leads to increased insulin secretion and decreased glucagon secretion, ultimately reducing hepatic glucose production and lowering blood glucose levels.</li><li><strong>Metformin Hydrochloride</strong>: A biguanide that decreases basal and postprandial glucose levels. It works by reducing hepatic glucose production, decreasing glucose absorption in the intestine, and improving insulin sensitivity by increasing peripheral glucose uptake.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults</strong>: Initiate with one tablet twice daily (morning and evening), based on the current dose of Metformin. The combination can replace separate doses of Metformin and Vildagliptin.</li><li>Doses above 100 mg of Vildagliptin are not recommended.</li><li>It may be taken with or just after food to minimize gastrointestinal issues.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>No significant pharmacokinetic interactions with drugs like glibenclamide, pioglitazone, amlodipine, or simvastatin.</li><li>Furosemide, nifedipine, and glyburide may increase the blood levels of Metformin.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Vildagliptin, Metformin, or any excipients.</li><li>Renal dysfunction, acute myocardial infarction, sepsis, or congestive heart failure.</li><li>Metabolic acidosis or diabetic ketoacidosis, with or without coma.</li><li>Discontinue before and after radiologic studies involving iodinated contrast.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Headache, tremor, dizziness, nausea, hypoglycemia.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Should not be used during pregnancy unless the benefit outweighs the potential risk.</li><li>Should not be used in breastfeeding women, as it is unclear if the drugs are excreted in human milk.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Lactic acidosis</strong>: Metformin accumulation can lead to lactic acidosis. Discontinue immediately if symptoms arise.</li><li>Regular monitoring of renal function, liver enzymes, and serum creatinine is advised.</li><li>Discontinue prior to elective surgery requiring general anesthesia and resume 48 hours later.</li><li>Careful monitoring is required in elderly patients and those with hepatic or renal impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Populations:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pediatrics</strong>: Not recommended for children under 18 years.</li><li><strong>Elderly</strong>: Should have regular renal function checks due to the potential for decreased renal function.</li><li><strong>Renal Impairment</strong>: Contraindicated in patients with significant renal dysfunction (serum creatinine &gt;1.5 mg/dl for males or &gt;1.4 mg/dl for females).</li><li><strong>Hepatic Impairment</strong>: Not recommended in patients with hepatic dysfunction.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry place, away from light and heat. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '763_1734264383.jpg', 9, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 17:06:23', '2024-12-15 17:06:23'),
(212, 'Bisocor', 'Bisoprolol Fumarate', 7.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '2.5 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Hypertension</strong>: Used to manage high blood pressure.</li><li><strong>Angina</strong>: For the treatment of chest pain (angina).</li><li><strong>Moderate to severe heart failure</strong>: As part of the management for heart failure.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Anti-adrenergic agent (Beta blockers)</li><li>Beta-adrenoceptor blocking drugs</li><li>Beta-blockers</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong> Bisoprolol Hemifumarate is a highly selective ß1 blocker, with a stronger affinity for ß1 receptors in the heart compared to other available beta-blockers. It selectively blocks ß1 adrenergic receptors, leading to reduced heart rate and cardiac output, thus lowering blood pressure. Unlike non-ß1 selective beta-blockers, Bisoprolol does not negatively affect lipid metabolism or cholesterol fractions, including HDL-cholesterol, over the long term.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Hypertension</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Usual starting dose is 5 mg once daily (2.5 mg may be suitable for some).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If 5 mg is inadequate, the dose may be increased to 10 mg, and then 20 mg once daily if necessary.</li><li><strong>Angina</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Typically 10 mg once daily (5 mg may be sufficient for some).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Maximum dose is 20 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Heart Failure</strong>:</li><li>Start with 1.25 mg once daily for one week, increasing gradually:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">2.5 mg once daily for the second week,</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">3.75 mg once daily for the third week,</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">5 mg once daily for the next 4 weeks,</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">7.5 mg once daily for 4 weeks,</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Maximum dose is 10 mg daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>Bisoprolol should not be combined with other ß-blockers.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Cardiogenic shock</li><li>Overt heart failure</li><li>Second or third degree A-V block</li><li>Right ventricular failure due to pulmonary hypertension</li><li>Sinus bradycardia</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Gastrointestinal disturbances</li><li>Bradycardia (slow heart rate)</li><li>Hypotension (low blood pressure)</li><li>Headache</li><li>Fatigue</li><li>Sleep disturbances</li><li>Dizziness, vertigo</li><li>Thrombocytopenia (low platelet count)</li><li>Visual disturbances</li><li>Alopecia (hair loss)</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Safety during pregnancy has not been established.</li><li>No available data for lactation.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Regular monitoring of renal, hepatic, and hematopoietic function is recommended during long-term treatment with Bisoprolol.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry place, away from light and heat.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1893_1734264627.webp', 4, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 17:10:27', '2024-12-15 17:10:27'),
(213, 'Rosutin', 'Rosuvastatin', 22.00, 15, 'Tablet', '15 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong>:</p><ul><li>Heterozygous Hypercholesterolemia (Familial and Non-familial)</li><li>Homozygous Hypercholesterolemia (Familial)</li><li>Mixed Dyslipidemia (Fredrickson Type IIa and IIb)</li><li>Primary prevention of cardiovascular disease</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong>:</p><ul><li>Other Anti-anginal &amp; Anti-ischaemic Drugs, Statins</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong>:</p><p>Rosutin 10 mg is a selective, competitive inhibitor of HMG-CoA reductase, which is involved in converting 3-hydroxy-3-methyl glutaryl coenzyme A to mevalonate, a precursor to cholesterol. It works in two ways:</p><ol><li>It increases the number of LDL receptors on liver cells, enhancing the uptake and breakdown of LDL cholesterol.</li><li>It inhibits the synthesis of VLDL, reducing the number of VLDL and LDL particles.</li></ol><p><strong>Dosage</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Adults</strong>: 5-40 mg once daily (do not exceed 40 mg unless required).</li><li><strong>Homozygous Familial Hypercholesterolemia (HoFH)</strong>: Starting dose is 20 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Pediatric Patients with HeFH</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Age 8-10 years: 5-10 mg/day</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Age 10-17 years: 5-20 mg/day</li><li><strong>Pediatric Patients with HoFH</strong>: 20 mg/day for ages 7-17 years.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong>:</p><p>Can be taken with or without food, at any time of the day.</p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Cyclosporine</strong>: Limit Rosutin to 5 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Gemfibrozil</strong>: Avoid combination; limit to 10 mg/day if necessary.</li><li><strong>Lopinavir/Ritonavir or Atazanavir/Ritonavir</strong>: Limit Rosutin to 10 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Coumarin Anticoagulants</strong>: May prolong INR. Monitor INR frequently.</li><li><strong>Lipid-lowering therapies (e.g., fibrates, niacin)</strong>: Increased risk of muscle effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong>:</p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Rosutin components</li><li>Active liver disease or unexplained persistent liver enzyme elevations</li><li>Pregnancy or breastfeeding</li><li>Women who may become pregnant</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong>:</p><ul><li>Common: Headache, myalgia, constipation, asthenia, abdominal pain, nausea.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong>:</p><p>Safety during pregnancy is not established. It is unknown whether Rosutin is excreted in human milk.</p><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Skeletal Muscle Effects</strong>: Risks of myopathy and rhabdomyolysis increase with higher doses, older age, hypothyroidism, renal impairment, or use with certain medications. Discontinue if symptoms appear.</li><li><strong>Liver Enzyme Monitoring</strong>: Monitor liver enzymes before and during treatment for persistent elevations.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong>:</p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, protected from light and moisture.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1739_1734264983.png', 3, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 17:16:23', '2024-12-15 17:16:23'),
(214, 'Karkuma Organic Imunne Plus', 'Nourishes Immune System and Health', 850.00, 1, 'x 120\'s capsule pack', '120\'s capsule in a pack', 'Capsule', '450 mg', 'no', 'yes', '<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Karkuma Organic Imunne Plus 450 mg is a functional food that helps maintain a strong immune system and supple health. The antioxidant-rich curcumin from turmeric promotes healthy inflammation, and Piperine helps the body absorb curcumin.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Key Ingredients:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Organic Turmeric Powder&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Organic Curcuminoids</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Organic Black Pepper Extract</span></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Key Benefits:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Helps to increase the beauty and glow of the skin.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Boosts Immune System.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Helps in digestion.</span></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Read the label carefully before use</li><li>Store it in a cool and dry place</li><li>Do not exceed the recommended dosage</li></ul>', 'active', '1273_1734265008.webp', 46, 8, NULL, '2024-12-15 17:16:48', '2024-12-15 17:16:48'),
(215, 'Anclog', 'Clopidogrel Bisulphate', 12.03, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '75 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Anclog 75 mg</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Acute Coronary Syndrome (ACS)</strong>: Reduces the incidence of myocardial infarction (MI) and stroke in patients with non-ST-segment elevation ACS (unstable angina or NSTEMI).</li><li><strong>Recent MI, Stroke, or Peripheral Arterial Disease</strong>: Reduces the risk of MI and stroke in patients with a history of recent MI, stroke, or established peripheral arterial disease.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Anti-platelet drugs</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Clopidogrel, a prodrug, inhibits platelet activation and aggregation by binding irreversibly to the P2Y12 ADP receptors on platelets. Its platelet aggregation inhibitory effects can be seen within 2 hours of a single oral dose, reaching steady state between 3 and 7 days with repeated daily doses.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Acute Coronary Syndrome</strong>: Start with a 300 mg loading dose (4 tablets), followed by 75 mg once daily. Avoiding the loading dose will delay the onset of antiplatelet effect.</li><li><strong>Recent MI, Stroke, or Peripheral Arterial Disease</strong>: 75 mg once daily without a loading dose. Can be taken with or without food.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Increased bleeding risk</strong>: NSAIDs, warfarin, SSRIs, SNRIs</li><li><strong>CYP2C19 inhibitors (e.g., omeprazole, esomeprazole)</strong>: Avoid these drugs with clopidogrel as they may reduce its effectiveness.</li><li><strong>Repaglinide</strong>: Avoid concomitant use, as clopidogrel increases repaglinide plasma concentrations.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to clopidogrel or its components</li><li>Active bleeding conditions like peptic ulcer or intracranial hemorrhage</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Common: Bleeding, diarrhea, gastrointestinal discomfort, skin reactions</li><li>Rare: Acquired hemophilia, anemia, angioedema, arthritis, bone marrow disorders</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Should only be used during pregnancy if necessary, as there are no well-controlled studies.</li><li>It is unknown if clopidogrel is excreted in breast milk. Nursing decisions should balance the drug\'s importance for the mother.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Genetic variations or CYP2C19 inhibitors (e.g., omeprazole) may impair clopidogrel\'s effectiveness.</li><li>Increased risk of bleeding due to prolonged platelet aggregation.</li><li>Discontinue 5 days before surgeries with high bleeding risk. Resume once hemostasis is achieved.</li><li>Thrombotic Thrombocytopenic Purpura (TTP) has been reported; requires urgent treatment.</li><li>Possible hypersensitivity reactions.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Overdose can lead to bleeding complications, and platelet transfusion may help restore clotting ability.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C in a dry place, protected from light. Keep out of reach of children. Do not freeze.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li>Not recommended for pediatric use. No dosage adjustments are needed for the elderly.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>Clopidogrel, as a prodrug, inhibits platelet aggregation through irreversible binding to the P2Y12 receptor, with effects visible within hours and reaching steady-state inhibition in a few days.</p>', 'active', '829_1734265198.webp', 4, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 17:19:58', '2024-12-15 17:19:58'),
(216, 'Vigorex', 'Sildenafil Citrate', 30.10, 5, 'Tablet', '5 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '50 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Erectile Dysfunction</strong>: Sildenafil helps in treating erectile dysfunction by enhancing the effects of nitric oxide (NO) and promoting smooth muscle relaxation in the corpus cavernosum, leading to increased blood flow to the penis.</li><li><strong>Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension</strong>: Sildenafil is used to treat pulmonary arterial hypertension by dilating the pulmonary arteries, improving blood flow, and reducing the workload of the heart.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong>: Drugs for Erectile Dysfunction</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li>Sildenafil selectively inhibits phosphodiesterase type 5 (PDE5), an enzyme responsible for the degradation of cyclic guanosine monophosphate (cGMP) in the corpus cavernosum. By inhibiting PDE5, Sildenafil increases cGMP levels, leading to smooth muscle relaxation and increased blood flow.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Erectile Dysfunction</strong>: Typically, 50 mg taken approximately 1 hour before sexual activity. Dose can be adjusted between 25 mg to 100 mg based on efficacy and tolerance. Maximum frequency: once per day.</li><li><strong>Pulmonary Arterial Hypertension</strong>: 20 mg, three times daily, spaced 4-6 hours apart, with or without food.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong>:</p><ul><li>Sildenafil may take longer to work if taken with a heavy meal.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong>:</p><ul><li>Sildenafil metabolism is influenced by the cytochrome P450 (CYP) enzymes, primarily CYP3A4. Co-administration with CYP3A4 inhibitors (e.g., ketoconazole, erythromycin) may increase Sildenafil plasma concentrations.</li><li>Combining Sildenafil with nitrates or nitric oxide donors is contraindicated due to the risk of severe hypotension.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong>:</p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Sildenafil or any component of the drug.</li><li>Use in patients taking organic nitrates or nitric oxide donors.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong>:</p><ul><li>Common: Headache, flushing, dyspepsia, nasal congestion, dizziness, visual disturbances.</li><li>Serious: Priapism (prolonged erection), sudden vision loss, hearing loss, cardiovascular events (e.g., heart attack, stroke), and syncope.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong>:</p><ul><li>Category B (no adequate studies in pregnant women). Sildenafil is not intended for use by women.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong>:</p><ul><li>Caution in patients with cardiovascular disease, bleeding disorders, or anatomical deformation of the penis.</li><li>Monitor for hypotension when combined with alpha-blockers or antihypertensive drugs.</li><li>Use cautiously in elderly patients and those with renal or hepatic impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong>:</p><ul><li>Overdose may lead to increased incidence of adverse effects. Renal dialysis is not effective in removing Sildenafil due to its high plasma protein binding.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage</strong>:</p><ul><li>Store in a dry place, away from light and heat, and out of the reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong>:</p><ul><li>Sildenafil enhances the effect of nitric oxide (NO), leading to increased levels of cGMP, which causes smooth muscle relaxation and increased blood flow in the corpus cavernosum during sexual stimulation.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacokinetics</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Absorption</strong>: Rapid absorption with peak plasma concentration within 30-120 minutes.</li><li><strong>Metabolism</strong>: Primarily metabolized by the liver via CYP3A4.</li><li><strong>Excretion</strong>: Primarily excreted via the feces (80%) and urine (13%).</li></ul><p><strong>Special Populations</strong>:</p><ul><li>Elderly: Reduced clearance, higher plasma levels.</li><li>Hepatic and Renal Impairment: Caution is advised with dose adjustments based on clearance rates.</li></ul><p><strong>Note</strong>: Always consult a healthcare provider before using Sildenafil to ensure its safety and appropriateness for your condition.</p>', 'active', '957_1734265509.webp', 4, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 17:25:09', '2024-12-15 17:25:09'),
(217, 'Karkuma Organic Turmeric Immune Booster', 'Nourishes Immune System and Health', 390.00, 1, 'Bottle (80gm)', '80 gm bottle', 'Powder', '80 gm', 'no', 'yes', '<p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Karkuma Organic Turmeric Immune Booster 80 gm is a functional food that helps maintain a strong immune system and supple health. The antioxidant-rich curcumin from turmeric promotes healthy inflammation, and Piperine helps the body absorb curcumin.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Key Ingredients:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Organic Turmeric Powder&nbsp;</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Organic Curcuminoids</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Organic Black Pepper Extract</span></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Key Benefits:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Helps to increase the beauty and glow of the skin.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Boosts Immune System.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">Helps in digestion.</span></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li>Read the label carefully before use</li><li>Store it in a cool and dry place</li><li>Do not exceed the recommended dosage</li></ul>', 'active', '1983_1734265992.webp', 46, 8, NULL, '2024-12-15 17:33:12', '2024-12-15 17:33:12'),
(218, 'Karkuma Organic Apple Cider Vinegar', 'Beneficial to Good Health', 650.00, 1, 'Bottle (480gm)', '480 gm glass bottle', 'Vinegar', '480 gm', 'no', 'yes', '<p>Karkuma Organic Apple Cider Vinegar 480 gm<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\"> is Sourced from the world’s largest producer of commercial vinegar, Karkuma Apple Cider Vinegar with the Mother is known for its multi-purpose usage in modern days.&nbsp; The refined taste of one of the best tonics is essential for every household.</span></p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Key Benefits:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Helps to lose weight</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Supports to reduce blood sugar</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Promotes good gut health</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Supports to boost skin health</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Boosts Energy</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Promotes smooth digestion</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Supports to lose belly fat</span></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Directions For Use:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">1-2 tablespoons of apple cider vinegar should be mixed with 100-200 ml of water.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Eating before meals helps reduce insulin spikes to control glucose. Straws should be used to protect tooth enamel. And after eating should be cleaned well.</span></li></ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Safety Information:</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Pregnant or lactating women, diabetics, and people with known medical conditions and/or taking drugs should consult with a licensed physician prior to taking dietary supplements.</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Read the information carefully before use</span></li><li><span style=\"color: rgb(33, 33, 33);\">Keep out of reach of children.</span></li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '662_1734266228.webp', 46, 8, NULL, '2024-12-15 17:37:08', '2024-12-15 17:37:08'),
(219, 'Karkuma Organic Superfood', 'Balances Immunity Naturally', 1000.00, 1, 'x 120\'s capsule pack', '120\'s capsule in a pack', 'Capsule', '450 mg', 'no', 'yes', '<p class=\"ql-align-justify\">The&nbsp;<strong>Karkuma Superfood</strong>&nbsp;is a functional food product, specially formulated for the betterment of women’s menstrual health. Its all raw materials are&nbsp;<a href=\"https://organicnutrition.com.bd/pages/certificate\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color: rgb(108, 189, 69);\">United State Department of Agriculture (USDA) Organic certiﬁed</a>&nbsp;and collected from the different authentic sources in the world.</p>', 'active', '433_1734266465.webp', 46, 8, NULL, '2024-12-15 17:41:05', '2024-12-15 17:41:05');
INSERT INTO `products` (`id`, `productName`, `genericName`, `retail_max_price`, `cart_qty_inc`, `cart_text`, `unit_in_pack`, `type`, `quantity`, `prescription`, `feature`, `description`, `status`, `coverImage`, `company_id`, `category_id`, `add_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(220, 'Karkuma Organic Honey', 'Beneficial for Health and Wellness', 750.00, 1, 'x 400 gm glass jar', '400 gm glass jar', 'Honey', '400 gm', 'no', 'yes', '<p>The Karkuma Organic Honey is loaded with more than 900 plant compounds and extracted from the heart of the beehive. It is collected from a variety of flowers and is the rarest honey in the world. The uniqueness of the black honey provides us with health benefits that go beyond the benefits of regular honey. This honey is a magic remedy for daily consumption. It is loaded with nutrition and enzymes, beneficial for our health and wellness.&nbsp;</p><ul><li><strong>USDA Organic Certified</strong></li><li><strong>Net weight: 400g&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Origin: West Africa&nbsp;</strong></li><li><strong>Packaging: Glass Jar with Metal Cap</strong></li><li><strong>Cash on Delivery: Available</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Tastes like... unlike anything you have ever tasted before</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(72, 72, 72);\">In the first spoon, you will feel the nectar and pollen of thousands of wildflowers melt in your mouth&nbsp;to&nbsp;give you a unique sweet grainy texture feel that only exists in raw unfiltered honey. The gratifying aftertaste lingers in your mouth and forces you to take the second spoon. And then, you will have elevated yourself to&nbsp;the level where you will never go back to ordinary honey.&nbsp;</span></p><p><strong>A rare&nbsp;delicacy</strong></p><p>Very few&nbsp;forests exist in the world that are not contaminated by pollution.&nbsp;This naturally black and thick honey can only be found in the deepest forests and is extremely difficult to collect making it a rare delicacy for honey lovers.&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Yes! it is USDA-Certified Organic</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(72, 72, 72);\">We know it\'s not wrapped in a jute bag top with a hay rope like most \'Organic\' claimed products, but our certificates speak for our products. This honey is sourced from&nbsp;Africa, a USDA-certified company (USA-based company operating in West African countries), and packed in our&nbsp;CODEX (WHO/FAO) GMP Certified, USFDA Registered, USDA Organic Certified, ISO 22000: 2018 Certified&nbsp;&nbsp;facility in Bangladesh.</span>&nbsp;</p><p>Organic Nutrition Ltd. is also a Member of IFOAM, Bonn, Germany.</p>', 'active', '1949_1734266777.webp', 46, 8, NULL, '2024-12-15 17:46:17', '2024-12-15 17:52:35'),
(221, 'Febus', 'Febuxostat', 15.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '40 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Drugs used in Gout</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li>Febus 40 mg is a non-purine, selective xanthine oxidase (XO) inhibitor that reduces serum uric acid by inhibiting xanthine oxidase, the enzyme responsible for uric acid production. It does so by preventing the breakdown of hypoxanthine to xanthine and further to uric acid. At therapeutic concentrations, Febus 40 mg does not inhibit other enzymes involved in purine and pyrimidine metabolism.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li>The recommended starting dose is 40 mg once daily. If the target serum uric acid level of less than 6 mg/dL is not achieved after 2 weeks, the dose can be increased to 80 mg once daily.</li><li>Febus 40 mg can be taken with or without food or antacids.</li><li>No dose adjustment is necessary for patients with mild to moderate renal or hepatic impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>Concomitant use with azathioprine, mercaptopurine, or theophylline may increase the plasma concentrations of these drugs, potentially leading to severe toxicity.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Febus 40 mg is contraindicated in patients who are taking azathioprine, mercaptopurine, or theophylline.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common side effects include liver function abnormalities, nausea, arthralgia, and rash.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Febus 40 mg is classified as Pregnancy Category C. There are no adequate studies in pregnant women, so it should only be used if the benefits justify the risks.</li><li>It is not known whether Febus 40 mg is excreted in human milk, so caution is advised for nursing women.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Gout Flare:</strong> Gout flares may increase during the initiation of treatment. Prophylactic therapy (e.g., NSAIDs or colchicine) may be beneficial for up to six months.</li><li><strong>Cardiovascular Events:</strong> Febus 40 mg may increase the risk of cardiovascular thromboembolic events compared to allopurinol. Patients should be monitored for signs of myocardial infarction (MI) or stroke.</li><li><strong>Liver Enzyme Elevation:</strong> Liver function tests should be monitored periodically as elevations in transaminase levels may occur.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose:</strong></p><ul><li>Febus 40 mg has been studied in doses up to 300 mg daily in healthy subjects for seven days without evidence of dose-limiting toxicity.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture, and out of the reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pediatric Use:</strong> Safety and effectiveness have not been established for patients under 18 years of age.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Febus 40 mg is a selective xanthine oxidase inhibitor that decreases uric acid levels by inhibiting xanthine oxidase.</li></ul>', 'active', '79_1742305803.jpg', 44, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 17:47:58', '2025-03-18 18:50:03'),
(222, 'Karkuma Organic Honey', 'Beneficial for Health and Wellness', 570.00, 1, 'x 300 gm glass jar', '300 gm glass jar', 'Honey', '300 gm', 'no', 'yes', '<p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">The Karkuma Organic Honey is loaded with more than 900 plant compounds and extracted from the heart of the beehive. </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\">It is collected from a variety of flowers and is the rarest honey in the world.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\"> The uniqueness of the black honey provides us with health benefits that go beyond the benefits of regular honey.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\"> This honey is a magic remedy for daily consumption.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\"> It is loaded with nutrition and enzymes, beneficial for our health and wellness. </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\"> USDA Organic Certified</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\"> Net weight: 300g </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\"> Origin: West Africa </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(51, 51, 51);\"> Packaging: Glass Jar with Metal Cap </span></p>', 'active', '1192_1734266977.jpg', 46, 8, NULL, '2024-12-15 17:49:37', '2024-12-15 17:52:19'),
(223, 'Prosan', 'Losartan Potassium', 8.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '50 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Prosan 50 mg:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Hypertension:</strong> Prosan 50 mg is used to manage high blood pressure and can be taken alone or in combination with other antihypertensive medications, such as thiazide diuretics.</li><li><strong>Renal Protection in Type-2 Diabetic Patients with Proteinuria:</strong> For hypertensive individuals with type-2 diabetes and proteinuria (urine albumin to creatinine ratio &gt;300 mg/g), Prosan 50 mg helps delay the progression of kidney disease.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong> Angiotensin II receptor blocker</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><p>Prosan 50 mg is an orally active angiotensin II receptor blocker (ARB), the first of its kind without a peptide. It works by binding to the AT1 receptor found in various tissues like the heart, kidneys, adrenal glands, and vascular smooth muscle, inhibiting vasoconstriction and aldosterone production, both of which contribute to high blood pressure.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Starting Dose:</strong> For most patients, the initial dose is 50 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Adjustment:</strong> If the effect of 50 mg is inadequate, the dose may be increased to 25 mg twice daily.</li><li><strong>For Certain Conditions:</strong> In patients with intravascular volume depletion (e.g., those on high-dose diuretics), a starting dose of 25 mg once daily is recommended.</li><li><strong>Range:</strong> The daily dose typically ranges from 25 mg to 100 mg.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Decreased Metabolism:</strong> Rifampicin and fluconazole may reduce the levels of Prosan’s active metabolite.</li><li><strong>Enhanced Effect with Diuretics:</strong> When used with hydrochlorothiazide, the antihypertensive effect may be enhanced.</li><li><strong>Potassium Increase Risk:</strong> Concurrent use of potassium-sparing diuretics, potassium supplements, or salt substitutes containing potassium may increase serum potassium.</li><li><strong>Reduced Effect with NSAIDs:</strong> Indomethacin may reduce Prosan’s antihypertensive effect.</li><li><strong>Renal Impairment Risk:</strong> Combining Prosan with an ACE inhibitor, ARB, anti-inflammatory drugs, or thiazide diuretics may increase the risk of kidney damage.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Prosan 50 mg is not recommended for pregnant women or those with hypersensitivity to any of its ingredients.</li><li>It should not be used together with Aliskiren in diabetic patients.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common Effects:</strong> Dizziness, diarrhea, nasal congestion, cough, and upper respiratory infections.</li><li><strong>Other Effects:</strong> Fatigue, edema, chest pain, nausea, headaches, and pharyngitis.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> Category D—Prosan should not be used in the second and third trimesters of pregnancy due to risks to the fetus, including decreased renal function and increased fetal morbidity and mortality.</li><li><strong>Lactation:</strong> It is unclear whether Prosan is excreted in human milk. The decision to either discontinue breastfeeding or stop the medication should be based on its importance to the mother.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy Risks:</strong> Use during the second and third trimesters can harm the fetus, affecting renal function.</li><li><strong>Volume Depletion:</strong> Symptomatic hypotension may occur in patients with low blood volume (e.g., those on high-dose diuretics).</li><li><strong>Liver and Kidney Concerns:</strong> Patients with cirrhosis may experience increased plasma levels, and those with renal impairment could face changes in kidney function, including renal failure.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong></p><p>Store in a cool, dry place, away from heat and light. Keep out of the reach of children.</p><p><strong>Drug Class:</strong> Angiotensin II receptor blocker</p><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><p>Prosan 50 mg binds to the AT1 receptors, inhibiting vasoconstriction and aldosterone production. This results in a reduction of blood pressure by relaxing blood vessels and decreasing fluid retention.</p>', 'active', '325_1734267161.jpg', 3, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 17:52:41', '2024-12-15 17:52:41'),
(224, 'Prazopress ER', 'Prazosin Hydrochloride', 17.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '5 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Hypertension:</strong> Prazosin is used to treat all grades of essential (primary) hypertension and secondary hypertension. It can be the sole agent or combined with diuretics or other antihypertensive drugs as needed. It is safe for hypertensive patients with impaired renal function.</li><li><strong>Left Ventricular Failure:</strong> Prazosin is used in the treatment of left ventricular failure, especially in patients unresponsive to conventional therapy like diuretics and cardiac glycosides.</li><li><strong>Raynaud\'s Phenomenon and Raynaud\'s Disease:</strong> It helps reduce the frequency and severity of attacks in these conditions.</li><li><strong>Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia:</strong> As an adjunct in the treatment of urinary obstruction due to benign prostatic hyperplasia, particularly in patients awaiting surgery.</li></ol><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Alpha adrenoceptor blocking drugs.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><p>Prazosin works by reducing total peripheral vascular resistance through selective inhibition of alpha-1-adrenoreceptors on vascular smooth muscle. It lowers blood pressure, particularly the diastolic pressure, without causing rebound hypertension when discontinued. It also improves cardiac output in left ventricular failure patients and reduces the symptoms of Raynaud\'s disease. In benign prostatic hyperplasia, it improves urinary pressure by blocking alpha-1 receptors on the prostate and urethra.</p><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Hypertension:</strong> Start with 0.5 mg at bedtime, gradually increasing to a total daily dosage of up to 20 mg. It can be combined with other antihypertensives.</li><li><strong>Left Ventricular Failure:</strong> Start with 0.5 mg 2-4 times daily, increasing up to 4-20 mg in divided doses.</li><li><strong>Raynaud’s Disease:</strong> Start with 0.5 mg twice daily, adjusting according to response.</li><li><strong>Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia:</strong> Start with 0.5 mg twice daily, with a typical maintenance dose of 2 mg twice daily. Doses above 4 mg should be used with caution.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration:</strong></p><p>Take with or without food. The starting dose should be taken in the evening, at least 2-3 hours before bedtime.</p><p><strong>Interactions:</strong></p><p>Prazosin XR has no major adverse interactions with cardiac-glycosides, hypoglycemic agents, tranquilizers, antiarrhythmic agents, or common analgesics.</p><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><p>Contraindicated in patients with known sensitivity to quinazolines.</p><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><p>Common side effects include dizziness, headache, drowsiness, nausea, and palpitations. Other potential side effects include orthostatic hypotension, gastrointestinal issues, edema, tachycardia, and sexual dysfunction. Rare side effects include hallucinations, depression, and skin reactions.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation:</strong></p><p>Category C. Use only if the benefit outweighs the risk. Prazosin is excreted in milk, so caution is advised in nursing mothers.</p><p><strong>Precautions:</strong></p><ul><li>For <strong>hypertension</strong>, start with a low dose to prevent postural hypotension.</li><li>In <strong>left ventricular failure</strong>, monitor closely to avoid excessive fluid retention.</li><li><strong>Raynaud’s Disease:</strong> Caution when used with other blood pressure-lowering agents.</li><li><strong>Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia:</strong> Monitor blood pressure in elderly patients.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects:</strong></p><p>In case of overdose, hypotension should be treated by restoring blood pressure, with shock managed using volume expanders or vasopressors. Prazosin is not dialyzable.</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong></p><p>Store below 30°C, away from light and moisture, and keep out of the reach of children.</p><p><strong>Use in Special Populations:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Renal Impairment:</strong> Start with a low dose and adjust cautiously.</li><li><strong>Hepatic Dysfunction:</strong> Start with a low dose and adjust cautiously.</li><li><strong>Elderly:</strong> Begin with the lowest possible dose due to increased sensitivity to hypotension.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '946_1734267712.webp', 8, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 18:01:52', '2024-12-15 18:01:52'),
(225, 'Linax', 'Linagliptin', 8.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '5 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Monotherapy</strong>: For patients who cannot manage their diabetes with diet and exercise alone, and where metformin is contraindicated due to renal issues or intolerance.</li><li><strong>Combination Therapy</strong>: For patients who are not achieving adequate glycemic control with diet, exercise, and metformin alone. It can be combined with other medications like sulfonylureas to improve efficacy.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Dipeptidyl Peptidase-4 (DPP-4) inhibitor</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Linax works by inhibiting DPP-4, which normally breaks down incretin hormones like GLP-1 and GIP. This leads to enhanced insulin secretion in response to meals and a reduction in glucagon secretion, helping control blood sugar levels.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Recommended Dose</strong>: 5 mg once daily.</li><li>It can be taken with or without food, at any time of day.</li><li>If combined with metformin or sulfonylurea, no dose modification for Linax is typically necessary, though a lower dose of sulfonylurea may be used to reduce the risk of hypoglycemia.</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction</strong></p><p>Linax does not significantly interact with common medications like metformin, sulfonylureas, warfarin, or oral contraceptives. It has a weak inhibitory effect on the CYP3A4 enzyme.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Linax’s active ingredient or any excipients.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Possible side effects include:</p><ul><li><strong>Hypoglycemia</strong> (when used with metformin or sulfonylurea)</li><li><strong>Nasopharyngitis</strong></li><li><strong>Cough</strong></li><li><strong>Pancreatitis</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy</strong>: Category B; limited data are available, so it should be used only when necessary.</li><li><strong>Lactation</strong>: The transfer into breast milk is unknown, so caution is advised.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid if allergic to any of the ingredients.</li><li>Monitor for signs of pancreatitis or other adverse effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Store in a dry place, away from heat and light, and out of the reach of children.</p>', 'active', '115_1734268104.jpg', 30, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 18:08:24', '2024-12-15 18:08:24'),
(226, 'Lantus Cartridge', 'Insulin Glargine [rDNA]', 982.00, 1, 'Injection', '1 piece in a box', 'Injection', '100IU per ml', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p>Lantus Cartridge 100IU/ml is used to improve blood glucose control in adults and children with type 1 diabetes and in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Long-acting Insulin</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Lantus is a recombinant human insulin analogue (insulin glargine) used for subcutaneous injections. It has a long duration of action (up to 24 hours) and helps lower blood glucose by stimulating glucose uptake in muscles and fat while inhibiting glucose production by the liver. It also suppresses lipolysis and proteolysis and enhances protein synthesis.</p><p><strong>Dosage</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Type 1 Diabetes</strong>: Insulin glargine is used once daily, alongside short-acting insulin to manage total daily insulin requirements.</li><li><strong>Type 2 Diabetes</strong>: Start with 10 units or 0.2 units/kg once daily, then adjust based on individual needs.</li><li><strong>Switching Insulin</strong>: Adjust dose when transitioning from other insulins (e.g., NPH).</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong></p><ul><li>Inject subcutaneously once daily, at the same time each day.</li><li><strong>Cartridge</strong>: Attach to pen, gently mix insulin, and inject.</li><li><strong>Vial</strong>: Shake gently, use syringe to withdraw correct dose, and inject subcutaneously.</li></ul><p><strong>Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Reduced Insulin Requirement</strong>: Oral anti-diabetic medications, ACE inhibitors, fluoxetine, salicylates, etc.</li><li><strong>Increased Insulin Requirement</strong>: Thiazides, glucocorticoids, thyroid hormones, etc.</li><li>Drugs such as beta-blockers and alcohol may alter insulin\'s effectiveness.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Not for use in individuals hypersensitive to insulin glargine or any of its components.</p><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Potential side effects include hypoglycemia, allergic reactions, injection site reactions, lipodystrophy, rash, and pruritus.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy</strong>: Category C. Should be used only if benefits outweigh risks.</li><li><strong>Lactation</strong>: Caution is recommended due to unknown excretion in breast milk.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Blood glucose must be monitored regularly.</li><li>Do not mix with other insulins or dilute.</li><li>Adjust doses in cases of renal or hepatic impairment.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><p>Overdose can lead to hypoglycemia. Severe cases may need glucose or glucagon treatment.</p><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><p>Store between 2°C to 8°C. Avoid freezing. Insulin in use can be kept at room temperature for up to one month.</p><p><br></p><p>This summary provides the key points about Lantus Cartridge 100IU/ml for safe usage.</p>', 'active', '1360_1734269053.png', 45, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 18:24:13', '2024-12-15 18:24:13'),
(227, 'Bextram Silver', 'Multivitamin + Multimineral A-Z silver preparation', 360.00, 1, 'x 30\'s tablet bottle', '30 tablet\'s in a bottle', 'Tablet', 'A to Z', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications of Bextram Silver</strong></p><p>This is specially formulated for the prevention and treatment of vitamin and mineral deficiencies for adults over 45 years of age.&nbsp;This Silver is also indicated to meet the increase demands of vitamin and minerals for adults over 45 years of age.</p><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><p>Each tablet contains: Vitamin A 3500 IU, Vitamin C 60 mg, Vitamin D 400 IU, Vitamin E 45 IU, Vitamin K 10 mcg, Thiamin 1.5 mg, Riboflavin 1.7 mg, Niacin 20 mg, Vitamin B6 3 mg, Folic acid 400 mcg, Vitamin B12 25 mcg, Biotin 30 mcg, Pantothenic acid 10 mg, Calcium 200 mg, Phosphorous 48 mg, Iodine 150 mcg, Magnesium 100 mg, Zinc 15 mg, Selenium 20 mcg, Copper 2 mg, Manganese 2 mg, Chromium 150 mcg, Molybdenum 75 mcg, Chloride 72 mg, Potassium 80 mg, Boron 150 mcg, Nickel 5 mcg, Silicon 2 mg, Vanadium 10 mcg, Lutein 250 mcg, Lycopene 300 mcg.</p><p><strong>Theropeutic Class</strong></p><p>Multi-vitamin &amp; Multi-mineral combined preparations</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>This preparation is a comprehensive well-balanced multivitamin and multimineral preparation scientifically adjusted and designed to serve as the complete nutritional program for the elderly people. This preparation maintains a healthy body and active lifestyle and keeps proper nutrition covered for elderly people</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration of Bextram Silver</strong></p><p>One tablet once daily with food or as indicated by the physician.</p><p><strong>Dosage of Bextram Silver</strong></p><p>One tablet once daily with food or as indicated by the physician.</p><p><strong>Interaction of Bextram Silver</strong></p><p>No drug interactions have been reported.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>This product is contraindicated in patients with known hypersensitivity to any of the ingredients. Do not take this product if taking other vitamin A supplements.</p><p><strong>Side Effects of Bextram Silver</strong></p><p>Generally, this preparation is well tolerated. Allergic sensitization has been reported following oral administration of folic acid. Vitamin C and vitamin E may cause diarrhea and other gastrointestinal disturbances.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><p>Recommended by the consultation with physician.</p><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><p>Long term intake of high levels of vitamin A (excluding that sourced from beta carotene) may increase the risk of osteoporosis in postmenopausal women.</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Keep below 30°C temperature, away from light &amp; moisture. Keep out of the reach of children.</p><p><strong>Drug Classes</strong></p><p>Multi-vitamin &amp; Multi-mineral combined preparations</p><p><strong>Mode Of Action</strong></p><p>This preparation is a comprehensive well-balanced multivitamin and multimineral preparation scientifically adjusted and designed to serve as the complete nutritional program for the elderly people. This preparation maintains a healthy body and active lifestyle and keeps proper nutrition covered for elderly people</p><p><strong>Pregnancy</strong></p><p>Recommended by the consultation with physician.</p>', 'active', '771_1734277243.jpg', 3, 8, NULL, '2024-12-15 20:40:43', '2024-12-15 20:40:43'),
(228, 'Bextram Gold', 'Multivitamin + Multimineral A-Z gold preparation', 360.00, 1, 'x 30\'s tablet bottle', '30 tablet\'s in a bottle', 'Tablet', 'A to Z', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications of Bextram Gold</strong></p><p>Bextram Gold is indicated for preventing and treating deficiencies in vitamins and minerals. This comprehensive daily nutritional supplement is also recommended to meet the heightened requirements for vitamins and minerals in various situations, including physical and emotional stress, chronic diseases, infectious illnesses, osteoporosis, injuries or wounds, surgeries, poor digestion, old age, pregnancy and lactation, decreased appetite, excessive dieting, exposure to environmental pollution, and strenuous exercise, among others.</p><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><p>Each tablet of Bextram Gold contains the following essential nutrients:</p><ul><li>Vitamin A: 5000 IU</li><li>Vitamin C: 60 mg</li><li>Vitamin D: 400 IU</li><li>Vitamin E: 30 IU</li><li>Vitamin K: 25 mcg</li><li>Vitamin B1 (Thiamine): 1.5 mg</li><li>Vitamin B2 (Riboflavin): 1.7 mg</li><li>Vitamin B3 (Niacin): 20 mg</li><li>Vitamin B6 (Pyridoxine): 2 mg</li><li>Folic acid: 400 mcg</li><li>Biotin: 30 mcg</li><li>Pantothenate: 10 mg</li><li>Calcium: 162 mg</li><li>Iron: 18 mg</li><li>Phosphorus: 109 mg</li><li>Iodine: 150 mcg</li><li>Magnesium: 100 mg</li><li>Zinc: 15 mg</li><li>Selenium: 20 mcg</li><li>Copper: 2 mg</li><li>Manganese: 2 mg</li><li>Chromium: 120 mcg</li><li>Molybdenum: 75 mcg</li><li>Chloride: 72 mg</li><li>Potassium: 80 mg</li><li>Boron: 150 mcg</li><li>Nickel: 5 mcg</li><li>Silicon: 2 mg</li><li>Tin: 10 mcg</li><li>Vanadium: 10 mcg</li><li>Lutein: 250 mcg</li><li>Cyanocobalamin: 6 mcg</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Multi-vitamin &amp; Multi-mineral combined preparations</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Multivitamin + Multimineral A-Z Gold Preparation is a supplement that combines most vitamins and minerals in a single tablet. This preparation typically contains 32 high-potency vitamins and minerals. It maintains a healthy body and an active lifestyle by providing essential nutrients that may be lacking in one\'s diet.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration of Bextram Gold</strong></p><p>The general dosage for adults is one tablet daily. The tablet can be taken with or without food. If you are pregnant or lactating, you may need to take a higher dosage of Bextram Gold.</p><p><strong>Interaction of Bextram Gold</strong></p><p>Bextram Gold is generally considered safe and has no known drug interactions.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Bextram Gold is contraindicated in patients with known hypersensitivity to any of the ingredients.</p><p><strong>Side Effects of Bextram Gold</strong></p><p>In most cases, this preparation is well tolerated. However, there may be occasional occurrences of diarrhea while undergoing beta-carotene treatment, and it\'s possible for the skin to take on a mild yellowish tint. Vitamin C and vitamin E may lead to diarrhea and other gastrointestinal disturbances.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><p>Bextram Gold is generally safe for pregnant and lactating women, but it is important to speak to your doctor before taking any supplement during pregnancy or lactation.</p><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><p>Long term intake of high levels of vitamin A (excluding that sourced from beta-carotene) may increase the risk of osteoporosis in postmenopausal women.</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Keep in a dry place, away from light and heat. Keep out of the reach of children.</p><p><strong>Drug Classes</strong></p><p>Multi-vitamin &amp; Multi-mineral combined preparations</p><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><h2>This is a film-coated tablet, which combines 32 high potency vitamins and minerals. This preparation maintains a healthy body and active lifestyle.</h2>', 'active', '911_1734277535.webp', 3, 8, NULL, '2024-12-15 20:45:35', '2024-12-15 20:45:35'),
(229, 'Filwel Gold', 'Multivitamin + Multimineral A-Z gold preparation', 360.00, 1, 'x 30\'s tablet bottle', '30 tablet\'s in a bottle', 'Tablet', 'A to Z', 'no', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Filwel Gold</strong></p><p>Filwel Gold is indicated for preventing and treating deficiencies in vitamins and minerals. This comprehensive daily nutritional supplement is also recommended to meet the heightened requirements for vitamins and minerals in various situations, including physical and emotional stress, chronic diseases, infectious illnesses, osteoporosis, injuries or wounds, surgeries, poor digestion, old age, pregnancy and lactation, decreased appetite, excessive dieting, exposure to environmental pollution, and strenuous exercise, among others.</p><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><p>Each tablet of Filwel Gold contains the following essential nutrients:</p><ul><li>Vitamin A: 5000 IU</li><li>Vitamin C: 60 mg</li><li>Vitamin D: 400 IU</li><li>Vitamin E: 30 IU</li><li>Vitamin K: 25 mcg</li><li>Vitamin B1 (Thiamine): 1.5 mg</li><li>Vitamin B2 (Riboflavin): 1.7 mg</li><li>Vitamin B3 (Niacin): 20 mg</li><li>Vitamin B6 (Pyridoxine): 2 mg</li><li>Folic acid: 400 mcg</li><li>Biotin: 30 mcg</li><li>Pantothenate: 10 mg</li><li>Calcium: 162 mg</li><li>Iron: 18 mg</li><li>Phosphorus: 109 mg</li><li>Iodine: 150 mcg</li><li>Magnesium: 100 mg</li><li>Zinc: 15 mg</li><li>Selenium: 20 mcg</li><li>Copper: 2 mg</li><li>Manganese: 2 mg</li><li>Chromium: 120 mcg</li><li>Molybdenum: 75 mcg</li><li>Chloride: 72 mg</li><li>Potassium: 80 mg</li><li>Boron: 150 mcg</li><li>Nickel: 5 mcg</li><li>Silicon: 2 mg</li><li>Tin: 10 mcg</li><li>Vanadium: 10 mcg</li><li>Lutein: 250 mcg</li><li>Cyanocobalamin: 6 mcg</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Multi-vitamin &amp; Multi-mineral combined preparations</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Multivitamin + Multimineral A-Z Gold Preparation is a supplement that combines most vitamins and minerals in a single tablet. This preparation typically contains 32 high-potency vitamins and minerals. It maintains a healthy body and an active lifestyle by providing essential nutrients that may be lacking in one\'s diet.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration of Filwel Gold</strong></p><p>The general dosage for adults is one tablet daily. The tablet can be taken with or without food. If you are pregnant or lactating, you may need to take a higher dosage of Filwel Gold.</p><p><strong>Interaction of Filwel Gold</strong></p><p>Filwel Gold is generally considered safe and has no known drug interactions.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Filwel Gold is contraindicated in patients with known hypersensitivity to any of the ingredients.</p><p><strong>Side Effects of Filwel Gold</strong></p><p>In most cases, this preparation is well tolerated. However, there may be occasional occurrences of diarrhea while undergoing beta-carotene treatment, and it\'s possible for the skin to take on a mild yellowish tint. Vitamin C and vitamin E may lead to diarrhea and other gastrointestinal disturbances.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><p>Filwel Gold is generally safe for pregnant and lactating women, but it is important to speak to your doctor before taking any supplement during pregnancy or lactation.</p><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><p>Long term intake of high levels of vitamin A (excluding that sourced from beta-carotene) may increase the risk of osteoporosis in postmenopausal women.</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Keep in a dry place, away from light and heat. Keep out of the reach of children.</p><p><strong>Drug Classes</strong></p><p>Multi-vitamin &amp; Multi-mineral combined preparations</p><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>This is a film-coated tablet, which combines 32 high potency vitamins and minerals. This preparation maintains a healthy body and active lifestyle.</p>', 'active', '38_1734278189.webp', 4, 8, NULL, '2024-12-15 20:54:43', '2024-12-15 20:56:29'),
(230, 'Filwel Silver', 'Multivitamin & Multimineral [A-Z silver preparation]', 360.00, 1, 'x 30\'s tablet bottle', '30 tablet\'s in a bottle', 'Tablet', 'A to Z', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications of Filwel Silver</strong></p><p>This is specially formulated for the prevention and treatment of vitamin and mineral deficiencies for adults over 45 years of age. Filwel Silver is also indicated to meet the increased demands of vitamins and minerals for adults over 45 years of age.</p><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><p>Each tablet contains:</p><ul><li>Vitamin A: 3500 IU</li><li>Vitamin C: 60 mg</li><li>Vitamin D: 400 IU</li><li>Vitamin E: 45 IU</li><li>Vitamin K: 10 mcg</li><li>Thiamin: 1.5 mg</li><li>Riboflavin: 1.7 mg</li><li>Niacin: 20 mg</li><li>Vitamin B6: 3 mg</li><li>Folic acid: 400 mcg</li><li>Vitamin B12: 25 mcg</li><li>Biotin: 30 mcg</li><li>Pantothenic acid: 10 mg</li><li>Calcium: 200 mg</li><li>Phosphorus: 48 mg</li><li>Iodine: 150 mcg</li><li>Magnesium: 100 mg</li><li>Zinc: 15 mg</li><li>Selenium: 20 mcg</li><li>Copper: 2 mg</li><li>Manganese: 2 mg</li><li>Chromium: 150 mcg</li><li>Molybdenum: 75 mcg</li><li>Chloride: 72 mg</li><li>Potassium: 80 mg</li><li>Boron: 150 mcg</li><li>Nickel: 5 mcg</li><li>Silicon: 2 mg</li><li>Vanadium: 10 mcg</li><li>Lutein: 250 mcg</li><li>Lycopene: 300 mcg</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Multi-vitamin &amp; Multi-mineral combined preparations</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>This preparation is a comprehensive, well-balanced multivitamin and multimineral formulation scientifically adjusted and designed to serve as a complete nutritional program for elderly individuals. It helps maintain a healthy body and an active lifestyle, ensuring that proper nutrition needs are met for seniors.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration of Filwel Silver</strong></p><p>One tablet once daily with food or as indicated by the physician.</p><p><strong>Interaction of Filwel Silver</strong></p><p>No drug interactions have been reported.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>This product is contraindicated in patients with known hypersensitivity to any of the ingredients. Do not take this product if you are taking other vitamin A supplements.</p><p><strong>Side Effects of Filwel Silver</strong></p><p>Generally, this preparation is well tolerated. However, allergic sensitization has been reported following oral administration of folic acid. Vitamin C and vitamin E may cause diarrhea and other gastrointestinal disturbances.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><p>Consult with your physician before taking Filwel Silver during pregnancy or lactation.</p><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><p>Long-term intake of high levels of vitamin A (excluding that sourced from beta carotene) may increase the risk of osteoporosis in postmenopausal women.</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Keep below 30°C, away from light and moisture. Keep out of the reach of children.</p><p><strong>Drug Classes</strong></p><p>Multi-vitamin &amp; Multi-mineral combined preparations</p><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>This preparation is a comprehensive, well-balanced multivitamin and multimineral formulation scientifically adjusted and designed to serve as a complete nutritional program for elderly individuals. It helps maintain a healthy body and active lifestyle, ensuring that proper nutrition needs are met.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy</strong></p><p>Consult with your physician before use during pregnancy.</p>', 'active', '784_1734278614.png', 4, 8, NULL, '2024-12-15 21:01:33', '2024-12-15 21:03:34'),
(231, 'Proviten Gold', 'Multivitamin + Multimineral A-Z gold preparation', 360.00, 1, 'x 30\'s tablet bottle', '30 tablet\'s in a bottle', 'Tablet', 'A to Z', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications of Proviten Gold</strong></p><p>Proviten Gold is indicated for preventing and treating deficiencies in vitamins and minerals. This comprehensive daily nutritional supplement is also recommended to meet the heightened requirements for vitamins and minerals in various situations, including physical and emotional stress, chronic diseases, infectious illnesses, osteoporosis, injuries or wounds, surgeries, poor digestion, old age, pregnancy and lactation, decreased appetite, excessive dieting, exposure to environmental pollution, and strenuous exercise, among others.</p><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><p>Each tablet of Proviten Gold contains the following essential nutrients:</p><ul><li>Vitamin A: 5000 IU</li><li>Vitamin C: 60 mg</li><li>Vitamin D: 400 IU</li><li>Vitamin E: 30 IU</li><li>Vitamin K: 25 mcg</li><li>Vitamin B1 (Thiamine): 1.5 mg</li><li>Vitamin B2 (Riboflavin): 1.7 mg</li><li>Vitamin B3 (Niacin): 20 mg</li><li>Vitamin B6 (Pyridoxine): 2 mg</li><li>Folic acid: 400 mcg</li><li>Biotin: 30 mcg</li><li>Pantothenate: 10 mg</li><li>Calcium: 162 mg</li><li>Iron: 18 mg</li><li>Phosphorus: 109 mg</li><li>Iodine: 150 mcg</li><li>Magnesium: 100 mg</li><li>Zinc: 15 mg</li><li>Selenium: 20 mcg</li><li>Copper: 2 mg</li><li>Manganese: 2 mg</li><li>Chromium: 120 mcg</li><li>Molybdenum: 75 mcg</li><li>Chloride: 72 mg</li><li>Potassium: 80 mg</li><li>Boron: 150 mcg</li><li>Nickel: 5 mcg</li><li>Silicon: 2 mg</li><li>Tin: 10 mcg</li><li>Vanadium: 10 mcg</li><li>Lutein: 250 mcg</li><li>Cyanocobalamin: 6 mcg</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Multi-vitamin &amp; Multi-mineral combined preparations</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Multivitamin + Multimineral A-Z Gold Preparation is a supplement that combines most vitamins and minerals in a single tablet. This preparation typically contains 32 high-potency vitamins and minerals. It maintains a healthy body and an active lifestyle by providing essential nutrients that may be lacking in one\'s diet.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration of Proviten Gold</strong></p><p>The general dosage for adults is one tablet daily. The tablet can be taken with or without food. If you are pregnant or lactating, you may need to take a higher dosage of Proviten Gold.</p><p><strong>Interaction of Proviten Gold</strong></p><p>Proviten Gold is generally considered safe and has no known drug interactions.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Proviten Gold is contraindicated in patients with known hypersensitivity to any of the ingredients.</p><p><strong>Side Effects of Proviten Gold</strong></p><p>In most cases, this preparation is well tolerated. However, there may be occasional occurrences of diarrhea while undergoing beta-carotene treatment, and it\'s possible for the skin to take on a mild yellowish tint. Vitamin C and vitamin E may lead to diarrhea and other gastrointestinal disturbances.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><p>Proviten Gold is generally safe for pregnant and lactating women, but it is important to speak to your doctor before taking any supplement during pregnancy or lactation.</p><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><p>Long-term intake of high levels of vitamin A (excluding that sourced from beta carotene) may increase the risk of osteoporosis in postmenopausal women.</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Keep in a dry place, away from light and heat. Keep out of the reach of children.</p><p><strong>Drug Classes</strong></p><p>Multi-vitamin &amp; Multi-mineral combined preparations</p><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>This is a film-coated tablet, which combines 32 high-potency vitamins and minerals. This preparation maintains a healthy body and active lifestyle.</p>', 'active', '1119_1734278958.webp', 2, 8, NULL, '2024-12-15 21:09:18', '2024-12-15 21:09:18'),
(232, 'Proviten Silver', 'Multivitamin + Multimineral A-Z silver preparation', 360.00, 1, 'x 30\'s tablet bottle', '30 tablet\'s in a bottle', 'Tablet', 'A to Z', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Indications of Proviten Silver</strong></p><p>This is specially formulated for the prevention and treatment of vitamin and mineral deficiencies for adults over 45 years of age. Proviten Silver is also indicated to meet the increased demands for vitamins and minerals for adults over 45 years of age.</p><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><p>Each tablet contains:</p><ul><li>Vitamin A: 3500 IU</li><li>Vitamin C: 60 mg</li><li>Vitamin D: 400 IU</li><li>Vitamin E: 45 IU</li><li>Vitamin K: 10 mcg</li><li>Thiamin: 1.5 mg</li><li>Riboflavin: 1.7 mg</li><li>Niacin: 20 mg</li><li>Vitamin B6: 3 mg</li><li>Folic acid: 400 mcg</li><li>Vitamin B12: 25 mcg</li><li>Biotin: 30 mcg</li><li>Pantothenic acid: 10 mg</li><li>Calcium: 200 mg</li><li>Phosphorus: 48 mg</li><li>Iodine: 150 mcg</li><li>Magnesium: 100 mg</li><li>Zinc: 15 mg</li><li>Selenium: 20 mcg</li><li>Copper: 2 mg</li><li>Manganese: 2 mg</li><li>Chromium: 150 mcg</li><li>Molybdenum: 75 mcg</li><li>Chloride: 72 mg</li><li>Potassium: 80 mg</li><li>Boron: 150 mcg</li><li>Nickel: 5 mcg</li><li>Silicon: 2 mg</li><li>Vanadium: 10 mcg</li><li>Lutein: 250 mcg</li><li>Lycopene: 300 mcg</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Multi-vitamin &amp; Multi-mineral combined preparations</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>This preparation is a comprehensive, well-balanced multivitamin and multimineral formulation scientifically adjusted and designed to serve as a complete nutritional program for elderly individuals. It helps maintain a healthy body and an active lifestyle, ensuring proper nutrition needs are met for older adults.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration of Proviten Silver</strong></p><p>One tablet once daily with food or as indicated by the physician.</p><p><strong>Interaction of Proviten Silver</strong></p><p>No drug interactions have been reported.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>This product is contraindicated in patients with known hypersensitivity to any of the ingredients. Do not take this product if you are taking other vitamin A supplements.</p><p><strong>Side Effects of Proviten Silver</strong></p><p>Generally, this preparation is well tolerated. However, allergic sensitization has been reported following oral administration of folic acid. Vitamin C and vitamin E may cause diarrhea and other gastrointestinal disturbances.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><p>Consult with your physician before taking Proviten Silver during pregnancy or lactation.</p><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><p>Long-term intake of high levels of vitamin A (excluding that sourced from beta carotene) may increase the risk of osteoporosis in postmenopausal women.</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Keep below 30°C, away from light and moisture. Keep out of the reach of children.</p><p><strong>Drug Classes</strong></p><p>Multi-vitamin &amp; Multi-mineral combined preparations</p><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>This preparation is a comprehensive, well-balanced multivitamin and multimineral formulation scientifically adjusted and designed to serve as a complete nutritional program for elderly individuals. It helps maintain a healthy body and active lifestyle, ensuring that proper nutrition needs are met.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy</strong></p><p>Consult with your physician before use during pregnancy.</p>', 'active', '1534_1734279169.webp', 2, 8, NULL, '2024-12-15 21:12:49', '2024-12-15 21:12:49'),
(233, 'Jardian', 'Empagliflozin', 40.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '25 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications for Jardian 25 mg</strong></p><p>Jardian 25 mg is prescribed for:</p><ul><li>Improving glycemic control in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus as an adjunct to diet and exercise.</li><li>Reducing the risk of cardiovascular death in adults with type 2 diabetes mellitus and established cardiovascular disease.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Sodium-Glucose Co-Transporter-2 (SGLT2) Inhibitors.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Jardian 25 mg works as an SGLT2 inhibitor, targeting co-transporters in the kidney responsible for reabsorbing glucose from the glomerular filtrate. By inhibiting SGLT2, the drug enhances glucose excretion via urine, lowering renal glucose reabsorption and the glucose threshold. This process reduces hyperglycemia and provides additional benefits such as aiding weight loss and lowering blood pressure.</p><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><ul><li>The initial dose of Jardian 25 mg is 10 mg once daily, taken in the morning with or without food.</li><li>If tolerated, the dose may be increased to 25 mg once daily.</li><li>In patients with volume depletion, ensure the condition is corrected before starting the medication.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Diuretics</strong>: Co-administration can increase urine output.</li><li><strong>Insulin or Insulin Secretagogues</strong>: Combining with these drugs raises the risk of hypoglycemia.</li><li><strong>Urine Glucose Testing</strong>: Not recommended for glycemic control as Jardian causes increased glucose excretion. Alternative methods should be used.</li><li><strong>1,5-AG Assay</strong>: Monitoring glycemic control via this assay is unreliable; alternative methods are advised.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Jardian 25 mg should not be used in patients with:</p><ul><li>Severe hypersensitivity to the drug or its components.</li><li>Severe renal impairment, end-stage renal disease, or those undergoing dialysis.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common side effects include:</p><ul><li>Urinary tract infections.</li><li>Female genital fungal infections.</li><li>Dehydration, low blood pressure, weakness, dizziness, and increased thirst.</li></ul><p><strong>Use During Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>There are no adequate studies in pregnant women. Jardian 25 mg should only be used if the benefits outweigh potential risks to the fetus.</li><li>It is unclear whether the drug is excreted in human breast milk; therefore, it is not recommended for breastfeeding mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions and Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Assess renal function prior to starting treatment and periodically thereafter.</li><li>Do not initiate treatment in patients with an eGFR below 45 ml/min/1.73 m².</li><li>No dose adjustment is needed for patients with an eGFR ≥ 45 ml/min/1.73 m².</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Management</strong></p><p>In case of overdose:</p><ul><li>Provide supportive measures, such as gastrointestinal decontamination, clinical monitoring, and supportive treatment.</li><li>The role of hemodialysis in removing Jardian 25 mg remains unstudied.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Instructions</strong></p><p>Store below 30°C in a cool, dry place, away from light and moisture. Keep out of reach of children.</p><p><strong>Drug Class</strong></p><p>Sodium-Glucose Co-Transporter-2 (SGLT2) Inhibitors.</p><p><strong>Mechanism of Action</strong></p><p>Jardian 25 mg inhibits SGLT2, a key protein in renal glucose reabsorption, promoting glucose excretion and lowering blood sugar levels. This mechanism also supports weight reduction and decreases blood pressure.</p><p>This avoids direct copying and retains the original meaning in a fresh presentation.</p>', 'active', '419_1734287222.png', 3, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 23:27:02', '2024-12-15 23:27:02');
INSERT INTO `products` (`id`, `productName`, `genericName`, `retail_max_price`, `cart_qty_inc`, `cart_text`, `unit_in_pack`, `type`, `quantity`, `prescription`, `feature`, `description`, `status`, `coverImage`, `company_id`, `category_id`, `add_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(234, 'Lopirel Plus', 'Clopidogrel + Aspirin', 12.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '75 mg+75 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Lopirel Plus</strong></p><p><strong>Acute Coronary Syndrome (ACS):</strong></p><p>Lopirel Plus is used to reduce the risk of Myocardial Infarction (MI) and Stroke in:</p><ul><li>Patients with non-ST-segment elevation ACS, such as unstable angina (UA) or non-ST-elevation Myocardial Infarction (NSTEMI).</li><li>Patients with acute ST-segment elevation ACS (STEMI).</li></ul><p><strong>Recent MI, Stroke, or Peripheral Arterial Disease:</strong></p><p>It is indicated for reducing the risk of MI and Stroke in patients with:</p><ul><li>Established peripheral arterial disease.</li><li>A history of recent MI or Stroke.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Anti-platelet drugs.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Lopirel Plus combines two active ingredients:</p><p><strong>Clopidogrel:</strong></p><ul><li>A prodrug that irreversibly inhibits platelet aggregation.</li><li>Its active metabolite binds to the P2Y12 ADP receptors on platelets, inhibiting activation.</li><li>Platelet aggregation inhibition begins within 2 hours of a single dose and reaches steady state between Day 3 and Day 7 with daily doses of 75 mg.</li></ul><p><strong>Aspirin:</strong></p><ul><li>Inhibits platelet aggregation by irreversibly blocking cyclooxygenase (COX), reducing thromboxane A2 production, a key driver of platelet aggregation and vasoconstriction.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><p><strong>Recommended Dose:</strong></p><p>One tablet daily.</p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><p><strong>Increased Bleeding Risk:</strong></p><ul><li>Oral anticoagulants, NSAIDs, Metamizole, SSRIs, and CYP2C19 inhibitors.</li><li><strong>Other Interactions:</strong></li><li>Tonofovir, Valproic acid, Varicella vaccine, Acetazolamide, and Nicorandil.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Clopidogrel, Aspirin, or any component of the product.</li><li>Active pathological bleeding (e.g., peptic ulcer or intracranial hemorrhage).</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Generally well tolerated.</li><li>Rarely, hypersensitivity reactions such as rash, angioedema, or hematologic abnormalities have been reported.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Use during the first and second trimesters only if necessary.</li><li>Contraindicated in the third trimester due to risk of bleeding complications.</li><li>Aspirin is excreted in human milk; Clopidogrel\'s excretion in breast milk is unknown. Avoid use during breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>May prolong bleeding time.</li><li><strong>Thrombotic Thrombocytopenic Purpura (TTP):</strong> Rare but serious, requires immediate attention.</li><li><strong>Reye\'s Syndrome Risk:</strong> Avoid in children or individuals with viral infections (e.g., chickenpox, flu symptoms).</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Management</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Clopidogrel Overdose:</strong> Can lead to bleeding complications; platelet transfusion may restore clotting ability.</li><li><strong>Aspirin Overdose:</strong> Symptoms include dizziness, tinnitus, confusion, or gastrointestinal issues. Severe cases may cause metabolic acidosis or respiratory failure, treated with hemodialysis and supportive care.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Instructions</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C in a cool, dry place away from light and moisture.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li>Not recommended for children under 12 years unless benefits outweigh risks.</li><li>Aspirin may contribute to Reye’s syndrome in children.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p><strong>Clopidogrel:</strong> Irreversibly inhibits ADP-mediated platelet activation and aggregation.</p><p><strong>Aspirin:</strong> Blocks COX, inhibiting thromboxane A2 formation, reducing platelet aggregation and vasoconstriction.</p>', 'active', '1700_1734287586.webp', 2, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 23:33:06', '2024-12-15 23:33:06'),
(235, 'Comet', 'Metformin Hydrochloride', 6.02, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '850 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications for Comet 850 mg:</strong></p><p>Comet 850 mg is indicated for managing type 2 diabetes mellitus, particularly in overweight individuals when diet and exercise alone do not achieve sufficient glycemic control.</p><ul><li><strong>Adults:</strong> Can be used alone (monotherapy) or combined with other oral antidiabetic agents or insulin.</li><li><strong>Children and Adolescents (10 years and older):</strong> Can be used alone or with insulin.</li><li>In overweight adult patients with type 2 diabetes, Metformin has been shown to reduce complications associated with diabetes when used as a first-line therapy after diet adjustments.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Biguanides</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><p>Metformin, a biguanide, is an oral antihyperglycemic medication for managing type 2 diabetes. Unlike sulfonylureas, it does not cause hypoglycemia. Metformin works by:</p><ol><li>Reducing glucose production in the liver.</li><li>Improving insulin sensitivity to enhance glucose uptake and use.</li><li>Decreasing glucose absorption in the intestines.</li></ol><p><strong>Dosage and Administration:</strong></p><p><strong>Immediate-Release Tablets:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults:</strong> Initial dose is typically 500 mg twice daily or 850 mg once daily with meals.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Dosage increases: By 500 mg weekly or 850 mg biweekly, up to 2000 mg/day in divided doses.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For patients needing additional glycemic control: Maximum dose is 2550 mg/day, divided.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Doses above 2000 mg/day may be better tolerated when divided into three doses.</li><li><strong>Children:</strong> Initial dose is 500 mg twice daily with meals.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Dosage increases: 500 mg weekly increments up to 2000 mg/day, divided into doses.</li></ul><p><strong>Extended-Release Tablets:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults:</strong> Start with 500 mg once daily with the evening meal.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Increase dose by 500 mg weekly, up to a maximum of 2000 mg once daily (or 1000 mg twice daily).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Patients can switch from immediate-release to extended-release, adhering to the maximum dose.</li><li><strong>Children:</strong> Extended-release tablets are not recommended due to lack of study data.</li></ul><p><strong>Renal Impairment:</strong></p><ul><li>Avoid use in patients with eGFR below 30 mL/min/1.73 m². Assess risks if eGFR drops below 45 mL/min/1.73 m².</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Increased Risk of Lactic Acidosis:</strong> Co-administration with carbonic anhydrase inhibitors (e.g., topiramate) or drugs that reduce Metformin clearance (e.g., ranolazine, dolutegravir, cimetidine).</li><li><strong>Alcohol:</strong> Potentiates Metformin\'s effects on lactate metabolism.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Metformin or its components.</li><li>Acute metabolic acidosis, including lactic acidosis and diabetic ketoacidosis.</li><li>Severe renal failure (eGFR &lt; 30 mL/min).</li><li>Conditions that may impair kidney function or cause tissue hypoxia, such as severe dehydration, infection, or cardiac/respiratory failure.</li><li>Hepatic insufficiency, acute alcohol intoxication, or chronic alcoholism.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common:</strong> Gastrointestinal discomfort (nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, abdominal pain, loss of appetite). Often occurs at treatment initiation and improves over time.</li><li><strong>Rare but Serious:</strong> Lactic acidosis, decreased vitamin B12 absorption (potential for megaloblastic anemia), liver function abnormalities, skin reactions (e.g., rash, pruritus).</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> Studies do not show a clear link between Metformin use and major birth defects or adverse maternal outcomes.</li><li><strong>Lactation:</strong> Metformin passes into breast milk but typically does not harm breastfeeding infants. A risk-benefit assessment is recommended.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions and Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Monitor renal function regularly; impaired function increases the risk of lactic acidosis.</li><li>Long-term use may lower vitamin B12 levels, potentially causing anemia or neuropathy.</li><li>Increased risk of hypoglycemia when combined with insulin or insulin secretagogues.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Management:</strong></p><ul><li>While Metformin overdose (up to 85 grams) typically does not cause hypoglycemia, it can result in lactic acidosis. This condition requires immediate medical treatment, often with hemodialysis.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong></p><p>Store below 30°C, away from moisture and light. Keep out of reach of children.</p><p>This version maintains accuracy while avoiding duplication of original phrasing. Let me know if further refinements are needed!</p>', 'active', '941_1734287883.jpg', 4, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 23:38:03', '2024-12-15 23:38:03'),
(236, 'Osartil', 'Losartan Potassium', 5.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '25 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Hypertension:</strong> Used alone or in combination with other antihypertensives (e.g., thiazide diuretics) to manage high blood pressure.</li><li><strong>Renal Protection in Type 2 Diabetes with Proteinuria:</strong> Recommended for hypertensive type-2 diabetics with significant proteinuria (urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio &gt;300 mg/g) to slow kidney disease progression.</li></ol><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><p>Angiotensin II receptor blocker (ARB).</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><p>Osartil 25 mg, an orally active non-peptide ARB, selectively blocks the AT1 receptor found in the heart, kidneys, adrenal glands, and vascular smooth muscle. This action reduces vasoconstriction and aldosterone secretion, both contributing to hypertension.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Standard Dose:</strong> 50 mg once daily (starting and maintenance).</li><li><strong>Alternative Dosage:</strong> 25 mg twice daily if 50 mg is insufficient.</li><li><strong>Special Populations:</strong> Begin with 25 mg once daily in patients with intravascular volume depletion (e.g., on high-dose diuretics).</li><li><strong>Total Daily Range:</strong> 25–100 mg, administered once or in divided doses.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ol><li><strong>Reduced Efficacy:</strong> Rifampicin and fluconazole may lower active metabolite levels.</li><li><strong>Increased Effects:</strong> Hydrochlorothiazide enhances antihypertensive effects.</li><li><strong>Hyperkalemia Risk:</strong> Use with potassium-sparing diuretics, potassium supplements, or potassium-rich salt substitutes may elevate serum potassium.</li><li><strong>NSAIDs (e.g., indomethacin):</strong> Can reduce antihypertensive efficacy and increase the risk of renal impairment when combined with ACE inhibitors, ARBs, or diuretics.</li></ol><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any component.</li><li>Pregnancy (Category D).</li><li>Combination with Aliskiren in diabetic patients.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common side effects include dizziness, nasal congestion, cough, upper respiratory infections, fatigue, diarrhea, and headaches. Less frequent effects are chest pain, nausea, oedema, and pharyngitis.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Warnings &amp; Precautions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> Use in the second or third trimester can harm the fetus, including reduced renal function.</li><li><strong>Renal &amp; Hepatic Function:</strong> Monitor closely in patients with renal impairment or liver cirrhosis.</li><li><strong>Volume Depletion:</strong> Symptomatic hypotension may occur in volume-depleted individuals.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy Risk:</strong> Classified as Category D. Avoid use during pregnancy.</li><li><strong>Lactation:</strong> Unknown if excreted in human milk; consider risks to the infant versus benefits to the mother.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Store in a dry place, protected from heat and light. Keep out of reach of children.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Drug Class:</strong> Angiotensin II receptor blocker.</p><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong> Inhibits AT1 receptors, reducing vasoconstriction and aldosterone production to lower blood pressure.</p><p>This version retains the necessary details while ensuring originality. Let me know if you need any further adjustments!</p>', 'active', '1173_1734288168.webp', 2, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 23:42:48', '2024-12-15 23:42:48'),
(237, 'Mixtard 30 Penfill', 'Insulin Human [rDNA] + Isophane Insulin Human', 460.00, 1, 'x 3 ml penfill', '3 ml penfill', 'Penfill', '30%+70% in 100 IU/ml', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Type 1 Diabetes</strong>: Used for all patients with Type 1 diabetes.</li><li><strong>Type 2 Diabetes</strong>: For patients inadequately controlled by diet or oral hypoglycemic agents.</li><li><strong>Acute Situations</strong>: Stabilization in diabetic ketoacidosis, hyperosmolar non-ketotic syndrome, or during stress (e.g., major surgery or serious illness).</li><li><strong>Gestational Diabetes</strong>: Effective in pregnancy-induced diabetes.</li></ul><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><p>Each mL contains:</p><ul><li><strong>30% Soluble Insulin Human (Regular)</strong> and <strong>70% Isophane Insulin Human (rDNA)</strong> for 30/70 mixtures.</li><li><strong>50% Soluble Insulin Human (Regular)</strong> and <strong>50% Isophane Insulin Human</strong> for 50/50 mixtures.</li><li>Available in concentrations of <strong>40 IU/mL</strong> or <strong>100 IU/mL</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Intermediate-acting insulin.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Mixtard 30 Penfill mimics natural insulin, manufactured via recombinant DNA technology. It facilitates glucose metabolism by promoting glucose uptake in the liver, muscle, and fat while reducing gluconeogenesis.</p><ul><li><strong>Onset</strong>: 30 minutes after injection.</li><li><strong>Peak Effect</strong>: 2–8 hours.</li><li><strong>Duration</strong>: Approximately 24 hours.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Type 1 Diabetes</strong>: Typical daily insulin requirement is <strong>0.5–1.0 IU/kg</strong>.</li><li><strong>Pre-pubertal Children</strong>: Usually <strong>0.7–1.0 IU/kg</strong>.</li><li><strong>Type 2 Diabetes</strong>: Initial doses are lower, e.g., <strong>0.3–0.6 IU/kg/day</strong>.</li><li>Dosage should be individualized, accounting for factors like diet, activity levels, and medical advice.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong></p><ul><li>Administer <strong>subcutaneously</strong> (upper arm, thigh, buttock, or abdominal wall).</li><li>Inject <strong>30 minutes before meals</strong>.</li><li>Rotate injection sites to prevent tissue damage.</li><li>Never inject intravenously.</li></ul><p><strong>Preparation Steps</strong>:</p><ol><li>Wash hands and sanitize the vial.</li><li>Mix insulin by gently rotating the vial.</li><li>Draw the correct dosage into the syringe, checking for air bubbles.</li><li>Inject at a 45° angle into clean skin.</li></ol><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Increased Insulin Requirement</strong>: Oral contraceptives, corticosteroids, thyroid hormones.</li><li><strong>Reduced Insulin Requirement</strong>: Salicylates, sulfonamides, antidepressants.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Hypoglycemia</strong>.</li><li><strong>Allergy</strong> to insulin or excipients.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common</strong>: Hypoglycemia, with symptoms appearing suddenly.</li><li><strong>Rare</strong>: Allergic reactions like redness, swelling, or itching at the injection site. Usually transient.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Safe during pregnancy as insulin does not cross the placenta.</li><li>Insulin therapy poses no risk to breastfeeding infants.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions and Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Incorrect dosing or discontinuation may lead to <strong>hyperglycemia</strong>.</li><li><strong>Hypoglycemia</strong> can occur with skipped meals or unplanned strenuous activity.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><p>Excessive insulin can cause severe <strong>hypoglycemia</strong>. Immediate medical attention is required if symptoms appear. Frequent episodes necessitate therapy reassessment.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a refrigerator at <strong>2–8°C</strong>. Do not freeze.</li><li>For in-use insulin: keep at room temperature for up to one month, away from heat and light.</li></ul><p>This summary is accurate and adheres to general medical guidelines. For personalized use, consult a healthcare professional.</p>', 'active', '1078_1734288491.png', 42, 12, NULL, '2024-12-15 23:48:11', '2025-05-08 20:37:23'),
(238, 'Rovast', 'Rosuvastatin', 20.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Rovast 10 mg</strong></p><p><strong>Rovast 10 mg</strong> is indicated for:</p><ul><li><strong>Heterozygous Hypercholesterolemia</strong> (Familial and Non-familial)</li><li><strong>Homozygous Hypercholesterolemia</strong> (Familial)</li><li><strong>Mixed Dyslipidemia</strong> (Fredrickson Type IIa and IIb)</li><li><strong>Primary Prevention of Cardiovascular Disease</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Statins</li><li>Other Anti-anginal &amp; Anti-Ischaemic Drugs</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Rovast 10 mg is a selective, competitive inhibitor of <strong>HMG-CoA reductase</strong>, the enzyme responsible for converting 3-hydroxy-3-methyl glutaryl coenzyme A to mevalonate, a precursor of cholesterol. Its lipid-modifying effects are achieved through:</p><ol><li><strong>Increased hepatic LDL receptors:</strong> Enhances LDL uptake and catabolism.</li><li><strong>Reduced hepatic VLDL synthesis:</strong> Lowers the total number of VLDL and LDL particles.</li></ol><p><strong>Dosage</strong></p><ul><li><strong>General Dose Range:</strong> 5–40 mg once daily (40 mg reserved for patients not achieving LDL-C goal with 20 mg).</li><li><strong>Homozygous Familial Hypercholesterolemia (HoFH):</strong> Start with 20 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Pediatric Patients (8–17 years):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">HeFH: 5–10 mg/day (8–9 years), 5–20 mg/day (10–17 years).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">HoFH: 20 mg/day.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong></p><ul><li>Can be taken <strong>with or without food</strong>, at any time of the day.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Cyclosporine:</strong> Increases exposure to Rovast. Maximum dose: 5 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Gemfibrozil:</strong> Avoid combination; if necessary, limit dosage to 10 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Lopinavir/Ritonavir or Atazanavir/Ritonavir:</strong> Elevates exposure. Limit dose to 10 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Coumarin Anticoagulants:</strong> Can prolong INR. Monitor INR frequently until stable.</li><li><strong>Concomitant Lipid-Lowering Therapies:</strong> Combining with fibrates or niacin may increase risk of skeletal muscle effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to components of the drug.</li><li>Liver disease or unexplained persistent hepatic transaminase elevation.</li><li>Pregnancy and lactation.</li><li>Nursing mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Rovast 10 mg is generally well-tolerated. Common adverse effects include:</p><ul><li>Headache</li><li>Myalgia</li><li>Constipation</li><li>Asthenia</li><li>Abdominal pain</li><li>Nausea</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> Safety not established. Contraindicated in pregnant women.</li><li><strong>Lactation:</strong> Unknown if excreted in human milk; avoid use.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Skeletal Muscle Effects:</strong> Includes myopathy and rhabdomyolysis, with higher risk at 40 mg dose, in elderly patients (&gt;65 years), and in those with hypothyroidism or renal impairment. Promptly report muscle pain, tenderness, or weakness.</li><li><strong>Liver Enzyme Monitoring:</strong> Persistent hepatic transaminase elevations may occur. Monitor liver enzymes before and during treatment.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><ul><li>Store below <strong>30°C</strong>, protected from light and moisture.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li>Adjust dosage and monitor closely in patients with liver or renal impairment.</li><li>Avoid use in pregnant and breastfeeding women.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1446_1734289307.png', 1, 12, NULL, '2024-12-16 00:01:47', '2024-12-16 00:01:47'),
(239, 'Carvista', 'Carvedilol', 3.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '6.25 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Carvista 6.25 mg</strong></p><p><strong>Carvista 6.25 mg</strong> is indicated for the management of mild, moderate, or severe heart failure due to ischemic or cardiomyopathic causes. It is used in combination with other therapies, such as digitalis, diuretics, and ACE inhibitors, to help slow disease progression, as demonstrated by a reduction in cardiovascular mortality, hospitalization, or the need for medication adjustments. Carvista 6.25 mg may also be considered in patients who cannot tolerate ACE inhibitors or are not receiving digitalis, hydralazine, or nitrate therapy.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Alpha adrenoceptor blocking drugs</li><li>Beta-adrenoceptor blocking drugs</li><li>Beta-blockers</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Carvista 6.25 mg is a <strong>non-selective β-adrenergic blocker</strong> with <strong>α-1 adrenergic blocking properties</strong>, providing vasodilation. It reduces total peripheral resistance and promotes vasodilation, contributing to its antihypertensive effects.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><p><strong>Hypertension</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Initial dose</strong>: 12.5 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Maintenance dose</strong>: 25 mg once daily after two days, with potential increases at intervals of at least two weeks, up to a maximum of 50 mg per day (administered as single or divided doses).</li><li><strong>Elderly patients</strong>: An initial dose of 12.5 mg daily may suffice.</li></ul><p><strong>Angina</strong>:</p><ul><li><strong>Initial dose</strong>: 12.5 mg twice daily for the first two days.</li><li><strong>Maintenance dose</strong>: 25 mg twice daily.</li><li><strong>Maximum dose</strong> for elderly patients: 50 mg per day in divided doses.</li></ul><p><strong>Heart Failure</strong> (requires close supervision):</p><ul><li><strong>Initial dose</strong>: 3.125 mg twice daily with food.</li><li>Titrate the dose at intervals of at least two weeks:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">6.25 mg twice daily,</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">12.5 mg twice daily,</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Up to 25 mg twice daily.</li><li><strong>Maximum doses</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">25 mg twice daily for patients &lt;85 kg.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">50 mg twice daily for patients &gt;85 kg.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Digoxin</strong>: Increases digoxin levels; monitor closely when starting, adjusting, or discontinuing Carvista.</li><li><strong>Rifampin</strong>: Reduces the effectiveness of Carvista by decreasing its bioavailability.</li><li><strong>Warfarin</strong>: Does not affect plasma protein binding.</li><li><strong>Clonidine</strong>: Can potentiate withdrawal effects; use cautiously.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Carvista 6.25 mg is contraindicated in patients with:</p><ul><li>Decompensated heart failure needing intravenous inotropic therapy</li><li>Bronchial asthma or related bronchospastic conditions</li><li>Second or third-degree AV block</li><li>Sick sinus syndrome without a pacemaker</li><li>Cardiogenic shock</li><li>Severe bradycardia</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common</strong>: Postural hypotension, dizziness, fatigue, headache, gastrointestinal issues, bradycardia.</li><li><strong>Occasional</strong>: Peripheral edema, dry mouth or eyes, disturbed vision, sexual dysfunction, sleep disturbances.</li><li><strong>Rare</strong>: Liver enzyme changes, thrombocytopenia, Raynaud’s phenomenon, depression, psoriasis exacerbation.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions and Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Use cautiously in hepatic impairment.</li><li>In heart failure, monitor renal function and clinical status for 2-3 hours after initiation or dose adjustments.</li><li>Avoid abrupt dose increases without ensuring stability.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy</strong>: Not recommended due to lack of adequate studies.</li><li><strong>Lactation</strong>: As Carvista and its metabolites are excreted in breast milk, breastfeeding is not recommended.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Management</strong></p><p><strong>Symptoms</strong>: Severe hypotension, bradycardia, heart failure, cardiac arrest, bronchospasms, vomiting, and seizures.</p><p><strong>Treatment</strong>:</p><ul><li>Atropine for bradycardia.</li><li>IV glucagon or sympathomimetics for ventricular function support.</li><li>Vasopressors (e.g., norepinephrine) for vasodilation.</li><li>Diazepam or clonazepam for seizures.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C.</li><li>Protect from light and moisture.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li>Safety and efficacy in pediatric patients are not established.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Class</strong></p><ul><li>Alpha adrenoceptor blocking drugs</li><li>Beta-adrenoceptor blocking drugs</li><li>Beta-blockers</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action</strong></p><p>Carvista 6.25 mg works as a <strong>non-selective β-adrenergic antagonist</strong> with <strong>α-1 adrenergic blocking activity</strong>. It exhibits antiproliferative and antioxidant properties, making it effective for managing hypertension, angina, and congestive heart failure.</p>', 'active', '205_1734289659.webp', 2, 12, NULL, '2024-12-16 00:07:39', '2024-12-16 00:07:39'),
(240, 'Floriz', 'Biotin', 20.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '1000 mcg', 'yes', 'no', '<p>I<strong>ndications of Floriz 1000 mcg</strong></p><p>Floriz 1000 mcg is used to address:</p><ul><li>Hair loss</li><li>Weak, brittle, splitting, or soft nails</li><li>Eczema and dermatitis</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Herbal and Nutraceuticals</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Floriz 1000 mcg, also known as vitamin H (biotin), plays a crucial role in several physiological functions:</p><ul><li><strong>Fatty Acid Synthesis</strong>: Essential for energy production and cellular function.</li><li><strong>Amino Acid Catabolism</strong>: Aids in the breakdown and utilization of amino acids.</li><li><strong>Gluconeogenesis</strong>: Supports glucose production.</li></ul><p>Biotin acts as a cofactor for enzymatic carboxylation processes involving pyruvate and acetyl-CoA. It is important for the growth and renewal of skin, hair, and nails, influencing keratin structure and epidermal cell differentiation. Biotin deficiency can lead to symptoms like hair loss, dermatitis, and systemic issues such as aciduria.</p><p><strong>Dosage and Administration</strong></p><p>The dosage of Floriz 1000 mcg depends on the condition and age group:</p><ul><li><strong>Adults</strong>: Generally, 1–3 tablets daily or as advised by a physician.</li><li><strong>Children with Deficiency</strong>: In severe cases, 5–10 tablets daily (crushed and mixed with water or juice) or as prescribed by a physician.</li></ul><p>Symptoms of deficiency in children, typically between 1 week and 2 years of age, include seizures, developmental delays, hypotonia, ataxia, hyperventilation, and coma.</p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Anticonvulsants</strong>: May lower plasma biotin levels.</li><li><strong>Antibiotics</strong>: Can reduce biotin contributions from intestinal microflora.</li><li><strong>Raw Egg Whites</strong>: Contain avidin, which hinders biotin absorption when consumed in excess.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Contraindicated in individuals with hypersensitivity to any of the product\'s components.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Insufficient clinical data exists regarding the safe use of Floriz 1000 mcg during pregnancy and lactation.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool, dry place, protected from light and moisture.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1507_1734289873.png', 10, 12, NULL, '2024-12-16 00:11:13', '2024-12-16 00:11:13'),
(241, 'Bisopro', 'Bisoprolol Fumarate', 6.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '2.5 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications for Bisopro 2.5 mg</strong></p><p>Bisopro 2.5 mg is used to treat the following conditions:</p><ul><li>High blood pressure (Hypertension)</li><li>Angina (chest pain due to reduced blood flow to the heart)</li><li>Moderate to severe heart failure</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Bisopro belongs to the class of beta-blockers, specifically beta-adrenergic receptor blocking agents.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Bisoprolol Hemifumarate is a highly selective beta-1 (ß1) adrenergic receptor blocker. It preferentially targets ß1 receptors in the heart and vascular smooth muscle, reducing heart rate and cardiac output, which in turn helps lower blood pressure. Unlike non-selective beta-blockers, Bisoprolol does not significantly affect lipid metabolism or HDL cholesterol levels, even during long-term use.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><p>The dosage should be tailored to individual patient needs:</p><ul><li><strong>Hypertension:</strong></li><li>The standard starting dose is 5 mg once daily. For some patients, 2.5 mg may be sufficient. If necessary, the dose can be increased to 10 mg or up to a maximum of 20 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Angina:</strong></li><li>The usual dose is 10 mg once daily, but some patients may respond well to 5 mg. Maximum dose: 20 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Heart Failure:</strong></li><li>Start with 1.25 mg once daily (preferably in the morning) for one week. If tolerated, gradually increase the dose weekly to 2.5 mg, then 3.75 mg, and later to 5 mg for four weeks. Further increases to 7.5 mg and a maximum of 10 mg daily can follow, based on patient response.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><p>Bisoprolol should not be used with other beta-blockers due to the risk of additive effects.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Avoid use in patients with:</p><ul><li>Cardiogenic shock</li><li>Severe heart failure</li><li>Second or third-degree atrioventricular (A-V) block</li><li>Right ventricular failure caused by pulmonary hypertension</li><li>Sinus bradycardia</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Reported side effects include:</p><ul><li>Gastrointestinal issues (nausea, diarrhea)</li><li>Bradycardia (slow heart rate)</li><li>Low blood pressure (hypotension)</li><li>Fatigue, headache, dizziness, or sleep disturbances</li><li>Rare: Thrombocytopenia, visual disturbances, alopecia</li></ul><p><strong>Use During Pregnancy and Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> The safety of Bisopro during pregnancy is not well-established.</li><li><strong>Lactation:</strong> There is insufficient data on its safety for breastfeeding mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions</strong></p><p>Regular monitoring of kidney, liver, and blood function is recommended during long-term treatment with Bisoprolol.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Storage</strong></p><p>Store in a dry, cool place away from heat and light. Keep out of the reach of children.</p><p><br></p><p>This revision ensures the content is clear, informative, and avoids verbatim copying.</p>', 'active', '1524_1734290142.png', 2, 12, NULL, '2024-12-16 00:15:42', '2024-12-16 00:15:42'),
(242, 'Rivamer', 'Rivastigmine Tartrate', 23.00, 10, 'Capsul', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Capsule', '1.5 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong> Rivamer 1.5 mg is used for the symptomatic treatment of mild to moderately severe Alzheimer\'s disease and mild to moderately severe dementia in patients with Parkinson\'s disease.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong> Drugs for Dementia</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong> Rivastigmine, a carbamate derivative related to physostigmine, works by inhibiting cholinesterase enzymes (like acetylcholinesterase and butyrylcholinesterase). This inhibition prevents the breakdown of acetylcholine, thereby increasing its concentration at the synapse, which helps improve communication between nerve cells. Rivastigmine selectively targets brain enzymes over peripheral ones.</p><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Capsules:</strong> The initial dose is 1.5 mg twice a day. After a minimum of two weeks, if tolerated, the dose may be increased to 3 mg twice a day. Subsequent doses can be raised to 4.5 mg and then 6 mg twice a day, based on tolerance. The maximum daily dose is 12 mg (6 mg twice daily). Treatment can be continued as long as there is therapeutic benefit. If therapy is interrupted for several days, restart at 1.5 mg twice daily and titrate upwards as tolerated.</li><li><strong>Transdermal Patch:</strong> Begin with a 4.6 mg/24 hours patch, and after at least 4 weeks, if well tolerated, increase to 9.5 mg/24 hours. Further increases to 13.3 mg/24 hours can occur after additional 4 weeks. For severe Alzheimer\'s, use 13.3 mg/24 hours.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration:</strong> Rivastigmine should be taken twice daily, ideally with meals.</p><p><strong>Drug Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li>Rivastigmine may intensify the effects of succinylcholine-type muscle relaxants during anesthesia, so caution is required with anesthetics.</li><li>Avoid using with other cholinomimetic agents or anticholinergic drugs.</li><li>No major drug interactions have been observed with digoxin, warfarin, diazepam, or fluoxetine.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong> Rivastigmine should not be used in individuals with a hypersensitivity to the drug or other carbamate derivatives.</p><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong> Common side effects are gastrointestinal issues such as nausea (38%) and vomiting (23%), especially during dose increases. Women may experience more gastrointestinal issues than men. Weight loss has also been noted.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong> Rivastigmine should only be used during pregnancy if absolutely necessary. It is excreted in animal milk, so it is recommended that breastfeeding be avoided during treatment.</p><p><strong>Precautions:</strong> Use cautiously in patients with a history of conduction defects, respiratory issues, and those with asthma or obstructive pulmonary disease. It may increase gastric acid secretion, exacerbate urinary obstruction or seizures, and worsen extrapyramidal symptoms. Renal or mild to moderate liver impairment requires monitoring. Weight should be monitored regularly.</p><p><strong>Overdose:</strong> Symptoms of overdose may include nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, hypertension, hallucinations, bradycardia, or syncope. In most cases of overdose, there are no serious symptoms. Treatment involves discontinuing the drug temporarily, managing symptoms, and administering atropine in severe cases.</p><p><strong>Storage:</strong> Store in a cool, dry place, protected from light.</p><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong> Rivastigmine increases acetylcholine levels in the brain by inhibiting acetylcholinesterase and butyrylcholinesterase. Its action is more selective to brain enzymes than those in peripheral tissues.</p><p>This version avoids a direct copy of the original text but preserves all essential information.</p>', 'active', '1753_1734290345.png', 16, 12, NULL, '2024-12-16 00:19:05', '2024-12-16 00:19:05'),
(243, 'Intimate', 'Tadalafil', 35.11, 5, 'Tablet', '5 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Intimate 10 mg:</strong> Intimate 10 mg is indicated for:</p><ul><li>Erectile Dysfunction (ED)</li><li>Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia (BPH)</li><li>Both Erectile Dysfunction and symptoms of Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong> Drugs for Erectile Dysfunction.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong> Intimate 10 mg is a selective phosphodiesterase type 5 (PDE5) inhibitor. By inhibiting PDE5, it increases cGMP in smooth muscle cells, causing smooth muscle relaxation and enhanced blood flow into the corpus cavernosum, resulting in a penile erection. PDE5 is also found in the smooth muscles of the prostate and bladder wall. Its inhibition increases cGMP concentrations, promoting smooth muscle relaxation in the prostate and bladder, potentially improving blood flow to the urinary tract and widening the bladder neck, leading to improved voiding.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Erectile Dysfunction:</strong> The typical starting dose is 10 mg, which may be adjusted to 20 mg or reduced to 5 mg based on individual needs. The maximum frequency is once daily. Intimate 10 mg is effective for up to 36 hours.</li><li><strong>Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia:</strong> The recommended dose is 5 mg, taken at the same time every day.</li><li><strong>Combined Erectile Dysfunction and Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia:</strong> The recommended dose is 5 mg daily at the same time.</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction:</strong> Intimate 10 mg may interact with:</p><ul><li>Nitrates (e.g., Isosorbide, Nitroglycerin)</li><li>Alpha-adrenergic blockers</li><li>Antihypertensives</li><li>Alcohol</li><li>Antacids (magnesium hydroxide/aluminum hydroxide)</li><li>Antifungals like Ketoconazole, Ritonavir, Erythromycin, Itraconazole</li><li>Grapefruit juice</li><li>Other HIV protease inhibitors</li><li>Rifampin, Carbamazepine, Phenytoin, and Phenobarbital.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Concurrent use of Nitrates (e.g., Nitroglycerin, Isosorbide), as it may amplify hypotensive effects.</li><li>Known hypersensitivity to Intimate 10 mg.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong> Common side effects include:</p><ul><li>Headache</li><li>Dyspepsia</li><li>Back pain</li><li>Myalgia</li><li>Nasal congestion and pharyngitis</li></ul><p>Rare side effects may include:</p><ul><li>Changes in vision (e.g., color vision, sudden vision loss)</li><li>Hearing loss</li><li>Stevens-Johnson Syndrome</li><li>Exfoliative dermatitis</li><li>Cardiovascular issues (e.g., angina, stroke, myocardial infarction)</li><li>Severe hypotension</li><li>Tachycardia</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong> Intimate 10 mg is assigned to pregnancy category B by the USFDA. It should only be used during pregnancy when the benefits outweigh the risks. There is no data on its excretion in human milk, so caution is advised when administering to nursing women.</p><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Use with caution in individuals with angina, renal or hepatic impairment, and those taking Nitrates, Alpha Blockers, Alcohol, CYP3A4 Inhibitors (e.g., Ritonavir, Ketoconazole, Itraconazole), or other PDE5 inhibitors.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong> Store in a dry place, away from light and heat. Keep out of the reach of children.</p><p><strong>Drug Class:</strong> Drugs for Erectile Dysfunction.</p><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong> Intimate 10 mg is a selective PDE5 inhibitor that promotes smooth muscle relaxation and increased blood flow to the penis, causing an erection. In the prostate and bladder, it may improve blood flow and facilitate better voiding by relaxing smooth muscle.</p>', 'active', '1813_1734290561.webp', 4, 12, NULL, '2024-12-16 00:22:41', '2024-12-16 00:22:41'),
(244, 'Co-dopa', 'Levodopa + Carbidopa', 7.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '110 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Co-Dopa 110 mg</strong></p><p>Co-Dopa 110 mg, containing levodopa and carbidopa, is used for treating Parkinson\'s disease, post-encephalitic Parkinsonism, and symptomatic Parkinsonism resulting from carbon monoxide or manganese intoxication.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Antiparkinson drugs</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Parkinson\'s disease symptoms are linked to dopamine depletion in the corpus striatum. Levodopa, a dopamine precursor, crosses the blood-brain barrier and is converted to dopamine in the brain. Carbidopa prevents peripheral decarboxylation of levodopa, enhancing its availability for brain transport.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Initial Dosage</strong>: The optimal dose is determined by titration. Starting with Levodopa 100 mg and Carbidopa 10 mg, one tablet can be taken 3–4 times a day. Increase the dose by one tablet daily or every other day until 8 tablets daily are reached.</li><li><strong>Maintenance Dose</strong>: Individualized therapy should be adjusted based on therapeutic response. If more levodopa is needed, Levodopa 250 mg and Carbidopa 25 mg can replace the lower dose, with adjustments as needed, up to a maximum of 8 tablets per day. Dosages exceeding 200 mg of carbidopa daily have limited experience.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Reduced effects</strong>: Pyridoxine, phenothiazines, haloperidol, reserpine, diazepam, oxazepam, chlordiazepoxide, phenobarbital.</li><li><strong>Enhanced effects</strong>: Carbidopa, amantadine, anticholinergics, amphetamines, sympathomimetic agents.</li><li><strong>Synergistic effects</strong>: Type B MAO inhibitors.</li><li><strong>Reversal</strong>: Pyridoxine reverses levodopa effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Nonselective MAO inhibitors (must be stopped at least two weeks before starting Co-Dopa).</li><li>Hypersensitivity to any component of the drug.</li><li>Narrow-angle glaucoma.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common side effects include dyskinesias (choreiform, dystonic, involuntary movements) and nausea.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy Category C</strong>: Caution is advised.</li><li>Levodopa is excreted in human milk, so caution is recommended when nursing.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><p>Levodopa may cause dyskinesias, requiring possible dosage reduction. Use cautiously in patients with severe cardiovascular, pulmonary, renal, hepatic, or endocrine conditions.</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Store below 30°C, protect from light and moisture. Keep out of children\'s reach.</p><p><strong>Use in Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Children</strong>: Safety and effectiveness in those under 18 have not been established.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1920_1734290838.png', 8, 12, NULL, '2024-12-16 00:27:18', '2024-12-16 00:27:18'),
(245, 'Rivotril', 'Clonazepam', 14.00, 10, 'Tablet', NULL, 'Tablet', '2 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adjunct anti-epileptic drugs</strong></li><li><strong>Benzodiazepine hypnotics</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Rivotril works by enhancing the action of GABA (gamma-aminobutyric acid), which is an inhibitory neurotransmitter in the brain. This action reduces the transmission of nerve signals in the motor cortex, helping to suppress abnormal electrical activity related to seizures. It is effective in both focal and generalized seizures.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>For Seizure Disorders (Adults)</strong>: Begin with 1.5 mg per day, divided into three doses. The dosage can be adjusted by 0.5-1 mg every three days, up to a maximum of 20 mg per day.</li><li><strong>For Panic Disorder (Adults)</strong>: Start with 0.25 mg twice daily and increase to 1 mg per day after three days, as needed.</li><li><strong>For Pediatric Patients</strong>: For children up to 10 years or 30 kg, the dosage ranges from 0.01-0.03 mg/kg/day, not exceeding 0.05 mg/kg/day, divided into multiple doses.</li><li><strong>Injection Dosage</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Children</strong>: 0.5 mg via slow IV injection.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Adults</strong>: 1 mg via slow IV injection or infusion, with the option to repeat if necessary (typically 1-4 mg).</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction</strong></p><p>Rivotril does not appear to affect the metabolism of phenytoin, carbamazepine, or phenobarbital, though its effects on other drugs\' metabolism are not well studied.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Hypersensitivity</strong> to benzodiazepines or significant liver disease.</li><li>Should not be used in cases of acute narrow-angle glaucoma, though it can be used in patients with open-angle glaucoma under appropriate treatment.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common side effects include CNS depression, such as drowsiness (50% of patients), ataxia (30%), and behavior problems in around 25% of patients. Other side effects may include abnormal eye movements, aphonia, tremor, confusion, amnesia, and, in rare cases, hallucinations or psychosis.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><p>Rivotril should only be used during pregnancy if the benefits outweigh the risks. It is not recommended during breastfeeding.</p><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>It may increase the risk of generalized tonic-clonic seizures when administered to patients with multiple coexisting seizure disorders.</li><li>Caution should be exercised when combining Rivotril with valproic acid as it can lead to absence status.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Symptoms &amp; Treatment</strong></p><p>Overdose can lead to drowsiness, ataxia, dysarthria, nystagmus, and, in severe cases, coma, hypotension, and cardiorespiratory depression. In case of overdose, activated charcoal can be administered to prevent further absorption, and flumazenil may be used in severe cases, though it should be administered under close supervision.</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Store in a dry place away from light and heat, and keep out of reach of children.</p><p><strong>Reconstitution &amp; Administration (IV)</strong></p><p>For intravenous injection, dilute the vial contents with 1 ml of water for injection. The infusion must be prepared immediately before use and should not exceed 8 hours. Avoid using sodium bicarbonate solutions.</p><p><strong>Geriatric &amp; Pediatric Use</strong></p><p>Elderly patients may have heightened sensitivity to the effects of benzodiazepines, requiring closer monitoring. In pediatric patients, special attention should be paid to respiratory issues, particularly in younger children.</p><p><strong>Renal &amp; Hepatic Impairment</strong></p><p>Renal impairment does not significantly affect Rivotril’s pharmacokinetics. In patients with hepatic impairment (such as cirrhosis), the drug\'s clearance may be reduced, and dosage adjustments may be necessary.</p><p>This medication is an effective anticonvulsant and anxiolytic but requires careful management due to its potential side effects and the need for dosage adjustments based on patient-specific factors.</p>', 'active', '1432_1734292466.png', 10, 12, NULL, '2024-12-16 00:54:26', '2024-12-16 00:54:26');
INSERT INTO `products` (`id`, `productName`, `genericName`, `retail_max_price`, `cart_qty_inc`, `cart_text`, `unit_in_pack`, `type`, `quantity`, `prescription`, `feature`, `description`, `status`, `coverImage`, `company_id`, `category_id`, `add_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(246, 'Rocovas', 'Rosuvastatin', 20.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Heterozygous Hypercholesterolemia (Familial and Non-familial)</strong></li><li><strong>Homozygous Hypercholesterolemia (Familial)</strong></li><li><strong>Mixed Dyslipidemia (Fredrickson Type IIa and IIb)</strong></li><li><strong>Primary Prevention of Cardiovascular Disease</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Other Anti-anginal &amp; Anti-ischaemic drugs</strong></li><li><strong>Statins</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><p>Rocovas 10 mg is a selective and competitive inhibitor of HMG-CoA reductase, the enzyme responsible for converting 3-hydroxy-3-methyl glutaryl coenzyme A into mevalonate, a precursor of cholesterol. Its effects occur in two main ways:</p><ol><li><strong>Increases the number of hepatic LDL receptors</strong>, leading to enhanced uptake and breakdown of LDL.</li><li><strong>Inhibits the synthesis of VLDL</strong> in the liver, which reduces the levels of VLDL and LDL particles in the bloodstream.</li></ol><p><strong>Dosage:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults:</strong> 5-40 mg once daily, with the 40 mg dose recommended only for patients who do not reach LDL-C goals with 20 mg.</li><li><strong>Pediatric patients with HeFH (Heterozygous Familial Hypercholesterolemia):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">5-10 mg/day for those aged 8 to &lt;10 years.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">5-20 mg/day for those aged 10 to 17 years.</li><li><strong>Pediatric patients with HoFH (Homozygous Familial Hypercholesterolemia):</strong> Starting dose of 20 mg/day for those aged 7 to 17 years.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration:</strong></p><ul><li>Rocovas 10 mg can be taken <strong>with or without food</strong>, at any time of the day.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Cyclosporine:</strong> Increased exposure, limit to 5 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Gemfibrozil:</strong> Avoid use together; if necessary, limit Rocovas to 10 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Lopinavir/Ritonavir or Atazanavir/Ritonavir:</strong> Elevated exposure, limit to 10 mg daily.</li><li><strong>Coumarin anticoagulants:</strong> May increase INR; monitor closely.</li><li><strong>Concomitant lipid-lowering drugs (fibrates, niacin):</strong> Increased risk of muscle effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Hypersensitivity</strong> to Rocovas or any of its components.</li><li><strong>Liver disease</strong>, especially with unexplained persistent elevations in hepatic transaminase levels.</li><li><strong>Pregnant and breastfeeding women</strong>.</li><li><strong>Women who may become pregnant</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Common side effects include <strong>headache, myalgia, constipation, asthenia, abdominal pain, and nausea</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Safety during pregnancy is not established.</li><li>It is not known if Rocovas 10 mg is excreted in human milk.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Skeletal muscle effects</strong> (e.g., myopathy, rhabdomyolysis) are a significant risk, especially with higher doses (40 mg), advanced age (&gt;65), hypothyroidism, renal impairment, and when combined with certain drugs like cyclosporine or lopinavir/ritonavir. Patients should report unexplained muscle pain or weakness.</li><li><strong>Liver enzyme monitoring</strong> is necessary before and during treatment, especially with elevated hepatic transaminases.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage:</strong></p><ul><li>Store below <strong>30°C</strong>, away from light and moisture.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Children:</strong> The safety and effectiveness in pediatric patients have not been established.</li></ul><p>This information provides a comprehensive overview of Rocovas 10 mg for healthcare providers and patients, ensuring safe and effective usage.</p>', 'active', '288_1734292697.png', 2, 12, NULL, '2024-12-16 00:58:17', '2024-12-16 00:58:17'),
(247, 'Camlosart', 'Amlodipine + Olmesartan Medoxomil', 12.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '5 mg+20 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p><strong>Camlosart 5 mg/20 mg</strong> is indicated for the treatment of hypertension, either as monotherapy or in combination with other antihypertensive agents. It may be used as an initial therapy in patients likely to require multiple agents to achieve blood pressure control.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Combined Antihypertensive Preparations</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Amlodipine</strong>: A dihydropyridine calcium channel blocker that reduces peripheral vascular resistance and blood pressure by inhibiting calcium influx into vascular smooth and cardiac muscle.</li><li><strong>Olmesartan</strong>: An angiotensin II receptor blocker (ARB) that blocks the AT1 receptor subtype, resulting in vasodilation and blood pressure reduction without affecting pulse rate.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Initial Therapy</strong>: Start with one tablet (5/20 mg) once daily. If needed, the dose may be increased after 1–2 weeks to a maximum of two tablets (10/40 mg) once daily. Can be taken with or without food. Not recommended as initial therapy in patients ≥75 years or with hepatic impairment.</li><li><strong>Replacement Therapy</strong>: Substitutes for individually titrated components. Adjust the dose of one or both components as necessary for blood pressure control.</li><li><strong>Add-on Therapy</strong>: Used for patients inadequately controlled with either amlodipine or olmesartan alone.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><p>No significant pharmacokinetic interactions have been observed between amlodipine and olmesartan. No specific interaction studies with the combination product have been conducted.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to amlodipine, olmesartan, or any component of the product.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Common adverse effects:</p><ul><li>Edema</li><li>Dizziness</li><li>Flushing</li><li>Palpitations</li></ul><p>Less common effects:</p><ul><li>Vomiting, diarrhea</li><li>Alopecia</li><li>Pruritus, urticaria</li><li>Rhabdomyolysis (rare)</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy</strong>: Discontinue immediately when pregnancy is detected. Drugs affecting the renin-angiotensin system during the second and third trimesters may harm the fetus.</li><li><strong>Lactation</strong>: Use caution; consider discontinuing the drug or breastfeeding based on the drug\'s necessity to the mother.</li><li><strong>Hypotension</strong>: May occur in volume- or salt-depleted patients.</li><li><strong>Vasodilation Risk</strong>: Use with caution in patients with severe aortic stenosis.</li><li><strong>Heart Conditions</strong>: May increase the risk of angina or myocardial infarction in those with severe obstructive coronary artery disease. Use cautiously in heart failure.</li><li><strong>Renal/Hepatic Impairment</strong>: Adjust dosage and monitor closely.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Olmesartan</strong>: Overdose may result in hypotension and tachycardia; bradycardia can occur due to vagal stimulation.</li><li><strong>Amlodipine</strong>: Overdose may cause significant hypotension and reflex tachycardia. Severe cases may lead to shock.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C in a cool, dry place.</li><li>Protect from light and moisture.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li>Not established for pediatric use.</li><li>Exercise caution in elderly patients and those with hepatic or renal impairment.</li></ul><p>This version avoids direct promotional phrasing while preserving the critical details necessary for clinical understanding. Let me know if you\'d like further adjustments!</p>', 'active', '495_1734292910.webp', 4, 12, NULL, '2024-12-16 01:01:50', '2024-12-16 01:01:50'),
(248, 'Supermom Mild Baby Wipes', 'Wipes', 235.00, 1, 'Packet', '120\'s wipes in a pack', 'Wipes', '120 wipes', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Supermom Mild Baby Wipes</strong></p><p>Supermom Mild Baby Wipes are a popular choice for gentle yet effective cleaning for little babies. They are made of soft and absorbent materials to effectively clean and moisturize delicate skin without the risk of irritation. Supermom Mild Baby Wipes are also hypoallergenic and dermatologically tested to ensure peace of mind for worried parents.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions of Supermom Mild Baby Wipes</strong></p><ul><li>Open the wipe container and remove a wipe.</li><li>Use the wipe to clean the area that needs to be cleaned.</li><li>Dispose of the wipe in the trash can.</li><li>Close the wipe container.</li></ul><p><strong>Safety Information</strong></p><ul><li>Read the label carefully before use.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Disposal Instructions</strong></p><ul><li>Dispose of Supermom Mild Baby Wipes in the trash.</li><li>Do not flush Supermom Mild Baby Wipes down the toilet.</li><li>Do not put Supermom Mild Baby Wipes in recycling bins or compost piles.</li></ul>', 'active', '1217_1734328466.jpg', 13, 9, NULL, '2024-12-16 10:54:26', '2024-12-16 10:54:26'),
(249, 'Avonee Small Pant Diaper(4-8Kg)', 'Diaper', 890.00, 1, 'Packet', '42 pcs diapers in a box', 'Diaper', '42 pcs', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Avonee Pant Style Diaper S 42s (4-8kg)</strong></p><p>Avonee Pant Style Diaper S 42s (4-8kg) prioritizes the comfort and well-being of your baby. It is made of soft and breathable materials to ensure optimal comfort and keep your baby\'s skin dry and healthy. The Avonee Pant Style Diaper S 42s (4-8kg) also features a secure fit to prevent leaks and ensures your baby stays clean and fresh all day long. It has easy-to-use fasteners and a wetness indicator that lets you know when it\'s time for a change.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions of Avonee Pant Style Diaper S 42s (4-8kg)</strong></p><ul><li>Open the Avonee Pant Style Diaper S 42s (4-8kg) and place it under the baby.</li><li>Make sure the Avonee Pant Style Diaper S 42s (4-8kg) is fitted snugly but not too tight.</li><li>If the baby has pooped, wipe the area clean with wipes and apply Avonee Pant Style Diaper S 42s (4-8kg) cream if necessary.</li><li>Close the Avonee Pant Style Diaper S 42s (4-8kg) and fasten the tabs.</li><li>Dispose of the dirty Avonee Pant Style Diaper S 42s (4-8kg) properly.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Avonee Pant Style Diaper S 42s (4-8kg) can be stored at room temperature (between 20 and 25 degrees Celsius or 68 and 77 degrees Fahrenheit). They should not be stored in direct sunlight or heat, as this can cause them to dry out or become brittle.</p><p><strong>Safety Information</strong></p><ul><li>Change Avonee Pant Style Diaper S 42s (4-8kg) often, especially after the baby has wet or pooped.</li><li>Do not leave a wet or soiled Avonee Pant Style Diaper S 42s (4-8kg) on the baby for too long.</li><li>Do not flush dirty Avonee Pant Style Diaper S 42s (4-8kg) down the toilet.</li><li>Keep Avonee Pant Style Diaper S 42s (4-8kg) out of the reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Disposal Instructions</strong></p><ul><li>Dispose of dirty Avonee Pant Style Diaper S 42s (4-8kg) in a sealed bag or container.</li><li>Place the sealed bag or container in the trash.</li></ul>', 'active', '942_1734328791.jpg', 47, 9, NULL, '2024-12-16 10:59:51', '2024-12-16 11:00:59'),
(250, 'Bashundhara Diapant Baby Diaper S (4-8 kg)', 'Diaper', 140.00, 1, 'Packet', '5\'s in a box', 'Diaper', '5 pcs', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Bashundhara Baby Diaper Mini S 5s (4-8kg)</strong></p><p>Bashundhara Baby Diaper Mini S 5s (4-8kg) prioritizes the comfort and well-being of your baby. It is made of soft and breathable materials to ensure optimal comfort and keep your baby\'s skin dry and healthy. The Bashundhara Baby Diaper Mini S 5s (4-8kg) also features a secure fit to prevent leaks and ensures your baby stays clean and fresh all day long. It has easy-to-use fasteners and a wetness indicator that lets you know when it\'s time for a change.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions of Bashundhara Baby Diaper Mini S 5s (4-8kg)</strong></p><ul><li>Open the Bashundhara Baby Diaper Mini S 5s (4-8kg) and place it under the baby.</li><li>Make sure the Bashundhara Baby Diaper Mini S 5s (4-8kg) is fitted snugly but not too tight.</li><li>If the baby has pooped, wipe the area clean with wipes and apply Bashundhara Baby Diaper Mini S 5s (4-8kg) cream if necessary.</li><li>Close the Bashundhara Baby Diaper Mini S 5s (4-8kg) and fasten the tabs.</li><li>Dispose of the dirty Bashundhara Baby Diaper Mini S 5s (4-8kg) properly.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Bashundhara Baby Diaper Mini S 5s (4-8kg) can be stored at room temperature (between 20 and 25 degrees Celsius or 68 and 77 degrees Fahrenheit). They should not be stored in direct sunlight or heat, as this can cause them to dry out or become brittle.</p><p><strong>Safety Information</strong></p><ul><li>Change Bashundhara Baby Diaper Mini S 5s (4-8kg) often, especially after the baby has wet or pooped.</li><li>Do not leave a wet or soiled Bashundhara Baby Diaper Mini S 5s (4-8kg) on the baby for too long.</li><li>Do not flush dirty Bashundhara Baby Diaper Mini S 5s (4-8kg) down the toilet.</li><li>Keep Bashundhara Baby Diaper Mini S 5s (4-8kg) out of the reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Disposal Instructions</strong></p><ul><li>Dispose of dirty Bashundhara Baby Diaper Mini S 5s (4-8kg) in a sealed bag or container.</li><li>Place the sealed bag or container in the trash.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1527_1734329216.jpg', 48, 9, NULL, '2024-12-16 11:06:56', '2024-12-16 11:06:56'),
(251, 'Avonee Pant Style Diaper(M 7-12kg)', 'Diaper', 890.00, 1, 'Packet', '40\'s diaper in a packet', 'Diaper', '40 pcs', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Avonee Pant Style Diaper M 40s (7-12kg)</strong></p><p>Avonee Pant Style Diaper M 40s (7-12kg) prioritizes the comfort and well-being of your baby. It is made of soft and breathable materials to ensure optimal comfort and keep your baby\'s skin dry and healthy. The Avonee Pant Style Diaper M 40s (7-12kg) also features a secure fit to prevent leaks and ensures your baby stays clean and fresh all day long. It has easy-to-use fasteners and a wetness indicator that lets you know when it\'s time for a change.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions of Avonee Pant Style Diaper M 40s (7-12kg)</strong></p><ul><li>Open the Avonee Pant Style Diaper M 40s (7-12kg) and place it under the baby.</li><li>Make sure the Avonee Pant Style Diaper M 40s (7-12kg) is fitted snugly but not too tight.</li><li>If the baby has pooped, wipe the area clean with wipes and apply Avonee Pant Style Diaper M 40s (7-12kg) cream if necessary.</li><li>Close the Avonee Pant Style Diaper M 40s (7-12kg) and fasten the tabs.</li><li>Dispose of the dirty Avonee Pant Style Diaper M 40s (7-12kg) properly.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Avonee Pant Style Diaper M 40s (7-12kg) can be stored at room temperature (between 20 and 25 degrees Celsius or 68 and 77 degrees Fahrenheit). They should not be stored in direct sunlight or heat, as this can cause them to dry out or become brittle.</p><p><strong>Safety Information</strong></p><ul><li>Change Avonee Pant Style Diaper M 40s (7-12kg) often, especially after the baby has wet or pooped.</li><li>Do not leave a wet or soiled Avonee Pant Style Diaper M 40s (7-12kg) on the baby for too long.</li><li>Do not flush dirty Avonee Pant Style Diaper M 40s (7-12kg) down the toilet.</li><li>Keep Avonee Pant Style Diaper M 40s (7-12kg) out of the reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Disposal Instructions</strong></p><ul><li>Dispose of dirty Avonee Pant Style Diaper M 40s (7-12kg) in a sealed bag or container.</li><li>Place the sealed bag or container in the trash.</li></ul>', 'active', '812_1734331031.webp', 47, 9, NULL, '2024-12-16 11:37:11', '2024-12-16 11:37:11'),
(252, 'Avonee Pant Style Diaper L (9-14kg)', 'Diaper', 890.00, 1, 'Packet', '34 pcs in a box', 'Diaper', '34 pcs', 'no', 'yes', '<p><strong>Avonee Pant Style Diaper L 34s (9-14kg)</strong></p><p>Avonee Pant Style Diaper L 34s (9-14kg) prioritizes the comfort and well-being of your baby. It is made of soft and breathable materials to ensure optimal comfort and keep your baby\'s skin dry and healthy. The Avonee Pant Style Diaper L 34s (9-14kg) also features a secure fit to prevent leaks and ensures your baby stays clean and fresh all day long. It has easy-to-use fasteners and a wetness indicator that lets you know when it\'s time for a change.</p><p><strong>Usage Instructions of Avonee Pant Style Diaper L 34s (9-14kg)</strong></p><ul><li>Open the Avonee Pant Style Diaper L 34s (9-14kg) and place it under the baby.</li><li>Make sure the Avonee Pant Style Diaper L 34s (9-14kg) is fitted snugly but not too tight.</li><li>If the baby has pooped, wipe the area clean with wipes and apply Avonee Pant Style Diaper L 34s (9-14kg) cream if necessary.</li><li>Close the Avonee Pant Style Diaper L 34s (9-14kg) and fasten the tabs.</li><li>Dispose of the dirty Avonee Pant Style Diaper L 34s (9-14kg) properly.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Avonee Pant Style Diaper L 34s (9-14kg) can be stored at room temperature (between 20 and 25 degrees Celsius or 68 and 77 degrees Fahrenheit). They should not be stored in direct sunlight or heat, as this can cause them to dry out or become brittle.</p><p><strong>Safety Information</strong></p><ul><li>Change Avonee Pant Style Diaper L 34s (9-14kg) often, especially after the baby has wet or pooped.</li><li>Do not leave a wet or soiled Avonee Pant Style Diaper L 34s (9-14kg) on the baby for too long.</li><li>Do not flush dirty Avonee Pant Style Diaper L 34s (9-14kg) down the toilet.</li><li>Keep Avonee Pant Style Diaper L 34s (9-14kg) out of the reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Disposal Instructions</strong></p><ul><li>Dispose of dirty Avonee Pant Style Diaper L 34s (9-14kg) in a sealed bag or container.</li><li>Place the sealed bag or container in the trash.</li></ul>', 'active', '326_1734331279.jpeg', 47, 9, NULL, '2024-12-16 11:41:19', '2024-12-16 11:41:19'),
