(949, 'Pizo-A', 'Pizotifen', 3.01, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '0.5 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><br></p><p><strong> Indications for Rocovas 5 mg</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is indicated for:</p><ul><li><strong>Heterozygous Hypercholesterolemia</strong> (Familial and Non-familial)</li><li><strong>Homozygous Hypercholesterolemia</strong> (Familial)</li><li><strong>Mixed Dyslipidemia</strong> (Fredrickson Type IIa and IIb)</li><li><strong>Primary prevention of cardiovascular disease</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Statins</li><li>Other Anti-anginal &amp; Anti-ischemic drugs</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is a selective and competitive inhibitor of HMG-CoA reductase, the enzyme responsible for converting 3-hydroxy-3-methyl glutaryl coenzyme A to mevalonate, a cholesterol precursor. It reduces lipid levels in two ways:</p><ol><li><strong>Increases hepatic LDL receptors</strong>: Enhances uptake and breakdown of LDL.</li><li><strong>Inhibits hepatic synthesis of VLDL</strong>: Reduces overall VLDL and LDL particles.</li></ol><p><strong>Dosage of Rocovas 5 mg</strong></p><ul><li><strong>General dose range</strong>: 5-40 mg once daily. (Use 40 mg only for patients not achieving LDL-C goals with 20 mg).</li><li><strong>Homozygous Familial Hypercholesterolemia (HoFH)</strong>: Starting dose of 20 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Pediatric patients</strong>:</li><li>With HeFH (8-10 years): 5-10 mg/day.</li><li>With HeFH (10-17 years): 5-20 mg/day.</li><li>With HoFH (7-17 years): 20 mg/day.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg can be taken with or without food at any time of the day.</p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Cyclosporine</strong>: Increases exposure; do not exceed 5 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Gemfibrozil</strong>: Avoid if possible; if needed, limit the dose to 10 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Lopinavir/Ritonavir or Atazanavir/Ritonavir</strong>: Increases exposure; limit the dose to 10 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Coumarin anticoagulants</strong>: May prolong INR; monitor INR frequently.</li><li><strong>Lipid-lowering therapies</strong>: Combining with fibrates or niacin increases the risk of muscle-related side effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is contraindicated in:</p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any of its components.</li><li>Liver disease, including unexplained persistent elevation of hepatic transaminases.</li><li>Pregnant women or women planning to conceive.</li><li>Nursing mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is generally well-tolerated. Common side effects include:</p><ul><li>Headache</li><li>Myalgia</li><li>Constipation</li><li>Asthenia</li><li>Abdominal pain</li><li>Nausea</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1595_1738273357.webp', 5, 12, NULL, '2025-01-31 02:42:37', '2025-01-31 02:42:37'),
(950, 'Tigirate', 'Fenofibrate', 7.06, 10, 'Capsul', '10 Capsul in a strip', 'Capsule', '200 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><br></p><p><strong> Indications for Rocovas 5 mg</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is indicated for:</p><ul><li><strong>Heterozygous Hypercholesterolemia</strong> (Familial and Non-familial)</li><li><strong>Homozygous Hypercholesterolemia</strong> (Familial)</li><li><strong>Mixed Dyslipidemia</strong> (Fredrickson Type IIa and IIb)</li><li><strong>Primary prevention of cardiovascular disease</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Statins</li><li>Other Anti-anginal &amp; Anti-ischemic drugs</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is a selective and competitive inhibitor of HMG-CoA reductase, the enzyme responsible for converting 3-hydroxy-3-methyl glutaryl coenzyme A to mevalonate, a cholesterol precursor. It reduces lipid levels in two ways:</p><ol><li><strong>Increases hepatic LDL receptors</strong>: Enhances uptake and breakdown of LDL.</li><li><strong>Inhibits hepatic synthesis of VLDL</strong>: Reduces overall VLDL and LDL particles.</li></ol><p><strong>Dosage of Rocovas 5 mg</strong></p><ul><li><strong>General dose range</strong>: 5-40 mg once daily. (Use 40 mg only for patients not achieving LDL-C goals with 20 mg).</li><li><strong>Homozygous Familial Hypercholesterolemia (HoFH)</strong>: Starting dose of 20 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Pediatric patients</strong>:</li><li>With HeFH (8-10 years): 5-10 mg/day.</li><li>With HeFH (10-17 years): 5-20 mg/day.</li><li>With HoFH (7-17 years): 20 mg/day.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg can be taken with or without food at any time of the day.</p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Cyclosporine</strong>: Increases exposure; do not exceed 5 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Gemfibrozil</strong>: Avoid if possible; if needed, limit the dose to 10 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Lopinavir/Ritonavir or Atazanavir/Ritonavir</strong>: Increases exposure; limit the dose to 10 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Coumarin anticoagulants</strong>: May prolong INR; monitor INR frequently.</li><li><strong>Lipid-lowering therapies</strong>: Combining with fibrates or niacin increases the risk of muscle-related side effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is contraindicated in:</p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any of its components.</li><li>Liver disease, including unexplained persistent elevation of hepatic transaminases.</li><li>Pregnant women or women planning to conceive.</li><li>Nursing mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is generally well-tolerated. Common side effects include:</p><ul><li>Headache</li><li>Myalgia</li><li>Constipation</li><li>Asthenia</li><li>Abdominal pain</li><li>Nausea</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '323_1738273420.webp', 7, 12, NULL, '2025-01-31 02:43:40', '2025-01-31 02:43:40'),
(951, 'Supotaria', 'Glycopyrrolate', 20.00, 6, 'Capsul', '6 Capsul in a strip', 'Capsule', '50 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><br></p><p>Indications for Rocovas 5 mg</p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is indicated for:</p><p>•	Heterozygous Hypercholesterolemia (Familial and Non-familial)</p><p>•	Homozygous Hypercholesterolemia (Familial)</p><p>•	Mixed Dyslipidemia (Fredrickson Type IIa and IIb)</p><p>•	Primary prevention of cardiovascular disease</p><p>Therapeutic Class</p><p>•	Statins</p><p>•	Other Anti-anginal &amp; Anti-ischemic drugs</p><p>Pharmacology</p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is a selective and competitive inhibitor of HMG-CoA reductase, the enzyme responsible for converting 3-hydroxy-3-methyl glutaryl coenzyme A to mevalonate, a cholesterol precursor. It reduces lipid levels in two ways:</p><p>1.	Increases hepatic LDL receptors: Enhances uptake and breakdown of LDL.</p><p>2.	Inhibits hepatic synthesis of VLDL: Reduces overall VLDL and LDL particles.</p><p>Dosage of Rocovas 5 mg</p><p>•	General dose range: 5-40 mg once daily. (Use 40 mg only for patients not achieving LDL-C goals with 20 mg).</p><p>•	Homozygous Familial Hypercholesterolemia (HoFH): Starting dose of 20 mg/day.</p><p>•	Pediatric patients:</p><p>•	With HeFH (8-10 years): 5-10 mg/day.</p><p>•	With HeFH (10-17 years): 5-20 mg/day.</p><p>•	With HoFH (7-17 years): 20 mg/day.</p><p>Administration</p><p>Rocovas 5 mg can be taken with or without food at any time of the day.</p><p>Drug Interactions</p><p>•	Cyclosporine: Increases exposure; do not exceed 5 mg once daily.</p><p>•	Gemfibrozil: Avoid if possible; if needed, limit the dose to 10 mg once daily.</p><p>•	Lopinavir/Ritonavir or Atazanavir/Ritonavir: Increases exposure; limit the dose to 10 mg once daily.</p><p>•	Coumarin anticoagulants: May prolong INR; monitor INR frequently.</p><p>•	Lipid-lowering therapies: Combining with fibrates or niacin increases the risk of muscle-related side effects.</p><p>Contraindications</p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is contraindicated in:</p><p>•	Hypersensitivity to any of its components.</p><p>•	Liver disease, including unexplained persistent elevation of hepatic transaminases.</p><p>•	Pregnant women or women planning to conceive.</p><p>•	Nursing mothers.</p><p>Side Effects</p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is generally well-tolerated. Common side effects include:</p><p>•	Headache</p><p>•	Myalgia</p><p>•	Constipation</p><p>•	Asthenia</p><p>•	Abdominal pain</p><p>•	Nausea</p><p><br></p>', 'active', '49_1738273627.jpg', 2, 12, NULL, '2025-01-31 02:47:07', '2025-01-31 02:47:07'),
