(1048, 'Soritene', 'Tazarotene', 151.00, 1, 'Cream', '1 piece in a box', 'Cream', '0.1%', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Indications for Rocovas 5 mg</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Rocovas 5 mg is indicated for:</span></p><ul><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Heterozygous Hypercholesterolemia</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> (Familial and Non-familial)</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Homozygous Hypercholesterolemia</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> (Familial)</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Mixed Dyslipidemia</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\"> (Fredrickson Type IIa and IIb)</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Primary prevention of cardiovascular disease</strong></li></ul><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Statins</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Other Anti-anginal &amp; Anti-ischemic drugs</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Pharmacology</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Rocovas 5 mg is a selective and competitive inhibitor of HMG-CoA reductase, the enzyme responsible for converting 3-hydroxy-3-methyl glutaryl coenzyme A to mevalonate, a cholesterol precursor. It reduces lipid levels in two ways:</span></p><ol><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Increases hepatic LDL receptors</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">: Enhances uptake and breakdown of LDL.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Inhibits hepatic synthesis of VLDL</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">: Reduces overall VLDL and LDL particles.</span></li></ol><p><strong style=\"background-color: transpare