parent;\">Dosage of Rocovas 5 mg</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">General dose range</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">: 5-40 mg once daily. (Use 40 mg only for patients not achieving LDL-C goals with 20 mg).</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Homozygous Familial Hypercholesterolemia (HoFH)</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">: Starting dose of 20 mg/day.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Pediatric patients</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">:</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">With HeFH (8-10 years): 5-10 mg/day.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">With HeFH (10-17 years): 5-20 mg/day.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">With HoFH (7-17 years): 20 mg/day.</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Administration</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Rocovas 5 mg can be taken with or without food at any time of the day.</span></p><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Cyclosporine</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">: Increases exposure; do not exceed 5 mg once daily.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Gemfibrozil</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">: Avoid if possible; if needed, limit the dose to 10 mg once daily.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Lopinavir/Ritonavir or Atazanavir/Ritonavir</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">: Increases exposure; limit the dose to 10 mg once daily.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Coumarin anticoagulants</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">: May prolong INR; monitor INR frequently.</span></li><li><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Lipid-lowering therapies</strong><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">: Combining with fibrates or niacin increases the risk of muscle-related side effects.</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Contraindications</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Rocovas 5 mg is contraindicated in:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Hypersensitivity to any of its components.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Liver disease, including unexplained persistent elevation of hepatic transaminases.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Pregnant women or women planning to conceive.</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Nursing mothers.</span></li></ul><p><strong style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Side Effects</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Rocovas 5 mg is generally well-tolerated. Common side effects include:</span></p><ul><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Headache</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Myalgia</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Constipation</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Asthenia</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Abdominal pain</span></li><li><span style=\"background-color: transparent;\">Nausea</span></li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '217_1738349306.webp', 29, 12, NULL, '2025-01-31 23:48:26', '2025-01-31 23:48:26'),
