rong>: Increases exposure; limit the dose to 10 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Coumarin anticoagulants</strong>: May prolong INR; monitor INR frequently.</li><li><strong>Lipid-lowering therapies</strong>: Combining with fibrates or niacin increases the risk of muscle-related side effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is contraindicated in:</p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any of its components.</li><li>Liver disease, including unexplained persistent elevation of hepatic transaminases.</li><li>Pregnant women or women planning to conceive.</li><li>Nursing mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is generally well-tolerated. Common side effects include:</p><ul><li>Headache</li><li>Myalgia</li><li>Constipation</li><li>Asthenia</li><li>Abdominal pain</li><li>Nausea</li></ul>', 'in-active', '1270_1738358232.webp', 5, 12, NULL, '2025-02-01 02:17:12', '2025-05-12 18:17:02'),
