 mg can be taken with or without food at any time of the day.</span></p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Cyclosporine</strong>: Increases exposure; do not exceed 5 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Gemfibrozil</strong>: Avoid if possible; if needed, limit the dose to 10 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Lopinavir/Ritonavir or Atazanavir/Ritonavir</strong>: Increases exposure; limit the dose to 10 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Coumarin anticoagulants</strong>: May prolong INR; monitor INR frequently.</li><li><strong>Lipid-lowering therapies</strong>: Combining with fibrates or niacin increases the risk of muscle-related side effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(245, 245, 245); color: rgb(52, 73, 94);\">Rocovas 5 mg is contraindicated in:</span></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any of its components.</li><li>Liver disease, including unexplained persistent elevation of hepatic transaminases.</li><li>Pregnant women or women planning to conceive.</li><li>Nursing mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p><span style=\"background-color: rgb(245, 245, 245); color: rgb(52, 73, 94);\">Rocovas 5 mg is generally well-tolerated. Common side effects include:</span></p><ul><li>Headache</li><li>Myalgia</li><li>Constipation</li><li>Asthenia</li><li>Abdominal pain</li><li>Nausea</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '90_1738367565.webp', 44, 12, NULL, '2025-02-01 04:52:45', '2025-02-01 04:52:45'),
