(1530, 'Ketomar', 'Ketotifen Fumarate', 65.00, 1, 'x 100 ml bottle', '100 ml bottle', 'Syrup', '1 mg/5 ml', 'yes', 'no', '<p><br></p><p><strong> Indications for Rocovas 5 mg</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is indicated for:</p><ul><li><strong>Heterozygous Hypercholesterolemia</strong> (Familial and Non-familial)</li><li><strong>Homozygous Hypercholesterolemia</strong> (Familial)</li><li><strong>Mixed Dyslipidemia</strong> (Fredrickson Type IIa and IIb)</li><li><strong>Primary prevention of cardiovascular disease</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Statins</li><li>Other Anti-anginal &amp; Anti-ischemic drugs</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is a selective and competitive inhibitor of HMG-CoA reductase, the enzyme responsible for converting 3-hydroxy-3-methyl glutaryl coenzyme A to mevalonate, a cholesterol precursor. It reduces lipid levels in two ways:</p><ol><li><strong>Increases hepatic LDL receptors</strong>: Enhances uptake and breakdown of LDL.</li><li><strong>Inhibits hepatic synthesis of VLDL</strong>: Reduces overall VLDL and LDL particles.</li></ol><p><strong>Dosage of Rocovas 5 mg</strong></p><ul><li><strong>General dose range</strong>: 5-40 mg once daily. (Use 40 mg only for patients not achieving LDL-C goals with 20 mg).</li><li><strong>Homozygous Familial Hypercholesterolemia (HoFH)</strong>: Starting dose of 20 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Pediatric patients</strong>:</li><li>With HeFH (8-10 years): 5-10 mg/day.</li><li>With HeFH (10-17 years): 5-20 mg/day.</li><li>With HoFH (7-17 years): 20 mg/day.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg can be taken with or without food at any time of the day.</p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Cyclosporine</strong>: Increases exposure; do not exceed 5 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Gemfibrozil</strong>: Avoid if possible; if needed, limit the dose to 10 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Lopinavir/Ritonavir or Atazanavir/Ritonavir</strong>: Increases exposure; limit the dose to 10 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Coumarin anticoagulants</strong>: May prolong INR; monitor INR frequently.</li><li><strong>Lipid-lowering therapies</strong>: Combining with fibrates or niacin increases the risk of muscle-related side effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is contraindicated in:</p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any of its components.</li><li>Liver disease, including unexplained persistent elevation of hepatic transaminases.</li><li>Pregnant women or women planning to conceive.</li><li>Nursing mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is generally well-tolerated. Common side effects include:</p><ul><li>Headache</li><li>Myalgia</li><li>Constipation</li><li>Asthenia</li><li>Abdominal pain</li><li>Nausea</li></ul>', 'active', '1846_1738702529.webp', 2, 12, NULL, '2025-02-05 01:55:29', '2025-05-04 16:17:10'),
