s exposure; limit the dose to 10 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Coumarin anticoagulants</strong>: May prolong INR; monitor INR frequently.</li><li><strong>Lipid-lowering therapies</strong>: Combining with fibrates or niacin increases the risk of muscle-related side effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is contraindicated in:</p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any of its components.</li><li>Liver disease, including unexplained persistent elevation of hepatic transaminases.</li><li>Pregnant women or women planning to conceive.</li><li>Nursing mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is generally well-tolerated. Common side effects include:</p><ul><li>Headache</li><li>Myalgia</li><li>Constipation</li><li>Asthenia</li><li>Abdominal pain</li><li>Nausea</li></ul>', 'in-active', '1943_1741276162.webp', 1, 12, NULL, '2025-03-06 20:49:22', '2025-05-08 20:15:54'),
(2665, 'Mirasol XR', 'Mirabegron', 55.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '50 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p>Mirasol XR tablet is indicated for the symptomatic treatment of urgency, increased micturition frequency and urgency incontinence as may occur in adult patients with overactive bladder (OAB) syndrome.</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Mirabegron is the first beta-3 adrenoceptor agonist. Mirabegron exerts its effect via a dual mechanism, both directly acts on the bladder smooth muscle and also via the sensory nervous system, it increases the levels of cyclic adenosine monophosphate (cyclic AMP) and leads to relaxation of the detrusor smooth muscle during storage phase of urinary bladder fill-void cycle by activation of beta-3 adrenoceptor which increase bladder capacity.</p><p><strong>Dosage</strong></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(57, 121, 80);\">Adults including elderly</span>: The recommended starting dose is Mirabegron 25 mg tablet once daily with or without food. Based on individual patient efficacy and tolerability the dose may be increased to Mirabegron 50 mg tablet once daily.</p><p><br></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(57, 121, 80);\">Renal or hepatic impairment</span>:</p><ul><li>Patients with severe renal impairment (ClCr 15 to 29 mL/min or eGFR 15 to 29 mL/min/1.73 m2) or moderate hepatic impairment (Child-Pugh Class B), the daily dose of Mirabegron should not exceed 25 mg tablet once daily.</li><li>Mirabegron has not been studied in patients with end stage renal disease (GFR &lt;15 mL/min/1.73 m2 or patients requiring haemodialysis) or severe hepatic impairment (Child Pugh Class C) and it is therefore not recommended for use in these patient populations.</li></ul><p><span style=\"color: rgb(57, 121, 80);\">Gender</span>: No dose adjustment is necessary according to gender.</p><p><br></p><ul><li><span style=\"color: rgb(57, 121, 80);\">Paediatric population</span>: The safety and efficacy of Mirabegron in children below 18 years of age have not yet been established.</li></ul>', 'active', '745_1741503395.jpg', 3, 12, NULL, '2025-03-06 20:50:10', '2025-03-09 11:56:35'),
(2666, 'Utrobin', 'Solifenacin Succinate', 30.00, 10, 'Tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications for Rocovas 5 mg</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is indicated for:</p><ul><li><strong>Heterozygous Hypercholesterolemia</strong> (Familial and Non-familial)</li><li><strong>Homozygous Hypercholesterolemia</strong> (Familial)</li><li><strong>Mixed Dyslipidemia</strong> (Fredrickson Type IIa and IIb)</li><li><strong>Primary prevention of cardiovascular disease</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><ul><li>Statins</li><li>Other Anti-anginal &amp; Anti-ischemic drugs</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is a selective and competitive inhibitor of HMG-CoA reductase, the enzyme responsible for converting 3-hydroxy-3-methyl glutaryl coenzyme A to mevalonate, a cholesterol precursor. It reduces lipid levels in two ways:</p><ol><li><strong>Increases hepatic LDL receptors</strong>: Enhances uptake and breakdown of LDL.</li><li><strong>Inhibits hepatic synthesis of VLDL</strong>: Reduces overall VLDL and LDL particles.</li></ol><p><strong>Dosage of Rocovas 5 mg</strong></p><ul><li><strong>General dose range</strong>: 5-40 mg once daily. (Use 40 mg only for patients not achieving LDL-C goals with 20 mg).</li><li><strong>Homozygous Familial Hypercholesterolemia (HoFH)</strong>: Starting dose of 20 mg/day.</li><li><strong>Pediatric patients</strong>:</li><li>With HeFH (8-10 years): 5-10 mg/day.</li><li>With HeFH (10-17 years): 5-20 mg/day.</li><li>With HoFH (7-17 years): 20 mg/day.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg can be taken with or without food at any time of the day.</p><p><strong>Drug Interactions</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Cyclosporine</strong>: Increases exposure; do not exceed 5 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Gemfibrozil</strong>: Avoid if possible; if needed, limit the dose to 10 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Lopinavir/Ritonavir or Atazanavir/Ritonavir</strong>: Increases exposure; limit the dose to 10 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Coumarin anticoagulants</strong>: May prolong INR; monitor INR frequently.</li><li><strong>Lipid-lowering therapies</strong>: Combining with fibrates or niacin increases the risk of muscle-related side effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is contraindicated in:</p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to any of its components.</li><li>Liver disease, including unexplained persistent elevation of hepatic transaminases.</li><li>Pregnant women or women planning to conceive.</li><li>Nursing mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p>Rocovas 5 mg is generally well-tolerated. Common side effects include:</p><ul><li>Headache</li><li>Myalgia</li><li>Constipation</li><li>Asthenia</li><li>Abdominal pain</li><li>Nausea</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1935_1741276271.webp', 8, 12, NULL, '2025-03-06 20:51:11', '2025-03-06 20:51:11'),
