n of raw egg whites interferes with Cutin 5000 mcg absorption.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Contraindicated in patients with known hypersensitivity to any of the ingredients.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Sufficient clinical data is not available to use in pregnant women and lactating mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool and dry place, away from light and moisture.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1228_1742125254.webp', 5, 12, NULL, '2025-03-16 16:40:54', '2025-03-16 16:40:54'),
(3088, 'Famiclav', 'Cefuroxime Axetil + Clavulanic Acid', 35.00, 7, 'Tablet', '7 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '250 mg+62.50 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Cutin 5000 mcg</strong></p><p>Cutin 5000 mcg is indicated for hair loss, weak, brittle, splitting or soft nails, eczema, and dermatitis.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Herbal and Nutraceuticals</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Cutin 5000 mcg is an essential vitamin, also known as vitamin H. It is involved in vital physiological functions like fatty acid synthesis, amino acid catabolism, and gluconeogenesis. It acts as a cofactor in the enzymatic carboxylation of pyruvate and acetyl-CoA. Cutin 5000 mcg influences the growth and differentiation of epidermal cells, making it crucial for the formation and renewal of the skin, hair, and nails. It functions as a coenzyme for mitochondrial carboxylases in hair roots and improves keratin structure. Cutin 5000 mcg deficiency may lead to hair loss and a variety of systemic symptoms such as dermatitis and aciduria. Cutin 5000 mcg is one of the most prescribed nutritional supplements for any kind of hair loss.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration of Cutin 5000 mcg</strong></p><p>The dosage of Cutin 5000 mcg varies depending on the disease condition and age group. Generally, 1-3 tablets per day or as advised by the physician. In children, Cutin 5000 mcg deficiency affects those between 1 week and 2 years of age, often exhibiting seizures, hypotonia, developmental delay, ataxia, hyperventilation, and coma. In this case, 5-10 tablets daily should be crushed and mixed with water or fruit juice, or as advised by the physician.</p><p><strong>Interaction of Cutin 5000 mcg</strong></p><ul><li>There are indications that anticonvulsant drugs may lower the plasma level of Cutin 5000 mcg.</li><li>Antibiotic use may decrease the Cutin 5000 mcg contribution to the body made by the microflora of the large intestine.</li><li>Excessive consumption of raw egg whites interferes with Cutin 5000 mcg absorption.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Contraindicated in patients with known hypersensitivity to any of the ingredients.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>Sufficient clinical data is not available to use in pregnant women and lactating mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a cool and dry place, away from light and moisture.</li><li>Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><br></p>', 'active', '1667_1742125302.webp', 5, 12, NULL, '2025-03-16 16:41:42', '2025-03-16 16:41:42'),
