rong>Prolactinoma</strong> (pituitary tumor).</li></ul><h3><strong>Side Effects</strong>:</h3><ul><li><strong>Rare</strong>: Transient intestinal cramps, extrapyramidal symptoms in children, increased prolactin leading to <strong>galactorrhea</strong> (milk production) and <strong>gynecomastia</strong> (enlarged breasts in men).</li><li><strong>Allergic reactions</strong> like rash and urticaria.</li></ul><h3><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong>:</h3><ul><li>Safety during <strong>pregnancy</strong> is not established; avoid unless necessary.</li><li><strong>Excreted in breast milk</strong> but in minimal amounts; generally not harmful.</li></ul><h3><strong>Precautions</strong>:</h3><ul><li>Use cautiously in <strong>children</strong>, especially those under 1 year, due to the risk of neurological side effects.</li><li>Caution in patients with <strong>hepatic or renal disorders</strong>.</li></ul><h3><strong>Overdose</strong>:</h3><ul><li>Symptoms may include <strong>drowsiness</strong>, <strong>disorientation</strong>, and <strong>extrapyramidal symptoms</strong>.</li><li>Treatment: <strong>Activated charcoal</strong>, and if necessary, <strong>anticholinergic drugs</strong> or <strong>antiparkinson drugs</strong> to manage side effects.</li></ul><h3><strong>Storage Conditions</strong>:</h3><ul><li>Store below <strong>30°C</strong>, away from light and moisture, and keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><h3><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong>:</h3><ul><li><strong>Motility Stimulants</strong>, <strong>Dopamine Antagonists</strong>, <strong>Prokinetic Drugs</strong>.</li></ul><h3><strong>Mode of Action</strong>:</h3><ul><li>Blocks dopamine receptors in the stomach and CTZ, promoting gastric emptying, enhancing peristalsis, regulating pyloric contractions, and increasing esophageal motility, preventing regurgitation of gastric contents.</li></ul><h3><strong>Pediatric Use</strong>:</h3><ul><li><strong>Infants</strong>: Use with caution due to the immature blood-brain barrier and potential for side effects.</li><li><strong>Liver or kidney disorders</strong>: Adjustments may be needed due to extensive metabolism in the liver or impaired renal elimination.</li></ul>', 'in-active', '1278_1742446469.jpg', 27, 12, 'mdlikhon202324@gmail.com', '2025-03-20 09:54:29', '2025-05-08 14:35:33'),
