g daily.</li><li><strong>Adult IV Dosage</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Chemotherapy-induced nausea and vomiting (CINV): 0.25 mg IV administered over 30 seconds, approximately 30 minutes before chemotherapy.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Radiotherapy-induced nausea and vomiting (RINV): 0.25 mg IV administered over 30 seconds, approximately 30 minutes before each radiation fraction.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Post-operative nausea and vomiting (PONV): 0.075 mg IV administered over 10 seconds, immediately before anesthesia induction.</li><li><strong>Children (1 month to 17 years)</strong>: 20 mcg/kg body weight, with a maximum dose of 1.5 mg.</li><li>রেজিস্টার্ড চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ মোতাবেক ঔষধ সেবন করুন*</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction</strong></p><p> In clinical trials, Palotic has been safely administered with corticosteroids, analgesics, antiemetics, antispasmodics, and anticholinergic agents. It does not inhibit the antitumor activity of chemotherapy drugs like cisplatin, cyclophosphamide, cytarabine, doxorubicin, or mitomycin C. There are no significant pharmacokinetic interactions with metoclopramide, and Palotic does not inhibit or induce major CYP enzymes (CYP1A2, CYP2D6, CYP3A4), suggesting a low risk of clinically significant drug interactions.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p> Palonosetron is contraindicated in patients with a known hypersensitivity to the drug or any of its components.</p><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><p> Common side effects include headaches and constipation.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy Category B</strong>: Palonosetron should be used during pregnancy only if clearly needed, as its safety has not been fully established.</li><li><strong>Lactation</strong>: It is unknown if Palonosetron is excreted in breast milk, so it should be used with caution while breastfeeding.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Elderly</strong>: No dosage adjustment is recommended for patients over 65 years of age.</li><li><strong>Children</strong>: A single IV dose of 20 mcg/kg body weight, with a maximum dose of 1.5 mg, is recommended for children aged 1 month to 10 years.</li><li><strong>Renal and Hepatic Impairment</strong>: No dosage adjustment is recommended for patients with renal or hepatic dysfunction.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><p> There is no known antidote for Palotic overdose. Supportive care should be provided in case of overdose.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p> Anti-emetic drugs</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p> Store in a cool, dry place, protected from light.</p><p><br></p><p>4o mini</p>', 'active', '904_1742448747.webp', 17, 12, 'mdlikhon202324@gmail.com', '2025-03-20 10:32:27', '2025-03-20 10:32:27'),
