(4102, 'Deltasone', 'Prednisolone', 60.00, 1, 'Bottle', '50 ml bottle', 'Oral Solution', '5 mg/5 ml', 'yes', 'no', '<p>Updated</p>', 'active', '186_1742649556.jpg', 6, 12, 'fazlearabbi97@gmail.com', '2025-03-22 18:19:16', '2025-03-22 18:19:16'),
(4103, 'Ketoral', 'Ketoconazole', 9.06, 10, 'tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '200 mg', 'no', 'no', '<h3>Indications of Ketoral 200 mg</h3><p>Ketoral 200 mg therapeutic shampoo is used for the prevention and treatment of infections where the yeast <em>Malassezia furfur</em> (previously called <em>Pityrosporum orbiculare</em>) is involved. These conditions include:</p><ul><li>Dandruff</li><li>Seborrhoeic dermatitis</li><li>Tinea (pityriasis) versicolor</li></ul><h3>Therapeutic Class</h3><p>Drugs for subcutaneous and mycoses</p><h3>Pharmacology</h3><p>Ketoral 200 mg 2% shampoo is a broad-spectrum imidazole-dioxolane, synthetic antifungal agent. It inhibits the in vitro growth of common dermatophytes and yeasts by altering the permeability of the cell membrane. The organisms affected include:</p><ul><li><strong>Dermatophytes</strong>: <em>Trichophyton rubrum</em>, <em>T. mentagrophytes</em>, <em>T. tonsurans</em>, <em>Microsporum canis</em>, <em>M. audouini</em>, <em>M. gypseum</em>, <em>Epidermophyton floccosum</em></li><li><strong>Yeasts</strong>: <em>Candida albicans</em>, <em>Malassezia ovale</em> (Pityrosporum ovale), <em>C. tropicalis</em></li><li>The organism responsible for tinea versicolor: <em>Malassezia furfur</em> (Pityrosporum orbiculare)</li></ul><h3>Dosage &amp; Administration of Ketoral 200 mg</h3><p><strong>For topical administration in adults, elderly, and children:</strong></p><ol><li>Wash affected areas and leave for 3-5 minutes before rinsing.</li><li><strong>Treatment:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Dandruff and seborrhoeic dermatitis</strong>: Wash hair twice weekly for 2-4 weeks.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Tinea versicolor</strong>: Use once daily for a maximum of 5 days.</li></ul><ol><li><strong>Prophylaxis:</strong></li></ol><ul><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Dandruff and seborrhoeic dermatitis</strong>: Use once every 1-2 weeks.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Tinea versicolor</strong>: Use once daily for a maximum of 3 days before exposure to sunshine.</li></ul><ol><li>If no clinical improvement is observed after the treatment period, the diagnosis should be reevaluated.</li></ol><h3>Interaction of Ketoral 200 mg</h3><p>No information was found regarding interactions for the shampoo form of Ketoral 200 mg.</p><h3>Contraindications</h3><p>Ketoral 200 mg therapeutic shampoo is contraindicated in individuals who have shown hypersensitivity to Ketoral 200 mg or any of its excipients.</p><h3>Side Effects of Ketoral 200 mg</h3><p>In clinical trials, side effects were rare:</p><ul><li>In 11 double-blind trials with 264 patients using Ketoral 200 mg 2% shampoo for dandruff or seborrheic dermatitis, less than 1% of patients reported increased hair loss and irritation.</li><li>In three open-label trials with 41 patients using the shampoo 4-10 times weekly for six months, side effects included:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Abnormal hair texture</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Scalp pustules</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Mild dryness of the skin</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Itching</li><li>As with other shampoos, oiliness and dryness of hair and scalp have been reported.</li><li>Rare reports of hair discoloration in worldwide use.</li></ul><h3>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</h3><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy Category C</strong>: There are no adequate and well-controlled studies in pregnant or lactating women. However, data from a limited number of exposed pregnancies indicate no adverse effects on pregnancy or fetal health.</li><li>Animal studies show reproductive toxicity at doses not relevant to topical administration.</li><li>No effects on breastfed infants are anticipated as plasma concentrations of Ketoral 200 mg are not detectable after topical use on the scalp. Plasma levels may be detected with whole-body application, but no known risks exist for pregnancy or lactation.</li><li>Use during pregnancy only if the potential benefit justifies the potential risk to the fetus.</li></ul><h3>Precautions &amp; Warnings</h3><ul><li>In patients with prolonged use of topical corticosteroids, it is recommended to gradually withdraw steroid therapy over 2-3 weeks while using Ketoral 200 mg therapeutic shampoo to avoid rebound effects.</li><li>Avoid contact with the eyes. If the shampoo enters the eyes, rinse immediately with plenty of water.</li></ul><h3>Overdose Effects of Ketoral 200 mg</h3><p>No specific information is available for the treatment of overdose with Ketoral 200 mg shampoo unless taken at doses higher than recommended. In the case of accidental ingestion, supportive and symptomatic measures should be followed. Do not induce vomiting or perform gastric lavage to avoid aspiration.</p><h3>Storage Conditions</h3><ul><li>Store at a temperature below 25°C, away from heat and light.</li><li>Do not store in the bathroom.</li><li>Keep away from children and pets.</li></ul><h3>Use in Special Populations</h3><ul><li><strong>Pediatric Use</strong>: Safety and effectiveness in children have not been established.</li><li><strong>Geriatric Use</strong>: Normal adult dosage is appropriate.</li></ul>', 'active', '695_1742649795.webp', 4, 1, 'rajubinahmed@gmail.com', '2025-03-22 18:23:15', '2025-05-03 23:06:37'),
(4104, 'Fexoral', 'Fexofenadine Hydrochloride', 48.00, 1, 'x 50 ml bottle', '50 ml bottle', 'Oral Suspension', '30 mg/5 ml', 'yes', 'no', '<p>Updated</p>', 'active', '805_1742649948.png', 17, 12, 'fazlearabbi97@gmail.com', '2025-03-22 18:25:48', '2025-05-02 17:57:30'),
(4105, 'Ebatin', 'Ebastine', 60.00, 1, 'x 30 ml bottle', '30 ml bottle', 'Syrup', '5 mg/5 ml', 'yes', 'no', '<p>Updated..</p>', 'active', '1633_1742650139.jpg', 17, 12, 'fazlearabbi97@gmail.com', '2025-03-22 18:28:59', '2025-05-02 09:06:27'),
(4106, 'Biocal-D', 'Algae Calcium + Vitamin D3', 11.00, 30, 'tablet', '30 tablet in a pack', 'Tablet', '500 mg+200 IU', 'no', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Biocal-D</strong></p><p>This combination is used for the treatment of osteoporosis, osteomalacia, rickets, tetany, and parathyroid disease. Calcium supplements are often used to ensure adequate dietary intake in conditions such as pregnancy &amp; lactation, osteogenesis and tooth formation (as an adjunct with definite treatment), and therapy with anti-seizure medications. It is also used as a routine supplement and phosphate binder in chronic renal failure.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Specific mineral &amp; vitamin combined preparations</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Biocal-D is a preparation of Calcium Carbonate and Vitamin D3 (Cholecalciferol). Calcium is necessary for many normal functions of our body, especially bone formation and maintenance. Vitamin D3 helps with the absorption &amp; reabsorption of Calcium. Vitamin D3 also stimulates bone formation. Clinical studies showed that Calcium and Vitamin D3 together help in bone growth and the prevention of osteoporosis &amp; bone fractures.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration of Biocal-D</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Calcium 500 mg and Vitamin D3 200 IU Tablet</strong>: 2 tablets daily or 1 tablet twice daily.</li><li><strong>Calcium 500 mg and Vitamin D3 400 IU Tablet</strong>: 1 tablet twice daily.</li></ul><p>It is best taken with or just after a meal to improve absorption.</p><p><strong>Interaction of Biocal-D</strong></p><p>It may interact with calcium, aluminium, or magnesium-containing antacids &amp; other calcium supplements, calcitriol &amp; other vitamin D3 supplements, digoxin, tetracycline, doxycycline, minocycline, or oxytetracycline.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Biocal-D is contraindicated in cases of hypercalcaemia, hyperthyroidism, renal calculi &amp; nephrolithiasis, and Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome.</p><p><strong>Side Effects of Biocal-D</strong></p><p>Biocal-D is generally well tolerated. However, if you experience nausea, vomiting, stomach cramps, dry mouth, increased thirst, increased urination, or any other unusual symptoms, consult your physician. Constipation may also occur.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><p>This combination should be used as directed by a physician during pregnancy or while breastfeeding.</p><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><p>If you have any pre-existing heart disease or kidney disease, precautions should be taken.</p><p><strong>Overdose Effects of Biocal-D</strong></p><p>Symptoms of overdose may include nausea and vomiting, severe drowsiness, dry mouth, loss of appetite, metallic taste, stomach cramps, diarrhea, headache, and constipation.</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Keep in a dry place away from light and heat. Keep out of the reach of children.</p>', 'active', '1282_1742650309.webp', 44, 1, 'rajubinahmed@gmail.com', '2025-03-22 18:31:49', '2025-05-03 00:54:07'),
(4107, 'Neocilor', 'Desloratadine', 30.00, 1, 'x 50 ml bottle', '50 ml bottle', 'Syrup', '2.5 mg/5 ml', 'yes', 'no', '<p>Updated..</p>', 'active', '1595_1742650391.jpg', 2, 12, 'fazlearabbi97@gmail.com', '2025-03-22 18:33:11', '2025-05-05 08:20:20'),
(4108, 'Fixal', 'Fexofenadine Hydrochloride', 9.00, 10, 'tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '120 mg', 'no', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Fixal 120 mg:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Allergic Rhinitis:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">In adults and children aged 12 years and older, Fixal 120 mg is recommended for the relief of seasonal and persistent allergic rhinitis symptoms, including sneezing, rhinorrhea, lacrimation, itchy eyes, nose, palate, and throat.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">It improves work/activity productivity and quality of life in patients with allergic rhinitis.</li><li><strong>Chronic Idiopathic Urticaria:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Fixal is also recommended for the treatment of symptoms associated with chronic idiopathic urticaria in adults and children aged 12 years and older.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">It effectively reduces the number of wheals and pruritus in affected patients, improving work/activity productivity and overall quality of life.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Non-sedating antihistamines.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology:</strong></p><ul><li>Fixal 120 mg is a selective peripheral H1-receptor antagonist. It works by blocking the histamine receptor, which mediates allergic responses.</li><li>After oral administration, it is quickly absorbed, reaching peak plasma concentrations in 2 to 3 hours.</li><li>It does not cross the blood-brain barrier, which is why it does not produce sedative effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Seasonal Allergic Rhinitis (Adults and children 12 years and older):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">60 mg twice daily or 120 mg once daily or 180 mg once daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">In case of impaired renal function: 60 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Children (6-11 years):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">30 mg twice daily or 60 mg once daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">In case of impaired renal function: 30 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Children (2-11 years) – Suspension (5 ml = 30 mg):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">30 mg (5 ml) twice daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">In case of impaired renal function: 30 mg (5 ml) once daily.</li><li><strong>Chronic Idiopathic Urticaria (Adults and children 12 years and older):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">60 mg twice daily or 120 mg once daily or 180 mg once daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">In case of impaired renal function: 60 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Children (6-11 years):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">30 mg twice daily or 60 mg once daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">In case of impaired renal function: 30 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Children (6 months to less than 2 years) – Suspension (2.5 ml = 15 mg):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">15 mg (2.5 ml) twice daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">In case of impaired renal function: 15 mg (2.5 ml) once daily.</li><li><strong>Children (2-11 years) – Suspension (5 ml = 30 mg):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">30 mg (5 ml) twice daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">In case of impaired renal function: 30 mg (5 ml) once daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction of Fixal 120 mg:</strong></p><ul><li>Co-administration with <strong>erythromycin</strong> or <strong>ketoconazole</strong> may cause a 2-3 fold increase in fexofenadine levels, though no effect on the QT interval or increased adverse reactions have been observed.</li><li><strong>Omeprazole</strong> shows no interaction with fexofenadine.</li><li>Fexofenadine bioavailability decreases if taken 15 minutes before antacids containing <strong>aluminum</strong> and <strong>magnesium hydroxide</strong>.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications:</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to Fixal 120 mg or any of its components.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common:</strong> Headache, fatigue, dizziness, nausea, and issues at the administration site.</li><li><strong>Uncommon:</strong> Exhaustion, hypersensitivity reactions (angioedema, chest tightness, dyspnea, flushing, anaphylaxis), anxiety, nightmares, insomnia, palpitations, tachycardia, diarrhea, rash, pruritus, and urticaria.</li><li><strong>Rare:</strong> No common frequency can be calculated.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation:</strong></p><ul><li>Category C by the US FDA, indicating potential risks. Avoid use during pregnancy and lactation unless the benefits outweigh the risks.</li><li>Fexofenadine passes into human milk, thus not recommended for nursing mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings:</strong></p><ul><li>Use cautiously in elderly individuals and those with renal or hepatic impairment.</li><li>Patients with a history of cardiovascular issues may be at risk for tachycardia and palpitations.</li><li>Fexofenadine does not significantly affect the central nervous system, so it is unlikely to impair the ability to drive or operate machinery. However, individual responses should be assessed.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects:</strong></p><ul><li>Overdose may lead to symptoms such as dry mouth, drowsiness, fatigue, and dizziness.</li><li>In clinical studies, participants received high doses (up to 800 mg) without significant adverse effects.</li><li>Treatment focuses on symptom management, as hemodialysis does not effectively remove fexofenadine from the blood.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions:</strong></p><ul><li>Store in a dry place, away from heat and light. Keep out of reach of children.</li></ul><p><strong>Drug Class:</strong></p><ul><li>Non-sedating antihistamines.</li></ul><p><strong>Mode of Action:</strong></p><ul><li>Fexofenadine is an inverse agonist of the H1 histamine receptor, preventing histamine-induced allergic reactions like pruritus, rhinorrhea, and watery eyes. It stabilizes the inactive state of the H1 receptor and does not affect other neurotransmitter systems like serotonin, dopamine, or acetylcholine.</li></ul>', 'active', '339_1742650413.webp', 7, 1, 'rajubinahmed@gmail.com', '2025-03-22 18:33:33', '2025-05-03 10:41:42');
INSERT INTO `products` (`id`, `productName`, `genericName`, `retail_max_price`, `cart_qty_inc`, `cart_text`, `unit_in_pack`, `type`, `quantity`, `prescription`, `feature`, `description`, `status`, `coverImage`, `company_id`, `category_id`, `add_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(4109, 'Halobet', 'Halobetasol Propionate', 130.00, 1, 'x 20 gm tube', '20 gm tube', 'Ointment', '0.05%', 'no', 'no', '<h3>Indications of Halobet 0.05%</h3><p>Halobet 0.05% is a super-high potent corticosteroid indicated for the relief of the inflammatory and pruritic manifestations of corticosteroid-responsive dermatoses. Treatment beyond two consecutive weeks is not recommended, and the total dosage should not exceed 50 gm/week due to the potential for the drug to suppress the Hypothalamic-Pituitary-Adrenal (HPA) axis.</p><h3>Therapeutic Class</h3><p>Other Topical Corticosteroids</p><h3>Pharmacology</h3><p>Like other topical corticosteroids, Halobet 0.05% has anti-inflammatory, antipruritic, and vasoconstrictive actions. The mechanism of anti-inflammatory activity is not fully understood but is thought to involve the induction of phospholipase A2 inhibitory proteins, called lipocortins. These proteins help control the biosynthesis of potent mediators of inflammation, such as prostaglandins and leukotrienes, by inhibiting the release of arachidonic acid, a precursor to these mediators.</p><h3>Dosage &amp; Administration</h3><p>Apply a thin layer of Halobetasol Cream or Ointment to the affected skin once or twice daily as directed by the physician, and rub it in gently and completely. Treatment should be limited to two weeks, and amounts greater than 50 gm/week should not be used. As with other highly active corticosteroids, therapy should be discontinued when control has been achieved. If no improvement is seen within two weeks, reassessment of the diagnosis may be necessary. Halobetasol should not be used with occlusive dressings. Use in children under 12 years of age is not recommended.</p><h3>Contraindications</h3><p>Halobet 0.05% is contraindicated in patients with a history of hypersensitivity to any of the components of the preparation.</p><h3>Side Effects</h3><p>Possible adverse effects include:</p><ul><li>Burning</li><li>Itching</li><li>Dryness</li><li>Folliculitis acne</li><li>Hypopigmentation</li><li>Perioral dermatitis</li><li>Allergic contact dermatitis</li><li>Skin atrophy</li><li>Secondary infections</li><li>Striae</li><li>Miliaria</li></ul><h3>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</h3><p>Topical corticosteroids should be used during pregnancy only if the potential benefit justifies the potential risk to the fetus. It is not known whether topical administration of corticosteroids could result in detectable quantities in breast milk, so caution should be exercised when used by nursing women.</p><h3>Precautions &amp; Warnings</h3><p>Systemic absorption of topical corticosteroids can lead to:</p><ul><li>Reversible HPA axis suppression</li><li>Cushing\'s syndrome</li><li>Hyperglycemia</li><li>Glucosuria</li></ul><p>Patients receiving large doses of potent topical steroids on large surface areas or under occlusive dressings should be periodically evaluated for evidence of HPA axis suppression using tests like urinary free cortisol and ACTH stimulation tests. If suppression is noted, consider reducing the frequency or switching to a less potent steroid.</p><h3>Overdose Effects</h3><p>Topically applied Halobetasol propionate Cream can be absorbed in sufficient amounts to cause systemic effects.</p><h3>Storage Conditions</h3><p>Store below 30°C. Keep out of reach of children.</p><h3>Use in Special Populations</h3><ul><li><strong>Use in children under 12 years of age:</strong> Not recommended. Safety and effectiveness have not been established, and children are more susceptible to HPA axis suppression.</li><li><strong>Use with occlusive dressings:</strong> Not recommended.</li></ul><h3>Drug Classes</h3><p>Other Topical Corticosteroids</p><h3>Mode of Action</h3><p>Like other topical corticosteroids, Halobet 0.05% has anti-inflammatory, antipruritic, and vasoconstrictive actions. The mechanism of action is primarily through the induction of lipocortins, which inhibit the release of arachidonic acid from membrane phospholipids, thereby reducing the production of inflammatory mediators.</p><h3>Pregnancy</h3><p>Topical corticosteroids should only be used during pregnancy if the potential benefit outweighs the risk to the fetus.</p><h3>Pediatric Use</h3><p>Safety and effectiveness in pediatric patients have not been established. Children are more at risk of HPA axis suppression when treated with potent topical corticosteroids.</p>', 'active', '42_1742650529.webp', 4, 1, 'rajubinahmed@gmail.com', '2025-03-22 18:35:29', '2025-04-15 10:19:15'),
(4110, 'Bilanex', 'Bilastine', 140.00, 1, 'Bottle', '60 ml bottle', 'Oral Solution', '12.5 mg/5 ml', 'yes', 'no', '<p>updated</p>', 'active', '119_1742650541.jpg', 55, 12, 'fazlearabbi97@gmail.com', '2025-03-22 18:35:41', '2025-03-22 18:35:41'),
(4111, 'Bilamin', 'Bilastine', 140.00, 1, 'Bottle', '60 ml bottle', 'Oral Solution', '12.5 mg/5 ml', 'yes', 'no', '<p>updated</p>', 'active', '1007_1742650659.jpg', 30, 12, 'fazlearabbi97@gmail.com', '2025-03-22 18:37:39', '2025-03-22 18:37:39'),
(4112, 'Renova', 'Paracetamol', 1.20, 10, 'tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '500 mg', 'no', 'no', '<h3>Indications of Renova 500 mg</h3><p>Renova 500 mg is indicated for:</p><ul><li>Fever</li><li>Common cold and influenza</li><li>Headache</li><li>Toothache</li><li>Earache</li><li>Bodyache</li><li>Myalgia (muscle pain)</li><li>Neuralgia (nerve pain)</li><li>Dysmenorrhoea (painful menstruation)</li><li>Sprains</li><li>Colic pain</li><li>Back pain</li><li>Post-operative pain</li><li>Postpartum pain</li><li>Inflammatory pain</li><li>Post-vaccination pain in children</li><li>Rheumatic and osteoarthritic pain and stiffness of joints</li></ul><h3>Therapeutic Class</h3><p>Non-opioid analgesics</p><h3>Pharmacology</h3><p>Renova 500 mg (Acetaminophen) has <strong>analgesic</strong> and <strong>antipyretic</strong> properties with weak <strong>anti-inflammatory</strong> activity. It primarily acts in the <strong>central nervous system (CNS)</strong>, increasing the pain threshold by inhibiting the cyclooxygenase enzymes (COX-1, COX-2, COX-3), which are involved in prostaglandin synthesis. Acetaminophen is a <strong>para-aminophenol derivative</strong> and is considered one of the safest and fastest-acting analgesics with minimal side effects compared to aspirin.</p><h3>Dosage &amp; Administration</h3><h4>Tablet:</h4><ul><li><strong>Adults</strong>: 1-2 tablets every 4 to 6 hours (maximum 4 gm, or 8 tablets, per day)</li><li><strong>Children (6-12 years)</strong>: ½ to 1 tablet 3 to 4 times daily (max dose of 2.6 gm/day for long-term treatment)</li></ul><h4>Extended Release Tablet:</h4><ul><li><strong>Adults &amp; Children over 12 years</strong>: 2 tablets every 6 to 8 hours (maximum of 6 tablets in 24 hours). Do not crush the tablet.</li></ul><h4>Syrup/Suspension:</h4><ul><li><strong>Children under 3 months</strong>: 10 mg/kg body weight, 3 to 4 times daily (5 mg/kg if jaundiced)</li><li><strong>3 months to 1 year</strong>: ½ to 1 teaspoon 3 to 4 times daily</li><li><strong>1-5 years</strong>: 1-2 teaspoons 3 to 4 times daily</li><li><strong>6-12 years</strong>: 2-4 teaspoons 3 to 4 times daily</li><li><strong>Adults</strong>: 4-8 teaspoons 3 to 4 times daily</li></ul><h4>Suppository:</h4><ul><li><strong>Children 3-12 months</strong>: 60-120 mg, 4 times daily</li><li><strong>Children 1-5 years</strong>: 125-250 mg, 4 times daily</li><li><strong>Children 6-12 years</strong>: 250-500 mg, 4 times daily</li><li><strong>Adults &amp; children over 12 years</strong>: 0.5-1 gm, 4 times daily</li></ul><h4>Paediatric Drop:</h4><ul><li><strong>Children Up to 3 months</strong>: 0.5 ml (40 mg)</li><li><strong>4 to 11 months</strong>: 1.0 ml (80 mg)</li><li><strong>1 to 2 years</strong>: 1.5 ml (120 mg)</li><li>Do not exceed 5 doses per day for a maximum of 5 days.</li></ul><h4>Renova 500 mg Tablet with Actizorb Technology:</h4><ul><li>Dissolves up to 5 times faster than standard Renova tablets. It is a fast-acting and safe analgesic with antipyretic properties, suitable for those who cannot tolerate aspirin or other analgesics.</li><li><strong>Adults and children over 12 years</strong>: 1-2 tablets every 4-6 hours (max 8 tablets in 24 hours)</li><li><strong>Children (7-11 years)</strong>: ½-1 tablet every 4-6 hours (max 4 tablets in 24 hours)</li></ul><h3>Interaction of Renova 500 mg</h3><ul><li><strong>Barbiturates, tricyclic antidepressants, and alcohol</strong> may reduce the ability to metabolize large doses of Renova 500 mg.</li><li><strong>Alcohol</strong> increases the hepatotoxicity of Renova 500 mg in overdose.</li><li><strong>Chronic use of anticonvulsants or oral contraceptives</strong> may induce liver enzymes and reduce Renova 500 mg’s effectiveness due to increased first-pass metabolism or clearance.</li></ul><h3>Contraindications</h3><ul><li>Known hypersensitivity to Renova 500 mg.</li></ul><h3>Side Effects of Renova 500 mg</h3><ul><li>Mild side effects, but can include:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Haematological reactions (thrombocytopenia, leucopenia, pancytopenia, neutropenia, agranulocytosis)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Pancreatitis</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Skin rashes and other allergic reactions</li></ul><h3>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</h3><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy Category B (USFDA)</strong>: Should be used during pregnancy only if clearly needed.</li><li><strong>Lactation</strong>: Excreted in breast milk; maternal use in normal therapeutic doses does not appear to pose a risk to the nursing infant.</li></ul><h3>Precautions &amp; Warnings</h3><ul><li>Caution in patients with impaired <strong>kidney or liver function</strong>.</li><li>Care when taken with other drugs affecting the liver.</li></ul><h3>Overdose Effects of Renova 500 mg</h3><ul><li><strong>First 24 hours</strong>: Pallor, nausea, vomiting, anorexia, and abdominal pain.</li><li><strong>12-48 hours post-ingestion</strong>: Liver damage may become evident.</li><li><strong>Metabolic effects</strong>: Abnormal glucose metabolism and metabolic acidosis.</li></ul><h3>Storage Conditions</h3><ul><li>Store in a dry place, away from light and heat.</li><li>Keep out of the reach of children.</li></ul><h3>Drug Classes</h3><ul><li>Non-opioid analgesics</li></ul><h3>Mode of Action</h3><p>Renova 500 mg works primarily in the CNS to increase the pain threshold by inhibiting COX-1, COX-2, and COX-3 enzymes, which are involved in prostaglandin synthesis. It is fast-acting, safe, and has minimal side effects compared to aspirin.</p>', 'active', '1244_1742650667.webp', 7, 1, 'rajubinahmed@gmail.com', '2025-03-22 18:37:47', '2025-05-04 15:11:01'),
(4113, 'I-Gold', 'Vitamin C + Vitamin E + Lutein + Copper + Zinc', 13.00, 10, 'Capsule', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Capsule', '60 mg+30 mg+6 mg+2 mg+15 mg', 'no', 'no', '<p>description</p>', 'active', '1366_1742650795.jpg', 29, 1, 'rajubinahmed@gmail.com', '2025-03-22 18:39:55', '2025-04-19 07:22:24'),
