(4592, 'Fenofex', 'Fexofenadine Hydrochloride', 60.00, 1, 'x 50 ml bottle', '50 ml bottle', 'Oral Suspension', '30 mg/5 ml', 'no', 'no', '<p><br></p>', 'active', '736_1742844341.webp', 2, 1, 'rajubinahmed@gmail.com', '2025-03-25 00:25:41', '2025-05-02 17:50:27'),
(4593, 'Calbotol', 'Calcium Citrate + Calcitriol', 13.00, 30, 'tablet', '30 tablet in a pot', 'Tablet', '1200 mg+0.25 mcg', 'no', 'no', '<p><br></p>', 'active', '1221_1742844401.webp', 4, 1, 'rajubinahmed@gmail.com', '2025-03-25 00:26:41', '2025-05-03 01:08:00'),
(4594, 'EPL Plus', 'Carbonyl Iron + Folic Acid + Zinc Sulfate + Vitamin B Complex + Vitamin C', 3.50, 10, 'strip', '10 capsule in a strip', 'Capsule', 'N/A', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p> This capsule is indicated for the treatment and prophylaxis of iron, folic acid, zinc, vitamin B complex, and vitamin C deficiency, especially during pregnancy and lactation.</p><p> <em>রেজিস্টার্ড চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ মোতাবেক ঔষধ সেবন করুন</em></p><p><strong>Composition</strong></p><p> Each capsule contains:</p><ul><li>Elemental Iron (as Carbonyl Iron) INN 50 mg</li><li>Zinc Sulphate Monohydrate BP 61.80 mg (equivalent to Zinc 22.50 mg)</li><li>Folic Acid BP 0.5 mg</li><li>Nicotinamide BP 10 mg</li><li>Riboflavin BP 2 mg</li><li>Pyridoxine Hydrochloride BP 1 mg</li><li>Ascorbic Acid USP 50 mg</li><li>Thiamine Mononitrate BP 2 mg</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Carbonyl Iron</strong>: More effective and safer choice for iron supplementation, with higher bioavailability, low toxicity, and better gastrointestinal tolerance.</li><li><strong>Folic Acid</strong>: Vital for the healthy development of the neural tube and for cell division from a single cell to a fully developed baby.</li><li><strong>Vitamin B Complex</strong>: Necessary for the growth and development of unborn babies.</li><li><strong>Vitamin C</strong>: Plays a role in collagen formation in the fetal membrane.</li><li><strong>Zinc</strong>: A critical nutrient for fetal growth and development, central nervous system development, and ensuring better maternal and infant health.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adult</strong>: One capsule daily before food or as directed by the physician.</li><li><strong>Use in Children &amp; Adolescents</strong>: Upon consultation with a doctor, recommended for use in children &amp; adolescents.</li><li> <em>রেজিস্টার্ড চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ মোতাবেক ঔষধ সেবন করুন</em></li></ul><p><strong>Interaction</strong></p><ul><li>Carbonyl Iron decreases the absorption of tetracycline antibiotics, quinolone antibiotics, levodopa, levothyroxine, methyldopa, and penicillamine.</li><li>Folic Acid interacts with antiepileptics, potentially reducing plasma concentrations of phenobarbital, phenytoin, and primidone.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Contraindicated in patients with a known hypersensitivity to any of the ingredients.</li><li>Iron therapy is contraindicated in the presence of haemolytic anaemia.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Allergic sensitization has been reported following oral administration of folic acid.</li><li>Oral iron preparations may cause constipation, particularly in older patients.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li>The use of any drug during the first trimester of pregnancy should be avoided if possible. Iron administration during the first trimester requires definitive evidence of iron deficiency.</li><li>Prophylaxis of iron deficiency, where an inadequate diet necessitates supplementary zinc and folic acid, is justified during the remainder of pregnancy.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Special care should be taken in patients who may develop iron overload, such as those with haemochromatosis, hemolytic anaemia, or red blood cell aplasia.</li><li>Iron chelates with tetracycline, and absorption may be impaired.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><p> Symptoms of carbonyl iron overdose include decreased energy, nausea, abdominal pain, tarry stool, weak, rapid pulse, fever, coma, and seizures.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p> Iron, Vitamin &amp; Mineral Combined preparation</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p> Store at a temperature not exceeding 30°C in a dry place. Protect from moisture.</p>', 'active', '397_1742844429.jpg', 64, 12, 'mahidsiam1@gmail.com', '2025-03-25 00:27:09', '2025-03-25 00:27:09'),
