(4613, 'Flomyst F', 'Fluticasone Propionate + Formoterol Fumarate', 625.00, 1, 'x 120 metered doses', '120 metered doses', 'Inhaler', '(125 mcg+5 mcg)/puff', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p>Flomyst F is indicated for the following conditions:</p><ul><li><strong>Asthma</strong>: Flomyst F is a fixed-dose combination of Fluticasone Propionate and Formoterol Fumarate, indicated in the regular treatment of asthma where the use of a combination product (an inhaled corticosteroid and a long-acting ß2 agonist) is appropriate:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For patients not adequately controlled with inhaled corticosteroids and \"as required\" inhaled short-acting ß2 agonist.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For patients already adequately controlled on both an inhaled corticosteroid and a long-acting ß2 agonist.</li><li><strong>COPD</strong>: Flomyst F is recommended when a long-acting ß2 agonist/Inhaled corticosteroid is indicated and patients are unable to use other long-acting ß2 agonist/Inhaled corticosteroid.</li></ul><p>Fluticasone Propionate 125 mcg and Formoterol Fumarate 5 mcg inhaler are indicated in adults and adolescents aged 12 years and above.</p><p><em>রেজিস্টার্ড চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ মোতাবেক ঔষধ সেবন করুন</em></p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Flomyst F is a pressurized inhalation suspension containing two active ingredients:</p><ul><li><strong>Fluticasone Propionate</strong>: A steroid that reduces swelling and inflammation in the lungs.</li><li><strong>Formoterol Fumarate Dihydrate</strong>: A long-acting beta-2 agonist (bronchodilator) that helps to keep the airways in the lungs open, making it easier to breathe.</li></ul><p>Together, these two active ingredients improve breathing and help prevent asthma-related breathing problems. However, this medication does not work during an asthma attack, for which a fast-acting bronchodilator (e.g., salbutamol) should be used.</p><p><strong>Dosage</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Asthma</strong>:</li><li><strong>Fluticasone Propionate 125 mcg &amp; Formoterol Fumarate 5 mcg inhaler</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">The recommended dose for adults and adolescents aged 12 years and above: Two inhalations (puffs) twice daily (morning and evening).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">For adults: If asthma is not well-controlled, the dose can be increased to the highest strength of the combination (Fluticasone Propionate 250 mcg &amp; Formoterol Fumarate 10 mcg inhaler), two inhalations (puffs) twice daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Children under 12 years</strong>: No data available, not recommended for use in children under 12.</li><li><strong>Fluticasone Propionate 250 mcg &amp; Formoterol Fumarate 10 mcg inhaler</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Recommended dose for adults: Two inhalations (puffs) twice daily.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Adolescents under 18 years and children</strong>: Not recommended for use.</li><li><strong>COPD</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Fluticasone Propionate 250 mcg &amp; Formoterol Fumarate 10 mcg inhaler</strong>: Two inhalations (puffs) twice daily.</li></ul><p><em>রেজিস্টার্ড চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ মোতাবেক ঔষধ সেবন করুন</em></p><p><strong>Administration</strong></p><ol><li>Remove the cap.</li><li>Shake the inhaler vigorously at least six times before use.</li><li>If the inhaler has not been used for a week or more, shake it well and release one puff into the air.</li><li>Breathe out fully and hold the inhaler upright.</li><li>Place the actuator into your mouth, between your teeth, and close your lips around the mouthpiece.</li><li>While breathing deeply and slowly, press down firmly on the canister to release the medicine.</li><li>After inhaling, hold your breath for at least 10 seconds (or as long as comfortable).</li><li>If your doctor has prescribed more than one inhalation, wait 1 minute between puffs, shake the inhaler well, and repeat steps 4-7.</li><li>After use, replace the cap.</li><li>Rinse your mouth with water after each treatment.</li></ol><p><strong>Cleaning the Inhaler</strong>:</p><p>Clean the inhaler once a week. Remove the canister and rinse the plastic actuator and cap in warm water (do not wet the metal canister). Dry thoroughly before reassembling.</p><p><em>রেজিস্টার্ড চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ মোতাবেক ঔষধ সেবন করুন</em></p><p><strong>Interaction</strong></p><p>No formal drug interaction studies have been performed. Fluticasone Propionate is a substrate of CYP 3A4. Co-administration with strong CYP 3A4 inhibitors (e.g., Ritonavir, Atazanavir, Ketoconazole) may require caution in long-term treatment.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Not for acute asthma symptoms. A fast-acting bronchodilator should be used in case of an asthma attack.</li><li>Not for the prophylactic use in exercise-induced asthma.</li><li>Not for initiation during exacerbations or if asthma is acutely deteriorating.</li><li>Should not be used as the first treatment for asthma.</li><li>Use with caution in patients with pulmonary tuberculosis, infections, diabetes, thyroid disorders, heart conditions, and prolonged QTc intervals.</li><li>Paradoxical bronchospasm may occur. Discontinue and seek medical advice if this happens.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Paradoxical bronchospasm, which may lead to increased wheezing and shortness of breath.</li><li>Hypersensitivity reactions (rare).</li><li>Dysphonia (hoarseness), candidiasis (thrush), which can be relieved by rinsing the mouth after use.</li><li>Possible systemic effects from corticosteroids, including Cushing’s syndrome, adrenal suppression, growth retardation in children, bone mineral density decrease, and psychological effects.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy</strong>: Not recommended unless the benefit to the mother outweighs the potential risk to the fetus.</li><li><strong>Breastfeeding</strong>: It is not known if the active ingredients are excreted in breast milk. A decision should be made whether to continue therapy or breastfeeding, considering the benefits for both mother and child.</li><li><strong>Fertility</strong>: No effects on fertility observed in animal studies.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li>No dose adjustment needed for elderly patients.</li><li>Limited data on use in patients with hepatic or renal impairment.</li><li>Regular monitoring of growth is advised for children on prolonged corticosteroid therapy.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Formoterol Fumarate</strong>: Symptoms may include angina, hypertension, tachycardia, arrhythmia, tremor, muscle cramps, insomnia, and metabolic disturbances.</li><li><strong>Fluticasone Propionate</strong>: Acute overdose may cause suppression of the hypothalamic-pituitary-adrenal axis.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Respiratory corticosteroids</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Store in a cool, dry place, away from light.</p>', 'active', '1513_1742845692.jpg', 3, 12, 'mahidsiam1@gmail.com', '2025-03-25 00:48:12', '2025-05-03 08:12:26'),
(4614, 'Aristo D3', 'Cholecalciferol [Vitamin D3]', 20.00, 10, 'capsule', '10 capsule in a strip', 'Capsule', '20000 IU', 'no', 'no', '<p><br></p>', 'active', '30_1742845744.webp', 29, 1, 'rajubinahmed@gmail.com', '2025-03-25 00:49:04', '2025-05-01 22:27:13'),
