(4633, 'Loratin Fast', 'Loratadine', 4.00, 10, 'tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '10 mg', 'no', 'no', '<p><br></p>', 'active', '1131_1742846957.webp', 4, 1, 'rajubinahmed@gmail.com', '2025-03-25 01:09:17', '2025-05-03 23:31:57'),
(4634, 'Protecor', 'Vitamin C + Vitamin E', 6.00, 1, 'pot', '30 tablet in a pot', 'Tablet', '250 mg+200 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p> The active ingredients of Vitamin C and Vitamin E have been linked with reduced risks of cardiovascular diseases in humans. Concurrent intake of Vitamin E and Vitamin C suggests that their action may be synergistic.</p><ul><li>রেজিস্টার্ড চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ মোতাবেক ঔষধ সেবন করুন*</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Vitamin C:</strong> Necessary for collagen formation and tissue repair. It plays a role in oxidation/reduction reactions as well as other metabolic pathways, including the synthesis of catecholamines, carnitine, and steroids. Vitamin C also plays a role in the conversion of folic acid to folinic acid.</li><li><strong>Vitamin E:</strong> Plays a role in protecting red blood cells against hemolysis, has protective effects against free radicals on polyunsaturated fatty acids found in cell membranes, and prevents the oxidation of vitamins A and C.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><p> Vitamin C &amp; E capsule is administered orally. The adult dose is 1 capsule daily or as directed by the registered physician.</p><ul><li>রেজিস্টার্ড চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ মোতাবেক ঔষধ সেবন করুন*</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Vitamin C:</strong> Is incompatible in solution with Aminophylline, Bleomycin, Erythromycin, Lactobionate, Nafcillin, Nitrofurantoin Sodium, Conjugated oestrogens, Sodium bicarbonate, Sulphafurazole diethanolamine, Chloramphenicol sodium succinate, Chlorthiazide sodium, and Hydrocortisone sodium succinate.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Vitamin C increases the apparent half-life of Paracetamol and enhances iron absorption from the gastrointestinal tract.</li><li><strong>Vitamin E:</strong> No potentially useful drug interactions with Vitamin E have been described. However, high doses of Vitamin E can impair intestinal absorption of Vitamin A and K.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Vitamin C:</strong> Megadoses of Vitamin C have been contraindicated for patients with hyperoxaluria. A pregnant woman taking more than 5 gm daily may suffer from fetal abortion. Higher doses of Vitamin C have been reported to cause failure of conception.</li><li><strong>Vitamin E:</strong> There is no absolute contraindication for Vitamin E.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Vitamin C:</strong> Is usually well tolerated. Large doses may cause diarrhea and other gastrointestinal disturbances.</li><li><strong>Vitamin E:</strong> Is usually well tolerated. Large doses may cause diarrhea, abdominal discomfort, and other gastrointestinal disturbances. It has also been reported to cause fatigue and weakness.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> Category A. Adequate and well-controlled human studies have failed to demonstrate a risk to the fetus in the first trimester of pregnancy, and there is no evidence of risk in later trimesters.</li><li><strong>Lactation:</strong> Safe for use during lactation.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Vitamin C should be given with care to patients with hyperoxaluria.</li><li>In patients taking oral anticoagulants or estrogens, Vitamin E should be given carefully, as it has been found to antagonize the effects of Vitamin K, leading to an increase in blood clotting time in these patients.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p> Anti-oxidant Multivitamin preparations, Specific combined vitamin preparations</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p> Keep below 30°C, away from light and moisture. Keep out of the reach of children.</p>', 'active', '254_1742846957.webp', 7, 12, 'mahidsiam1@gmail.com', '2025-03-25 01:09:17', '2025-03-25 01:09:17');
