(4638, 'Reversair CT', 'Montelukast Sodium', 18.00, 10, 'tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Chewable Tablet', '10 mg', 'no', 'no', '<p><br></p>', 'active', '745_1742847348.png', 44, 1, 'rajubinahmed@gmail.com', '2025-03-25 01:15:48', '2025-05-04 16:41:17'),
(4639, 'Protide', 'Salmeterol + Fluticasone Propionate', 595.00, 1, 'x 120 metered', '120 metered doses', 'Inhaler', '(25 mcg+125 mcg)/puff', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p>Protide is indicated in the regular treatment of asthma where the use of a combination product (long-acting β2-agonist and inhaled corticosteroid) is appropriate:</p><ul><li>Patients not adequately controlled with inhaled corticosteroids and \'as needed\' inhaled short-acting β2-agonist, or</li><li>Patients already adequately controlled on both inhaled corticosteroid and long-acting β2-agonist.</li><li>রেজিস্টার্ড চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ মোতাবেক ঔষধ সেবন করুন*</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Salmeterol Xinafoate:</strong> A selective, long-acting beta-2 agonist used in the treatment of asthma and other forms of diffuse airway obstruction.</li><li><strong>Fluticasone Propionate:</strong> A corticosteroid with mainly glucocorticoid activity. It exerts a topical effect on the lungs without significant systemic effects at usual doses.</li><li><strong>Salmeterol:</strong> Protects against symptoms.</li><li><strong>Fluticasone Propionate:</strong> Improves lung function and prevents exacerbations.</li><li>Both drugs offer a more convenient regimen for patients on concurrent β-agonist and inhaled corticosteroid therapy.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Inhaler:</strong></li><li><strong>Adults and Adolescents (12 years and older):</strong></li><li>2 puffs of 25 µg Salmeterol and 50 µg Fluticasone Propionate twice daily, or</li><li>2 puffs of 25 µg Salmeterol and 125 µg Fluticasone Propionate twice daily, or</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">2 puffs of 25 µg Salmeterol and 250 µg Fluticasone Propionate twice daily.</li><li><strong>Children (4-12 years):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">2 puffs of 25 µg Salmeterol and 50 µg Fluticasone Propionate twice daily.</li><li><strong>Inhalation Capsule (For Asthma):</strong></li><li><strong>Adults and Adolescents (12 years and older):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Salmeterol 50 µg &amp; Fluticasone 100 µg or 250 µg twice daily (morning and evening, 12 hours apart).</li><li><strong>Pediatric Patients (4-11 years):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Salmeterol 50 µg &amp; Fluticasone 100 µg twice daily (morning and evening, 12 hours apart).</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Maximum Dose:</strong> Salmeterol 50 µg &amp; Fluticasone 500 µg twice daily.</li><li><strong>Maxhaler (For Asthma):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\"><strong>Adults and Adolescents (12 years and older):</strong>50/100 inhaler: One Inhalation twice daily</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">50/250 inhaler: One Inhalation twice daily</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">50/500 inhaler: One Inhalation twice daily</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Children (4 years and older):</strong>50/100 inhaler: One Inhalation twice daily (max dose: 100 mcg fluticasone propionate twice daily).</li><li><strong>Maxhaler (For COPD):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Adults:</strong> One Inhalation twice daily.</li></ul><p><strong>Administration</strong></p><ul><li>Shake the inhaler well before each use.</li><li>If the inhaler is new or unused for over a week, release one puff into the air before use.</li><li>Exhale fully, place the inhaler in your mouth, and inhale deeply while pressing the inhaler.</li><li>Hold your breath for at least 10 seconds after inhalation.</li><li>Wait 1 minute between puffs if more than one inhalation is prescribed.</li><li>Clean the inhaler weekly (do not immerse the metal canister in water).</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction</strong></p><ul><li>Both non-selective and selective β-blockers should be avoided in asthma patients unless absolutely necessary.</li><li>Co-administration with strong CYP3A4 inhibitors (e.g., ketoconazole, ritonavir) may increase systemic exposure to Fluticasone Propionate.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Contraindicated in patients with a history of hypersensitivity to Salmeterol Xinafoate, Fluticasone Propionate, or any excipients.</li><li>Contraindicated in the primary treatment of status asthmaticus or other acute asthma episodes.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Salmeterol:</strong> Tremors, palpitations, headache, cardiac arrhythmias (in susceptible patients), hypersensitivity reactions (rash, oedema, angioedema), muscle cramps, oropharyngeal irritation.</li><li><strong>Fluticasone Propionate:</strong> Hoarseness, candidiasis (thrush), hypersensitivity reactions, facial and oropharyngeal oedema. Gargling with water after use can relieve hoarseness and candidiasis.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> Should only be used if the benefit to the mother outweighs any potential risk to the fetus, as there is insufficient experience in human pregnancy.</li><li><strong>Lactation:</strong> Should only be used if the benefit to the mother outweighs the risk to the child, as there is limited data available.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Not for use during an acute asthma exacerbation.</li><li>Serious asthma-related adverse events may occur during treatment.</li><li>Paradoxical bronchospasm may occur; it should be treated with a short-acting inhaled bronchodilator.</li><li>In COPD patients, be vigilant for pneumonia.</li><li>Long-term use of inhaled corticosteroids may cause systemic effects like Cushing\'s syndrome, bone mineral density reduction, cataracts, and glaucoma. Regular reviews and dose titration are essential.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li>Inhaled corticosteroids may affect growth velocity in pediatric patients. Long-term effects on final adult height are unknown.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Salmeterol Overdose:</strong> Symptoms include seizures, hypertension, tachycardia, arrhythmias, nervousness, headache, tremor, muscle cramps, and others.</li><li><strong>Fluticasone Propionate Overdose:</strong> May cause temporary adrenal suppression, but this is usually self-limiting. Chronic overdose may lead to adrenal suppression.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Long-acting selective β-adrenoceptor stimulants, Respiratory corticosteroids</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><ul><li>Store below 30°C.</li><li>Do not puncture or incinerate the pressurized canister, even if empty.</li><li>Keep away from eyes and out of the reach of children.</li><li>Avoid direct sunlight and heat.</li></ul>', 'active', '1873_1742847380.webp', 8, 12, 'mahidsiam1@gmail.com', '2025-03-25 01:16:20', '2025-05-05 19:41:09'),
(4640, 'Uroza', 'Flavoxate Hydrochloride', 18.00, 10, 'tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '200 mg', 'no', 'no', '<p><br></p>', 'active', '41_1742847611.jpg', 58, 1, 'rajubinahmed@gmail.com', '2025-03-25 01:20:11', '2025-05-04 22:44:25'),
(4641, 'Ascon-F 200', 'Beclomethasone Dipropionate + Formoterol Fumarate', 550.00, 1, 'Metered-Dose Inhaler (MDI)', '1 inhaler', 'Inhaler', '(200 mcg+6 mcg)/puff', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><p>Ascon-F is indicated for the treatment of <strong>asthma</strong> and <strong>COPD</strong>.</p><ul><li><strong>Asthma</strong>: This inhaler is indicated in the regular treatment of asthma where the use of a combination of inhaled corticosteroid and long-acting P2 adrenergic agonist is appropriate.</li><li><strong>COPD</strong>: This inhaler is indicated for the symptomatic treatment of severe COPD and a history of repeated exacerbations despite regular therapy with long-acting bronchodilators.</li></ul><p><em>রেজিস্টার্ড চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ মোতাবেক ঔষধ সেবন করুন</em>.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>Ascon-F is a combination of <strong>Beclomethasone Dipropionate BP</strong> and <strong>Formoterol Fumarate Dihydrate BP</strong>. It is an HFA-based, environment-friendly inhaler, which does not contain chlorofluorocarbon (CFC), a compound responsible for ozone layer depletion.</p><ul><li><strong>Beclomethasone Dipropionate</strong>: A synthetic halogenated corticosteroid with potent anti-inflammatory activity. When given by inhalation, it exerts a glucocorticoid anti-inflammatory action in the lungs, without the side effects typically associated with systemic steroids.</li><li><strong>Formoterol Fumarate Dihydrate</strong>: A long-acting selective P2 adrenergic agonist with a rapid onset of action. Inhaled Formoterol acts in the lungs as a bronchodilator, providing long-lasting relief.</li></ul><p><strong>Dosage</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Asthma</strong>: The dosage should be adjusted based on disease severity. Once control is achieved, the dose should be titrated to the lowest effective dose.</li><li><strong>Maintenance Therapy</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Adults &amp; Adolescents (18 years &amp; above): One or two inhalations twice daily. The maximum daily dose is 4 inhalations.</li><li><strong>Maintenance and Reliever Therapy</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Adults &amp; Adolescents (18 years &amp; above): One inhalation twice daily. If symptoms persist, an additional inhalation should be taken. The maximum daily dose is 8 inhalations.</li><li><strong>COPD</strong>: 2 inhalations twice daily.</li></ul><p><em>রেজিস্টার্ড চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ মোতাবেক ঔষধ সেবন করুন</em>.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Administration</strong></p><p>Using an inhaler may seem simple, but many patients do not know the correct technique. Improper use can result in less medication reaching the lungs. Correct and regular use will prevent or lessen the severity of asthma attacks.</p><p>Steps for effective inhaler use (According to \"National Asthma Guidelines for Medical Practitioners\" by the Asthma Association):</p><ol><li>Remove the cap.</li><li>Shake the inhaler (at least six times) vigorously before use.</li><li>If the inhaler is new or hasn\'t been used for a week or more, shake it well and release one puff into the air to ensure it works.</li><li>Breathe out as fully as comfortably possible and hold the inhaler upright.</li><li>Place the actuator into your mouth between your teeth, closing your lips around the mouthpiece.</li><li>While breathing in deeply and slowly, press down firmly on the canister to release the medicine.</li><li>Remove the inhaler from your mouth. Hold your breath for at least 10 seconds or as long as is comfortable.</li><li>If your doctor prescribed more than one inhalation, wait 1 minute between puffs, shake the inhaler well, and repeat steps 4 to 7.</li><li>After use, replace the cap on the mouthpiece and rinse your mouth with water.</li></ol><p><strong>Cleaning</strong>: Clean your inhaler at least once a week. Remove the canister and rinse the plastic actuator and cap in warm water (do not immerse the metal canister). Dry thoroughly and replace the canister gently.</p><p><em>রেজিস্টার্ড চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ মোতাবেক ঔষধ সেবন করুন</em>.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Interaction</strong></p><ul><li><strong>With medicine</strong>: Concomitant treatment with beta-adrenergic drugs, quinidine, disopyramide, procainamides, phenothiazines, antihistamines, MAO inhibitors, and tricyclic antidepressants should be avoided.</li><li><strong>With food &amp; others</strong>: No data found on interaction with food for this medicine.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Ascon-F is contraindicated in patients with hypersensitivity to any of the ingredients.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common side effects</strong>: Hypokalemia, headache, tremor, palpitations, cough, muscle spasms, and prolongation of QT interval.</li><li><strong>Rare side effects</strong>: Rash, urticaria, pruritus, erythema, and oedema of the eyes, face, lips, or throat may occur.</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy</strong>: Administration of this inhaler in pregnant women should only be considered if the expected benefit to the mother outweighs any possible risk to the fetus.</li><li><strong>Lactation</strong>: Administration during lactation should only be considered if the expected benefit to the mother outweighs any possible risk to the child.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Severe Exacerbation</strong>: Treatment with Beclomethasone and Formoterol should not be initiated during a severe exacerbation or if patients have significantly worsening or acutely deteriorating asthma.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Respiratory corticosteroids.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><ul><li>Do not puncture, break, or incinerate the pressurized canister even when apparently empty.</li><li>Avoid direct sunlight and heat.</li><li>Store below 30°C in a dry place, protected from light.</li><li>Keep away from children and eyes.</li></ul>', 'active', '974_1742847655.webp', 5, 12, 'mahidsiam1@gmail.com', '2025-03-25 01:20:55', '2025-03-25 01:20:55'),
