(4647, 'Isobgul', 'Ispaghula Husk [Psyllium]', 10.00, 30, 'x 3.5 gm sachet', '3.5 gm sachet', 'Sachet', '3.5 gm/sachet', 'no', 'no', '<p><br></p>', 'active', '368_1742848088.jpg', 26, 1, 'rajubinahmed@gmail.com', '2025-03-25 01:28:08', '2025-05-03 21:07:37'),
(4648, 'Ritch', 'Fexofenadine Hydrochloride', 5.04, 10, 'strip', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '60 mg', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Allergic Rhinitis</strong>: Ritch is indicated for the relief of symptoms associated with seasonal and perennial allergic rhinitis in adults and children aged 12 years and over. Symptoms effectively treated include sneezing, rhinorrhea, lacrimation, itchy red eyes, and itchy nose/palate/throat.</li><li> <em>রেজিস্টার্ড চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ মোতাবেক ঔষধ সেবন করুন</em>.</li></ul><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p>The <strong>H1 histamine receptor</strong> mediates hypersensitivity and allergic reactions. When exposed to an allergen, mast cells and basophils degranulate, releasing histamine and other inflammatory mediators. Histamine binds to H1 receptors, triggering the release of pro-inflammatory cytokines, leading to symptoms such as pruritus, rhinorrhea, and watery eyes.</p><p><strong>Fexofenadine</strong> is considered an \"inverse agonist\" of the H1 receptor because it stabilizes the inactive form of the receptor, preventing activation and subsequent downstream effects. It has potent and selective affinity for H1 receptors and does not exhibit antidopaminergic, antiserotonergic, anticholinergic, sedative, or adrenergic blocking activity. Fexofenadine does not cross the blood-brain barrier, minimizing CNS effects.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Allergic Rhinitis</strong>:</li><li><strong>Adults and children 12 years and older</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Tablet: 60 mg twice daily or 120 mg once daily or 180 mg once daily</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">In case of impaired renal function: 60 mg once daily</li><li><strong>Children 6 to 11 years</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Tablet: 30 mg twice daily or 60 mg once daily</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">In case of impaired renal function: 30 mg once daily</li><li><strong>Children 2 to 11 years</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Suspension: 30 mg or 5 ml twice daily</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">In case of impaired renal function: 30 mg or 5 ml once daily</li><li><strong>Chronic Idiopathic Urticaria</strong>:</li><li><strong>Adults and children 12 years and older</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Tablet: 60 mg twice daily or 120 mg once daily or 180 mg once daily</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">In case of impaired renal function: 60 mg once daily</li><li><strong>Children 6 to 11 years</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Tablet: 30 mg twice daily or 60 mg once daily</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">In case of impaired renal function: 30 mg once daily</li><li><strong>Children 6 months to less than 2 years</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Suspension: 15 mg or 2.5 ml (1/2 tsp) twice daily</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">In case of impaired renal function: 15 mg or 2.5 ml (1/2 tsp) once daily</li><li><strong>Children 2 to 11 years</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-2\">Suspension: 30 mg or 5 ml (1 tsp) twice daily</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">In case of impaired renal function: 30 mg or 5 ml (1 tsp) once daily</li></ul><p><em>রেজিস্টার্ড চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ মোতাবেক ঔষধ সেবন করুন</em>.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Interaction</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Ritch</strong> does not undergo hepatic biotransformation, so it does not interact with other medications through hepatic mechanisms.</li><li><strong>Erythromycin</strong> or <strong>ketoconazole</strong> co-administration may increase plasma levels of fexofenadine by 2-3 times. This increase is not accompanied by QT interval changes or increased adverse reactions compared to the individual use of each medication.</li><li><strong>Antacids containing aluminum and magnesium hydroxide</strong> should not be taken within 2 hours before or after taking Ritch, as they reduce bioavailability due to binding in the gastrointestinal tract.</li></ul><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><p>Ritch is contraindicated in patients with known hypersensitivity to <strong>Fexofenadine Hydrochloride</strong> or any of its ingredients.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Side Effects</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Common</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Nervous system: headache, drowsiness, dizziness</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Gastrointestinal: nausea</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">General disorders: fatigue</li><li><strong>Rare/Uncommon</strong>:</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Immune system: hypersensitivity reactions (angioedema, chest tightness, dyspnoea, flushing, anaphylaxis)</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Psychiatric: insomnia, nervousness, sleep disorders</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Cardiac: tachycardia, palpitations</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Gastrointestinal: diarrhea</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Skin: rash, urticaria, pruritus</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Pregnancy</strong>: There are limited data on Fexofenadine in pregnant women. Animal studies show no direct or indirect harmful effects, but Fexofenadine should only be used during pregnancy if necessary.</li><li><strong>Lactation</strong>: Fexofenadine has been found to cross into breast milk. Therefore, it is not recommended for breastfeeding mothers.</li></ul><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Caution is advised when administering <strong>Ritch</strong> to elderly patients or those with renal or hepatic impairment.</li><li>Patients with a history of cardiovascular disease should be aware that antihistamines may cause tachycardia and palpitations.</li><li><strong>Driving and machine use</strong>: Fexofenadine is unlikely to affect the ability to drive or operate machinery. However, individuals should check their personal response before engaging in activities requiring concentration.</li></ul><p><strong>Use in Special Populations</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Renal and hepatic impaired patients</strong>: Dose adjustments are necessary, especially in those with renal impairment. The starting dose for renal impairment is 60 mg once daily.</li><li><strong>Elderly</strong>: There is increased bioavailability in individuals over 65 years, and caution should be exercised.</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><ul><li>Symptoms: Dizziness, drowsiness, fatigue, and dry mouth.</li><li>Overdose with doses up to <strong>800 mg</strong> and up to <strong>690 mg twice daily</strong> for a month showed no significant adverse reactions. Standard supportive treatment should be provided, as <strong>haemodialysis</strong> does not effectively remove Ritch from the bloodstream.</li></ul><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Non-sedating antihistamines.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Store in a dry place, away from light and heat, and keep out of the reach of children.</p><p><br></p><p><strong>Chemical Structure</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Molecular Formula</strong>: C32H39NO4</li><li><strong>Chemical Structure</strong>: Fexofenadine Hydrochloride</li></ul><p><strong>Common Questions about Ritch 60 mg Tablet</strong></p><ul><li><strong>What is Ritch 60 mg Tablet?</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">An antihistamine that blocks histamine to alleviate allergy symptoms.</li><li><strong>What are the uses of Ritch 60 mg Tablet?</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">It treats allergic rhinitis and urticaria, providing relief from symptoms like sneezing, itching, and runny nose.</li><li><strong>What are the side effects?</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Common side effects include dizziness, headache, nausea, and fatigue.</li><li><strong>Can Ritch 60 mg Tablet make you sleepy?</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Yes, it can cause sleepiness in some people.</li><li><strong>What should I do in case of an overdose?</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">If you suspect an overdose, contact your doctor immediately.</li><li><strong>How quickly does Ritch 60 mg Tablet work?</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">It works within an hour, with peak effects observed in 6 hours.</li><li><strong>Can I take antacids with Ritch?</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">No, antacids should be taken at least 2 hours before or after Ritch.</li></ul><p><strong>Quick Tips</strong></p><ul><li>Ritch is a non-sedating antihistamine, effective for allergy relief.</li><li>Avoid taking it with fruit juices, especially grapefruit juice, as they may reduce its effectiveness.</li><li>Do not use antacids near the time of taking Ritch as they can reduce its absorption.</li></ul><p><em>রেজিস্টার্ড চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ মোতাবেক ঔষধ সেবন করুন</em>.</p>', 'active', '1541_1742848130.webp', 44, 12, 'mahidsiam1@gmail.com', '2025-03-25 01:28:50', '2025-03-25 01:28:50'),
