, a decision should be made whether to discontinue nursing or to discontinue the drug, taking into account the benefit of the drug to the mother.</p><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><p>Patients should be cautioned that Protocid tablet should not be split, chewed, or crushed. Long-term therapy of Protocid may lead to malabsorption of cyanocobalamin (Vitamin B12) or may increase the risk of osteoporosis-related disorders.</p><p><strong>Overdose Effects</strong></p><p>There are no known symptoms of overdosage in humans. Since Protocid is highly protein bound, it is not readily dialyzable. Apart from symptomatic and supportive management, no specific therapy is recommended.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p>Proton Pump Inhibitor</p><p><strong>Reconstitution</strong></p><p><em>Direction for use of IV injection:</em> Protocid lyophilized powder and 0.9% Sodium Chloride Injection is for intravenous administration only and must not be given by any other route. Protocid IV injection should be given as a slow intravenous injection. The solution for IV injection is obtained by adding 10 ml 0.9% Sodium Chloride Injection to the vial containing powder. After reconstitution, the injection should be given slowly over a period of at least 2 to 5 minutes. Use only freshly prepared solution. The reconstituted solution may be stored at room temperature (up to 30° C) for a maximum of 4 hours.</p><p><em>Direction for use of IV infusion:</em> Protocid IV infusion should be given as an intravenous infusion over a period of approximately 15 minutes. Protocid IV infusion should be reconstituted with 10 ml of 0.9% Sodium Chloride Injection and further diluted (admixed) with 0.9% Sodium Chloride Injection or 5% Dextrose or Lactated Ringer\'s Injection to a final volume of 100 ml. The reconstituted solution may be stored at room temperature (up to 30° C) for a maximum of 4 hours prior to further dilution. The admixed solution may be stored at room temperature (up to 30° C) and must be used within 24 hours from the time of initial reconstitution.</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p>Keep in a dry place, away from light and heat. Keep out of the reach of children.</p><p><strong>Chemical Structure</strong></p><p>Molecular Formula: C16H15F2N3O4S</p><p>Chemical Structure: Chemical Structure of Pantoprazole Sodium</p><p><strong>Common Questions about Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection</strong></p><p><strong>What is Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection?</strong></p><p>Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection is a proton pump inhibitor. It suppresses the final step in gastric acid production. It is used to treat Peptic ulcer diseases, GERD, Ulcer induced by NSAIDs, Eradication of Helicobacter pylori, Zollinger-Ellison Syndrome.</p><p><strong>How long do I need to use Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection before I see improvement in my condition?</strong></p><p>Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection is to be taken till the time you see an improvement in your health conditions.</p><p><strong>At what frequency do I need to use Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection?</strong></p><p>Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection should be taken in the dosage as prescribed by the doctor.</p><p><strong>Should I use Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection on an empty stomach, before food, or after food?</strong></p><p>Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection should be taken prior to the meal, approximately 30 minutes before it, in the prescribed dosage.</p><p><strong>What are the instructions for the storage and disposal of Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection?</strong></p><p>Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection should be kept in a cool dry place and in its original packaging. Make sure this medication remains unreachable to children and pets.</p><p><strong>What are the effects of Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection on older adults?</strong></p><p>Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection may increase the risk for bone fractures, especially with longer use, and higher doses in older adults. Consult your doctor about ways to prevent bone loss/fracture.</p><p><strong>How long does it take for Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection to work?</strong></p><p>You should start to feel better within 2 to 3 days. It may take up to 4 weeks for this medication to work properly, so you may still have some symptoms during this time.</p><p><strong>Is Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection safe?</strong></p><p>Yes, Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection is relatively safe. It is advised to consult the doctor before consuming Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection.</p><p><strong>Does Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection cause weight gain?</strong></p><p>In rare cases, the consumption of Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection can cause weight gain. You are advised to consult your doctor for any weight-related concerns.</p><p><strong>What are the side effects of Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection?</strong></p><p>The side effects of Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection aren\'t that common. Still, people face the following issues sometimes - headache, diarrhea, constipation, and allergic reactions.</p><p><strong>Can I take Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection if I am pregnant or breastfeeding?</strong></p><p>Though Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection isn’t a serious issue for pregnant or breastfeeding persons, it’s advised not to take the medicine unless prescribed by your doctor.</p><p><strong>What should I do if I miss a dose of Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection?</strong></p><p>If you miss a dose of Protocid 40 mg/vial Injection, take it as soon as you remember. However, if it is close to the time for your next dose, skip the missed dose and take your next dose at the regular time.</p><p><em>রেজিস্টার্ড চিকিৎসকের পরামর্শ মোতাবেক ঔষধ সেবন করুন</em></p><p><br></p><p>This version ensures all the headings are bolded for clarity and emphasis. Let me know if you need further modifications!</p>', 'active', '421_1743293163.webp', 5, 12, 'mahidsiam1@gmail.com', '2025-03-30 04:06:03', '2025-05-05 19:41:53');
