(6114, 'Angimet MR', 'Trimetazidine Dihydrochloride', 6.00, 10, 'tablet', '10 tablet in a strip', 'Tablet', '35 mg', 'yes', 'no', NULL, 'active', '1654_1744213999.jpg', 43, 12, 'mahidsiam1@gmail.com', '2025-04-09 19:53:19', '2025-04-09 19:53:19'),
(6115, 'Laclose', 'Lactulose', 120.37, 1, 'Bottle', '100 ml bottle', 'Oral Solution', '3.35 gm/5 ml', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Laclose 3.35 gm/5 ml</strong></p><p> <strong>Constipation (Chronic Constipation):</strong></p><p> In every case of chronic constipation, initial treatment should consist of a diet rich in fiber (vegetables, salads, fruits, etc.), a generous amount of liquids, and regular physical exercise. Laclose 3.35 gm/5 ml is only to be taken when these measures prove insufficient.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p> Osmotic purgatives</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p> Laclose 3.35 gm/5 ml is a synthetic disaccharide. It is metabolized in the colon by saccharolytic bacteria, producing low molecular weight organic acids (mainly lactic acid), which lower the pH of the colon contents. This promotes water retention by an osmotic effect, thereby increasing peristaltic activity. Laclose is minimally absorbed, so pharmacokinetics of the absorbed portion are not relevant to its main therapeutic action.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration of Laclose 3.35 gm/5 ml</strong></p><ul><li><strong>In Constipation (Chronic Constipation):</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Adults:</strong> Initially 3–6 teaspoons daily; for long-term therapy: 1½–6 teaspoons daily</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Children up to 14 years:</strong> Initially 3 teaspoons daily; for long-term therapy: 1–2 teaspoons daily</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Infants and toddlers:</strong> Initially 1–2 teaspoons daily; for long-term therapy: 1 teaspoon daily</li><li><strong>In Damaged Intestinal Flora:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Adults:</strong> 1–2 teaspoons daily</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Children:</strong> 1 teaspoon daily</li><li><strong>For Reduction of Blood Ammonia Level:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Hyperammonemia in Hepatopathy:</strong> Maximum of 18–30 teaspoons daily</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Portal Systemic Encephalopathy:</strong> Hourly doses of 6–9 teaspoons may be used to induce rapid laxation. Once laxative effect is achieved, the dose should be reduced.</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction of Laclose 3.35 gm/5 ml</strong></p><p> No significant drug interactions. However, the glycosidic effect of cardiac glycosides can be intensified by potassium deficiency due to misuse.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity to galactose and/or lactose</li><li>Galactose-free diet</li><li>Gastro-cardial symptom complex</li><li>Suspected intestinal obstruction</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects of Laclose 3.35 gm/5 ml</strong></p><ul><li>Occasionally flatulence, cramps, and abdominal discomfort may occur at the beginning of treatment (usually resolved by dose reduction)</li><li>Overdose can cause diarrhea</li><li>Abuse may result in loss of electrolytes, especially potassium</li></ul><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><p> US FDA Pregnancy Category B. Studies show no adverse effects. However, the decision to use during pregnancy and lactation must be made by a registered physician.</p><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li>Use with caution in patients who are intolerant to Laclose</li><li>In (pre) coma hepaticum, higher doses are required and should be monitored, especially in diabetic patients</li></ul><p><strong>Overdose Effects of Laclose 3.35 gm/5 ml</strong></p><p> There are no reported cases of accidental overdose. In such cases, symptoms like diarrhea and abdominal cramps are expected.</p><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p> Keep in a dry place away from light and heat. Keep out of the reach of children.</p>', 'active', '1412_1744214001.jpg', 7, 12, 'meraj.wdev@gmail.com', '2025-04-09 19:53:21', '2025-04-09 19:53:21'),
