(6124, 'Ural-K', 'Potassium Citrate + Citric Acid', 200.00, 1, 'Bottle', '200 ml bottle', 'Oral Solution', '(1500 mg+250 mg)/5 ml', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Administration Instructions</strong></p><p> Oral solution should be taken diluted in water according to directions, followed by additional water if desired. Palatability is enhanced if chilled before taking. Proper dilution may help prevent gastrointestinal injury associated with the oral ingestion of concentrated potassium salt preparations.</p><p><strong>Dosage Guidelines</strong></p><p><strong>To Relieve Discomfort in UTI</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults and children over 6 years:</strong> 10 ml 3 times daily, diluted with 1 glass of water</li><li><strong>Children 1–6 years:</strong> 5 ml 3 times daily, diluted with ½ glass of water</li></ul><p><strong>To Prevent Kidney Stones, with a Uricosuric Agent to Prevent Gout, and in Acidosis Caused by Kidney Diseases</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Adults:</strong> 10–15 ml 4 times daily (or as directed by the physician), diluted with 1 glass of water</li><li><strong>Pediatric:</strong> 5–10 ml 4 times daily (or as directed by the physician), diluted with ½ glass of water</li></ul>', 'active', '1491_1744214551.jpg', 3, 12, 'meraj.wdev@gmail.com', '2025-04-09 20:02:31', '2025-04-09 20:02:31'),
