(6200, 'Optear', 'Povidone Iodine', 90.00, 1, 'Drop', '10 ml drop', 'Ophthalmic Solution', '5% v/v', 'yes', 'no', '<p><strong>Indications of Optear 5%</strong></p><p> <strong>Cream or ointment:</strong></p><p> <strong>Therapeutically:</strong> As an adjunct to systemic therapy in the following indications:</p><ul><li>Primary or secondary topical infections</li><li>Infected surgical incisions</li><li>Infected decubitus or stasis ulcers</li><li>Pyodermas</li><li>Secondarily infected dermatoses</li><li>Infected traumatic lesions</li></ul><p><strong>Prophylactically:</strong></p><ul><li>To prevent microbial contamination in burns, incisions, and other topical lesions</li><li>For degerming skin in hyperalimentation, the umbilical area, or circumcision</li><li>Its use for abrasions, minor cuts, and wounds prevents the development of infections and permits wound healing</li></ul><p><strong>Solution:</strong></p><ul><li>For the prevention and treatment of surface infections, as well as to degerm the skin, mucous membrane, and hyperalimentation procedures</li><li>For seborrhea</li><li>For preoperative and postoperative scrubbing and washing of hospital operating rooms and equipment</li><li>For preoperative prepping of the operative site, including the vagina</li><li>For disinfection of wounds, burns, lacerations, and abrasions</li><li>As a prophylactic anti-infective agent in house, hospital &amp; office procedures</li><li>Postoperative application to incisions to help prevent infection</li><li>In oral moniliasis (thrush); bacterial and mycotic skin infections, decubitus &amp; stasis ulcers</li><li>As a preoperative swab in the mouth &amp; throat</li></ul><p><strong>Gargle &amp; Mouthwash:</strong></p><p> It is a pleasantly flavored solution used for:</p><ul><li>The treatment of acute mucosal infections of the mouth and pharynx</li><li>For oral hygiene prior to, during, and after dental and oral surgery</li></ul><p><strong>Surgical Scrub:</strong></p><p> It is a golden surfactant solution that forms rich, golden lather, used:</p><ul><li>As an antiseptic skin cleanser for preoperative and postoperative scrubbing and washing by surgeons and operation theatre staff and preoperative preparation of patients\' skin</li></ul><p><strong>Powder:</strong></p><p> Used for topical application in the following indications:</p><ul><li>Superficial wounds</li><li>Minor cuts</li><li>Burns</li><li>Abrasions</li><li>Lacerations</li><li>In the treatment and prevention of infections</li></ul><p><strong>Ophthalmic Solution:</strong></p><p> Povidone is used for the symptomatic treatment of dry eye conditions, including keratoconjunctivitis sicca. It is also given as a substitute for tear fluid in case of the unstable tear film or insufficient moistening of the eye surface.</p><p><strong>Therapeutic Class</strong></p><p> Iodine compounds (Anti-septic Preparations)</p><p><strong>Pharmacology</strong></p><p> Povidone-Iodine contains Povidone-Iodine, a stable chemical complex of polyvinylpyrrolidone (PVP) and elemental iodine. It exhibits non-selective broad-spectrum germicidal action and acts as a bactericide (both gram-positive and gram-negative), fungicide, virucide, sporicide, amebicide, insecticide, and nematocide. It is effective even in dilute solutions and does not develop resistance in microorganisms. Povidone-Iodine is safer and easier to use than classic iodine preparations, with low systemic toxicity. It is non-sensitizing and does not cause pain when applied to wounds or mucous membranes. Povidone-Iodine will not permanently stain skin, natural fibers, or hard surfaces and is less irritating than conventional iodine preparations.</p><p><strong>Dosage &amp; Administration of Optear 5%</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Cream or ointment:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For the treatment of infection: Apply once or twice daily or at dressing changes for a maximum of 14 days.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">For the prevention of infection: Apply once or twice a week for as long as necessary.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">The affected skin should be cleaned and dried. May be covered with a dressing or bandage.</li><li><strong>Solution:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Apply full strength as often as needed as paint, spray, or wet soak. May be bandaged (where necessary).</li><li><strong>Gargle &amp; Mouthwash:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\">Adults and children over 6 years of age: Use undiluted or diluted with an equal volume of warm water. Gargle or rinse with up to 10 mL for up to 30 seconds without swallowing. Repeat up to four times daily for up to 14 consecutive days or as directed.</li><li><strong>Surgical Scrub:</strong></li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Preoperative and Postoperative washing by Operating Personnel:</strong> Wet hands and forearms with water. Pour about 5 mL of Optear 5% Surgical Scrub on the palm of the hand and spread over both hands and forearms. Rub thoroughly for about five minutes. Use a brush if desired. Clean thoroughly under fingernails. Add a little water and develop copious suds. Rinse thoroughly under running water.</li><li class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>For Preoperative use on Patients:</strong> Apply 1 mL of Optear 5% Surgical Scrub (sufficient to cover an area of 20-30 square inches), develop lather, and scrub thoroughly for about five minutes. Rinse off with sterile gauze saturated with water.</li><li><strong>Powder:</strong> Apply a light dusting of powder to the affected area. When dry, it forms a protective antiseptic layer.</li><li><strong>Ophthalmic Solution:</strong> Instill 1 drop 4 times daily or as required, depending upon the severity of the disease, into the conjunctival sac.</li></ul><p><strong>Interaction of Optear 5%</strong></p><p> It interacts with strong alkali, sodium thiosulphate, sodium metabisulphite, and thiomersal. Concurrent use with lithium therapy may cause a hypothyroidic effect.</p><p><strong>Contraindications</strong></p><ul><li>Hypersensitivity reactions may occur.</li><li>Regular use in patients with thyroid disorders (especially nodular colloid goitre, endemic goitre, and Hashimoto\'s thyroiditis) or those receiving lithium therapy should be avoided.</li><li>In severely burnt patients, serum iodide levels should be assessed due to potential hepatic and renal impairment.</li><li>Optear 5% Powder should not be used in serious cavities and in children under the age of 2 years.</li></ul><p><strong>Side Effects of Optear 5%</strong></p><p> May cause hypersensitivity reactions and irritation of the skin and mucous membranes. Applying Povidone-Iodine to severe burns or large areas of denuded skin may produce systemic adverse effects such as metabolic acidosis, hypernatraemia, and renal function impairment. It may also interfere with thyroid function tests.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy &amp; Lactation</strong></p><p> Regular use of Povidone-Iodine should be avoided during pregnancy and lactation as absorbed iodine can cross the placental barrier and be secreted into breast milk. Though no adverse effects have been reported from limited use, caution is advised, and the therapeutic benefit should be balanced against the possible effects of iodine absorption on fetal thyroid function and development. Povidone-Iodine 1% Mouthwash Gargle should not be used for more than 14 days in pregnant and lactating women.</p><p><strong>Precautions &amp; Warnings</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Cream or ointment:</strong> In case of deep or puncture wounds or serious burns, consult a registered physician. Discontinue use and consult a physician if redness, irritation, swelling, or pain persists or increases or if infection occurs.</li><li><strong>Solution:</strong> In preoperative prepping, avoid \'pooling\' beneath the patient. Prolonged exposure to the wet solution may cause irritation or, rarely, severe skin reactions. If redness, irritation, swelling, or pain persists or increases, discontinue use and consult a physician.</li><li><strong>Gargle &amp; Mouthwash:</strong> Avoid regular use as prolonged use may lead to the absorption of significant iodine. Not for use in children under 6 years of age.</li><li><strong>Surgical Scrub:</strong> Caution is needed with regular applications to broken skin in patients with pre-existing renal insufficiency. It may permanently discolor white gold jewelry; it is recommended to remove such jewelry before use.</li><li><strong>Powder:</strong> Take care when using on known iodine sensitivity, although most people do not react to Povidone-Iodine. Excess powder can be washed off with warm water. Not to be administered internally.</li><li><strong>Ophthalmic Solution:</strong> Patients who experience blurred vision after application should avoid driving or using machinery until their vision clears. Contact lenses should not be worn during instillation, and there should be an interval of at least 30 minutes before reinsertion.</li></ul><p><strong>Storage Conditions</strong></p><p> Store below 25°C. Do not freeze. Keep in a cool, dry place, protected from light. Keep out of the reach of children. Do not touch the ophthalmic solution dropper tip to any surface, as this may contaminate the preparation. Do not use it after one month of the first opening.</p><p><strong>Drug Classes</strong></p><p> Iodine compounds (Anti-septic Preparations)</p><p><strong>Mode Of Action</strong></p><p> Optear 5% is a complex of iodine and an organic polymer, povidone. This polymerization makes Optear 5% superior to ordinary elemental iodine by prolonging its germicidal activity. It liberates elemental iodine slowly, giving rapid microbicidal activity against Gram-positive and Gram-negative bacteria, protozoa, viruses, fungi/yeasts, and spores. It is non-staining, exerts prolonged germicidal action, and remains active in the presence of soap, blood, serum, pus, mucosal secretions, and water.</p><p><strong>Pregnancy</strong></p><p> Optear 5% Cream, Solution, and Powder are not recommended during pregnancy due to the possibility of iodine absorption affecting the fetal thyroid. The use of Povidone-Iodine is usually compatible with breastfeeding, but consult a physician. Regular use of Gargle &amp; Mouthwash and Surgical Scrub should also be avoided during pregnancy and lactation. There is no experience regarding the safety of the Povidone eye drops in pregnancy or lactation, and its administration is not recommended unless absolutely necessary.</p>', 'active', '502_1744223516.jpg', 30, 12, 'meraj.wdev@gmail.com', '2025-04-09 22:31:56', '2025-04-09 22:31:56'),
